('ELEM','LS2',1,1,1,NULL,'Dr. Fe del Mundo is renowned for her significant contributions to which field of medicine in the Philippines?','Cardiology','Oncology','Pediatrics','Neurology','C','Dr. Fe del Mundo is a distinguished Filipino pediatrician known for founding the first pediatric hospital in the Philippines and for her groundbreaking work in child healthcare.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,2,NULL,'Who is known as the "Father of Modern Physics" and is famous for the theory of relativity?','Albert Einstein','Galileo Galilei','Isaac Newton','Niels Bohr','A','Albert Einstein is widely recognized as the "Father of Modern Physics" for his development of the theory of relativity, particularly the equation E=mc².',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,3,NULL,'How has the invention of the light bulb by Thomas Edison influenced modern society?','It has no influence','It is only useful for decoration','It has improved agricultural practices','It has revolutionized how we use energy and extend our productive hours','D','The light bulb drastically changed human activity by enabling work, learning, and other tasks to continue beyond daylight hours.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,4,NULL,'Which of the following is a key scientific value that encourages the pursuit of knowledge?','Apathy','Curiosity','Laziness','Indifference','B','Curiosity is a foundational scientific value that drives inquiry, experimentation, and the search for understanding.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,5,NULL,'Which scientific value promotes transparency and accountability in research?','Honesty','Ambiguity','Complacency','Disinterest','A','Honesty in reporting results ensures transparency and integrity, which are critical in scientific inquiry.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,6,NULL,'Why is critical thinking essential when evaluating the reliability of scientific data?','It encourages bias and subjective interpretations.','It allows for the acceptance of all claims without question.','It promotes the analysis of evidence and identification of potential flaws.','It simplifies the understanding of complex information without careful consideration.','C','Critical thinking helps scientists evaluate sources, verify results, and identify limitations or errors.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,7,NULL,'If you need to measure a small amount of salt for a recipe, which unit would be most appropriate?','Kilograms (kg)','Grams (g)','Milligrams (mg)','Degrees Centigrade (°C)','B','Salt for a recipe is measured in grams; milligrams are too small to be practical in a kitchen.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,8,NULL,'A scientist needs to record the temperature at which water boils. Which unit of measurement is MOST appropriate?','Milliliters (mL)','Grams (g)','Degrees Celsius (°C)','Kilopascals (kPa)','C','Temperature is commonly measured in °C in scientific settings, especially for physical changes like boiling.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,9,NULL,'How would using the wrong unit of measurement affect the outcome of a scientific experiment?','All units are interchangeable','It has no effect on the experiment','It only matters in complex experiments','It can lead to inaccurate results and unreliable data','D','Precision in units ensures consistency and comparability of results; wrong units can distort data interpretation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,10,NULL,'Why is it necessary to conduct multiple trials in a scientific experiment?','To introduce confusion in the findings.','To utilize only one method consistently.','To confirm results and reduce possible errors.','To make the experiment take longer to complete.','C','Repeating trials increases the reliability and accuracy of results by minimizing random errors.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,11,NULL,'What is one key feature of a fair test in scientific investigations?','Failing to record any measurements.','Disregarding results from different trials.','Changing several variables at the same time.','Maintaining constant variables while altering the independent one.','D','A fair test ensures that only the independent variable is changed, while all others are controlled. This ensures valid and reliable conclusions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,12,NULL,'How does accurately recording data impact the validity of an experiment?','It has no effect on the overall outcome.','It makes the analysis more complicated.','It is only important in more complex experiments.','It guarantees that results can be compared and repeated.','D','Precise and accurate data collection ensures experiments are replicable, which is a cornerstone of scientific validity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,13,NULL,'If a material feels rough to the touch, what property are you observing?','Color','Texture','Shape','Weight','B','Texture refers to how a material feels—whether it is smooth, rough, soft, or hard—when touched.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,14,NULL,'Which characteristic can be determined by using the sense of sight?','Texture','Smell','Color','Taste','C','Color is a physical property observable through vision. Unlike smell or texture, it doesn’t require touch or chemical interaction.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,15,NULL,'How does the ability to observe the properties of materials impact on their practical applications in everyday life?','It has no effect on material choices.','Observing properties complicates decisions','It helps choose the right materials for specific uses.','All materials are interchangeable regardless of properties','C','Understanding material properties helps us choose materials for appropriate tasks—e.g., metals for tools, plastic for insulation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,16,NULL,'Which state of matter has a definite shape and volume?','Liquid','Solid','Gas','Plasma','B','Solids maintain both a fixed shape and volume due to closely packed particles.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,17,NULL,'What property describes a liquid''s ability to take the shape of its container?','Definite shape','Definite volume','No definite shape','Hardness','C','Liquids do not have a definite shape but take the shape of their container, while maintaining a definite volume.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,18,NULL,'How would you explain the difference in properties between gases and solids in terms of shape and volume?','Solids and gases have the same properties','Solids have no shape or volume, while gases have both','Solids have a definite shape and volume, while gases have neither','Gases have a definite shape and volume, while solids change shape','C','Gases expand to fill any container (no definite shape or volume), while solids retain both shape and volume.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,19,NULL,'Which of the following is an example of a pure substance?','Salad','Saltwater','Distilled water','Air','C','A pure substance consists of only one type of particle or molecule. Distilled water is H₂O with no impurities.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,20,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately describes a mixture?','A mixture has distinct chemical properties.','A mixture is made up of only one type of particle.','A mixture has a uniform composition throughout.','A mixture can be separated into its components by physical means.','D','Mixtures are physical combinations of substances and can be separated without changing chemical properties.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,21,NULL,'Why is it important to distinguish between mixtures and pure substances in scientific applications?','It has no importance','Only mixtures are relevant in science','All substances behave the same way in experiments','Understanding the differences informs material selection and processing methods','D','Knowing whether a substance is pure or a mixture affects its behavior in experiments, its physical and chemical properties, and its appropriateness for various uses. Pure substances have consistent properties, while mixtures vary, which impacts processing and applications.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,22,NULL,'Which system helps us breathe?','Muscular system','Circulatory system','Digestive system','Respiratory system','D','The respiratory system, which includes the lungs and airways, is directly responsible for breathing, allowing the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,23,NULL,'What do the heart and blood vessels transport?','Food','Energy','Oxygen and Nutrients','Bones','C','The circulatory system, including the heart and blood vessels, is responsible for transporting oxygen, nutrients, hormones, and waste products throughout the body.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,24,NULL,'What does the skeletal system provide?','Movement','Support and protection','Digestion','Breathing','B','The skeletal system provides structural support and protects vital organs (e.g., the skull protects the brain, and ribs protect the heart and lungs).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,1,25,NULL,'Which part of the male reproductive system produces sperm?','Prostate','Penis','Testes','Vagina','C','The testes are the primary male reproductive organs responsible for producing sperm and the hormone testosterone.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,26,NULL,'What is the function of the uterus in the female reproductive system?','Egg production','Fetal development','Hormone production','Sperm delivery','B','The uterus is where the fertilized egg implants and where the fetus develops during pregnancy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,27,NULL,'Which part of the male reproductive system delivers sperm?','Prostate','Penis','Testes','Ovaries','B','The penis delivers sperm through the urethra during ejaculation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,28,NULL,'If a puppy has black fur like its mother, what kind of trait is the fur color?','Learned trait','Inherited trait','Acquired trait','Environmental trait','B','Fur color is a physical characteristic passed down genetically from parent to offspring.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,29,NULL,'What is one example of a physical characteristic passed from parents to offspring?','Learned skills','Eye color','Favorite food','Memorized fact','B','Eye color is an inherited trait controlled by genes passed from parents.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,30,NULL,'What is one way that an animal''s features might resemble its parents?','By learning the same tricks.','By having the same fur color.','By eating the same food.','By living in the same house.','B','Physical features such as fur color are inherited from the animal’s parents, not learned or influenced by environment alone.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,31,NULL,'What type of trait is this if a dog naturally retrieves objects without being taught?','Learned','Inherited behavioral','Physical','Environmental','B','Instinctive behaviors like retrieving in dogs are inherited and are not learned from the environment.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,32,NULL,'What is one example of an inherited physical trait mentioned in the concept?','Language','Hair texture','Learned tricks','Reading','B','Hair texture is determined by genetic inheritance, unlike language or reading, which are learned.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,33,NULL,'Which of the following is a trait that an animal is born with?','Ability to read','Instinct to hunt','Skill of riding a bike','Ability to speak a language','B','Instincts are inherited behaviors present at birth and do not require learning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,34,NULL,'What is one stage in the human life cycle?','Larva','Seedling','Adult','Pupa','C','"Adult" is one of the stages in the human life cycle; larva and pupa are insect stages, while seedling applies to plants.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,35,NULL,'“All living things, including humans, animals, and plants, go through life cycles. Plants also have life cycles, starting as seeds, germinating into seedlings, growing into mature plants, and producing seeds for the next generation.” What is the first stage of a plant''s life cycle mentioned in the text?','Mature plant','Seedling','Seed','Flower','C','A plant life cycle begins with a seed, which germinates into a seedling and grows into a mature plant.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,36,NULL,'What is one stage in the butterfly''s metamorphosis?','Puppy','Infant','Larva','Adult human','C','Larva is the second stage of complete metamorphosis in butterflies, following the egg stage.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,37,NULL,'Which part of a plant helps it stand upright?','Roots','Stems','Leaves','Flowers','B','Stems provide structural support and help the plant stay upright.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,38,NULL,'What is the function of the roots of a plant?','To make food','To hold the plant in place','Producing flowers','To protect seeds','B','Roots anchor the plant in the soil and absorb water and nutrients.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,39,NULL,'Which part of a plant helps it make food from sunlight?','Stems','Flowers','Leaves','Fruits','C','Leaves carry out photosynthesis, converting sunlight into food for the plant.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,40,NULL,'What type of animal eats only plants?','Carnivore','Herbivore','Omnivore','Microorganism','B','Herbivores are animals that exclusively feed on plant material.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,41,NULL,'What type of food does a carnivore eat?','Plants','Meat','Soil','Both plants and meat','B','Carnivores are animals that eat only meat. They rely on consuming other animals to meet their nutritional needs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,42,NULL,'Which of the following eats both plants and animals?','Herbivore','Omnivore','Carnivore','Aquatic animal','B','Omnivores consume both plant and animal matter. Examples include humans, bears, and pigs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,43,NULL,'Where do fish live?','Terrestrial','Aquatic','Aerial','Soil','B','Fish live in aquatic environments such as rivers, lakes, and oceans. They use gills to extract oxygen from water.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,44,NULL,'What type of habitat do most plants live in?','Aquatic','Aerial','Terrestrial','Inside other animals','C','Most plants grow on land, in terrestrial environments, where they receive sunlight, water, and nutrients from the soil.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,45,NULL,'Which of the following habitats is where birds spend a significant portion of their lives?','Terrestrial','Aquatic','Aerial','Underground','C','Birds are adapted to spend a significant amount of their time in the air (aerial habitat), though they may nest on land or trees.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,46,NULL,'Which animal group has feathers and wings?','Mammals','Amphibians','Fish','Birds','D','Feathers and wings are defining characteristics of birds. These features help most birds to fly, although not all birds are capable of flight. Feathers also play roles in insulation and mating displays.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,47,NULL,'What is one characteristic of mammals?','Gills','Scales','Fur or hair','Cold-blooded','C','Mammals are warm-blooded vertebrates with fur or hair, and they nurse their young with milk produced from mammary glands.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,48,NULL,'Which animal group is adapted to live in water and has gills?','Reptiles','Mammals','Fish','Amphibians','C','Fish are aquatic vertebrates that breathe using gills and move using fins, making them fully adapted to water environments.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,49,NULL,'What is one example of a non-living thing in a forest ecosystem?','Deer','Trees','Sunlight','Insects','C','Sunlight is an abiotic (non-living) factor. It affects plant growth and energy flow in ecosystems but is not alive.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,2,50,NULL,'What is one example of a living thing found in a pond ecosystem?','Water','Rocks','Fish','Oxygen','C','Fish are biotic (living) organisms and are part of the community interacting within the pond ecosystem.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,51,NULL,'Which of the following is a non-living component of an ecosystem?','Fungi','Bacteria','Soil','Grass','C','Soil is abiotic; it provides the foundation for plant growth but is not alive.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,52,NULL,'What is one technique for providing plants with necessary resources?','Ignoring them','Providing adequate water','Using excessive pesticides','Removing all surrounding soil','B','Water is essential for photosynthesis and nutrient transport in plants. Providing enough water is a key care technique.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,53,NULL,'Caring for plants and protecting animals is essential for maintaining healthy ecosystems and ensuring the well-being of our planet. Responsible practices involve understanding the needs of both plants and animals and implementing techniques that promote their survival. For plants, this includes providing adequate sunlight, water, and nutrients, as well as protecting them from pests and diseases. Techniques like proper watering, soil management, and integrated pest control are vital. For animals, responsible care involves providing suitable habitats, ensuring access to food and water, and protecting them from harm. This includes avoiding habitat destruction, preventing pollution, and respecting wildlife. Techniques such as creating wildlife corridors, establishing protected areas, and practicing ethical tourism are crucial. Discussing and demonstrating these practices help raise awareness about the importance of conservation and encourage individuals to act. By implementing appropriate techniques and fostering a culture of responsibility, we can contribute to a sustainable future where plants and animals thrive. What is one technique for protecting animals mentioned in the concept?','Habitat destruction','Preventing pollution','Introducing invasive species','Hunting endangered animals','B','Preventing pollution helps maintain healthy environments where animals can survive and reproduce.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,54,NULL,'Which is an appropriate technique for creating suitable animal habitats?','Filling in wetlands','Building on existing natural habitats','Establishing protected areas','Removing all-natural vegetation','C','Establishing protected areas ensures safe spaces for animals to live and reproduce without human interference.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,55,NULL,'Which of the following is the BEST way to help prevent illegal logging?','Ignore the problem.','Cut down trees in your own backyard.','Buy furniture made from illegally harvested wood.','Support companies and organizations that use sustainably sourced wood.','D','Supporting sustainable sources reduces the demand for illegally harvested wood and promotes forest conservation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,56,NULL,'What is one way to prevent illegal logging?','Ignoring regulations','Enforcing fishing laws','Encouraging dynamite fishing','Promoting sustainable forestry','D','Promoting sustainable forestry involves harvesting trees responsibly and planting new ones to replace them.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,57,NULL,'Which of the following is a way to prevent dynamite fishing?','Encouraging kaingin','Ignoring fishing laws','Promoting illegal logging','Educating communities about sustainable fishing methods','D','Education raises awareness of the damage caused by dynamite fishing and promotes safer fishing techniques.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,58,NULL,'Jose is trying to push a heavy wooden toy box across a carpeted floor. Which of the following would make it EASIER to push the toy box?','Push the box faster.','Push the box with less force.','Pushing the box on a rougher carpet','Lifting the box slightly to reduce contact with the carpet.','D','Reducing contact with the floor decreases friction, making it easier to move the object.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,59,NULL,'Paul is researching friction for a science project. He finds two sources: Source A: A website with a simple definition of friction but no diagrams or examples. Source B: A science textbook with a clear definition, diagrams illustrating different types of friction, and examples of friction in everyday life. Considering information literacy, which source would be MORE helpful for understanding the concept of friction?','Neither source is helpful.','Both sources are equally helpful.','Source A, because it''s easy to read.','Source B, because it provides a more complete and illustrative explanation.','D','Source B meets information literacy criteria by offering comprehensive content including visuals and real-life examples.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,60,NULL,'Two identical toy cars are released from the same height on two different ramps: one made of smooth, polished wood and the other made of rough, textured cardboard. The car on the wooden ramp travels much farther than the car on the cardboard ramp after reaching the bottom. Which statement BEST explains this difference?','The cardboard ramp is more colorful.','The wooden ramp creates less friction.','The wooden ramp is longer than the cardboard ramp.','The wooden ramp is heavier than the cardboard ramp.','B','The smoother surface of the wooden ramp reduces friction, allowing the toy car to travel farther.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,61,NULL,'Brian drops a crumpled piece of paper and a solid metal ball of the same mass from the same height. Considering air resistance, which object will likely hit the ground first?','The metal ball','The crumpled piece of paper','It depends on the color of the objects','Both will hit the ground at the same time','A','Air resistance affects objects with a larger surface area more significantly. Even if mass is the same, the metal ball is denser and more aerodynamic, allowing it to fall faster than the crumpled paper.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,62,NULL,'The ALS learners are researching the effect of air resistance on falling objects. You find two sources of information: Source A: A blog post claiming that heavier objects always fall faster, regardless of their shape. Source B: A physics textbook explaining that air resistance depends on factors like an object''s shape, surface area, and speed, and that it affects the rate at which objects fall. Which source provides more scientifically accurate information about the effect of air resistance on falling objects, and why?','Neither source is accurate.','Both sources are equally accurate.','Source A, because it''s a simple explanation.','Source B, because it considers multiple factors influencing air resistance.','D','Source B provides a scientific explanation by addressing shape, surface area, and speed, which are critical in understanding air resistance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,63,NULL,'Imagine you drop a small, light feather and a heavy, metal bolt from the same height at the same time. Which one will hit the ground first?','The feather will hit the ground first.','The metal bolt will hit the ground first.','They will hit the ground at almost the same time.','It depends on the color of the objects.','B','The feather has more surface area relative to its weight and is slowed down more by air resistance. The metal bolt falls faster.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,64,NULL,'Rosie observes several phenomena: a light bulb illuminating a room, a ringing bell producing sound, and a hot stove burner warming their hand. Which of these observations BEST demonstrates that heat is a transfer of energy, rather than a form of energy itself?','The ringing bell produces sound.','The light bulb illuminates the room.','The hot stove burner warming their hand.','All three observations demonstrate forms of energy.','C','Feeling warmth from a stove shows heat transferring from the hot object to a cooler one, not heat as a substance but as energy in transit.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,65,NULL,'The ALS learners are researching the nature of light, sound, and heat. They find two sources of information: Source A: A website claiming that heat is a form of energy, similar to light and sound. Source B: A science textbook explaining that light and sound are forms of energy, while heat is the transfer of thermal energy. Which source provides more scientifically accurate information about the nature of light, sound, and heat, and why?','Neither source is accurate.','Both sources are equally accurate.','Source A, because it''s a concise explanation.','Source B, because it correctly distinguishes between energy and energy transfer.','D','Source B makes the correct scientific distinction that heat is not a form of energy but the transfer of thermal energy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,66,NULL,'You hear the school bell ringing. What form of energy is being used to create the sound you hear?','Light energy','Heat energy','Sound energy','Chemical energy','C','Vibrations from the bell produce sound waves, which are a form of mechanical energy called sound energy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,67,NULL,'Brenda is looking for examples of simple machines in their school. Which of the following BEST exemplifies the use of an inclined plane to make work easier?','A flagpole','A seesaw','A pair of scissors','A ramp leading to the school''s entrance','D','A ramp is a classic example of an inclined plane, allowing objects to be moved upward with less effort.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,68,NULL,'The ALS learners are researching simple machines. They find two sources of information: Source A: A website showing pictures of various tools and labeling them as simple machines without explanation. Source B: A science textbook describing simple machines (inclined plane, wedge, lever, and pulley) and explaining how each works to make work easier. Which source provides more reliable and useful information for understanding simple machines, and why?','Neither source is useful.','Both sources are equally useful.','Source A, because it has many pictures.','Source B, because it provides descriptions and explanations of how simple machines work.','D','Source B gives explanations that build conceptual understanding, not just identification.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,69,NULL,'Rica is trying to move a heavy box up a flight of stairs. Which simple machine would be MOST effective to reduce the effort required, and why?','A lever, to pry the box up the stairs.','A wedge, to split the box into smaller pieces.','A pulley system, to lift the box vertically with less force.','An inclined plane (ramp), to reduce the steepness of the lift.','D','An inclined plane reduces the force needed to lift the box by allowing it to be rolled up gradually.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,70,NULL,'Which weather disturbance brings heavy rainfall and strong winds to the Philippines?','Typhoons','Earthquakes','Droughts','Volcanic eruptions','A','Typhoons are powerful tropical cyclones that frequently affect the Philippines, bringing rain and winds.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,71,NULL,'What type of weather disturbance can cause flash floods and lightning strikes in the Philippines?','Monsoons','Tsunamis','Heatwaves','Thunderstorms','D','Thunderstorms can lead to intense rain, causing flash floods, and produce lightning due to atmospheric charge imbalances.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,72,NULL,'Which weather disturbance results in prolonged periods of heavy rain in the Philippines?','Tornadoes','Monsoons','Blizzards','Sandstorms','B','Monsoons are seasonal winds that bring extended rainfall during the wet season in tropical countries.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,73,NULL,'How many distinct seasons does the Philippines have?','One','Two','Three','Four','B','The Philippines experiences two main seasons: the dry season and the wet (rainy) season.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,74,NULL,'What are the two distinct seasons in the Philippines?','Summer and winter','Spring and autumn','Wet and dry','Hot and cold','C','The Philippines'' climate is classified into wet and dry seasons, influenced by monsoons and trade winds.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',1,3,75,NULL,'Which of the following is a distinct season experienced in the Philippines?','Autumn','Spring','Dry season','Winter','C','The dry season is one of the two main climate periods in the Philippines, typically from November to April.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,1,NULL,'Which of the following BEST describes a significant contribution of Dr. Fe del Mundo to healthcare in the Philippines?','Establishing the first pediatric hospital in the country.','Promoting the widespread use of traditional herbal remedies.','Revolutionizing the treatment of infectious diseases in adults.','Developing innovative methods for infant care and disease prevention.','A','Dr. Fe del Mundo is celebrated for founding the Children’s Medical Center in 1957, the first pediatric hospital in the Philippines. This groundbreaking contribution significantly improved healthcare services for Filipino children by providing specialized care and promoting child health as a national concern. While she also promoted better care and disease prevention, her most distinct and impactful achievement was the establishment of the hospital.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,2,NULL,'Dr. Fe del Mundo, a Filipino scientist, is known for her contributions to:','Improving medical care for infants and children.','Developing the first airplane.','Creating the first computer.','Discovering a new planet.','A','Dr. del Mundo dedicated her career to pediatric medicine. She developed low-cost medical devices, promoted rural health, and worked extensively to improve health care delivery systems for infants and children. Her research and initiatives helped lower infant mortality rates and increased awareness of child health and nutrition in underserved communities.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,3,NULL,'Which of these inventions has significantly improved communication worldwide? Consider the impact and reach of the invention.','The wheel','The internet','The light bulb','The printing press','B','The internet is one of the most revolutionary inventions in history, drastically transforming communication. It enables instant messaging, email, video conferencing, social media, and access to vast amounts of information. Unlike earlier technologies, it connects billions of people globally in real time, bridging geographic and cultural divides and making communication faster, easier, and more inclusive.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,4,NULL,'When faced with a new technology that claims to improve health, what is a responsible first step you should take?','Immediately use technology without question','Rely on advertisements to make your decision','Ignore it and continue with previous methods','Research and evaluate the scientific evidence supporting the claims','D','A responsible first step is to critically assess any new technology before adopting it, especially those related to health. This includes reading scientific studies, checking for regulatory approval, and considering expert reviews. This approach upholds scientific values such as critical thinking, curiosity, and evidence-based decision-making.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,5,NULL,'Why is it important to verify the sources of information when learning about new scientific advancements?','It helps ensure that the information is accurate and reliable','Source verification is irrelevant for scientific topics','Only popular sources matter','All sources are equally valid','A','Verifying sources is a key part of scientific literacy and responsible citizenship. Not all information is accurate—some may be biased, outdated, or misleading. Ensuring that you rely on peer-reviewed research, trusted scientific institutions, and experts helps you make well-informed and responsible decisions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,6,NULL,'How can applying scientific values like honesty and integrity influence the development of new technologies?','It complicates the innovation process','It slows down technological progress','It is only relevant in academic settings','It ensures that technologies are developed responsibly and ethically','D','Honesty and integrity are fundamental to ethical scientific practices. When researchers and developers uphold these values, they ensure that technologies are not only safe, effective, and truthful, but also aligned with societal needs and ethical standards. This builds public trust and prevents misuse or harm.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,7,NULL,'You want to test which type of paper airplane flies the farthest. To make sure your test is fair, what should you do?','Use varied sizes of paper for each airplane.','Throw each airplane with a different amount of force.','Use several types of paper and different throwing techniques.','Throw each airplane from the same height and with the same force.','D','A fair test controls all variables except one—in this case, the type of paper. By throwing each airplane from the same height and with the same force, you ensure that differences in flight distance are due only to the type of paper, not other factors. This isolates the independent variable and helps ensure valid results.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,8,NULL,'Why is it important to accurately measure and record data in a scientific investigation?','It helps in understanding the theory behind the experiment','It ensures that the results are valid and can be replicated','Accurate measurements are not necessary','It makes the experiment easier','B','Accurate measurements and data recording are essential to produce reliable and replicable results. Other scientists must be able to repeat the experiment and achieve the same outcomes, which is only possible if the original data were recorded precisely and honestly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,9,NULL,'How can controlling variables in an experiment improve the reliability of the results?','It has no impact on results','It complicates the experiment','It makes the experiment less interesting','It allows for a clearer understanding of the relationship between independent and dependent variables','D','By controlling variables, scientists can determine whether changes in the dependent variable are caused by the independent variable. This improves the reliability and validity of the experiment, making the results more trustworthy and easier to interpret.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,10,NULL,'If you are selecting materials for a high-temperature cooking surface, which property would be most critical?','Color','Flexibility','Hardness','Heat resistance','D','A high-temperature cooking surface must resist heat without melting, burning, or degrading. Materials with high thermal resistance ensure safety and durability in cooking applications.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,11,NULL,'What property of metals makes them suitable for electrical wiring?','Color','Hardness','Conductivity','Flexibility','C','Metals like copper and aluminum are used in wiring because they conduct electricity efficiently, allowing for the easy flow of electrical current with minimal resistance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,12,NULL,'How can understanding the changes that materials undergo help in recycling efforts?','It has no impact','The materials can be recycled equally','Changes in materials make recycling more complicated.','Knowledge of changes can inform which materials can be reused or repurposed','D','Knowing how materials behave under heat, pressure, or chemical exposure helps determine whether they can be safely and effectively recycled, reducing waste and conserving resources.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,13,NULL,'If you need material for a flexible water bottle, which property would be most important to consider?','Hardness','Flexibility','Color','Size','B','A flexible water bottle must bend or compress without breaking. Flexibility ensures the bottle is convenient to carry and use, especially in outdoor or athletic settings.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,14,NULL,'Which of the following properties would help determine the best use for a material in construction?','Color','Taste','Flexibility','Hardness','D','In construction, hardness is a crucial property that measures a material’s resistance to deformation or scratching. It affects durability and load-bearing capacity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,15,NULL,'How does the texture of a material influence its use in everyday objects?','It has no influence','Texture only matters for appearance','All textures are equally suitable for every use','Different textures can affect grip, comfort, and aesthetic appeal','D','Texture plays a key role in how materials are used—rough textures provide grip (e.g., tool handles), while smooth textures may be used for comfort or appearance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,16,NULL,'If you heat a piece of ice and observe it melting into water, what type of change is occurring?','Chemical change','Physical change','Biological change','Thermal change','B','Melting is a physical change because the substance remains chemically the same (H₂O); only the state (solid to liquid) changes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,17,NULL,'Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?','Boiling water','Rusting iron','Mixing sand and salt','Dissolving sugar in water','B','Rusting involves a chemical reaction between iron and oxygen, forming a new substance (iron oxide). This cannot be reversed by physical means.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,18,NULL,'How would you explain the difference between physical and chemical changes to someone unfamiliar with the concepts?','Physical changes don''t involve any change in substances, while chemical changes do.','Physical changes involve new substances being formed.','Physical changes are always reversible, while chemical changes are not.','There is no difference; they are the same.','A','A physical change affects form or appearance (like melting), but the substance remains the same. A chemical change results in the formation of a new substance, like rust or burning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,19,NULL,'Liza poured a liquid from a tall, narrow glass into a short, wide bowl. Which of the following statements BEST describes what happens to the liquid?','The volume increases, but the shape changes.','The volume decreases, but the shape changes.','The volume remains the same, but the shape changes.','The volume remains the same, but the shape stays the same.','C','Liquids maintain a constant volume regardless of the container but adapt their shape to fit it. Liza’s action demonstrates this—though the container’s shape changes, the liquid''s volume stays the same.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,20,NULL,'Which of the following statements correctly describes the properties of gases?','Gases have a definite volume but no definite shape','Gases have neither a definite shape nor volume','Gases can be easily seen and measured','Gases have a definite shape and volume','B','Unlike solids and liquids, gases do not retain a fixed shape or volume. They spread out to fill any space available, which is a key property that distinguishes them.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,21,NULL,'How does understanding the properties of solids, liquids, and gases help in practical applications like cooking?','It has no relevance','Only solids are important in cooking','Cooking does not involve states of matter','Understanding these properties allows for better choices in materials and methods used in cooking','D','Cooking involves changes in states of matter (e.g., water turning to steam, butter melting). Knowing how solids, liquids, and gases behave helps in choosing the right ingredients and cookware and in applying heat effectively for desired results.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,22,NULL,'If a mixture consists of sand and salt, how can you separate them effectively?','Dissolve the salt in water and filter out the sand then evaporate the water to separate the salt','Boil the mixture','Use a magnet','Mix them more','A','Salt is soluble in water, while sand is not. By adding water, the salt dissolves, and the sand can be filtered out. Then, evaporation can recover the salt from the saltwater solution.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,23,NULL,'Which of the following best describes a homogeneous mixture?','The components can be visually distinguished.','The composition is uniform throughout.','It contains two or more phases.','It can be easily separated by physical means.','B','A homogeneous mixture has a consistent appearance and composition throughout, like saltwater or vinegar. You can''t distinguish one part from another by sight.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,24,NULL,'How does understanding the difference between heterogeneous and homogeneous mixtures impact practical applications, such as cooking?','It has no relevance to cooking.','All mixtures behave the same way in cooking.','Only homogeneous mixtures are used in cooking.','It allows for better ingredient selection and preparation methods based on the mixture type.','D','In cooking, knowing whether a mixture is homogeneous (e.g., a sauce) or heterogeneous (e.g., a salad) influences how ingredients are combined, cooked, or stored to ensure even flavor and texture.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,1,25,NULL,'If you have a sample of pure gold, which of the following properties can you expect it to have?','Variable composition','A mixture of metals','No distinct properties','High malleability and conductivity','D','Pure gold (Au) is a pure substance with distinct physical properties: it’s highly malleable (can be hammered into thin sheets) and a good conductor of electricity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,26,NULL,'Which of the following is a characteristic of pure substances?','They have varying compositions depending on the source.','They can be separated into simpler substances.','They always have a uniform composition.','They are always solid at room temperature.','C','Pure substances consist of only one type of particle, whether an element or compound, and always have consistent chemical and physical properties throughout.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,27,NULL,'Why is it important to know the properties of pure substances in scientific research?','It does not affect the outcome of the research.','Only mixtures are relevant in scientific studies.','Properties of pure substances are always the same.','Understanding these properties allows for accurate predictions and applications in experiments','D','Knowing the consistent properties of pure substances ensures that experimental results are predictable, reproducible, and reliable, which is essential in any scientific investigation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,28,NULL,'Which of the following best describes how the body systems work together to maintain overall health?','Each system works independently with no effect on others.','The systems compete for energy and space.','The systems function separately but in the same area of the body.','The systems have unique roles but are interconnected, affecting one another when one fails.','D','The paragraph emphasizes that although each body system (muscular, skeletal, digestive, circulatory, and respiratory) performs specific functions, they do not operate in isolation. Instead, they rely on one another to maintain balance and health. For instance, the respiratory and circulatory systems work together to deliver oxygen to muscles, which enables movement. If one system, such as the respiratory system, fails, the circulatory system cannot efficiently transport oxygen, thus impacting the entire body.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,29,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately reflects information found in the text about the circulatory system?','The circulatory system helps us breathe by taking in oxygen.','The circulatory system delivers nutrients to all parts of the body.','The circulatory system is made up of muscles and bones.','The circulatory system helps us turn food into energy.','B','According to the stem, "The circulatory system, with the heart and blood vessels, transports oxygen and nutrients." This means the circulatory system plays a key role in distributing essential materials (like oxygen and nutrients) to cells throughout the body via the blood.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,30,NULL,'The body is a machine with interconnected systems. If one system is not working correctly, which of the following is a potential consequence?','The body will automatically repair the damaged system.','The body will create a new replacement system.','Only that specific system will be affected.','Other body systems may also be affected.','D','The stem clearly states that "Each system has unique functions, but they work together; if one fails, others are affected." This highlights the interdependence of body systems. For example, if the respiratory system fails, the circulatory system cannot distribute oxygen efficiently, affecting the entire body.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,31,NULL,'If a couple is having difficulty conceiving, which organs in both the male and female reproductive systems could be involved, and how do their respective functions relate to this issue?','The male''s penis and the female''s vagina are the points of entry and exit.','The male''s prostate and the female''s uterus, since they both involve fluids.','The male''s testes and the female''s vagina, due to the transportation of sperm.','The male''s testes and the female''s ovaries and uterus are responsible for sperm production, egg production, and fetal development, respectively.','D','Testes produce sperm in males, and ovaries produce eggs in females. The uterus supports fetal development after fertilization. Any issue in these organs (low sperm count, ovulation issues, or uterine conditions) can affect fertility.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,32,NULL,'Which of the following accurately pairs the organs of the male and female reproductive systems with their primary functions?','Male: Testes (sperm delivery); Female: Ovaries (fetal development).','Male: Penis (hormone production); Female: Vagina (egg production).','Male: Prostate (sperm production); Female: Uterus (hormone production).','Male: Testes (sperm production); Female: Ovaries (egg and hormone production).','D','Testes produce sperm and testosterone, while ovaries produce eggs and hormones like estrogen and progesterone. This is a fundamental pairing of reproductive organs and their functions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,33,NULL,'The reproductive systems of males and females have different roles, but they work towards a common goal. Which of the following statements best illustrates how these systems interact to achieve that goal?','The male system provides a pathway for the female system''s hormone production.','The female system produces fluids that aid in the male system''s sperm delivery.','The hormones produced by both systems directly regulate each other''s functions.','The male system delivers sperm, which may fertilize an egg produced by the female system, leading to fetal development in the female''s uterus.','D','Testes produce sperm and testosterone, while ovaries produce eggs and hormones like estrogen and progesterone. This is a fundamental pairing of reproductive organs and their functions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,34,NULL,'If a teenager is experiencing emotional and physical changes during puberty and is concerned about maintaining reproductive health, what are the multiple aspects of self- care they should consider?','Only focusing on physical hygiene.','Only focusing on understanding hormonal changes.','Focusing on physical hygiene and safe sexual practices.','Focusing on physical hygiene, safe sexual practices, and regular check-ups.','D','Reproductive health involves not only cleanliness but also education on safe practices and seeking medical advice when needed, especially during puberty.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,35,NULL,'Which body system is MOST responsible for helping you move your arms and legs?','Digestive system','Circulatory system','Muscular system','Respiratory system','C','The muscular system includes muscles attached to bones, allowing movement of limbs through contraction and relaxation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,36,NULL,'The text describes puberty as a time of significant change and emphasizes the importance of reproductive health care. Which of the following is a possible consequence of neglecting reproductive health during puberty?','Enhanced emotional stability.','Increased physical growth.','A decrease in hormonal activity.','Increased risk of sexually transmitted infections.','D','Neglecting reproductive health (e.g., not practicing safe sex, poor hygiene) increases the risk of STIs, especially during puberty when sexual maturity begins.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,37,NULL,'If a plant is not producing seeds, which of its life cycle stages might be affected, and how does this affect its ability to continue its life cycle?','The seedling stage affects its ability to grow leaves.','The mature plant stage affects its ability to reproduce.','The germination stage affects its ability to sprout from a seed.','The seed stage affects its ability to start a new life cycle.','B','A plant must reach the mature stage to produce flowers and seeds. If it fails to do so, it cannot reproduce, interrupting its life cycle and preventing the next generation from forming.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,38,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately describes the relationship between the stages of a butterfly''s and a dog''s life cycles?','Both butterflies and dogs start as eggs and grow into adults.','Butterflies grow from puppies, and dogs grow from larvae.','Both butterflies and dogs have a seedling stage before becoming adults.','Butterflies undergo metamorphosis with distinct stages, while dogs grow continuously from puppies to adults.','D','Butterflies experience complete metamorphosis (egg, larva, pupa, adult), where each stage looks different. In contrast, dogs experience direct development, gradually growing and ability without changing their body structure.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,39,NULL,'Different organisms have various life cycles. What is the significance of each stage in these life cycles for the organism''s survival and reproduction?','Each stage has unique characteristics and functions that contribute to the organism''s survival and reproduction.','Each stage is independent and has no impact on the next.','Only the adult stage is important for reproduction.','Only the initial stage is important for survival.','A','Every stage in an organism''s life cycle plays a specific role—for example, growth, protection, or reproduction. These roles ensure the organism can survive, reach maturity, and reproduce successfully.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,40,NULL,'If a garden has plants that insects are damaging, bees that are gathering nectar from flowers, what two types of relationships are being demonstrated, and how do they affect the garden''s ecosystem?','Parasitism and mutualism, with insects harming plants and bees benefiting from flowers while also pollinating them.','Predation and commensalism, with insects harming plants and bees having no effect.','Mutualism and herbivory, with bees and plants benefiting each other, and insects benefiting from plants.','Herbivory and predation, with insects eating plants and bees eating insects.','C','Bees and flowers help each other (mutualism). Insects eating leaves feed on the plant (herbivory).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,41,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs the habitat and food source of animals in the community?','Fish (aquatic, carnivore/omnivore); Birds (aerial, carnivore/omnivore).','Fish (terrestrial, herbivore); Birds (aquatic, carnivore).','Fish (aerial, herbivore); Birds (terrestrial, omnivore).','Fish (terrestrial, carnivore); Birds (aquatic, herbivore).','A','Fish live in aquatic habitats and may be carnivores (eating smaller fish/invertebrates) or omnivores (eating plants and animals). Birds are aerial animals and can also be carnivores (e.g., hawks) or omnivores (e.g., crows). Other choices incorrectly pair animals with habitats or diets.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,42,NULL,'The concept intro describes various relationships between organisms. What is the key difference between predation and parasitism, and how does this difference affect the organisms involved?','Predation benefits both organisms, while parasitism harms both.','Predation is a type of mutualism, while parasitism is a type of commensalism.','Predation only occurs in aquatic environments, while parasitism occurs in terrestrial environments.','Predation involves one organism killing another for food, while parasitism involves one organism living off another without necessarily killing it.','D','Predation results in the immediate death of one organism to feed another (e.g., a lion eating a zebra). In parasitism, the parasite feeds on or inside the host over time, often harming it but not immediately killing it (e.g., a tapeworm in the intestines).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,43,NULL,'If a community garden has rabbits eating the vegetable plants, birds eating the insects on those plants, and fish living in a nearby pond, how would you classify these organisms based on their habitat and food sources, and how do these classifications relate to their interactions within the garden''s ecosystem?','Rabbits (terrestrial, carnivores), birds (aerial, herbivores), and fish (aquatic, omnivores), with no direct interactions.','Rabbits (terrestrial, herbivores), birds (aerial, carnivores), and fish (aquatic, omnivores), with the birds controlling insect populations that would harm the plants.','Rabbits (aerial, omnivores), birds (terrestrial, herbivores), and fish (terrestrial, carnivores) all compete for the same food source.','Rabbits (aquatic, herbivores), birds (terrestrial, carnivores), and fish (aerial, omnivores), with the fish eating the rabbits.','B','Rabbits live on land and eat plants → terrestrial herbivores; Birds, in this case, are eating insects → aerial carnivores; Fish live in water and often eat both plants and small organisms → aquatic omnivores; This interaction shows how organisms fulfill roles in the food web. Birds help protect plants by reducing insect populations, showing a beneficial indirect relationship in the garden ecosystem.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,44,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs an organism with its habitat and diet classification?','Bees (aquatic, carnivores); Lions (aerial, herbivores).','Bees (aerial, herbivores); Lions (terrestrial, carnivores).','Bees (terrestrial, omnivores); Lions (aquatic, omnivores).','Bees (aquatic, omnivores); Lions (aerial, herbivores)','B','Bees are aerial because they fly, and herbivores because they consume nectar/pollen (plant matter); Lions are terrestrial and carnivores, feeding on herbivorous animals like zebras; The other choices incorrectly place animals in habitats or dietary categories that don''t match their biology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,45,NULL,'The concept intro mentions various relationships between organisms. How does classifying an organism by its diet (herbivore, carnivore, omnivore) influence its potential relationships with other organisms in an ecosystem?','Diet classification determines whether an organism will engage in mutualism or commensalism only.','Diet classification dictates whether an organism will be a predator or prey, or if it will compete with other organisms for food.','Diet classification determines the organism’s habitat.','Diet classification has no impact on organism relationships.','B','An organism’s diet affects its ecological role: Carnivores may act as predators; Herbivores are typically prey; Omnivores can fit into various roles and may compete with other organisms for similar food sources.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,46,NULL,'In a forest ecosystem, owls hunt mice for food, and deer eat plants. If a disease reduces the mouse population, how will this affect the owl and deer populations, and what relationships are demonstrated?','Both owl and deer populations will increase, demonstrating parasitism and symbiosis.','Both owl and deer populations will decrease, demonstrating mutualism and predation.','The owl population will decrease, deer population will increase, demonstrating predation and herbivory.','The owl population will increase, and the deer population will decrease, demonstrating commensalism and mutualism.','C','A reduction in mice means less food for owls, leading to a decline in owl population (due to predation); Since deer are not directly affected by the mouse population, and there''s less predation-related disruption in the ecosystem, their numbers may increase; The relationships here are predation (owl-mouse) and herbivory (deer-plant).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,47,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs a relationship with its description?','Mutualism: one organism benefits, the other is harmed. Predation: both organism’s benefit.','Commensalism: both organisms are harmed. Parasitism: one organism eats another.','Symbiosis: a general term for close interactions. Predation: one organism kills and eats another.','Mutualism: one organism is harmed, commensalism: one organism is killed.','C','Symbiosis is an umbrella term that includes mutualism, commensalism, and parasitism—all involve close, long-term interactions; Predation involves a predator killing and consuming its prey; The other options contain incorrect pairings or definitions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,48,NULL,'The concept introduction describes various relationships, including symbiosis, predation, commensalism, and parasitism. How does the concept of symbiosis relate to other relationship types, and how does each of these relationships impact the organisms involved?','Symbiosis is unrelated to other relationship types; they all equally benefit all the organisms involved.','Symbiosis is a type of predation; it only affects the negative aspects of each organism.','Symbiosis relates only to organisms living on land; other relationships involve only sea-based creatures.','Symbiosis is a general term encompassing mutualism, commensalism, and parasitism, each impacting the involved organisms differently, with varying degrees of benefit and harm.','D','Symbiosis includes relationships where: Mutualism: both benefit; Commensalism: one benefits, the other is unaffected; Parasitism: one benefit, one is harmed. These classifications help explain the complexity and interdependence of ecosystems.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,49,NULL,'If a mammal species is observed to have thick fur, a layer of blubber, and the ability to hibernate, and a bird species in the same environment has dense feathers and a high metabolic rate, how do these multiple adaptations in both groups contribute to their survival in a cold environment?','The mammal''s adaptations provide insulation and energy conservation, while the bird''s adaptations provide insulation and heat production.','Both adapt by eating more plants.','Both adapt by hiding from predators.','Both adapt by living in water','A','Mammals use thick fur and blubber for insulation and hibernation to conserve energy in cold conditions. Birds have dense feathers for insulation and maintain high metabolic rates to produce body heat, allowing them to stay active in cold environments. These adaptations enhance their survival by reducing heat loss and maintaining body temperature.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,2,50,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs multiple adaptations with the animal groups they are found in?','Mammals: fur/blubber; Fish: fins/gills; Amphibians: dual respiration; Birds: wings/light bones.','Mammals: gills; Birds: scales; Reptiles: feathers.','Fish: fur; Reptiles: feathers; Amphibians: scales.','Birds: gills; Fish: feathers; Mammals: scales','A','Mammals have fur and, in some species like whales, blubber to insulate against cold; Fish use fins for swimming and gills for breathing in water; Amphibians exhibit dual respiration (gills in the larval stage and lungs in adulthood); Birds have wings and lightweight bones for flight.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,51,NULL,'How does the presence of physiological adaptations (e.g., warm-bloodedness, gills) and structural adaptations (e.g., fur, fins) within a single animal group influence its survival ability in diverse environments?','Only structural adaptations influence survival.','Only physiological adaptations influence survival.','Adaptations do not affect an organism’s survival.','The combination of both physiological and structural adaptations allows for greater flexibility and adaptability in diverse environments.','D','Structural adaptations like fins or fur help with locomotion and insulation, while physiological adaptations like warm-bloodedness or gills help regulate body processes. When both types are present, animals are better equipped to survive a wider range of environmental conditions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,52,NULL,'In a coral reef ecosystem, if there is a sudden increase in water temperature and a decline in the population of herbivorous fish, how would you analyze the interconnected effects of these abiotic (temperature) and biotic (fish population) factors on the overall health and biodiversity of the coral reef?','The increased temperature would lead to coral bleaching, reducing habitat, and the decrease in herbivorous fish would allow algae to overgrow, further harming the coral.','The increased temperature would only affect the coral, and the decrease in fish would only affect other fish.','The fish would eat more coral to survive the heat, and the coral would adapt to the fish.','Neither the temperature nor the fish population would have a measurable effect on the coral reef.','A','Elevated water temperatures cause coral bleaching—a stress response where corals expel the symbiotic algae (zooxanthellae) they rely on for energy, often resulting in coral death. Simultaneously, herbivorous fishlike parrotfish and surgeonfish help control algae growth. When their population declines, algae can dominate the reef, smother corals and further reduce biodiversity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,53,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs multiple biotic and abiotic factors with their significant impacts on a forest ecosystem?','Soil composition affects tree growth, rainfall affects animal populations, and predator populations affect prey populations.','Sunlight only affects tree growth, and animal populations only affect other animal populations.','Wind affects fish populations, and plant types affect soil composition.','Temperature affects reptile survival, and plant diversity influences insect populations.','A','Soil composition (an abiotic factor) directly influences plant health and growth. Rainfall, another abiotic factor, affects water availability for animals. Predators (biotic) regulate prey populations, maintaining ecological balance through natural population control.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,54,NULL,'A bee collects nectar from a flower and, in turn, helps the flower reproduce by spreading its pollen. What type of relationship is this?','Predation','Commensalism','Mutualism','Parasitism','C','Mutualism is a symbiotic relationship where both organisms benefit. In this case, the bee gains food (nectar), while the flower benefits through pollination, increasing its chances of reproduction.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,55,NULL,'A local park is facing issues with soil erosion, negatively impacting plant growth and a decrease in bird populations due to a lack of nesting sites. How would you analyze these interconnected problems and propose a multi-faceted approach to address plant health and bird conservation?','Propose a strategy that includes soil stabilization techniques (e.g., terracing, mulching) to improve plant growth, creating bird nesting boxes, and planting native trees to enhance bird habitats.','Use chemical fertilizers to accelerate plant growth and relocate the bird population to a different area.','Focus solely on planting erosion-resistant plants, ignoring the decline of the bird population.','Introduce non-native bird species to increase population numbers, disregarding soil erosion.','A','This option presents a holistic, eco-friendly approach that addresses both soil erosion and the decline in bird populations. Terracing and mulching are effective soil conservation techniques that help retain moisture and prevent erosion, while installing bird nesting boxes and planting native trees provide shelter and food sources for birds, encouraging them to return and thrive.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,56,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately reflects the interconnectedness of responsible plant and animal care practices, as discussed in the concept intro?','Plant care and animal protection are independent practices without relation to each other.','Responsible practices involve only focusing on the aesthetic value of plants and the entertainment value of animals.','Caring for plants is only about maximizing yield, while animal protection is only about preventing poaching.','Responsible practices include providing suitable habitats for animals, ensuring access to food and water, and providing adequate sunlight, water, and nutrients for plants, recognizing their interconnectedness.','D','Responsible environmental stewardship acknowledges that plants and animals are part of interconnected ecosystems. Proper care involves understanding and addressing their mutual dependencies—healthy plants provide shelter and food for animals, and animals can assist in plant pollination and seed dispersal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,57,NULL,'The concept introduction discusses the importance of responsible practices for plant and animal care. How does the concept of "habitat preservation" relate to both plant and animal well-being, and what are the long-term implications of neglecting habitat preservation for the ecosystem as a whole?','Habitat preservation is only relevant for animal protection.','Habitat preservation is only relevant for plant care.','Habitat preservation has no impact on the overall ecosystem.','Habitat preservation is crucial for both plant and animal survival, as it provides the necessary resources and conditions for both to thrive, and neglecting it can lead to ecosystem collapse.','D','Habitat preservation ensures that both plants and animals have access to the essential resources needed for survival. Destruction of natural habitats results in the loss of biodiversity, disrupts food chains, and can lead to ecological collapse. This option reflects the long-term ecological consequences of irresponsible human actions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,58,NULL,'A coastal community relies heavily on fishing, but dynamite fishing has become prevalent, leading to coral reef destruction and declining fish populations. Simultaneously, nearby forests are being rapidly cleared through illegal logging. How would you analyze these activities interconnected with environmental and socioeconomic impacts, and propose a comprehensive strategy to mitigate both issues?','Analyze the impacts on both marine and forest ecosystems, proposing strategies that include enforcing fishing laws, educating communities about sustainable fishing, promoting sustainable forestry, and reforestation efforts, considering the long-term socioeconomic effects on the community.','Introduce new, non-native fish species to compensate for the decline, and promote large-scale commercial logging for economic growth.','Encourage the community to abandon fishing and logging altogether without providing alternative livelihoods.','Focus solely on enforcing fishing laws, ignoring illegal logging, as they are separate issues.','A','This option addresses both the environmental and socioeconomic dimensions of the problem. It acknowledges the interconnectedness of illegal logging and dynamite fishing, and the need for holistic solutions. Enforcing laws, educating communities, and promoting sustainable practices are essential for mitigating damage while also considering the livelihood of the people affected.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,59,NULL,'As described in the concept introduction, which of the following statements accurately reflects the interconnected harmful effects of kaingin, illegal logging, and dynamite fishing?','Kaingin leads to soil erosion, illegal logging leads to habitat destruction, and dynamite fishing kills non-target species, but they do not influence each other.','These activities contribute to ecosystem disruption, habitat loss, and biodiversity decline, with overlapping and cumulative effects on the environment.','These activities have no interconnected effects and only harm the specific areas where they occur.','Only dynamite fishing has a long-term effect on the environment.','B','This option addresses both the environmental and socioeconomic dimensions of the problem. It acknowledges the interconnectedness of illegal logging and dynamite fishing, and the need for holistic solutions. Enforcing laws, educating communities, and promoting sustainable practices are essential for mitigating damage while also considering the livelihood of the people affected.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,60,NULL,'The concept introduction describes the harmful effects of human activities like kaingin, illegal logging, and dynamite fishing. How does the concept of "sustainable practices" relate to mitigating these harmful effects, and what are the long-term implications of ignoring sustainable practices for the environment?','Sustainable practices have no relation to mitigating harmful effects.','Sustainable practices only benefit the economy, not the environment.','Only laws and regulations can mitigate harmful environmental effects.','Sustainable practices, like crop rotation, reforestation, and sustainable fishing, are essential for mitigating harmful effects, and ignoring them can lead to irreversible environmental damage.','D','Sustainable practices offer long-term solutions to environmental degradation by reducing harm while allowing communities to continue using natural resources responsibly. Without these practices, environmental destruction becomes irreversible, threatening ecosystems and human livelihoods.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,61,NULL,'Why is it easier to slide a box across a smooth wooden floor than across a carpeted floor?','There is less friction on a smooth floor.','Friction is the same on both floors.','Friction is weaker on the carpeted floor.','The box is lighter on the smooth floor.','A','Carpeted surfaces are rougher than smooth wooden floors. Rough surfaces have more microscopic irregularities that increase resistance when an object moves across them. This means more friction is present on the carpet, making it harder to slide the box. Smooth floors have fewer irregularities, resulting in less friction and easier movement.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,62,NULL,'Joy is designing a braking system for a toy car. She needs to choose a material for the brake pads that will create a high frictional force when pressed against the wheels. She consults three sources: Source A: A website selling various materials, listing "friction coefficient" values for each. Source B: A blog post discussing the importance of brake pad material in car safety but not providing specific data. Source C: A scientific paper detailing experiments on the friction between different materials and wheel surfaces. To make the best choice, which sources should she prioritize and why, considering information literacy principles?','Source A, because it''s readily available and lists friction coefficients.','Source B, because it discusses the importance of brake pad material.','Source C, because it''s a scientific paper with experimental data.','Sources A and B, because they offer different perspectives.','C','Information literacy emphasizes using credible, evidence-based, and peer- reviewed sources for decision-making. Scientific papers offer experimental data and analysis, making them more reliable and valid than blogs or commercial websites. Source C provides measured results, which are critical for making an informed choice on material performance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,63,NULL,'The ALS learners are experimenting with sliding a wooden block across different surfaces: a smooth glass tabletop, a rough concrete floor, and a carpeted floor. They observe that the block slides farthest on the glass, less far on the carpet, and the shortest distance on the concrete. Which statement BEST explains these observations, considering the factors influencing friction?','The glass is colder than the concrete and carpet.','The different surfaces have different levels of roughness, affecting friction.','The concrete is harder than the glass and carpet.','The carpet is more absorbent than the glass and concrete.','B','The roughness of surfaces directly affects friction. The glass tabletop is the smoothest, creating less friction, so the block slides farther. Concrete is the roughest, producing more friction, so the block stops quickly. The carpet has moderate friction, so the sliding distance is between. Temperature and absorbency are not key factors in friction here.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,64,NULL,'Cherrelyn is designing a demonstration to show whether heavier objects fall faster than lighter objects due to gravity. She has a variety of objects: a bowling ball, a feather, a marble, and a balloon. Ignoring air resistance for the moment, which combination of objects best demonstrates the principle of constant gravitational acceleration, and why?','Dropping the bowling ball and the feather together.','Dropping the marble and the balloon together.','Dropping the bowling ball and the marble together.','Dropping all four objects together.','A','This combination is ideal because the feather and the bowling ball have drastically different masses and shapes, so under normal conditions, they fall at different rates due to air resistance. However, if dropped in a vacuum (where air resistance is removed), they will fall at the same rate, effectively demonstrating the concept that gravitational acceleration is independent of mass. This concept was famously proven in a 1971 Apollo 15 moon experiment by astronaut David Scott.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,65,NULL,'Rosie is researching the relationship between an object''s mass and its acceleration due to gravity. She consults two sources: Source A: A website stating that heavier objects always fall faster because gravity pulls on them harder. Source B: A physics textbook explaining that the acceleration due to gravity is constant for all objects near the Earth''s surface, regardless of their mass, in a vacuum. Considering information literacy principles, which source provides a more scientifically accurate explanation, and why?','Source A, because it''s a simple and easily understandable explanation.','Source B, because it''s consistent with the laws of physics and accounts for the absence of air resistance.','Both sources are equally accurate.','Neither source is accurate.','B','According to Newtonian physics, the acceleration due to gravity is constant (approximately 9.8 m/s²) for all objects regardless of mass when air resistance is not a factor. This principle is fundamental to classical mechanics and has been validated through experiments in vacuum conditions. Source B aligns with established scientific understanding and is supported by reputable educational resources, such as physics textbooks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,66,NULL,'A feather and a hammer are dropped from the same height on Earth. The hammer hits the ground much sooner than the feather. What is the MAIN reason for this difference in falling time?','Air resistance affects the feather more than the hammer.','The hammer is heavier than the feather.','Gravity pulls harder on the hammer.','The hammer is made of metal.','A','On Earth, the presence of air creates resistance. Lighter objects with larger surface areas (like feathers) experience more air resistance, which slows them down. Heavier and more compact objects (like hammers) are less affected. This is why, even though gravity pulls all objects equally in a vacuum, in real-world conditions, air resistance creates different falling times.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,67,'Light, sound, and heat energy are fundamental forces that shape our world and play crucial roles in our daily lives. From the moment we wake up to the time we go to sleep, these three forms of energy are constantly interacting with us, enabling us to see, communicate, and experience the world around us. They enable us to see, communicate, stay warm, and enjoy the world around us. By understanding the importance of these forms of energy, we can appreciate their value and make informed decisions about how we use and conserve them.','Ricky wants to reduce their family''s energy consumption at home. He identified several energy sources and uses incandescent light bulbs, a gas stove, a laptop computer, and a refrigerator. Which problem-solving approach would be MOST effective in reducing energy consumption, and why?','Replacing all the light bulbs with LEDs.','Turning off the gas stove when not in use.','Unplugging the laptop computer when not in use.','Analyzing the energy consumption of each appliance, prioritizing those with the highest energy use for efficiency improvements, and implementing a combination of strategies (e.g., replacing inefficient appliances, improving insulation).','D','This approach reflects a comprehensive, critical, and strategic way of solving the problem. Instead of addressing a single source of energy consumption, it evaluates all major appliances and identifies which uses the most energy. Combining solutions—such as replacing inefficient appliances like incandescent bulbs or an old refrigerator and improving insulation—yields greater energy savings.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,68,'Light, sound, and heat energy are fundamental forces that shape our world and play crucial roles in our daily lives. From the moment we wake up to the time we go to sleep, these three forms of energy are constantly interacting with us, enabling us to see, communicate, and experience the world around us. They enable us to see, communicate, stay warm, and enjoy the world around us. By understanding the importance of these forms of energy, we can appreciate their value and make informed decisions about how we use and conserve them.','Carlo is researching the sources and uses of energy in their school, home, and local community. He needs to gather reliable information. Which approach best demonstrates information literacy skills?','Consulting textbooks, scientific articles, and reputable websites on energy, comparing information from multiple sources to verify accuracy and identify potential biases.','Asking friends and family for their opinions on energy sources and uses.','Searching the internet for any website that mentions energy.','Watching videos on YouTube about energy.','A','Information literacy involves the ability to locate, evaluate, and use reliable and credible information effectively. Consulting multiple reputable and authoritative sources and comparing their content allows for a deeper and more accurate understanding while minimizing misinformation and bias.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,69,'Light, sound, and heat energy are fundamental forces that shape our world and play crucial roles in our daily lives. From the moment we wake up to the time we go to sleep, these three forms of energy are constantly interacting with us, enabling us to see, communicate, and experience the world around us. They enable us to see, communicate, stay warm, and enjoy the world around us. By understanding the importance of these forms of energy, we can appreciate their value and make informed decisions about how we use and conserve them.','Lisa is tasked with identifying sources and uses of light, sound, and heat energy in their school, home, and local community. Which approach would BEST demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of energy sources and uses, incorporating critical thinking about energy efficiency and sustainability?','Creating a table categorizing sources and uses by location (school, home, community) and energy type (light, sound, heat).','Analyzing the sources and uses, considering their energy efficiency and environmental impact, and proposing ways to improve sustainability in each location.','Drawing pictures of different energy sources and uses in each location.','Simply listing examples of light bulbs, radios, and ovens in each location.','B','Option B is the best choice because it goes beyond simple identification or description. It requires critical thinking, analysis, and evaluation—key scientific and 21st- century skills. By examining not just what the energy sources and uses are, but also how efficient and sustainable they are, Lisa demonstrates a deeper understanding. This approach also encourages students to think about solutions and real-world applications, which align with science learning goals that promote responsible decision-making and environmental awareness.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,70,NULL,'If a volcanic eruption is observed to produce a large cloud of ash, fast-moving currents of hot gas, and slow-moving streams of lava, how would you analyze the relationship between these ejected materials and the processes occurring within the volcano''s magma chamber and vents?','The ash is unrelated to the lava and gas, and all are independent events.','The lava is solely caused by surface water, and the ash and gas are from burning plant life.','Only the gas is related to the magma, and the ash and lava are unrelated to the volcano’s inner workings.','The ash cloud indicates a buildup of pressure within the magma chamber, the hot gas currents are pyroclastic flows, and the lava streams are the surface expression of the magma, all interconnected through the eruption process.','D','This choice accurately explains the interconnected nature of volcanic processes. A buildup of pressure in the magma chamber forces magma upward. The explosive release of gas and fragmented rock forms ash clouds and pyroclastic flows, while lava is the molten rock that reaches the surface. These materials are directly linked to the dynamics within the volcano’s magma chamber and vents.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,71,NULL,'Which of the following statements accurately pairs the formation process of volcanoes with the materials ejected during an eruption, as described in the concept introduction?','Magma cools on the surface, forming ash and gases.','Magma rises from the Earth''s mantle, accumulating in chambers, and erupts as lava, ash, and gases.','Volcanoes are formed by surface water and only eject water vapor.','Volcanoes are formed by erosion and eject only rocks.','B','Volcanoes are formed due to tectonic activity, where magma rises through the crust and collects in magma chambers. When pressure becomes too great, the magma erupts as lava, along with volcanic gases and ash. These materials are typical of volcanic eruptions and are all derived from the same internal source.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,72,NULL,'The scenario describes the formation of volcanoes, and the materials ejected during eruptions. How does the pressure buildup within a magma chamber relate to the type and intensity of materials ejected during a volcanic eruption, and what are the implications of this relationship for predicting volcanic hazards?','Higher pressure leads to more intense eruptions with larger volumes of ash and pyroclastic flows, indicating a greater hazard.','Pressure buildup has no relation to the materials ejected.','The materials ejected are random and unrelated to the internal pressure.','Only the lava flow is affected by pressure.','A','The pressure inside a magma chamber is a key factor in determining the explosiveness of a volcanic eruption. High-pressure buildup can cause violent eruptions, characterized by huge ash clouds, pyroclastic flows, and volcanic bombs. Understanding this relationship is critical for predicting volcanic hazards and issuing early warnings.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,73,NULL,'Marjorene is designing a science fair project to explain volcanoes. She wants to demonstrate the formation of volcanoes, and the materials ejected during eruptions. Which approach would best integrate these aspects and effectively communicate the concepts?','Creating a poster with definitions of volcanic materials (lava, ash, etc.) and a diagram of a volcano.','Designing an experiment simulating a volcanic eruption using baking soda and vinegar, then analyzing the materials produced and relating them to real volcanic processes.','Writing a report explaining the formation of volcanoes and listing the materials ejected.','Building a model volcano and simply labeling the different parts.','B','This hands-on experiment offers a visual and engaging simulation of volcanic eruptions. It not only demonstrates the eruption process but also allows learners to draw comparisons between the materials used (like vinegar and baking soda) and actual volcanic materials such as magma, gases, and ash. This approach fosters deeper understanding by integrating both the formation and eruption aspects in an interactive manner.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,74,NULL,'The ALS learners are researching volcanoes to create an informative presentation. They need to find reliable information about volcano formation, eruption processes, and the materials ejected. Which approach best demonstrates information literacy skills?','Using only information from a single website about volcanoes.','Searching the internet for any website or video mentioning volcanoes.','Relying solely on information from a popular science magazine article about a recent volcanic eruption.','Consulting multiple sources, including scientific journals, textbooks, and reputable websites on geology and volcanology, comparing information to verify accuracy and identify potential biases.','D','This hands-on experiment offers a visual and engaging simulation of volcanic eruptions. It not only demonstrates the eruption process but also allows learners to draw comparisons between the materials used (like vinegar and baking soda) and actual volcanic materials such as magma, gases, and ash. This approach fosters deeper understanding by integrating both the formation and eruption aspects in an interactive manner.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',2,3,75,NULL,'Detchie is preparing a presentation on volcanoes and wants to emphasize the relationship between plate tectonics and volcanic activity. Which approach would BEST demonstrate critical thinking about the interconnectedness of these geological processes?','Simply describing the different types of volcanoes.','Listing the materials ejected during volcanic eruptions.','Creating a timeline of major volcanic eruptions throughout history.','Explaining the theory of plate tectonics and then showing how volcanic activity is concentrated along plate boundaries, using examples of specific volcanoes and their geological settings.','D','This approach shows not just knowledge of volcanoes, but also the ability to connect ideas and analyze cause-and-effect relationships. Explaining plate tectonics and then applying that understanding to real-world examples demonstrates critical thinking and the application of scientific concepts to real scenarios.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,1,NULL,'Before adopting new health technology, what''s the most crucial first step?','Consult experts and examine scientific backing.','Immediately implement the technology in practice.','Ignore the technology and continue existing methods.','Base decisions on personal experiences and online comments.','A','Prioritizing evidence-based evaluation from reliable sources is crucial before adopting any new technology, especially in healthcare, where safety and effectiveness are paramount.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,2,NULL,'What''s the BEST source to assess a new technology''s environmental effect?','Discussions on social media platforms.','Opinions shared by friends and family members.','Information provided by technology developers.','Independent scientific studies and environmental reports.','D','Peer-reviewed scientific studies and environmental impact assessments provide the most objective and reliable data for evaluating technology’s environmental effects.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,3,NULL,'How do honesty and integrity in research influence technological progress?','They significantly impede technological advancement.','Their importance is limited to academic research settings.','They have a minimal influence on the development process.','They are crucial for creating reliable and beneficial innovations.','D','Honesty and integrity are fundamental to sound scientific practices, leading to trustworthy results and fostering innovation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,4,NULL,'A new fertilizer claims to double crop yields. What is a responsible way to test its effectiveness?','Use it on all crops without testing','Consult only local farmers for their experiences','Rely on advertisements to determine their effectiveness','Conduct a controlled experiment comparing it to a standard fertilizer','D','Conduct a controlled experiment comparing it to a standard fertilizer because this method is the most scientifically rigorous way to test the effectiveness of the new fertilizer. A controlled experiment allows researchers to isolate the variable being tested (the new fertilizer) while keeping other factors constant, such as soil type, water availability, and crop variety. By comparing the crop yields from the new fertilizer to those from a standard fertilizer, researchers can determine if the claims of doubling yields are valid. This approach ensures that the results are reliable and can be replicated in future studies.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,5,NULL,'What''s the MOST reliable source for a new medical treatment''s safety and effectiveness?','Accounts from patients shared on social media.','Information about the treatment''s financial cost.','Recommendations from well-known public figures.','Data from peer-reviewed research and clinical trials.','D','Clinical trial data and peer-reviewed research provide the most rigorous and objective evaluation of a medical treatment''s safety and effectiveness.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,6,NULL,'What''s the BEST approach when scientific findings conflict?','Disregard conflicting information entirely.','Accept the most widely publicized viewpoint.','Favor information aligning with personal beliefs.','Evaluate the reliability of sources and their evidence.','D','Critical thinking requires evaluating credibility and evidence from multiple sources before forming conclusions when faced with conflicting information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,7,NULL,'If you have a sample that appears uniform throughout and cannot be separated by physical means, what type of substance is it?','Mixture','Pure substance','Homogenous Mixture','Heterogeneous mixture','B','Pure substance because a sample that appears uniform throughout and cannot be separated by physical means is defined as a pure substance. Pure substances have a consistent and definite composition, meaning they consist of only one type of particle or compound. In contrast, mixtures can be physically separated into their components and may have varying compositions. Recognizing that a uniform sample that resists separation indicates a pure substance is fundamental in understanding material classifications in chemistry.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,8,NULL,'What defines a pure substance?','It''s always solid at room temperature.','It''s easily separated into its individual parts.','It has a variable and uncertain composition.','It has a consistent and well-defined composition.','D','A pure substance is defined by its consistent and unchanging chemical composition.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,9,NULL,'Why is distinguishing mixtures from pure substances vital in research?','It''s not significantly relevant to scientific research.','Only mixtures are essential for scientific investigations.','It directly affects experimental procedures and analysis.','All substances behave identically in scientific experiments.','C','The composition of a substance (pure or mixture) directly impacts experimental methods and the interpretation of results.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,10,NULL,'How would you classify a container of mixed nuts?','A pure substance.','A chemical compound.','A homogeneous mixture.','A heterogeneous mixture.','D','Mixed nuts are a heterogeneous mixture because the components are not uniformly distributed.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,11,NULL,'What''s thekey difference between mixtures and pure substances?','All mixtures pose inherent safety hazards.','Pure substances are separable; mixtures are not.','Mixtures have a fixed composition; pure substances don''t.','Mixtures have variable composition; pure substances are constant.','D','This accurately reflects the defining characteristic that distinguishes mixtures from pure substances.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,12,NULL,'How does understanding mixtures and pure substances help materials science?','It has no significant impact on materials science.','All materials are treated the same in materials science.','Only pure substances are relevant to materials science.','It''s essential for creating new materials and technologies.','D','Controlling and manipulating the composition of materials is fundamental to materials science.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,13,NULL,'If you have a mixture of oil and water, which separation method would you use to separate them effectively?','Filtration','Distillation','Decantation','Centrifugation','C','Decantation because this method is specifically designed for separating immiscible liquids, such as oil and water, which do not mix. In this process, the mixture is allowed to sit, enabling the denser liquid (water) to settle at the bottom while the less dense liquid (oil) floats on top. Once separated, the oil can be carefully poured off, leaving the water behind. Decantation is an effective and straightforward technique for this type of mixture.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,14,NULL,'What''s the basic principle for separating heterogeneous mixtures?','Chemical reactions are always necessary.','The mixture must always be in a solid state.','Temperature changes are always required for separation.','Components are unevenly distributed, allowing physical separation.','D','The uneven distribution of components in heterogeneous mixtures allows for physical separation methods.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,15,NULL,'How does understanding separation processes improve waste management?','It makes waste management more complex.','It''s irrelevant to effective waste management.','It enables the recovery of recyclable materials.','All materials are recyclable without prior separation.','C','Separation processes are crucial for recycling and resource recovery in waste management.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,16,NULL,'What''s the most effective way to separate salt from water?','Using a freezing method.','Employing a filtration process.','Utilizing an evaporation technique.','Through simple mixing procedures.','C','Evaporation removes the water, leaving the sugar behind.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,17,NULL,'Which method is most appropriate for separating a solid from a liquid in a heterogeneous mixture?','Filtration','Distillation','Evaporation','Chromatography','A','Filtration because this method is specifically designed for separating solids from liquids in heterogeneous mixtures. In a filtration process, the mixture is passed through a filter, which allows the liquid to pass through while retaining the solid particles. This technique is commonly used in various applications, such as in laboratories to separate precipitates from solutions or in everyday situations like filtering coffee.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,18,NULL,'Which of the following methods is BEST suited for separating a mixture of salt (dissolved) and water (homogeneous mixture)?','Using a sieve to separate the salt and water.','Using a magnet to separate the salt and water.','Boiling the water until it evaporates, leaving the salt behind.','Pouring the mixture through a filter paper to separate the salt and water.','C','Water turns into gas (water vapor) when you boil it. This process is called evaporation. Salt, however, doesn''t turn into a gas at the boiling point of water. It has a much higher boiling point. So, if you heat the saltwater and let the water boil away, the salt will be left behind in the container. It will be dry salt. This is a simple and effective way to separate the two.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,19,NULL,'An animal has scales and lives on land and in water. What can be inferred?','It needs a desert-like environment.','It needs a purely land-based environment.','It needs a purely water-based environment.','It needs an environment with both land and water.','D','The combination of scales and amphibious lifestyle suggests adaptation to both aquatic and terrestrial habitats.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,20,NULL,'How do the respiratory systems of fish, amphibians, and mammals demonstrate a relational progression in adaptation from aquatic to terrestrial environments?','Fish use gills, amphibians use gills and lungs, and mammals use lungs, showing a clear adaptation progression.','All three are assumed to use lungs, overlooking the actual differences in how each group breathes in their environment.','All three are said to use gills, which is incorrect and ignores the distinct respiratory systems developed through adaptation.','Fishes are said to use lungs, amphibians use gills, and mammals use gills, presenting a reversed and inaccurate view of evolution.','D','The respiratory systems of fish, amphibians, and mammals illustrate a clear evolutionary progression from aquatic to terrestrial environments. Fish rely solely on gills to extract oxygen from water, demonstrating a specialized adaptation for aquatic life. Amphibians exhibit a transitional phase, utilizing gills in their larval stage and developing lungs in their adult stage, reflecting their ability to live both in water and on land. Mammals, fully terrestrial, rely exclusively on lungs for efficient oxygen extraction from air. This progression highlights the adaptive changes in respiratory systems to accommodate the shift from water to land, showcasing the remarkable evolution of life.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,21,NULL,'How do an animal''s internal and external features affect adaptation?','Warm-blooded animals with fur/feathers adapt better to varied climates than cold- blooded animals with scales.','Internal features are said to affect habitat and external features to affect diet, overlooking their combined role in adaptation.','They are believed to have no connection to adaptation, ignoring how body coverings and temperature regulation support survival.','Cold-blooded animals with fur or feathers are said to adapt better than warm- blooded ones with scales, which is scientifically inaccurate.','A','This accurately reflects the relationship between physiological and external features and their impact on environmental adaptation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,22,NULL,'A mountain bird has thicker feathers and faster metabolism; a deep-sea fish has bioluminescence and pressure sensors. How do these adaptations relate to survival?','These adaptations enhance survival in extreme conditions; the bird for warmth, the fish for low light/high pressure.','Both adapted to escape predators using similar strategies, ignoring the distinct environmental challenges each species faces.','Both adaptations are often assumed to serve only visual appeal, overlooking their crucial roles in helping organisms survive in extreme environments.','The bird developed camouflage for protection, while the fish evolved speed, showing different responses to environmental pressures.','A','This correctly identifies the adaptive significance of the features in their respective environments.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,23,NULL,'How do the respiratory systems of fish, amphibians, and mammals demonstrate a relational progression in adaptation from aquatic to terrestrial environments, and how does this progression correlate with the evolution of other related anatomical features?','All three are assumed to use lungs, which overlooks how fish rely on gills and how amphibians use both gills and lungs.','All three are said to use gills, but this ignores the real respiratory differences and the evolutionary changes across species.','Fish are said to use lungs, amphibians use gills, and mammals use gills, presenting a reversed and inaccurate view of adaptation.','Fishes use gills, amphibians use gills and lungs, and mammals use lungs, showing a clear adaptation progression, correlating with the evolution of other features like limbs and body structure.','D','The respiratory systems of fish, amphibians, and mammals clearly demonstrate a relational progression in adaptation from aquatic to terrestrial environments. Fish utilize gills, which are highly efficient at extracting oxygen dissolved from water. Amphibians, representing a transitional phase, possess both gills (in larval stages) and lungs (in adult stages), reflecting their ability to live in both water and on land. Mammals, fully terrestrial, rely solely on lungs for efficient oxygen extraction from air. This progression correlates with the evolution of other related anatomical features, such as the development of limbs for terrestrial locomotion, changes in body structure to support life on land, and the evolution of specialized sensory organs suitable for terrestrial environments. Thus, the respiratory adaptations are interconnected with broader evolutionary changes that facilitated the transition from aquatic to terrestrial life.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,24,NULL,'How do physiological (e.g., warm-bloodedness) and behavioral (e.g., migration) adaptations help animals survive changing environments?','Only physiological adaptations are seen as important, failing to recognize how behaviors also help organisms adjust to their surroundings.','They are believed to be unrelated to environmental survival, ignoring how both types of adaptations support an organism’s ability to thrive.','Physiological adaptations offer internal control; behavioral adaptations offer external adjustments, enhancing survival in changing environments.','Only behavioral adaptations are viewed as essential, overlooking the role of internal bodily changes in responding to environmental challenges.','C','This correctly describes the complementary roles of physiological and behavioral adaptations in coping with environmental variability.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,1,25,NULL,'A mountain bird has thicker feathers and a faster metabolism; a deep-sea fish has bioluminescence and pressure sensors. How do these adaptations relate to survival?','Both adapted to avoid predators using the same method, which ignores the distinct strategies each species evolved.','The bird developed camouflage for protection, while the fish evolved speed, focusing on different survival needs.','These adaptations enhance survival in extreme conditions; the bird for warmth, the fish for low light/high pressure.','Both adaptations are mainly for appearance, overlooking how they function to improve survival in specific environments.','C','This correctly identifies the adaptive significance of the features in their respective environments.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,26,NULL,'How does the evolution of respiratory systems (fish gills, amphibian gills/lungs, mammal lungs) reflect adaptation to aquatic and terrestrial environments?','All three use lungs for respiration, overlooking how aquatic animals like fish rely on gills.','All three use gills for breathing, which is incorrect and ignores key differences in respiratory adaptations.','Fish use lungs, amphibians use gills, and mammals use gills, presenting an inaccurate and reversed understanding of adaptation.','Fish use gills, amphibians use gills/lungs, mammals use lungs, showing adaptation progression linked to limb and body structure evolution.','D','This correctly describes the evolutionary progression of respiratory systems and their correlation with other anatomical changes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,27,NULL,'How do physiological (e.g., warm-bloodedness) and behavioral (e.g., migration) adaptations help animals survive fluctuating environments?','They are often seen as unrelated, ignoring how both types of adaptations work together to enhance survival','Focusing only on physiological adaptations neglects the role of learned or instinctive behaviors in survival.','Emphasizing only behavioral adaptations ignores the importance of internal processes in adapting to the environment.','Physiological adaptations provide internal regulation; behavioral adaptations provide external adjustments, enhancing survival in fluctuating conditions.','D','This correctly describes the complementary roles of physiological and behavioral adaptations in coping with environmental variability.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,28,NULL,'A polar bear has thick fur and a layer of fat. A camel has thick fur and can go a long time without drinking water. How are these adaptations similar in helping the animals survive?','Both adaptations help them escape predators more effectively, improving their chances of survival in the wild.','Both adaptations help them maintain body heat in cold climates, supporting survival in extreme conditions.','Both adaptations help them locate and access food sources that are essential for survival in their environments.','Both adaptations help them survive in harsh environments by protecting them from the elements or providing essential resources.','D','While both polar bears and camels possess thick fur, the similarities end there in terms of its function. The thick fur of a polar bear serves primarily as insulation against the extreme cold of the Arctic. The blubber layer further enhances this insulation and provides an energy reserve. These adaptations are crucial for survival in a frigid environment. A camel''s thick fur, on the other hand, offers protection from the sun''s intense heat in the desert. The ability to go long periods without water is a separate, vital adaptation for desert survival, related to efficient water conservation and storage of fat reserves',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,29,NULL,'How do the giraffe''s long neck and the fish''s fins help them survive?','The long neck helps the giraffe reach food, and the fins help the fish swim and move.','The long neck helps the giraffe run fast, and the fins help the fish breathe, though breathing is done with gills.','The long neck keeps the giraffe warm, and the fins cool the fish, which are not supported by biological evidence.','The long neck scares predators, and the fins are used to attract other fish, though these are not their main functions.','A','Giraffe''s Long Neck: A giraffe''s extraordinarily long neck is a key adaptation for reaching high into trees to access leaves and buds’ other herbivores can''t reach. This gives them a significant advantage in obtaining food, a crucial aspect of survival. The long neck also provides a better advantage for spotting predators from afar. While a long neck might incidentally help with some aspects of defense, its primary function is food acquisition. Fish''s Fins: Fins are essential for a fish''s survival. They provide the means of locomotion, allowing the fish to move through the water to find food, escape predators, and navigate its environment. Different types of fins serve different purposes (e.g., caudal fin for propulsion, pectoral fins for steering), but all contribute to the fish''s ability to maneuver and survive in its aquatic habitat. Fins do not directly aid in breathing; gills are responsible for that function.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,30,NULL,'How do scales (reptiles) and fur (mammals) relate to their respective environmental advantages?','Scales may provide camouflage, while fur can play a role in mating displays and temperature control.','Scales help with swimming and protection, while fur aids in warmth and sensory perception in mammals.','Both offer survival benefits, but they serve distinct functions based on the species and environment.','Scales help conserve water in dry areas; fur provides insulation in changing climates, explaining their evolutionary advantages.','D','This accurately describes the adaptive significance of scales and fur in different environments.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,31,NULL,'A community garden has unhealthy plants (soil depletion, pests) and nearby wildlife suffers from habitat loss. What''s the BEST integrated solution?','Use soil enrichment, integrated pest management, and create wildlife corridors.','Rely only on chemical pest control, which can harm helpful species and damage the ecosystem.','Move wildlife and use synthetic fertilizers, missing the value of natural plant- animal interactions.','Abandon the garden and build shelters, ignoring the potential to support both plants and animals together.','A','This option addresses both plant and animal issues holistically, promoting sustainability.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,32,NULL,'How do the techniques of integrated pest management for plant care and habitat restoration for animal protection demonstrate a relational understanding of ecosystem balance, and how do these practices impact the overall biodiversity of a region?','They demonstrate an understanding of ecosystem balance by minimizing harmful chemical use and maximizing natural ecosystem processes, which benefit biodiversity.','These practices are assumed to have no effect on ecosystem stability or biodiversity, overlooking how reducing harmful chemicals and encouraging natural cycles directly support the health of diverse species.','These practices are thought to benefit plant growth while causing harm to animals in the area, ignoring how sustainable methods can support both plant and animal life by preserving natural interactions and reducing environmental stress.','These practices are believed to support animal populations while damaging plant health, failing to recognize that sustainable techniques are designed to promote harmony between species and enhance overall ecosystem function.','A','Integrated pest management (IPM) and habitat restoration demonstrate a relational understanding of ecosystem balance by emphasizing minimal disruption and maximum utilization of natural processes. IPM focuses on controlling pests through methods that minimize harmful chemical use, promote natural predators and maintain healthy plant populations, thus preserving the ecosystem''s integrity. Habitat restoration, on the other hand, aims to restore or create environments that support a diverse range of species, providing food, shelter, and breeding grounds. Both practices contribute to overall biodiversity by fostering a balanced ecosystem where various species can thrive. IPM prevents the loss of beneficial insects and maintains plant diversity, while habitat restoration increases species richness and abundance. These practices work in synergy to promote a healthy, diverse ecosystem, showcasing the importance of understanding and working with natural ecological processes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,33,NULL,'The scenario above describes various techniques for plant care and animal protection. How does implementing ethical tourism practices, which minimize disturbance to both plant and animal life, relate to the broader concept of responsible ecosystem stewardship?','Ethical tourism practices demonstrate responsible stewardship by recognizing the interconnectedness of plant and animal health and by minimizing any negative impact that human activities can have on the environment','Ethical tourism is often viewed as being solely focused on protecting animals from harm or exploitation, without acknowledging its broader role in supporting entire ecosystems, including plant conservation, habitat protection, and sustainable use of natural resources.','Some assume that ethical tourism is unrelated to ecosystem stewardship, overlooking how tourism choices—such as waste management, habitat preservation, and responsible interactions with wildlife—directly impact the health and sustainability of ecosystems.','Ethical tourism is believed to benefit only human communities through economic gain or cultural experiences, without considering how responsible tourism practices can also support environmental conservation, protect ecosystems, and promote the well-being of plant and animal life.','A','Ethical tourism practices directly relate to responsible ecosystem stewardship by prioritizing the minimization of disturbance to both plant and animal life. This approach recognizes the interconnectedness of all components within an ecosystem, understanding that human activities can have far-reaching impacts. By promoting practices that minimize negative impacts, such as limiting habitat intrusion, avoiding feeding or handling wildlife, and respecting plant life, ethical tourism contributes to the preservation of natural habitats and biodiversity. It demonstrates a commitment to sustainable interactions with the environment, ensuring that tourism benefits local communities without compromising the long-term health and integrity of the ecosystem.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,34,NULL,'If a local wildlife refuge is experiencing an increase in invasive plant species that are outcompeting native plants, and a corresponding decrease in native animal populations that rely on those plants for food and shelter, how would you develop an integrated strategy that addresses both the invasive plant problem and the native animal protection?','An integrated strategy would involve targeted removal of invasive plants, restoration of native plant habitats, and the creation of protected areas to support native animal populations, considering the interconnectedness of plant and animal health.','Ignore the spread of invasive plants completely and focus only on providing supplemental food to native animals, without addressing the degradation of their natural habitat caused by invasive species, which can reduce biodiversity and make the ecosystem less resilient over time.','Introduce a new animal species specifically to feed on the invasive plants, even though this could lead to unintended consequences such as the new species becoming invasive itself, disrupting food chains, or competing with native animals for resources, ultimately harming the balance of the ecosystem.','Apply broad-spectrum herbicides across the refuge to eliminate all plant life, including invasive species, without considering the harmful effects on native plant species, soil quality, water sources, and the animals that depend on native plants for food and shelter, which could severely damage the ecosystem in the long term.','A','An integrated strategy is essential to address the intertwined problems of invasive plant species and declining native animal populations in the wildlife refuge. This would involve targeted removal of invasive plants, focusing on methods that minimize harm to native species and the overall ecosystem, such as manual removal or species-specific biological controls. Simultaneously, restoration of native plant habitats through seeding or planting native species would help re-establish the food web and provide essential resources for native animals. Creating protected areas within the refuge, free from further invasive encroachment and human disturbance, would provide safe havens for native animal populations to recover. This holistic approach recognizes that plant and animal health are interdependent, and that a balanced ecosystem is crucial for the refuge''s long-term sustainability.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,35,NULL,'How does the relationship between sustainable water management for plant health and the creation of wildlife water sources for animal protection illustrate a relational approach to conservation, and how does this approach affect long-term ecosystem stability?','Focusing only on creating water sources for animals ignores how managing water use also supports plant and soil health.','Assuming water management helps only plants and wildlife sources help only animals overlook how both are interconnected.','Treating water management and wildlife water sources as separate overlooks their shared role in maintaining ecosystem stability.','They demonstrate a relational approach by recognizing that water is essential for both plants and animals and that the long-term stability of an ecosystem is dependent on a healthy water cycle.','D','The relationship between sustainable water management for plant health and the creation of wildlife water sources for animal protection illustrates a relational approach to conservation by acknowledging the fundamental role of water in supporting all life within an ecosystem. Sustainable water management practices, such as rainwater harvesting and efficient irrigation, ensure that plants receive adequate hydration, promoting healthy growth and maintaining ecosystem productivity. Similarly, creating wildlife water sources, like ponds or watering holes, provides essential drinking water for animals, supporting their survival and reproduction. This approach recognizes that the long-term stability of an ecosystem is dependent on a healthy water cycle, where water availability directly influences both plant and animal communities. By managing water resources sustainably, we ensure that both plant and animal needs are met, contributing to a balanced and resilient ecosystem.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,36,NULL,'How do soil management and wildlife corridors contribute to holistic ecosystem conservation?','Prioritizing soil management alone overlooks the role of connected habitats in supporting animal populations.','Focusing only on wildlife corridors neglects how soil quality impacts plant life, which animals depend on to survive.','Soil health and wildlife corridors are treated as separate issues, ignoring how both are vital to ecosystem conservation.','Healthy soil supports plant life, which supports animal life; corridors allow animal movement and maintain genetic diversity.','D','This accurately describes the interconnectedness of soil health, plant life, animal life, and habitat connectivity in ecosystem conservation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,37,NULL,'How does the analysis of the relationship between soil management techniques for plant health and the creation of wildlife corridors for animal movement contribute to a holistic understanding of ecosystem conservation?','Focusing only on wildlife corridors overlooks how healthy soil is essential for supporting the plants that animals rely on.','Treating soil care and habitat connectivity as unrelated ignores how both are vital to maintaining balanced ecosystems.','Connecting habitats helps animals move and stay genetically diverse, but this must work alongside strong soil and plant health.','Soil management and wildlife corridors contribute to holistic conservation by recognizing that healthy soil supports plant life, which in turn supports animal life.','D','This question asks how two specific conservation strategies—soil management and wildlife corridors—work together to support a holistic (whole-system) approach to ecosystem conservation. Reference Department of Education – Bureau of Alternative Learning System. (2010). Science Module 17: Taking Care of the Environment (Elementary Level). Department of Education.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,38,NULL,'How does integrating soil management for plant health with wildlife corridor development reflect a system-thinking approach to ecosystem conservation?','Wildlife corridors are seen as more critical for preserving ecosystems than efforts to manage and improve soil quality.','Soil care helps plants grow and corridors help animals migrate, but each works independently without affecting the other.','These methods address separate goals—soil for agriculture and corridors for animals—and do not work together in conservation.','Combining these practices shows how improving soil health supports plant life, which in turn sustains animal populations, and corridors allow genetic diversity through movement.','D','This choice reflects relational thinking by showing how interconnected practices contribute to ecosystem stability and biodiversity',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,39,NULL,'Rolando and Ailyn want to investigate how different surfaces affect the number of frictional forces. They plan to use a spring scale to measure the force needed to pull a wooden block across various surfaces. To ensure the reliability and validity of their results, and consider information literacy principles, what additional steps should the student take?','Rely on friends’ opinions about friction levels instead of using tested methods and repeated observations.','Perform the experiment just once per surface without repeating trials or ensuring consistent testing conditions.','Use wooden blocks of different sizes and weights, which may affect results and reduce the accuracy of comparisons.','Consult reliable scientific sources to understand friction and experimental design, then repeat measurements multiple times for each surface, maintaining consistent pulling angle and speed.','D','Option D is superior because it directly measures the force of friction while controlling other variables, ensuring reliable and valid results. This demonstrates relational understanding by integrating multiple aspects of experimental design (controlled variables, direct measurement, and valid conclusion).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,40,NULL,'Which of the following best illustrates a community’s use of integrated problem-solving in preparing for volcanic hazards?','Constructing shelters but not planning how people will reach them safely during an emergency.','Gathering emergency supplies while failing to establish a system for informing and coordinating with the public.','Prioritizing the mapping of hazard zones without including plans for evacuation, shelter, or public awareness efforts','Creating a plan that includes evacuation routes, shelters, communication systems, and public education, recognizing that each element supports the others.','D','option D. demonstrates relational problem-solving by integrating multiple preparedness components and recognizing their interdependence.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,41,NULL,'You roll a toy car down a ramp made of wood, then down a ramp made of carpet. The car rolls farther on the wood ramp. What does this tell you about the friction on each surface?','The carpet ramp is longer than the wood ramp.','The wood ramp is heavier than the carpet ramp.','The wood ramp is rougher than the carpet ramp.','The carpet ramp has more friction than the wood ramp.','D','Option D because the experiment demonstrates the relationship between surface texture and friction. Friction is a force that resists motion between two surfaces in contact. The amount of friction depends on several factors, including the types of materials and the roughness of the surfaces. Rougher surfaces create more friction than smoother surfaces.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,42,NULL,'A community is developing a volcanic eruption preparedness plan. They have access to several information sources: (A) a government website with official hazard maps and evacuation guidelines; (B) a local news website with anecdotal accounts of past eruptions; (C) a scientific journal article detailing the volcano''s geological history and eruption patterns; (D) a social media feed with real-time updates during an ongoing eruption. Which combination of sources would provide the MOST reliable and comprehensive information for developing a well-informed preparedness plan, demonstrating effective information literacy?','A and B only.','B and D only.','A and C only.','A, C, and potentially D (if the eruption is not the subject of the plan).','D','Option D is best because it combines authoritative sources (A and C) for long-term planning and acknowledges the potential use of real-time information (D) for situational awareness during an event, demonstrating relational understanding of how different information sources complement each other.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,43,NULL,'A volcano is about to erupt. Which of these actions would BEST protect you and your family before the eruption?','Delay taking safety steps until the eruption begins, losing valuable time for safe evacuation.','Remain indoors and watch television instead of preparing or responding to possible volcanic danger.','Step outside to observe the lava, putting yourself at serious risk from ash, gas, and flowing magma.','Pack an emergency bag with food, water, and a flashlight, and follow your family''s evacuation plan.','D','Emphasizes proactive preparation, a crucial element of disaster preparedness. Packing an emergency bag ensures access to essential supplies (food, water, light source) in case of a sudden evacuation order or disruption of services. This preparedness minimizes risks associated with immediate needs during a chaotic situation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,44,NULL,'A volcano has erupted, and ash is falling. You are inside your home. Which action is MOST important to do during the eruption?','Stay inside, close all windows and doors, and cover your mouth and nose with damp cloth.','Open windows and allow ash and gases to enter your home, increasing health and safety risks.','Carry on with your normal routine despite the eruption, ignoring safety precautions and warnings.','Go outdoors and expose yourself to falling ash, which can harm your lungs and eyes during an eruption.','A','Ash Inhalation: Volcanic ash is extremely dangerous to inhale. It composed of tiny, sharp particles of rock and glass that can irritate the lungs, eyes, and skin. Prolonged exposure can lead to serious respiratory problems. Closing windows and doors prevents ash from entering the house, minimizing inhalation risks. Respiratory Protection: Covering the mouth and nose with a damp cloth offers a rudimentary form of respiratory protection. While not a perfect filter, a damp cloth helps to trap some of the larger ash particles and moistens the air, making it slightly easier to breathe. Shelter in Place: Staying indoors is the safest course of action during ashfall. Buildings provide a barrier against falling ash and debris. This "shelter in place" strategy is a standard emergency response procedure for many natural disasters.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,45,NULL,'Which strategy best reflects critical thinking in designing an evacuation plan that accounts for diverse community needs and infrastructure challenges?','Setting up emergency shelters without planning how people will reach them or ensuring access for those in need.','Designing evacuation routes without evaluating road safety or how route conditions may affect overall evacuation efforts.','Creating a contact list for residents but not addressing how communication and transportation will work together in emergencies.','Developing a plan that includes evacuation logistics, communication protocols and support for vulnerable populations, recognizing how these elements interact.','D','This choice reflects relational critical thinking by integrating multiple preparedness factors and considering diverse needs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,46,NULL,'A volcano has erupted near your town. You need to find reliable information about what to do next. Which source would give you the BEST and most trustworthy information?','A news report from a well-known and reputable news organization.','A message passed along by a friend who got the information secondhand, without confirmed details.','A blog entry by someone claiming to be a volcanologist but offering no credentials or verified background.','A social media update shared by an unfamiliar user, offering no verified source or evidence for the information.','A','The best source for reliable information following a nearby volcanic eruption is a news report from a well-known and reputable news organization (option b). This is because established news organizations have several key advantages over other information sources in emergency situations: • Fact-Checking and Verification: Reputable news organizations employ fact- checkers and journalists trained to verify information before publication. They cross- reference data from multiple sources, ensuring accuracy and minimizing the spread of misinformation. This is crucial during emergencies when inaccurate information can be dangerous. • Expertise and Access: News organizations often have access to experts, including volcanologists, emergency management officials, and government agencies. They can provide informed analysis and up-to-date information directly from credible sources, ensuring the public receives accurate guidance. • Reach and Distribution: Established news outlets have broad reach and established distribution channels. They can disseminate critical information quickly and efficiently to a large audience, ensuring that the public receives timely warnings and instructions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,47,NULL,'If the Earth rotates on its axis every 24 hours, how would you calculate the time difference for two locations on opposite sides of the Earth?','Multiply the number of hours by two','Each location would have the same time','Account for 12 hours difference due to rotation','Measure the distance between the two locations','C','The Earth rotates on its axis once every 24 hours, which causes day and night. This rotation also creates time zones, as different parts of the Earth face the Sun at different times.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,48,NULL,'Which of the following best explains why we experience day and night?','The rotation of the Earth on its axis causes different portions to face the Sun.','The Sun appears to move across the sky, but it does not actually revolve around the Earth.','The Earth moves in a nearly circular path around the Sun, but this does not explain day and night.','The Earth and Moon interact through gravity, but the Moon does not control Earth’s Day and night cycle.','A','D) The rotation of the Earth on its axis causes different portions to face the Sun because this rotation is the key reason why we experience the cycle of day and night. As the Earth spins on its axis, different areas of the planet are exposed to sunlight while others are in shadow. This results in one side experiencing daylight while the opposite side is in darkness, creating the daily cycle of day and night.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,49,NULL,'Which of the following material properties is MOST directly related to a material''s resistance to scratching?','Ductility','Elasticity','Hardness','Tensile strength','C','Hardness is a measure of a material''s resistance to indentation or scratching. Tensile strength relates to pulling forces, ductility to deformation before fracture, and elasticity to its ability to return to its original shape after deformation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,2,50,NULL,'A material''s ability to be drawn into wires is primarily determined by its:','Ductility','Density','Hardness','Brittleness','A','Ductility is the measure of a material''s ability to deform under tensile stress; this is directly related to its ability to be drawn into wires.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,51,NULL,'The relationship between the microstructure of a metal and its mechanical properties is BEST described as:','Unpredictable; there is no consistent relationship.','Direct; microstructure significantly affects mechanical properties.','Independent; microstructure has no effect on mechanical properties.','Indirect; microstructure only slightly influences mechanical properties.','B','The arrangement of grains, defects, and phases within a material''s microstructure directly influences its strength, ductility, toughness, and other mechanical properties.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,52,NULL,'Considering the relationship between processing and properties, which material processing technique would MOST likely increase the strength of a metal?','Annealing','Quenching','Both b and c','Cold working','C','Cold working (plastic deformation) and quenching (rapid cooling from high temperature) both increase the strength of a metal by altering its microstructure. Annealing reduces strength.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,53,NULL,'Which pair of materials demonstrates the GREATEST difference in their thermal conductivity?','Glass and Plastic','Copper and Brass','Wood and Diamond','Aluminum and Steel','C','Diamond has exceptionally high thermal conductivity, while wood has very low thermal conductivity. The other options represent materials with more similar thermal conductivities.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,54,NULL,'You have a glass of orange juice. You know it contains orange juice concentrate, water, and possibly sugar. Which statement BEST describes the orange juice?','It’s a mixture because it’s made of different substances that can be separated.','It is identified as a pure substance based only on being a liquid, not on its chemical makeup.','It is labeled a pure substance due to its consistent color and taste, ignoring the substances within it.','It is considered a mixture simply because it is in liquid form, without regard to its actual composition.','A','Option D directly addresses this relational understanding by emphasizing that the orange juice is composed of multiple substances (water, concentrate, sugar) that can be physically separated (e.g., by evaporation or filtration). The other options present misconceptions about pure substances and mixtures. The question is framed to be relatable to the learners'' daily lives, uses simple language, and encourages critical thinking by requiring them to analyze the composition of a common beverage. The question avoids overly technical terminology and focuses on the fundamental concept of mixtures.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,55,NULL,'A composite material combines different materials to enhance specific properties. What is the PRIMARY reason for using composite materials?','To improve one or more properties beyond those of the individual components.','To lower overall production expenses by using materials that are more affordable when combined.','To streamline how products are made by using materials that are easier to shape or process together.','To enhance the appearance of the final material by blending components for a more appealing look.','A','The core principle behind composite materials is to combine the advantages of different materials (e.g., high strength and low weight) to create a material with superior overall performance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,56,NULL,'The main function of both the male and female reproductive systems is to:','Produce hormones that control growth and development.','Enable the body to produce and eliminate waste products.','Regulate the body''s temperature and maintain internal balance.','Allow for the creation of new human life through the joining of egg and sperm.','D','This question directly assesses relational understanding by requiring students to connect the functions of seemingly separate male and female reproductive systems to their shared, overarching purpose: reproduction. Option (c) highlights this relational understanding by emphasizing the fundamental role of both systems in creating new life through fertilization.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,57,NULL,'During puberty, the release of which hormone is MOST responsible for the development of secondary sexual characteristics in males?','Estrogen','Testosterone','Progesterone','Follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH)','B','Testosterone is the primary male sex hormone responsible for the development of secondary sexual characteristics like increased muscle mass, facial hair, and deeper voice.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,58,NULL,'What is a crucial aspect of maintaining reproductive health in both males and females?','Regular hygiene practices.','Avoiding all physical activity.','Ignoring any changes in the body.','Consuming only specific types of food.','A','Good hygiene is essential to prevent infections and maintain the health of the reproductive system.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,59,NULL,'Which physical adaptation in mammals living in cold climates best illustrates the relationship between environmental conditions and survival strategies?','Large ears for heat dissipation.','Brightly colored skin for visibility.','Long limbs for faster movement.','Thick fur or blubber for insulation.','D','Thick fur or blubber directly supports survival in cold climates, showing a relational link between environment and adaptation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,60,NULL,'Which adaptation in fish best demonstrates the relationship between structural features and survival in aquatic environments?','Lungs for breathing air.','Thick fur for insulation.','Strong legs for land movement.','Gills for extracting oxygen from water.','D','Gills are a structural adaptation that directly supports survival in water, showing the connection between form and function.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,61,NULL,'Which of the following is a common adaptation found in many fish species that enhances their ability to survive in aquatic environments?','Lungs for breathing air','Thick fur for insulation','Strong legs for locomotion on land','Gills for extracting oxygen from water','D','Gills are specialized respiratory organs that allow fish to extract dissolved oxygen from water, enabling them to survive in their aquatic habitat.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,62,NULL,'Consider the adaptations of birds for flight. Which of the following is NOT a key adaptation for flight in birds?','Feathers','Hollow bones','Large, strong legs','Streamlined body shape','C','While birds have legs, large and strong legs are more beneficial for terrestrial locomotion than for flight. Hollow bones, feathers, and a streamlined body shape all contribute to efficient flight.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,63,NULL,'You are sliding a wooden block across different surfaces: a smooth tabletop, a carpet, and a piece of sandpaper. The block slides farthest on the tabletop and shortest on the sandpaper. What can you conclude about friction?','Friction is stronger on rough surfaces.','Friction only happens on rough surfaces.','Friction is stronger on smoother surfaces.','Friction does not affect how far the block slides.','A','This question requires students to relate the observation (sliding distance) to the concept of friction. Option (c) correctly identifies the relationship: a shorter sliding distance indicates more friction, which is associated with rougher surfaces. The other options present misconceptions about friction.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,64,NULL,'You want to assess how the type of surface affects how easily a toy car rolls. Which of these is the MOST important step to make sure your test is fair?','Use the same toy car and the same starting point for each surface.','Use a different toy car on each surface, though differences in cars can affect the test results.','Try using a different ramp for every surface tested, which may affect how the car moves each time.','Push the car with varying amounts of force on each surface, which can lead to inconsistent outcomes.','A','This question assesses relational understanding by focusing on the design of a fair scientific investigation. Option (b) correctly identifies the importance of controlling variables (type of car and starting point) to isolate the effect of the surface type on the rolling distance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,65,NULL,'Which of the following is the BEST example of reducing friction to improve efficiency?','Using a rougher surface for tires.','Using sandpaper to roughen the surface.','Adding oil to a machine''s moving parts.','Increasing the weight of a moving object.','C','Oil acts as a lubricant, reducing friction between moving parts and increasing efficiency.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,66,NULL,'Cathren drops a feather and a small stone from the same height at the same time. The stone hits the ground first. What is the MAIN reason the stone falls faster than the feather?','Air resistance slows the feather down more than the stone.','The stone’s darker color does not significantly affect how quickly it falls compared to a feather in the air.','The stone’s smoother surface has less impact on its fall speed than the feather’s shape and air resistance.','The stone has more mass than the feather, but mass alone does not explain the difference in how fast they fall.','A','This question requires students to relate the observation (different falling times) to the concepts of gravity and air resistance. Option (c) correctly identifies that while gravity pulls on both objects equally, the feather''s larger surface area and lighter weight make it more susceptible to air resistance, slowing its descent.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,67,NULL,'Ignoring air resistance (imagine dropping objects in a vacuum), which of these statements is TRUE about how gravity affects falling objects?','Only objects made of metal fall due to gravity','Heavier objects always fall faster than lighter objects.','Lighter objects always fall faster than heavier objects.','All objects fall at the same rate regardless of their weight.','D','This question assesses relational understanding of the concept of gravity''s equal effect on all objects, independent of mass (when air resistance is negligible). Option (c) correctly states that in a vacuum, gravity accelerates all objects at the same rate.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,68,NULL,'Which statement BEST describes the relationship between mass and gravitational force?','The relationship is unpredictable.','Mass has no effect on gravitational force.','Greater mass results in less gravitational force.','Greater mass results in greater gravitational force.','D','The force of gravity is directly proportional to the mass of objects involved. A more massive object exerts a stronger gravitational pull.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,69,NULL,'It is daytime in Manila, Philippines. At the same time, it is nighttime in New York City. What is the MAIN reason for this difference?','The Earth tilted on its axis.','The Earth rotates on its axis.','The Earth revolves around the sun.','The Earth is closer to the sun during the day.','B','This question requires students to relate the observation (different times of day in various locations) to Earth''s rotation. Option (c) correctly identifies that Earth''s rotation on its axis is the primary reason different parts of the Earth experience day and night at different times.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,70,NULL,'Imagine you could travel in a spaceship that could instantly move to any point on Earth. If it is midday (noon) in London, England, where would you MOST likely find it to be midnight (12:00 AM)?','A location on the same side of the Earth as London.','A location slightly closer to the North Pole than London.','A location slightly closer to the South Pole than London.','A location on the opposite side of the Earth from London.','D','This question assesses relational understanding by requiring students to visualize Earth''s rotation and connect it to the concept of opposite sides experiencing different times of day. Option (D) correctly highlights that when it is midday in one location, the opposite side of the Earth will experience midnight due to Earth''s rotation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,71,NULL,'How does Earth''s tilt on its axis affect the seasons?','It causes changes in the amount of direct sunlight received at different latitudes.','It leads to varying lengths of daytime and nighttime across regions as the Earth moves around the Sun annually.','It slightly alters Earth’s distance from the Sun, but this change is not what causes the seasonal temperature shifts.','It does not influence how much direct sunlight different areas receive during the year or affect seasonal patterns.','A','The tilt causes different hemispheres to receive more direct sunlight at different times of the year, resulting in seasonal variations in temperature and daylight hours.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,72,NULL,'Which of the following phenomena is MOST directly related to Earth''s revolution around the Sun?','Earthquakes.','High and low tides.','The changing seasons.','The phases of the Moon.','C','Earth''s revolution and its tilted axis are the primary causes of the seasons.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,73,NULL,'The Earth''s axis is tilted at approximately 23.5 degrees relative to its orbital plane. What is a significant consequence of this tilt?','While the Earth spins steadily, day length still changes due to its tilted axis and orbit, influencing seasonal light.','Earth’s temperature changes with the seasons, driven by varying sunlight at different latitudes throughout the year.','The Earth’s rotation speed shifts slightly during the year, affecting how sunlight is distributed across regions seasonally.','The Earth experiences variations in the amount of sunlight received at different latitudes throughout the year, leading to seasons.','D','The tilt is the primary reason for the seasonal changes in temperature and daylight hours across different latitudes on Earth.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,74,NULL,'A volcanic eruption spews large amounts of ash into the stratosphere. What is the MOST likely immediate effect on global temperatures?','A significant increase in global temperatures.','A significant decrease in global temperatures.','No noticeable change in global temperatures.','Localized temperature increases near the volcano.','B','Volcanic ash and gases can block sunlight, leading to a temporary cooling effect on the planet.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS2',3,3,75,NULL,'After a volcanic eruption, which recovery strategy best demonstrates critical thinking by addressing interconnected community needs?','Distributing food and water while also assessing infrastructure damage and health risks, recognizing both as vital.','Prioritizing clean water access and health services before long-term housing, recognizing how health impacts recovery.','Restoring roads and buildings after addressing urgent health needs, acknowledging health’s role in safe rebuilding.','Supporting local business revival after ensuring clean water access and health care, recognizing their role in economic recovery.','B','This option shows relational critical thinking by prioritizing health and infrastructure in a way that supports long-term recovery.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,1,'Mrs. Baguitong is an online seller of ready-to-wear (RTW) clothing who delivers parcels from Monday to Saturday. Over the week, she dispatched a total of 39,947 RTW parcels. The breakdown for the first five days is as follows: 6,892 parcels on Monday, 5,782 on Tuesday, 7,534 on Wednesday, 4,658 on Thursday, and 6,436 on Friday resulting in a five-day total of 31,302 parcels.','How many parcels did Mrs. Baguitong deliver on Saturday?','8,645','8,465','6,845','6,485','A','Step 1 6,892 (Mon.) + 5,782 (Tues.) + 7, 534 (Wed.) + 4, 658 (Thurs.) + 6, 436 (Fri.) = 31, 302 Step 2 39, 947 – 31, 302 = 8, 645',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,2,'Mrs. Baguitong is an online seller of ready-to-wear (RTW) clothing who delivers parcels from Monday to Saturday. Over the week, she dispatched a total of 39,947 RTW parcels. The breakdown for the first five days is as follows: 6,892 parcels on Monday, 5,782 on Tuesday, 7,534 on Wednesday, 4,658 on Thursday, and 6,436 on Friday resulting in a five-day total of 31,302 parcels.','Based on the delivery data from Monday to Friday, which day did Mrs. Baguitong deliver the highest number of parcels?','Monday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','B','Day #s of Delivered Parcel Mon. 6,892 Tues. 5,782 Wed. 7,534 Thurs. 4,658 Fri. 6,436',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,3,'Berting supplies 2,895 buko pies daily to five stores in Wagwagan Market and continues this supply for 320 days each year.','How many Buko pies did each store receive from Berting in total over the course of the year?','815,820','581,280','518,820','185,280','D','Step 1 2895 ÷ 5 = 579 Step 2 579 × 320 = 185, 280',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,4,'Berting supplies 2,895 buko pies daily to five stores in Wagwagan Market and continues this supply for 320 days each year.','How many Buko pies did he supply in total during the year?','926,400','320,600','296,404','203,500','A','Solution: 2,895 x 320 = 926, 400 Buko Pie',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,5,'A pineapple juice factory made 124,800 pineapple juice in 26 days.','If the factory made the same number of juices every day, how many pineapples did it use per day?','6400','5200','4800','3585','C','Solution: 292,500 ÷ 6,500 = 45 days',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,6,'A pineapple juice factory made 124,800 pineapple juice in 26 days.','How many days would it take for the factory to produce 292,500 pineapple juices if it produces 6,500 each day?','6400','5200','4800','3585','D','Solution: 124,800 pineapples ÷ 26 days = 4,800 each day',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,7,'Janice is preparing snack boxes for a school activity. She starts with (8 + 2) small packs of cookies. Each pack costs ₱30, and she also buys a juice box for ₱20. She divides the total cost by 2 to split the bill with her best friend and then uses a ₱20 discount voucher. How much does Janice pay after the discount?','If Janice wants to prepare two sets of snacks how much will she pay in total?','PHP 300.00','PHP 320.00','PHP 400.00','PHP 420.00','A','Solution: [(8+2) × 30+20] ÷ 2−20 = Php 300.00',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,8,'Janice is preparing snack boxes for a school activity. She starts with (8 + 2) small packs of cookies. Each pack costs ₱30, and she also buys a juice box for ₱20. She divides the total cost by 2 to split the bill with her best friend and then uses a ₱20 discount voucher. How much does Janice pay after the discount?','Simplify the expression: [(8 + 2) × 30 + 20] ÷ 2 − 20','180','170','155','140','D','Solution: [(8 + 2) × 30 + 20] ÷ 2 − 20 (10 x 30 + 20) ÷ 2 – 20 (300 + 20) ÷ 2 – 20 320 ÷ 2 – 20 160 – 20 = 140',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,9,NULL,'Which is true about prime numbers?','Prime number is divisible by 3 or more numbers','A prime number is only divisible by 1 and itself','A prime number are all even numbers','A prime number is a decimal number.','B','A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has only two factors: • 1 • Itself This means a prime number can be divided only by 1 and by itself without leaving a remainder.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,10,NULL,'Brgy. Mawalangsala has a group of 10 senior citizens aged 60 to 70 years old. Based on the data provided, what is the greatest prime number between the ages of 60 and 70?','63','65','67','68','C','The numbers between 60 and 70 are: 61,62,63,64, 65, 67, 68, 69. The prime numbers are: 61,63, and 67. The greatest prime number is 67.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,11,'Marta is playing a Hopscotch or “Sudsud” using skip counting by 9s. She starts the game with 9, 18, 27, 36, __, __, 63, __. After playing Hopscotch, she goes to a charity event where she gives away 9 packs of notebooks to every school in attendance. She checks the total number of notebooks she received from donors and finds out that she has 2,331 notebooks.','Which statement justifies that 2,331 is divisible by 9?','Yes, because 9 is a factor of all numbers over 2,000','Yes, because the sum of its digits is divisible by 9.','No, because 2,331 is an odd number','No, because it ends in a 1','B','Solution: 2,331 = 2+3+3+1 =9',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,12,'Marta is playing a Hopscotch or “Sudsud” using skip counting by 9s. She starts the game with 9, 18, 27, 36, __, __, 63, __. After playing Hopscotch, she goes to a charity event where she gives away 9 packs of notebooks to every school in attendance. She checks the total number of notebooks she received from donors and finds out that she has 2,331 notebooks.','If you were Marta, what would the missing numbers be to reach the finishing line?','33, 43, and 75','42, 44, and 66','35, 55, and 78','45, 54, and 72','D','Solution: 9 = 9, 18, 27, 36, 45, 54, 63, 72',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,13,'Aling Rosal bought two pieces of banana cake for her six grandchildren. After giving all the banana cake to them, she bought another three pieces for her twelve visitors from Davao City.','If she divided the cakes equally among them, what fraction of the banana cake did each grandchild receive?','1/3 of a cake','1/4 of a cake','1/2 of a cake','2/3 of a cake','A','2 cakes shared by 6 grandchildren: 2/6 = 1/3 of a cake each.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,14,'Aling Rosal bought two pieces of banana cake for her six grandchildren. After giving all the banana cake to them, she bought another three pieces for her twelve visitors from Davao City.','What fraction of the banana cake did each visitor receive?','1/2 of a cake','1/3 of a cake','1/4 of a cake','1/6 of a cake','C','3 cakes shared by 12 visitors: 3/12 = 1/4 of a cake each.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,15,'Juan bought 1/2 kilo of caramel candies, 1/4 kilo of red bubble gum, and 1/5 kilo of lollipops for his younger sister''s birthday party. He put everything he bought into the bag.','Using the given statement, what kind of fraction is presented in the problem?','Mixed Number','Similar Fraction','Dissimilar Fraction','A whole number and a mixed number','C','1/2, 1/4, and 1/5 have different denominators, so they are dissimilar fractions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,16,'Juan bought 1/2 kilo of caramel candies, 1/4 kilo of red bubble gum, and 1/5 kilo of lollipops for his younger sister''s birthday party. He put everything he bought into the bag.','Why is it important to identify that 1/2, 1/4, and 1/5 are dissimilar fractions before adding the candies Juan bought?','Because similar fractions cannot be added.','Because fractions need common denominators first.','Because the total amount will always be more than 1 kilo.','Because fractions with different numerators are harder to count.','B','Dissimilar fractions must first be changed to a common denominator before they can be added.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,17,'Juan bought 1/2 kilo of caramel candies, 1/4 kilo of red bubble gum, and 1/5 kilo of lollipops for his younger sister''s birthday party. He put everything he bought into the bag.','How many kilos of sweets did Juan buy? Reduce your answer to the lowest terms.','2 1/4 kilos','1 1/10 kilos','19/20 kilos','4/40 kilos','C','Use the LCD 20: 1/2 = 10/20, 1/4 = 5/20, 1/5 = 4/20. Then 10/20 + 5/20 + 4/20 = 19/20 kilo.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,18,'Ana buys a birthday cake for her mother. When she gets home, her younger sister slices the cake into eight equal parts. After slicing, she eats 2 parts of the cake.','If 5 parts of the birthday cake were eaten, what is the reciprocal of the fraction formed?','8/3','8/5','3/2','7/8','B','5 of 8 parts is 5/8. The reciprocal swaps the numerator and denominator: 8/5.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,19,'Ana buys a birthday cake for her mother. When she gets home, her younger sister slices the cake into eight equal parts. After slicing, she eats 2 parts of the cake.','If the fraction of a cake eaten is 2/8, what is the reciprocal of that fraction?','8/2','2/3','1/4','2/8','A','The reciprocal of 2/8 is 8/2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,20,'Pablo went to the market to buy assorted vegetables. He bought 4 kilos of eggplant at PHP 45.00 per kilo, 5 kilos of chayote at PHP 15.00 per kilo, 3 kilos of Baguio beans at PHP 65.00 per kilo, and 4 kilos of cabbage at PHP 80.00 per kilo.','If Pablo wants to buy cabbage only and he wants to buy 8 kilos of cabbage. How much will he pay if he has 8 kilos of cabbage in total?','PHP 350.00','PHP 480.00','PHP 520.00','PHP 640.00','D','Steps: • What is given? 8 kilos Cabbage PHP 80.00/kilo • What are the operations to be used? Multiplication • What is the equation? 8 kls. × 80 = n • Solve for n. 8 kilos × PHP 80.00 = PHP 640.00',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,21,'Pablo went to the market to buy assorted vegetables. He bought 4 kilos of eggplant at PHP 45.00 per kilo, 5 kilos of chayote at PHP 15.00 per kilo, 3 kilos of Baguio beans at PHP 65.00 per kilo, and 4 kilos of cabbage at PHP 80.00 per kilo.','If the price of Chayote is PHP 15.00/kilo, how much will he pay for the Chayote?','PHP 35.00','PHP 50.00','PHP 75.00','PHP 90.00','C','Steps: 1. What is given? • 4 kilos of Eggplant • 5 kilos of Chayote • 3 kilos of Baguio Beans • 4 kilos of Cabbage 2. What operations will be used? • Multiplication 3. What is the equation? • (Price per kilo) × (Quantity of Chayote) • 15 × 5 = 75 • 5 kls. × 15 = n Solve for n. 5 kilos x PHP 15.00 = PHP 75.00',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,22,'Ms. Susi is an event organizer. One day, Ms. Loi booked her for a wedding anniversary event and requested a clothing design using primary colors. Ms. Susi bought 3 meters of blue fabric, 4.5 meters of red fabric, and 2 meters of green fabric.','Based on the given data, which of the following is a decimal number? I. 2.0 meters II. 4.5 meters III. 3 meters','I only','I and II','II only','II and III','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,23,'Ms. Susi is an event organizer. One day, Ms. Loi booked her for a wedding anniversary event and requested a clothing design using primary colors. Ms. Susi bought 3 meters of blue fabric, 4.5 meters of red fabric, and 2 meters of green fabric.','If Ms. Susi wants to cover the center table with the red fabric three times the given measurement, how many meters will she need?','6.4 meters','9.3 meters','13. 5 meters','22.5 meters','C','Solution: 3 x 4.5 meters = 13.5 meters',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,24,'Ms. Susi is an event organizer. One day, Ms. Loi booked her for a wedding anniversary event and requested a clothing design using primary colors. Ms. Susi bought 3 meters of blue fabric, 4.5 meters of red fabric, and 2 meters of green fabric.','How many meters does Ms. Susi need to buy?','6','7','8.5','9.5','D','Solution: 3 meters + 4.5 meters + 2 meters = 9.5 meters',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,1,25,'Decimal Place Value T H T O D T H T T H H U E N E E U H E U O N N E C N N O N N U D S S I T D U D S R M H R S T R A E A S E A H E N D L D N O D D S S T D U S H T S T S H A H S N O D U T S H A S N D T H S 6 5 4 3 . 3 5 6 4 8','Given: 285. 865, what is the place value of the underlined number?','Tenths','Hundredths','Thousandths','Tenths Thousandths','C','',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,26,NULL,'Using the table above, what is the place value of the underlined digit in the decimal number 43. 7823?','tenths','hundredths','ten thousandths','hundred thousandths','B','','LS3-L1-26.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,27,'Nelson measured a blue ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.538 meters, while Elias measured a green ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.549 meters.','Which digit is in the thousandths place in the length measured by Nelson?','1','3','5','8','D','Given: 1.538 The first digit after the decimal is 5 - tenths The second digit is 3 - hundredths The third digit is 8 - thousandths',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,28,'Nelson measured a blue ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.538 meters, while Elias measured a green ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.549 meters.','Which ribbon is longer based on the digit in the hundredths place?','Nelson’s ribbon, because 8 is greater than 9','Elias’s ribbon, because 9 is greater than 8','Nelson’s ribbon, because 3 is greater than 4','Elias’s ribbon, because 4 is greater than 3','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,29,'Nelson measured a blue ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.538 meters, while Elias measured a green ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.549 meters.','If we compare the ribbons of Nelson and Elias in the hundredths place, which is greater? Why?','Elias, because he has the digit 4 greater place value than digit 3.','Nelson, because he has the digit 5 greater place value than digit 4.','Nelson, because he has the digit 2 in the hundredths place, which is greater than Elias''s digit 4.','Both Elias and Nelson have the same measurement in hundredths place.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,30,'Nelson measured a blue ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.538 meters, while Elias measured a green ribbon for the sash, with a length of 1.549 meters.','What is the place value of the digit 3 in the decimal number 1.538?','Hundredths','Ones','Tenths','Thousandths','A','In 1.538, the first digit after the decimal point (5) is in the tenths place and the second digit (3) is in the hundredths place.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,31,NULL,'What is the equivalent fraction of 4/16?','1/8','1/5','1/4','1/2','C','Divide the numerator and denominator by 4: 4/16 = 1/4.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,32,NULL,'Which of the following fractions is equivalent to 7/14?','1/7','2/7','1/2','7/2','C','Divide both by 7: 7/14 = 1/2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,33,'Pedro colored 3 out of 6 parts of a rectangle.','Which fraction is equivalent to 3/6?','1/3','1/2','5/7','8/24','B','Divide both by 3: 3/6 = 1/2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,34,'Delia has 2,375 stickers in her collection. She bought 1,462 more stickers last week. Then, she gave away 829 stickers to her friends.','How many stickers does Delia have now?','3,008','3,567','3,837','4,108','A','(2,375 +1,462) - 829 = 3 008 So, Delia has 3 008 stickers at present.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,35,'Delia has 2,375 stickers in her collection. She bought 1,462 more stickers last week. Then, she gave away 829 stickers to her friends.','When you combine 2,375 and 1,462, what operation will be used?','Division','Multiplication','Subtraction','Addition','D','We need to add 2,375 and 1,462 to get the number of stickers.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,36,'Rosanna has 6 boxes of pencils, with each box containing 5 pencils. She gives 10 pencils to her mother and divides the rest among her 4 friends.','After giving away 10 pencils to her mother how many pencils were given to each friend?','5','10','15','20','A','Solution 1: We need to multiply 6 × 5 = 30 pencils Solution 2: Subtract 10 pencils from 30 30 – 10 = 20 Then, 20 ÷ 4 = 5 So, 5 pencils were given to each friend.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,37,'Rosanna has 6 boxes of pencils, with each box containing 5 pencils. She gives 10 pencils to her mother and divides the rest among her 4 friends.','How many pencils does Rosanna have in total?','145','156','164','187','B','We need to multiply 6 x 5 = 30 So, Rosanna has 30 pencils',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,38,'Menard wants to buy a school bag that costs PHP 540.60. He has already saved PHP 130.60, and his Ninong gave him PHP 200.00.','What operations to be used to solve the problem?','Addition only','Subtraction','Addition and Subtraction','Addition and Multiplication','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,39,'Menard wants to buy a school bag that costs PHP 540.60. He has already saved PHP 130.60, and his Ninong gave him PHP 200.00.','How much is needed to buy the bag?','PHP 330.60','PHP 375. 30','PHP 430.75','PHP 540.60','A','Given: Bag`s cost = Php 540.60 Menard saved money = Php 130.60 Ninong`s money gaved to Menard = Php 200.00 Solution 1: Addition Php 130.60 + Php 200.00 = Php 330.60 Menard`s money on hand Solution 2: Subtraction Php 540.60 – Php 330.60 = Php 210.00 needed to buy the bag',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,40,NULL,'What is the ratio for the shaded part to the whole rectangle?','7: 8','7:15','8: 15','15: 7','B','7 is the shaded part of a whole. 15 are the equal parts of a whole rectangle.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,41,'The students of Tambo Central School will be going on a field trip to Cagayan de Oro City. Their teacher adviser wants to rent a bus from a certain travel company, and according to the head of the company, a bus can transport 40 people.','How many buses are needed to transport 120 students?','3','4','5','6','A','1:40 = ___ :120 40 = 1 × 120 40n = 120 40 40 n = 3',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,42,'One of the schools in Iligan City conducted a survey and found that 75% of the students prefer online classes. The principal wants to use this data in a computer program that only accepts decimal input.','What is the rule for converting a percent to a decimal?','Divide the percent by 100','Multiply the percent by 100','Add the percent by 100','Subtract the percent by 100','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,43,'One of the schools in Iligan City conducted a survey and found that 75% of the students prefer online classes. The principal wants to use this data in a computer program that only accepts decimal input.','If the school has 100 students, how many students want to have an online class?','25','35','57','75','D','100 x 75% change it to decimal 75% = 0.75 Then multiply: 100 x 0.75 = 75',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,44,'One of the schools in Iligan City conducted a survey and found that 75% of the students prefer online classes. The principal wants to use this data in a computer program that only accepts decimal input.','What is 75% in percent?','0.25','0.50','0.75','0.90','C','To convert a percentage to a decimal, divide the percent by 100 or simply move the decimal point two places to the left.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,45,'During the school field trip, 25 students brought fruits, which accounted for 50% of the students who joined the trip.','What is 50% in fraction form?','1/50','1/5','1/2','2/1','C','50% = 50/100 = 1/2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,46,'Jan is designing a video game level where a ball splits into two smaller balls every time it''s hit.','In exponential notation, how will you define an exponent?','It is the number that is being multiplied repeatedly.','It is the number that is being added repeatedly.','It tells how many times the base is used as a factor.','It tells how many times the exponent is added.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,47,'Jan is designing a video game level where a ball splits into two smaller balls every time it''s hit.','If the ball is hit four times, how many balls will there be in total?','24','20','16','12','C','2⁴ = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 = 16',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,48,'Myrna is decorating cupcakes. She puts the same amount of icing on each cupcake. If she decorated 6 cupcakes and used a total of 60 units of icing, how much icing did she put on each cupcake?','How many units of icing did she put on its cupcake?','6','10','12','15','B','60 ÷ 6 = 10',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,49,'Myrna is decorating cupcakes. She puts the same amount of icing on each cupcake. If she decorated 6 cupcakes and used a total of 60 units of icing, how much icing did she put on each cupcake?','If Myrna added 4 cupcakes, how many units of icing did she put on each cupcake?','6','8','10','12','A','6 + 4 = 10 60 ÷ 10 = 6',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,2,50,'Juan is building a doghouse and has cut three pieces of wood to form a triangle. The lengths of the sides are equal.','What kind of triangle does Juan have?','Equilateral Triangle','Isosceles Triangle','Scalene Triangle','Obtuse Triangle','B','Isosceles Triangle: Two sides are equal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,51,NULL,'Rosalina is constructing a circle graph. She draws a line from the center of the circle straight to the edge. What is twice the length of the line drawn?','Radius','Diameter','Circumference','Chord','B','The diameter is a line segment that passes through center and meets the circumference at the opposite ends.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,52,'Anjielyn is working on her MAPEH project, where she needs to make a small paper flag. She wants the flag to be a rectangle, measuring 6 cm in length and 4 cm in width.','What should Anjielyn use for the task?','Compass','Protractor','Ruler','Measuring Tape','C','Since she only needs to measure a rectangular shape.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,53,NULL,'Miguel wants to measure the volume of his Rubik''s Cube. What is the unit of measurement for finding the volume of a cube?','Square units','Cubic units','Meters','Centimeters','B','Volume is measured in cubic units.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,54,'Sarah has a total of 24 apples and wants to distribute them evenly into 6 baskets. How many apples will each basket contain?','Which step in problem-solving is most important to apply first in solving Sarah’s situation?','Write the final answer','Check if the answer is correct','Understand what is important','Multiply the numbers given','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,55,'Liam is building a garden with three different shapes: a parallelogram, a trapezoid, and a rhombus. He wants to put a fence around each garden, so he needs to calculate the perimeter of each shape. He measured the sides as follows: ● Parallelogram: two sides are 8 meters and the other two are 5 meters. ● Trapezoid: sides are 6 meters, 7 meters, 5 meters, and 4 meters. ● Rhombus: all four sides are 6 meters. ● Rectangle: 2 sides are 6 meters and the other two are 7 meters.','Which shape will require the least length of fencing material?','Parallelogram','Trapezoid','Rhombus','Rectangle','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,56,NULL,'Given a circle with a radius of 6 cm, which of the following shows the correct solution in finding the circumference?','C = 3.14 × (6 cm)²','C = 2 × 3.14 × 6 cm','C = 3.14 × 6 cm','C = (2 × 3.14) ÷ 6','B','Circumference = 2 × π × r = 2 × 3.14 × 6 cm = 37.68 cm.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,57,'Juana is solving problems involving the area of different geometric shapes. She knows that to find the area of each shape, she must first identify the correct types of information (like base, height, side, or diagonals) and then apply the correct area formula. She is given these shapes and dimensions: Triangle: base = 10 cm, height = 8 cm Parallelogram: base = 12 cm, height = 5 cm Trapezoid: base₁ = 10 cm, base₂ = 6 cm, height = 4 cm Rhombus: diagonal₁ = 10 cm, diagonal₂ = 8 cm','Which of the following statements correctly defines the area of the square?','The area is the distance around the outside of the square.','The area is the amount of space inside the square.','The area is the length of one side of the square.','The area is the volume of the square.','B','The area of a shape is defined as the amount of space inside the shape. For a square, the area can be calculated using the formula A= side × side',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,58,'Imagine designing a playground and it is needed to calculate the area of various sections. One section is a composite figure made up of a rectangle and a triangle.','What does the term composite figure mean in this situation?','A figure made up of only one type of shape','A figure that includes both curved and straight lines','A figure formed by combining two or more simple shapes','A figure that cannot be measured using basic formulas','C','A composite figure is a shape that can be divided into multiple simple shapes, such as rectangles and triangles. To verify this definition, you would use: Primary sources like textbooks and academic journals. Secondary sources like educational websites and encyclopedias. Tertiary sources like review articles and summaries.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,59,'Juan is helping to design a new classroom display that shows the relationship between plane and solid figures.','Which of the following correctly matches a plane figure with its corresponding solid figure, and how would Juan explain this match to his classmates? A. Plane Figure: Square Solid Figure: Cube','','','','',NULL,'A square is a plane figure with four equal sides, and a cube is a solid figure with six square faces. B. Plane Figure: Circle Solid Figure: Sphere A circle is a plane figure with all points equidistant from the center, and a sphere is a solid figure where every point on the surface is equidistant from the center. C. Plane Figure: Triangle Solid Figure: Pyramid A triangle is a plane figure with three sides, and a pyramid has a triangular base and triangular faces that meet at a point. D. Plane Figure: Rectangle Solid Figure: Rectangular Prism A rectangle is a plane figure with opposite sides equal, and a rectangular prism has six rectangular faces. Answer: A. Plane Figure: Square Solid Figure: Cube A square is a plane figure with four equal sides, and a cube is a solid figure with six square faces.','LS3-L1-59.png',1,0),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,60,'The ALS teacher gives a task to learners on calculating the area of various shapes as performance output. The following shapes were given: Square Rectangle Circle Triangle','Which of the following correctly matches the shape with its area formula to solve a problem?','Shape: Square To find the area of a square, multiply the length of one side by width.','Shape: Rectangle To find the area of a rectangle, multiply the length of one side by itself.','Shape: Circle To find the area of a circle, multiply pi by twice of the radius.','Shape: Triangle To find the area of a triangle, multiply the base by height and then divide by 2.','D','To find the area of a triangle, multiply the base by the height and then divide by 2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,61,'Surface area refers to the total area that the surface of a three-dimensional object occupies. And given that different shapes have different surface areas based on geometry.','How would you define the surface area of a 3D object?','Surface area is the total volume of a 3D shape.','Surface area is the sum of the areas of all faces of the object.','Surface area is the perimeter of the object multiplied by its height.','Surface area is the area of the base of the shape multiplied by its height.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,62,'Juana is reading an online article where a community elder describes using the length of a forearm to measure cloth instead of using meters.','What is the most appropriate description of this type of measurement?','It is a universal scientific method used in modern construction.','It is an example of a non-standard or indigenous measurement system.','It is inaccurate and has no value in today’s society.','It is a metric measurement system recognized globally.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,63,'While researching online, Ruth finds a blog that says, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','Based on your understanding of 3D shapes, how should you evaluate this statement?','The statement is incorrect because cubes have more vertices than rectangular prisms.','The statement is incorrect because cubes have fewer faces than rectangular prisms.','The statement is correct because both shapes have 6 faces, 12 edges, and 8 vertices.','The statement is only true for rectangular prisms that are also spheres.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,64,'While researching online, Ruth finds a blog that says, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','She wants to understand the volume of these shapes. What is the first thing she needs to know?','The definition of volume as the space an object occupies.','How to count the number of faces and edges.','The material used to make the shapes.','Whether the shapes are the same color.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,65,'An ALS learner is riding his bicycle to the community learning center. On the way, he notices that his ride feels slower and more difficult. He stops to check the tire pressure using a small pressure gauge. The gauge reads 20 psi, while the recommended pressure written on the tire is 35 psi.','What is the most important reason to read and record the pressure?','To prove that the tire is the most expensive part of the bike.','To make sure the tire has enough air for safe and smooth riding.','To compare the color of the tire with other bikes.','To avoid using the bike altogether.','B','Reading and recording air pressure helps you decide if a tire is properly inflated. That’s using evidence (the pressure reading) to support a basic real-world argument whether it’s safe to ride or if the tire needs more air. This fits the Unistructural level because it checks understanding of one essential use.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,66,'The ALS teacher asked the learners to record their home’s electricity and water usage.','After recording the previous and present meter readings for electricity and water, what should the learner do next to determine the actual consumption?','Add the previous and present readings together','Multiply the previous reading by the present reading','Subtract the previous reading from the present reading','Divide the present reading by the previous reading','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,67,'The ALS teacher asked the learners to record their home’s electricity and water usage.','Given the previous month water reading is 1973 m3 and present water reading is given in the figure below: How many cubic meters of water was consumed?','38 m3','83 m3','1973 m3','2011 m3','A','Subtract the previous reading from the present reading: 2011 m3 − 1979 m3 = 38 m3','LS3-L1-67.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,68,'In the peaceful town of Kalilangan, Bukidnon, paying electric bills used to be very hard. But in January, a solar project called “Solar sa Tagbungtod” was started by the barangay. By March, families got solar panels, and by April, everyone learned how to use electricity better, turning off lights, charging devices during the day, and saving energy. Every month, the electric bill got lower, as shown in the graph. By December, the town had a night market lit up only by solar lamps—a sign of saving money, helping the environment, and a brighter future.\n\nThe graph below shows the electric consumption of the town.','What information does the graph provide about Kalilangan’s electric consumption?','The total electric consumption for each month','The trend in electric consumption over the months','The comparison of electric consumption between different months','The highest and lowest points of electric consumption','B','','LS3-L1-68.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,69,'In 2022, 320 learners enrolled ALS in Magandang Buhay. They wanted to learn and finish school. In 2023, more people enrolled, 410 learners. They told their friends and family how fun learning was. By 2024, the number grew to 540 learners. The classrooms were full of happy learners, ready to reach their dreams. Each year, the number got bigger, showing that more people believe in the power of education!','Which of the following statement is true? I. The number of ALS learners decreased in 2023. II. The number of ALS learners increased every year. III. In 2024, there were fewer learners than in 2022','I only','II only','I and III','II and III','B','Looking at the data, in 2022 - 320 learners, 2023 - 410 learners, and 2024 - 540 learners, it is increasing.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,70,'The Malipayon family lives in a small, happy home. Every month, they spend money on the things they need. Mama says, “We need to spend wisely, children!” Most of their money goes to food PHP 6,000.00 each month! “We eat healthy to stay strong,” says Papa. For electricity, they spend PHP 1,200.00, but they always turn off lights to save. They use PHP 500.00 for water and PHP 1,000.00 for transportation like riding the jeep to school and work. The kids need PHP 800.00 for school needs such as notebooks, pencils, and projects. By planning and tracking their expenses, the Malipayon family stays happy and prepared every month. “Being smart with money helps us live well,” says Ate Joy with a smile.','What does a pie graph help us understand?','How loud different sounds are','How to bake a pie step by step','How parts make up a whole','How fast a car can go','C','In this context, a pie graph helps us understand how the different parts (or categories) make up a complete whole. The chart shows how much each category contributes to the whole part.','LS3-L1-70.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,71,'The Malipayon family lives in a small, happy home. Every month, they spend money on the things they need. Mama says, “We need to spend wisely, children!” Most of their money goes to food PHP 6,000.00 each month! “We eat healthy to stay strong,” says Papa. For electricity, they spend PHP 1,200.00, but they always turn off lights to save. They use PHP 500.00 for water and PHP 1,000.00 for transportation like riding the jeep to school and work. The kids need PHP 800.00 for school needs such as notebooks, pencils, and projects. By planning and tracking their expenses, the Malipayon family stays happy and prepared every month. “Being smart with money helps us live well,” says Ate Joy with a smile.','What does each slice of a pie graph usually represent?','A timeline of historical events','A list of step-by-step instructions','A measurement of length and width','A part or category of the total information','D','A pie graph is a circular chart divided into slices, where each slice shows a part or category of the whole. These slices represent different data values or percentages that add up to 100%. Each slice gives a visual representation of how much that category contributes to the total.','LS3-L1-71.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,72,'Lila has a bag with 5 red marbles, 3 blue marbles, and 2 green marbles. She closes her eyes and picks one marble from the bag without looking.','What does probability tell us?','How fast something moves','How likely something is to happen','How much something weighs','How many steps are in a process','B','Probability is the measure of the chance that an event will happen. It doesn''t tell us how fast or heavy something is it just tells us how likely it is.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,73,'Lila has a bag with 5 red marbles, 3 blue marbles, and 2 green marbles. She closes her eyes and picks one marble from the bag without looking.','Which color marble is Lila most likely to pick?','Red','Blue','Green','All are equally likely','A','Because there are more red marbles (5) than blue (3) or green (2). So, the probability or chance of picking a red marble is higher.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,74,'An ALS learner roll a fair six-sided die. The die has the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 on its faces.','Which part of the information tells us how many possible outcomes there are when rolling the die?','The number on each side of the die','The total number of faces on the die','The speed at which the die is rolled','The color of the die','B','The total number of faces on the die (6 faces) is what gives us the total number of possible outcomes when we roll it. The other parts of the information, like the numbers or color, are not necessary to find the total outcomes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',1,3,75,'An ALS learner roll a fair six-sided die. The die has the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 on its faces.','If the learner rolls the die once, what is the total number of possible outcomes?','2','4','6','12','C','The die has 6 faces, and each face represents a different possible outcome (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6). So, the total number of possible outcomes when rolling the die is 6.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,1,'Maria has 3 times as many apples as Tomas. Together, they have 48 apples. How many apples does each person have?','Which of the following best describes the correct steps to solve this word problem?','1. Guess how many apples Tomas has 2. Add a random number for Maria 3. Check if the total is 48 4. Keep guessing until it works','1. Solve the equation right away 2. Make up numbers to test 3. Write the answer 4. Explain only if it''s wrong','1. Understand the problem: Identify who has what and the total 2. Make a plan: Let Tomas be x, then Maria is 3x, set up the equation x + 3x = 48 3. Solve the problem: 4x = 48, so x = 12 4. Check your answer: Tomas has 12, Maria has 36, and 12 + 36 = 48','1. Check the answer first 2. Write an equation 3. Solve it 4. Understand the problem last','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,2,'A coconut factory produced 235,784 coconut milk pack in January and 189,456 coconut milk pack in February. In March, 98,732 coconut milk pack were returned due to factory defects.','How many coconut milk packs were successfully produced in total over the three months? What is the total number of coconut milk packs successfully produced after subtracting the returned ones?','423,240','326,508','524,209','426, 680','B','1. Add January and February production: 235,784 + 189,456 = 425,240 2. Subtract the returned toys from March: 425,240 − 98,732 = 326,508',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,3,'Diding baked 248 Bagumbayan cookies for a school bake sale. She sold 175 Bagumbayan cookies. How many Bagumbayan cookies does she have left?','Which of the following best shows the correct steps for solving this word problem?','1. Write a number sentence 2. Check your answer 3. Guess the numbers 4. Solve with any operation','1. Solve the problem right away 2. Write any subtraction problem 3. Pick the answer that looks best 4. Check with a calculator','1. Understand the problem: What do you know? Diding had 248 Bagumbayan cookies and sold 175. 2. Make a plan: Use subtraction to find out how many are left. 3. Solve the problem: 248 − 175 = 73 4. Check your answer: Add 73 + 175 to see if you get 248','1. Check the answer first 2. Choose a random number 3. Subtract or add for fun 4. Think later','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,4,'A factory packs 128 boxes of Pinyato delicacies every day. How many Pinyato delicacies does the factory pack in 36 days?','How many Pinyato delicacies are packed after 36 days?','4,608','4,368','4,096','3,928','A','128 boxes × 36 days = 4,608 packs',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,5,NULL,'Given expression: 4 + 6 x (3 + 2) ÷ 5 − 3. Which of the following statements explain how the MDAS and GMDAS rules guide solving mathematical expressions?','MDAS and GMDAS are the same; you always solve from left to right regardless of the operation.','MDAS means multiplication and division come first, then addition and subtraction; GMDAS adds grouping symbols like parentheses, which are solved before any other operation.','GMDAS is only used when there are fractions, while MDAS is used for whole numbers.','In MDAS, you solve addition before multiplication, and in GMDAS, subtraction comes before grouping.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,6,NULL,'Simplify the expression 8 + (6 ÷ 2 × 3) − 4.','9','11','13','14','C','Grouping symbols first: 6 ÷ 2 = 3, 3 × 3 = 9 Now the expression is: 8+9−4 Addition and Subtraction (left to right): 8 + 9 =17 17 – 4 =13',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,7,'A 5th-grade learner was asked to differentiate between a prime number and a composite number.','Which of the following statements by a 5th-grade learner correctly describes the difference between a prime number and a composite number?','A prime number is divisible by only two numbers, while a composite number is divisible by two numbers.','A prime number has exactly two factors: 1 and itself, while a composite number has more than two factors.','A prime number is always an odd number, while a composite number is always even.','A prime number is larger than a composite number.','B','A prime number is a number greater than 1 that has exactly two factors - 1 and itself. Examples: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 A composite number is a number greater than 1 that has more than two factors. Examples: 4 (factors: 1, 2, 4), 6 (factors: 1, 2, 3, 6), 9, 12',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,8,'A 5th-grade learner was asked to differentiate between a prime number and a composite number.','Which of the following shows the correct prime factorization of 36?','2, 3, 6','2,3,2','2, 2, 3, 3','1, 2, 3, 6','C','To find the prime factors of 36, we break the number down into a product of prime numbers only. 1. Start with 36: 36 ÷ 2 = 18 (2 is a prime number) 2. Continue dividing18 ÷ 2 = 9 (again, 2 is a prime) 3. Now divide by 3 (the next smallest prime): 9÷3=3 4. Finally: 3 ÷ 3 = 1 So, the prime factorization of 36 is: 36 = 2 × 2 × 3 × 3',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,9,'A 5th-grade learner was asked to differentiate between a prime number and a composite number.','Which of the following sets are multiples of 8?','8, 16, 24, 32','8,15,22,30','4, 8, 12, 18','10, 18, 26, 34','A','These numbers are all multiples of 8, meaning they can be evenly divided by 8 with no remainder: • 8 ÷ 8 = 18 ÷ 8 = 1 • 16 ÷ 8 = 216 ÷ 8 = 2 • 24 ÷ 8 = 324 ÷ 8 = 3 • 32 ÷ 8 = 432 ÷ 8 = 4',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,10,'Mrs. Bagtong gave her students the number 60 and asked them to find its factors using different methods. Glenda listed all the factor pairs, Pablo used prime factorization, and Carlos used continuous division.','Which of the following correctly matches each method with what the student did?','● Glenda: Prime factorization ● Pablo: Continuous division ● Carlos: Listing','● Glenda: Listing ● Pablo: Prime factorization ● Carlo: Continuous division','● Glenda: Continuous division ● Pablo: Listing ● Carlos: Prime factorization','● Glenda: Prime factorization ● Pablo: Listing ● Carlos: Continuous division','B','Glenda: Listing → She finds all factor pairs of 60 (e.g., 1×60, 2×30, 3×20, 4×15, 5×12, 6×10) Pablo: Prime factorization → He writes 60 as a product of primes: 2 × 2 × 3 × 5 Carlos: Continuous division → He divides 60 by primes step-by-step until reaching 1',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,11,'Mylene was given two numbers: 24 and 36. She was asked to find their common factors and the greatest common factor (GCF) using three different methods: listing, prime factorization, and continuous division.','Which of the following correctly matches each method with Mylene''s approach to finding the common factors and the GCF?','Listing – Wrote down all the factors of 24 and 36. Prime Factorization – Found the prime factors of 24 and 36, then identified the GCF. Continuous Division – Divided 24 and 36 by common prime factors until the remainder was 1.','Listing – Wrote down all the factors of 24 and 36. Prime Factorization – Found the prime factors of 24 and 36, then identified the common factors. Continuous Division – Divided 24 and 36 by common prime factors until 1 was reached, then found the GCF.','Listing – Found the prime factors of 24 and 36. Prime Factorization – Wrote down all the factors of 24 and 36. Continuous Division – Divided 24 and 36 by common prime factors to find the GCF.','Listing – Wrote down the prime factors of 24 and 36. Prime Factorization – Wrote down all the factors of 24 and 36. Continuous Division – Divided by the smallest prime factor until the GCF was found.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,12,'Ramon is checking if 120 is divisible by 2, 3, 4, and 5. She remembers that each number has its own rule to test for divisibility.','Which of the following explanations best shows her understanding of how to apply these rules?','A number is divisible: by 2 if the last digit is 0 or 5; by 3 if the digit is multiple of 3; by 4 if it the last digit is 0; and by 5 if it is even number.','A number is divisible: by 2 if the last digit is even; by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3; by 4 if the last two digits is divisible by 4; and by 5 if the last digit is 0 or 5.','A number is divisible: by 2 if it is composed of two digits; by 3 if the last digit is 3; by 4 if it is even number; and by 5 if the sum of digits is 5.','A number is divisible: by 2 if the last digit is 2; by 3 if it is odd number; by 4 if the last digit is 4; and by 5 if it is more than 50.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,13,'Julito is checking if the number 360 is divisible by several numbers. He decides to apply the divisibility rules for 2, 5, and 10; 3, 6, and 9; 4, 8, and 12; and 7 and 11.','Which of the following correctly explains whether 360 is divisible by each group of numbers and why?','● 2, 5, 10: Yes, because 360 ends in 0 ● 3, 6, 9: Yes, because 3 + 6 + 0 = 9 (divisible by 3 and 9) and it''s even (divisible by 6) ● 4, 8, 12: No, because it doesn’t end in 8 or 12 ● 7 and 11: Yes, because it ends in 0 and is even','● 2, 5, 10: Yes, because 360 ends in 0 ● 3, 6, 9: Yes, because the sum of digits is 9 and it’s divisible by both 3 and 6 ● 4, 8, 12: Yes, because 60 is divisible by all three ● 7 and 11: No, because it is not divisible evenly by 7 or 11','● 2, 5, 10: No, because 360 is not odd ● 3, 6, 9: No, because 9 is not a factor of 360 ● 4, 8, 12: Yes, because it ends in 0 ● 7 and 11: Yes, because it is greater than 100','● 2, 5, 10: Yes, because it ends in a multiple of 5 ● 3, 6, 9: No, because only 3 is a factor of 360 ● 4, 8, 12: Yes, because 36 is divisible by 4 ● 7 and 11: Yes, because it has an even number of digits','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,14,'Berto is organizing a set of fractions into groups: proper fractions, improper fractions, and mixed numbers.','Which of the following statements best shows a clear understanding of how to differentiate them?','A proper fraction has a larger numerator than the denominator; an improper fraction has a denominator larger than the numerator; and a mixed number is a whole number only.','A proper fraction has a numerator smaller than the denominator; an improper fraction has a numerator equal to or greater than the denominator; a mixed number has a whole number and a proper fraction.','A proper fraction includes a whole number and a fraction; an improper fraction is always equal to 1; and a mixed number has two fractions.','A proper fraction and an improper fraction are the same; a mixed number is the result of adding two improper fractions.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,15,'Perlita is baking cookies. The recipe calls for 2 1/4 cups of flour. She only has a measuring cup marked in fourths, so she decides to convert the mixed number into an improper fraction. Later, her friend Lando measures 11/4 cups of sugar and wants to know how many whole cups that is.','Which of the following correctly shows the conversions they each need?','Perlita should write 2 1/4 as 6/4; Lando should write 11/4 as 2 3/4.','Perlita should write 2 1/4 as 9/4; Lando should write 11/4 as 2 3/4.','Perlita should write 2 1/4 as 8/4; Lando should write 11/4 as 3 1/4.','Perlita should write 2 1/4 as 10/4; Lando should write 11/4 as 2 2/4.','B','2 1/4 = (2 × 4 + 1)/4 = 9/4. 11 ÷ 4 = 2 remainder 3, so 11/4 = 2 3/4.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,16,NULL,'Lita is learning about equivalent fractions and is trying to find fractions that are equal to 1/2. She knows that fractions can be written in different forms but represent the same value. Which of the following sets correctly illustrates fractions that are equivalent to 1/2?','2/3, 4/6, 3/5','1/2, 2/4, 4/8','1/3, 3/6, 5/10','1/4, 3/6, 5/7','B','1/2 = 2/4 = 4/8, because each numerator is half of its denominator.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,17,'Marta bakes cookies and needs to measure ingredients in fractions. She needs 3/4 cup of sugar and 1/4 cup of flour. She accidentally poured the sugar and flour into the same bowl.','How much of the ingredients did Marta pour in total?','3/4 + 1/4 = 4/4','3/4 + 1/4 = 1/2','3/4 + 1/4 = 5/4','3/4 + 1/4 = 6/4','A','Same denominators: add the numerators. 3/4 + 1/4 = 4/4, which is 1 whole cup.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,18,NULL,'Lope has 7/8 of a chocolate bar. He decides to eat 3/8 of it. How much of the chocolate bar is left after he eats the 3/8?','7/8 − 3/8 = 1 1/4','7/8 − 3/8 = 1/2','7/8 − 3/8 = 5/8','7/8 − 3/8 = 2/8','B','7/8 − 3/8 = 4/8, and 4/8 in lowest terms is 1/2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,19,'Eva is making a fruit salad and uses fractions to measure the ingredients. She first adds 3/5 cup of banana, then adds 2/5 cup of avocado. After mixing, she decides to remove 1/5 cup of avocado because she added too much.','How much fruit is in the salad now?','3/5 + 2/5 − 1/5 = 4/5','3/5 + 2/5 − 1/5 = 6/5','3/5 + 2/5 − 1/5 = 5/5','3/5 + 2/5 − 1/5 = 2/5','A','3/5 + 2/5 = 5/5, then 5/5 − 1/5 = 4/5 cup.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,20,NULL,'Susan is working on a math assignment and needs to find fractions equivalent to 3/4. She tries a few different methods. Which of the following sets of fractions correctly shows fractions equivalent to 3/4?','6/8, 9/12, 12/16','2/5, 5/10, 7/8','4/6, 6/9, 8/12','3/5, 6/7, 9/11','A','Multiply 3/4 by 2/2, 3/3, and 4/4: 6/8, 9/12, 12/16.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,21,NULL,'Susing is preparing a recipe that requires 1/3 cup of sugar and 2/5 cup of flour. She wants to combine the ingredients but needs to convert the fractions to have a common denominator. What is the least common denominator (LCD) for 1/3 and 2/5?','3','5','15','8','C','The smallest number that both 3 and 5 divide into is 15.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,22,NULL,'Berta is comparing two fractions, 2/3 and 4/5, to add them together. To add them, she needs to convert both fractions to have a common denominator. What are the equivalent fractions for 2/3 and 4/5 with the same denominator?','2/3 = 6/9, 4/5 = 12/15','2/3 = 10/15, 4/5 = 12/15','2/3 = 4/6, 4/5 = 8/10','2/3 = 5/15, 4/5 = 6/15','B','The LCD is 15. 2/3 = 10/15 and 4/5 = 12/15.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,23,'Rovina makes a fruit salad and needs to add different amounts of ingredients. She has 2/3 cup of tapioca and 3/4 cup of mango. She wants to know the total amount of ingredients in her salad.','What is the total amount of ingredients in the salad?','2/3 + 3/4 = 10/12','2/3 + 3/4 = 17/12','2/3 + 3/4 = 5/7','2/3 + 3/4 = 13/12','B','LCD 12: 2/3 = 8/12 and 3/4 = 9/12. 8/12 + 9/12 = 17/12 (or 1 5/12) cups.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,24,'Joel is making a recipe that requires 5/6 cup of flour. However, he accidentally used 2/3 cup of flour.','How much more flour does Joel need?','1/3','3/6','1/2','1/6','D','2/3 = 4/6. 5/6 − 4/6 = 1/6 cup more.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,1,25,'Carol bakes cookies and needs to measure the ingredients in fractions. She adds 2/5 cup of sugar, then 3/4 cup of flour. After mixing, she decides to remove 1/2 cup of flour because she used too much.','How much of the ingredients does she have left?','2/5 + 3/4 − 1/2 = 31/20','2/5 + 3/4 − 1/2 = 13/20','2/5 + 3/4 − 1/2 = 7/20','2/5 + 3/4 − 1/2 = 17/20','B','LCD 20: 8/20 + 15/20 − 10/20 = 13/20 cup.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,26,NULL,'Carmen makes batches of muffins. Each batch requires 3/4 cup of milk. She has 2 1/4 cups of milk. How many full batches can she make using all the milk?','2 1/4 ÷ 3/4 = 3','2 1/4 ÷ 3/4 = 4','2 1/4 ÷ 3/4 = 2 1/2','2 1/4 ÷ 3/4 = 3 1/4','A','2 1/4 = 9/4. 9/4 ÷ 3/4 = 9/4 × 4/3 = 3 batches.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,27,NULL,'Kulas baked a pie and ate 6 out of 12 equal slices. He wants to express the fraction of the pie he ate in simplest form. Which of the following shows the correct simplified fraction?','6/12 = 2/4','6/12 = 1/2','6/12 = 3/4','6/12 = 1/3','B','Divide both by 6: 6/12 = 1/2. (2/4 is equal, but it is not in simplest form.)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,28,NULL,'Roberto is doubling a recipe that calls for 1 3/5 cups of milk. Before multiplying, he wants to change the mixed number into an improper fraction. Which of the following is the correct improper fraction for 1 3/5?','6/5','7/5','8/5','9/5','C','1 3/5 = (1 × 5 + 3)/5 = 8/5.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,29,NULL,'Juan is building a bookshelf and measures one of the wooden planks to be 2 2/3 feet long. Before calculating how many planks he can fit in a space, he wants to convert the measurement to an improper fraction. What is the correct improper fraction form of 2 2/3?','5/3','6/3','7/3','8/3','D','2 2/3 = (2 × 3 + 2)/3 = 8/3.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,30,NULL,'Darna prepared 18 sandwiches for a school event. She served 12 of them to her classmates. What fraction of the sandwiches were served, and what is this fraction in its lowest term?','12/18 = 2/3','12/18 = 3/4','12/18 = 4/5','12/18 = 1/2','A','12/18: divide both by 6 to get 2/3.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,31,'A recipe for banana bread calls for 1 1/2 cups of flour. Marco wants to make 2 2/3 batches of banana bread. How much flour does he need in total?','Which of the following steps correctly show how to find the total amount of flour needed?','Convert both to improper fractions and multiply: 1 1/2 = 3/2, 2 2/3 = 8/3; 3/2 × 8/3 = 24/6 = 4','Multiply whole numbers only: 1 × 2 = 2, then add the fractions separately','Add 1 1/2 and 2 2/3, then multiply the result by 2','Multiply the numerators and add the denominators: 1 1/2 × 2 2/3 = 3/8 × 8/3','A','Change mixed numbers to improper fractions, then multiply: 3/2 × 8/3 = 24/6 = 4 cups.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,32,NULL,'Which of the following word problems best illustrates a situation that requires both multiplication and division of fractions to solve?','Ava baked 3/4 of a cake and then ate 1/2 of it. How much of the whole cake did she eat?','A container holds 2 1/2 liters of juice. If each glass holds 1/4 liter, how many glasses can be filled?','A farmer has 2/3 of a field planted with vegetables. He wants to plant carrots on 3/5 of that area. How much of the whole field will be planted with carrots?','Ava has 2 1/4 meters of ribbon. She cuts it into pieces, each 3/8 meter long. How many pieces can she make, and if she only uses 2/3 of the pieces, how many will be used?','D','D needs division (2 1/4 ÷ 3/8 = 6 pieces) and then multiplication (2/3 × 6 = 4 pieces).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,33,NULL,'Sopia is shopping for fabric to make curtains. She needs 12.725 meters of fabric. How would you describe the place value of each digit in the decimal number 12.725?','The 1 is in the ones place, the 2 is in the tens place, the 7 is in the hundredths place, the 2 is in the thousandths place, and the 5 is in the tenths place.','The 1 is in the tens place, the 2 is in the ones place, the 7 is in the tenths place, the 2 is in the thousandths place, and the 5 is in the hundredths place.','The 1 is in the tens place, the 2 is in the ones place, the 7 is in the tenths place, the 2 is in the hundredths place, and the 5 is in the thousandths place.','The 1 is in the hundredths place, the 2 is in the tens place, the 7 is in the ones place, the 2 is in the thousandths place, and the 5 is in the tenths place.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,34,NULL,'Olivia is measuring the length of a table for a new project. She measures the length to be 4 meters and 56 centimeters. Which of the following decimal numbers correctly represents the length of the table to the hundredths place?','4.056 m','4.56 m','4.0056 m','4.565 m','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,35,NULL,'David is comparing the lengths of two ropes to determine which one is longer. The first rope is 5.78 meters long, and the second rope is 5.89 meters long. Which of the following is true about the comparison of the two lengths?','The first rope is longer than the second rope.','The second rope is longer than the first rope.','The lengths of both ropes are the same.','The second rope is shorter than the first rope.','B','Step-by-step: Look at the whole number part of both measurements: Both ropes start with 5 meters - so they are the same so far. Now compare the decimal part (the numbers after the dot): First rope: .78 Second rope: .89 Let’s compare 78 and 89 (just like whole numbers): 89 is bigger than 78 That means 5.89 meters is longer than 5.78 meters.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,36,NULL,'John is comparing the amounts of flour in three different bags. The amounts of flour in the bags are: 3.75 kg, 3.57 kg, and 3.85 kg. Arrange these amounts in ascending order (from least to greatest).','3.57 kg, 3.75 kg, 3.85 kg','3.75 kg, 3.57 kg, 3.85 kg','3.85 kg, 3.57 kg, 3.75 kg','3.75 kg, 3.85 kg, 3.57 kg','A','Step-by-step comparison: 1. Compare 3.75 kg and 3.57 kg → 3.57 kg is less than 3.75 kg 2. Compare 3.75 kg and 3.85 kg → 3.75 kg is less than 3.85 kg 3. Compare 3.57 kg and 3.85 kg → 3.57 kg is less than 3.85 kg Final order from least to greatest: 3.57 kg, 3.75 kg, 3.85 kg',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,37,'Plot the following decimal numbers on a number line: 2.315, 2.401, and 2.298.','Which of the following shows the correct order of these numbers on the number line from least to greatest value?','2.315, 2.298, 2.401','2.401, 2.315, 2.298','2.298, 2.315, 2.401','2.315, 2.401, 2.298','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,38,'Rejean is making ice candy. She measured 1.5389 liters of milk, but her recipe only needs the amount rounded to the nearest thousandth.','How much milk should she write down in her recipe after rounding??','1. 5 L','1.54 L','1.539 L','1.5389 L','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,39,NULL,'Nelson is preparing for a competition. He monitors his daily running distance. On Monday, he ran 5.6789 kilometers. He wishes to note his distance to the nearest thousandths in his training record. What should he note?','5.676 km','5.677 km','5.678 km','5.679 km','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,40,NULL,'Narcisa went to a store and bought 3 chocolates at ₱ 2.50 each. Is the total cost of chocolates a terminating decimal? Why?','Yes, because the total cost ends after three digits','Yes, because the total cost does not end after three digits','No, because the total cost does not end after three digits','No, because the total cost ends after three digits.','A','Multiply the price per kilogram by the number of kilograms: Total cost =3.75 × 2.50 =9.375 The decimal ends after three digits (0.375). Therefore, 9.375 is a terminating decimal. !',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,41,NULL,'Donina made a cake. She consumed 1/4 of the entire cake and left the rest of the cake for her sister. What decimal represents the remaining part of the cake?','0.25','0.50','0.75','0.90','C','1 − 1/4 = 3/4 = 0.75.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,42,'Alma bought 1.75 kilos of Sayote that cost PHP 75.00 per kilo and 2. 50 kilos of carrots that cost PHP 60.00 per kilo. How much did Alma pay for Sayote and Carrots?','In adding decimals, what is the first step that you will do?','Add zeros if needed','Add numbers from right to left','Write the decimal numbers in column','Place the decimal point in the answer','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,43,NULL,'Ramon saved ₱289.70 in November and spent ₱117.55 on a gift for his mother in December. How much of his savings were left?','PHP172.15','PHP162.20','PHP157.25','PHP112.30','A','Since the problem asking for What was left so, we need to subtract (apply the rule of subtracting decimal numbers) PHP 6.10 PHP 289.70 - PHP 117.55 PHP 172.15 Answer: Ramon has the remaining money of ₱172.15 after buying her mother a gift.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,44,'Ronnie saves PHP 12.50 daily from his allowance. How much will his money be after 2 weeks?','Which of the following equation represents the statement above?','PHP 12.50 + 7 = n','PHP 12.50 – 7 = n','PHP 12.50 x 14 = n','PHP 12. 50 ÷ 14 = n','C','Since we need to get his total saving for 2 weeks Knowing that in 1 week is equal to 7 days so, 2 x 7 =14 days since Ronnie saves 12.50 daily so we will multiply 12.50 x 14 = n',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,45,'Mang Carlos bought 3.5 kilograms of santol to make a jam. He wants to divide the santol equally into jars, with each jar holding 0.3 kilograms of santol.','What is the first step in finding the quotient of a decimal number?','Divide immediately the decimal','Move the decimal point to the right in both the divisor and the dividend to make the divisor a whole number.','Place the decimal point in the answer directly above its position in the dividend.','Put zeros after dividing the decimals.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,46,NULL,'Richella bought 9.216 meters of cloth to make potholder. If she uses 0.512 meters in each cloth, how many potholders she is able to make?','20','18','16','14','B','To find out how many potholders Richella can make, divide the total meters of cloth by the two meters of cloth used per potholder: 9.216 ÷ 0.512 = 18 So, there are 18 potholders that Richella can make',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,47,'Noel bought 2.5 kg of fish at PHP 138.50 a kilo, 3 packs of butter at PHP 35.50 each. He has PHP 750.00. How much was left of his money?','Which equation will solve the problem?','PHP 750.00 - [ (2.5 x PHP 138.50) + (3 x PHP 35.50) + (3 x PHP 32.75)} = N','PHP 750.00 - [ (2.5 + PHP 138.50) + (3 + PHP 35.50) + (3 + PHP 32.75)} = N','PHP 750.00 + [ (2.5 x PHP 138.50) + (3 x PHP 35.50) + (3 x PHP 32.75)} = N','PHP 750.00 - [ (2.5 x PHP 138.50) x (3 x PHP 35.50) x (3 x PHP 32.75)} = N','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,48,'Mr. Escoto mixes 2 liters of syrup with 6 liters of water to make fruit juice. He wants to make larger batches using the same ratio. As shown in the table below:\n\nBatch Syrup Water Total 1 2 6 8 2 4 12 16 3 6 18 24','What is the ratio of syrup to the water?','1:3','1:4','1:5','1:6','A','The ratio: 2:6 by simplying It becomes 1:3 The ratio 1:3 is maintained in every batch. If you double the syrup, you also double the water.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,49,NULL,'If 200 men can do a job in 10 days, how many men can do it in 25 days?','100','90','80','70','C','This is inverse proportion: men × days stays the same. 200 × 10 = 2,000. 2,000 ÷ 25 = 80 men.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,2,50,NULL,'Maribel''s Boutique is offering a 12.5% discount. What is the decimal and fraction form of the discount?','0.125, 1/8','1.25, 1/6','0.25, 1/4','0.36, 1/5','A','12.5% = 12.5 ÷ 100 = 0.125 = 125/1000 = 1/8.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,51,NULL,'Willy want to buy a phone that costs PHP 8000.00, but there''s a 15% discount on it. How much will he pay for the phone after the discount?','PHP 6,700.00','PHP 6,800.00','PHP 6,900.00','PHP 7,000.00','B','Original Price: PHP 8000 Discount Percentage: 15% (or 0.15 as a decimal) Discount Amount: PHP1,200 Final Price After Discount: PHP 6,800',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,52,NULL,'Alona is saving money to buy a new laptop. On her first day of saving, she saved PHP 5.00. On the second day, she saved PHP 10.00, and on the third day, she saved PHP 15.00. Each day, she increases the amount of money she saves by PHP 5.00. How much will she have saved by the 6th day?','PHP 60.00','PHP 90.00','PHP 100.00','PHP 105.00','D','Pattern: The amount of money saved increases by 5 each day. Rule: The amount saved on Day n is 5×n Total Saved by Day 6: 105',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,53,NULL,'Marvilyn designs a triangle garden with all sides measuring 5 meters. What kind of triangle is this based on the sides?','Scalene','Isosceles','Equilateral','Right','C','An equilateral triangle has all three sides equal. Since all sides are 5 meters, it is equilateral.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,54,NULL,'Alvin designs a triangular garden, one triangle design has angles measuring 90°, 45°, and 45°. What type of triangle is this based on its angles?','Acute','Obtuse','Right','Equilateral','C','A right triangle has one angle that measures exactly 90°. Since one angle is 90°, it is a right triangle.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,55,'Roger is helping his parents choose tiles to decorate their new patio floor. The store has tiles in various shapes like squares, rectangles, trapezoids, parallelograms, and rhombuses. Roger wants to understand the differences between these quadrilaterals to make the best design.','Roger sees a tile that has four equal sides and four right angles. Which type of quadrilateral is this?','Rhombus','Rectangle','Square','Trapezoid','C','A square has four equal sides and four right angles. A rhombus has equal sides but not necessarily right angles, and a rectangle has right angles but not certainly equal sides.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,56,NULL,'What is the midpoint of a circle?','The point that is equally distant from all points on the circle','The line that touches only one point on the circle','The longest distance across the circle','The curved line around the circle','A','The center is the immovable point inside a circle from which all points on the circle are the same distance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,57,NULL,'Why is it significant to use the right measuring tools in real-life situations like construction, cooking, or tailoring?','Measuring tools are only used for decoration','It helps guess the approximate size of objects','Measuring tools are not important in daily life','It ensures accuracy, safety, and quality in tasks','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,58,NULL,'Which should Pinky use to measure the length and width of a piece of wood?','Protractor','Measuring tape','Compass','Stopwatch','B','A measuring tape is flexible and ideal for measuring the length and width of longer or curved surfaces, like pieces of wood.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,59,NULL,'Which of the following is the correct equivalent value of 2 kilometer (km)?','100 meters','10 meters','2,000 meters','100,000 meters','C','1 kilometer = 1,000 meters This is part of the metric system, which is based on powers of 10',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,60,'Sarah has a total of 24 apples and wants to distribute them evenly among 6 baskets. How many apples will each basket contain?','To solve the problem, Sarah wrote the mathematical sentence: 24 ÷ 6 =? She also wants to explain her answer clearly using a real-life context that involves conversion of units. Which of the following best shows how Sarah could communicate her solution using correct reasoning and a conversion?','“Each basket will get 4 apples. If 1 apple weighs about 250 grams, then each basket will hold 1 kilogram of apples, because 250g × 4 = 1000g = 1kg.”','“Each basket will have 6 apples, because 6 × 6 = 36 and that is more than 24.”','“Each basket will get 3 apples. If 1 apple takes 200 milliliters of space, then each basket will have 600 milliliters of apples.”','“Each basket will get 4 apples, but since Sarah started with 30 apples, 6 would be left out.”','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,61,'Liam is building a garden with three different shapes: a parallelogram, a trapezoid, and a rhombus. He wants to put a fence around each garden, so he needs to calculate the perimeter of each shape. He measured the sides as follows: • Parallelogram: two sides are 8 meters and the other two are 5 meters. • Trapezoid: sides are 6 meters, 7 meters, 5 meters, and 4 meters. • Rhombus: all four sides are 6 meters','Which of the following shows the correct method and perimeter calculation for each shape?','● Parallelogram: P = 2 × (8 + 5) = 26 meters ● Trapezoid: P = 6 + 7 + 5 + 4 = 22 meters ● Rhombus: P = 4 × 6 = 24 meters','● Parallelogram: P = 8 + 5 = 13 meters ● Trapezoid: P = 2 × (6 + 7) = 26 meters ● Rhombus: P = 6 + 6 + 6 = 18 meters','● Parallelogram: P = 8 × 5 = 40 meters ● Trapezoid: P = 6 + 7 + 5 = 18 meters ● Rhombus: P = 4 + 6 = 10 meters','● Parallelogram: P = 2 × (5 + 5) = 20 meters ● Trapezoid: P = (6 + 4) × 2 = 20 meters ● Rhombus: P = 6 × 2 = 12 meters','A','Parallelogram: Formula: P = 2 × (base + side) Calculation: 2 × (8 + 5) = 26 meters Trapezoid: Formula: P = sum of all four sides Calculation: 6 + 7 + 5 + 4 = 22 meters Rhombus: Formula: P = 4 × side Calculation: 4 × 6 = 24 meters',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,62,'Juana is solving problems involving the areas of different geometric shapes. She knows that to find the area of each shape, she must first identify the correct types of information (such as base, height, side, or diagonals) and then apply the appropriate area formula. She is given the following shapes and dimensions: Triangle: base = 10 cm, height = 8 cm Parallelogram: base = 12 cm, height = 5 cm Trapezoid: base₁ = 10 cm, base₂ = 6 cm, height = 4 cm Rhombus: diagonal₁ = 10 cm, diagonal₂ = 8 cm','Which set of area formulas and information types correctly matches the shapes?','● Triangle: A = ½ × base × height ● Parallelogram: A = base × height ● Trapezoid: A = ½ × (base₁ + base₂) × height ● Rhombus: A = ½ × diagonal₁ × diagonal₂','● Triangle: A = base × height ● Parallelogram: A = ½ × base × height ● Trapezoid: A = base × height ● Rhombus: A = side × side','● Triangle: A = ½ × diagonal₁ × diagonal₂ ● Parallelogram: A = side × side ● Trapezoid: A = base + base × height ● Rhombus: A = ½ × base × height','● Triangle: A = base + height ● Parallelogram: A = 2 × base + 2 × height ● Trapezoid: A = ½ × height × side ● Rhombus: A = 4 × side','A','Triangle: A = 1/2 × base × height. Parallelogram: A = base × height. Trapezoid: A = 1/2 × (base1 + base2) × height. Rhombus: A = 1/2 × diagonal1 × diagonal2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,63,'Imagine designing a playground where it''s necessary to calculate the area of various sections. One section is a composite figure made up of a rectangle and a triangle. The rectangle is 10 meters long and 6 meters tall. The triangle sits on top of the rectangle and shares the same base (10 meters), with a height of 4 meters. To determine how much soft flooring is needed, you must calculate the total area of this section.','Which option correctly identifies the plane figures in the composite shape and selects the appropriate information and formulas to calculate the area?','● Plane Figures: Rectangle and Triangle ● Information Needed: Base and height of triangle, length and height of rectangle ● Formulas: o Rectangle → A = length × height o Triangle → A = ½ × base × height','● Plane Figures: Square and Triangle ● Information Needed: Diagonal of square and slant height of triangle ● Formulas: o Square → A = side × side o Triangle → A = base × height','● Plane Figures: Rectangle and Trapezoid ● Information Needed: All four sides of both shapes ● Formulas: o Rectangle → A = 2 × (length + width) o Trapezoid → A = ½ × (base₁ + base₂) × height','● Plane Figures: Triangle only ● Information Needed: Perimeter of triangle ● Formula: ● Triangle → A = side × side','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,64,'Juan is helping design a new classroom display that illustrates the relationship between plane and solid figures. He is researching information from textbooks, websites, and videos. To ensure the display is accurate, Juan needs to describe the characteristics of plane and solid figures and evaluate which source provides the most reliable information about their properties and differences.','Which of the following best helps Juan accurately describe plane and solid figures, and evaluate the quality of his sources?','Plane figures are flat but include round and box shapes. The best source is a website with lots of pictures, even if it’s not created by teachers.','Plane figures are solid like blocks; solid figures are flat and can’t be measured. The best source is a fun video from someone popular online.','Plane figures are just drawings with no real examples; solid figures are only used in science. The best source is a blog without a known author because it’s easy to read.','Plane figures are flat, with only length and width. Solid figures have length, width, and height. The best source is a math book that has been reviewed by teachers.','D','Plane figures: Correctly described as 2D (length and width), examples: square, triangle, circle. Solid figures: Correctly described as 3D (length, width, and height), examples: cube, sphere, cylinder. Evaluating sources: Textbooks are reliable because they are usually written and reviewed by experts, unlike unverified blogs or influencers.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,65,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, learners are solving real-life math problems. The facilitator shows a can of sardines, which is shaped like a cylinder. The label on the can wraps around the curved surface and also covers the top and bottom. The learner is asked to find how much label material is needed to fully cover the can.','If you are given a cylinder with a radius of 5 cm and a height of 10 cm, which of the following options correctly identifies the necessary information and applies the correct formula to calculate its surface area?','● Needed Information: Only the height ● Formula Used: SA = 2 × π × height ● Reason: The curved surface is enough to calculate the total area','● Needed Information: Radius and height ● Formula Used: SA = 2πr² + 2πrh ● Reason: A cylinder has two circular bases and one curved surface; 2πr² accounts for the top and bottom, and 2πrh covers the curved side.','● Needed Information: Radius only ● Formula Used: SA = πr² × 3 ● Reason: A cylinder has three parts, so just multiply the base area by three','● Needed Information: Radius and diameter ● Formula Used: SA = πd² + πrh ● Reason: The diameter helps to simplify the formula for surface area','B','Using indigenous or non-standard measures like a forearm (dangkal) is valid for estimating volume, as long as the same unit is used consistently for length, width, and height, and the volume is calculated by multiplying these three measurements.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,66,'Juana is reading an online article in which a community elder explains how they used the length of a forearm to measure cloth in the past, instead of using standard units like meters. Juana is curious about this practice and wants to understand how it relates to estimation, as well as how to determine if this kind of source provides useful and trustworthy information.','Inspired by this, Juana wants to estimate the volume of a storage basket using non- standard or indigenous units commonly used in her community. Which of the following best describes how Juana can estimate the volume of the basket using these units?','Juana measures only the basket’s height in "dangkal" units and multiplies it by 3, assuming baskets are round, to estimate the volume.','Juana uses a ruler to obtain exact measurements, converts them to inches, and disregards non-standard units as unreliable.','Juana measures the length, width, and height of the basket using the same non- standard unit (such as a forearm) and multiplies them to estimate the volume.','Juana estimates the volume by counting how many small stones fit inside the basket and guesses based on the weight of each stone.','C','Using indigenous or non-standard measures like a forearm (dangkal) is valid for estimating volume, as long as the same unit is used consistently for length, width, and height, and the volume is calculated by multiplying these three measurements.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,67,'Juana is reading an online article in which a community elder explains how they used the length of a forearm to measure cloth in the past, instead of using standard units like meters. Juana is curious about this practice and wants to understand how it relates to estimation, as well as how to determine if this kind of source provides useful and trustworthy information.','Which of the following best explains the meaning of estimation?','Estimation means finding an exact number.','Estimation means guessing without thinking.','Estimation means giving a close answer based on what you know.','Estimation means counting by tens.','C','Estimation means giving a close answer using what you already know, like using your forearm to measure cloth without a ruler. A trustworthy source is someone with real experience or knowledge, like a community elder or expert, and we should check if what they say makes sense.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,68,'While researching online, Ruth found a blog that said, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','Now, Ruth wants to know how to find the volume of both shapes and whether the blog provides reliable information. Which of the following correctly outlines the steps to find the volume and evaluates whether the blog is a trustworthy source?','To find the volume, add all the edges together, and trust the blog because it sounds credible.','To find the volume, multiply length × width × height, and check if the blog is written by a teacher or expert.','To find the volume, measure only the outside of the shape, and believe the blog if it has cool pictures.','To find the volume, count all the faces, and use the blog if it is easy to read and short.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,69,'Anna’s family checks their electricity meter every month. Last month, the reading was 1,250 kWh, and this month, it is 1,430 kWh. She wants to know how much electricity her family used this month and whether they used more or less than last month.','Which of the following correctly compares electricity consumption?','The family used 180 kWh more this month, so they consumed more electricity than last month.','The family used 180 kWh less this month, so they saved electricity.','The reading stayed the same, so they didn’t consume any more electricity this month.','The family used a total of 2,680 kWh electricity.','A','Present reading (1,430) minus Previous reading (1,250) = 180 kWh used Because the number went up, they used more electricity this month',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,70,'In 2022, 320 learners joined ALS in Magandang Buhay. They wanted to learn and finish school. In 2023, even more people joined—410 learners! They told their friends and family how fun learning was. By 2024, the number grew to 540. The classrooms were full of happy learners, all ready to achieve their dreams. Each year, the number continued to grow, showing that more people believe in the power of education!','Which among the graph below illustrates the data of the 3-year ALS Enrolment in the Division of Magandang Buhay?','','','','','A','','LS3-L2-70.png',1,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,71,'The Malipayon family lives in a small, happy home. Every month, they spend money on the things they need. Mama says, “We need to spend wisely, children!” Most of their money goes to food - ₱6,000 each month. “We eat healthily to stay strong,” says Papa. For electricity, they spend ₱1,200, but they always turn off the lights to save. They use ₱500 for water and ₱1,000 for transportation, like riding the jeep to school and work. The kids need ₱800 for school supplies such as notebooks, pencils, and projects. By planning and tracking their expenses, the Malipayon family stays happy and prepared every month. “Being smart with money helps us live well,” says Ate Joy with a smile.','Which pie chart correctly shows the average monthly expenses of Family Malipayon?','','','','','A','','LS3-L2-71.png',1,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,72,'The table below shows the age profile of ALS learners: Age Group Number of Learners 12 -15 40 16 -20 65 21 -25 30 26 - 30 15','Which graph correctly shows the distribution of learners in each age group?','','','','','A','','LS3-L2-72.png',1,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,73,'Look at the pie graph showing the ALS Learners'' Age Profile.','If a teacher wants to create activities that best fit the majority age group, which group should they focus on, and why?','12–15, because it has the smallest slice in the graph.','16–20, because it has the largest slice and the most learners.','21–25, because it is in the middle and represents the average age.','26–30, because it needs the most support due to fewer learners.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,74,'Lila has a bag containing 5 red marbles, 3 blue marbles, and 2 green marbles. She closes her eyes and picks one marble from the bag without looking.','Which of the following best describes the probability of picking red marble?','It is more likely to pick a red marble than any other color.','It is equally likely to pick a blue or red marble.','It is impossible to pick a red marble.','It is more likely to pick a green marble than red marble.','A','Lila has a total of: 5 red marbles 3 blue marbles 2 green marbles That means there are 10 marbles in all To find the chance (probability) of picking each color: • Red: 5 out of 10 marbles → !!!!! = 5/10 • Blue: 3 out of 10 marbles → !!! = 3/10 • Green: 2 out of 10 marbles → !! = 2/10 Since 5 red marbles is more than 3 blue or 2 green. So, red has the highest chance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',2,3,75,'An ALS learner rolls a fair six-sided die. The die has the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 on its faces. She wants to know the theoretical probability of rolling an even number.','Which set of outcomes should she use to correctly find the probability, and why?','1, 2, 3, 4, because most of the numbers are likely to appear.','1, 2, 3, 4, 5, because these are the numbers she remembers.','2, 4, 6, because she is only interested in even numbers.','1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, because it shows all possible outcomes needed to calculate the probability.','D','A fair six-sided die has six numbers, one on each face: 1 to 6. So, all the possible outcomes when rolling the die are: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6. Theoretical probability uses all possible outcomes to calculate the chance of something happening.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,1,'Delia baked 48 cookies and gave 36 of them to her neighbors.','Delia said: "I only kept 25% of the cookies I baked." Is this statement correct, based on the simplified fraction of cookies she kept?','No, 1/4 is 50%.','No, she kept 1/3, which is 33%.','Yes, 1/4 equals 25%.','Yes, because she kept most of the cookies.','C','She kept 48 − 36 = 12 cookies. 12/48 = 1/4 = 25%.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,2,'Delia baked 48 cookies and gave 36 of them to her neighbors.','What fraction of the cookies did she give away, and what is that fraction in its lowest term?','36/48 = 2/3','36/48 = 6/8','36/48 = 3/4','36/48 = 9/12','C','36/48: divide both by 12 to get 3/4.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,3,'A rectangular garden is 3/5 meters wide and 7/8 meters long. After planting, 1/4 of the area was left unused.','Which of the following steps correctly solve the problem of finding the used area?','Add 3/5 and 7/8, then subtract 1/4','Multiply 3/5 × 7/8, then multiply the result by 3/4','Multiply 3/5 × 7/8, then divide the result by 1/4','Multiply 3/5 × 7/8, then subtract 1/4 from the result','B','Area = 3/5 × 7/8. If 1/4 is unused, 3/4 is used, so multiply the area by 3/4.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,4,'A rectangular garden is 3/5 meters wide and 7/8 meters long. After planting, 1/4 of the area was left unused.','The gardener wants to place steppingstones in the unused area. Each steppingstone covers 1/80 square meters. What is the greatest number of whole steppingstones that can fit in the unused area without overlapping?','8','9','10','11','C','Area = 3/5 × 7/8 = 21/40 m². Unused = 1/4 × 21/40 = 21/160 m². 21/160 ÷ 1/80 = 21/160 × 80 = 10.5, so 10 whole steppingstones fit.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,5,'A rectangular garden is 3/5 meters wide and 7/8 meters long. After planting, 1/4 of the area was left unused.','How much area was used for planting?','63/160','15/40','55/160','11/40','A','3/5 × 7/8 = 21/40. Used = 3/4 × 21/40 = 63/160 m².',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,6,'A team of engineers are designing custom fuel cells for drones. Each drone requires a precise amount of a special fuel mixture. A large container holds 6 1/2 liters of this fuel. The engineers plan to fill smaller tanks, where each tank holds 3/5 of a liter. Additionally, a portion of the fuel needs to be set aside for testing, which uses 1 3/4 liters.','The engineers found a new design guide online stating each drone now only needs 1/2 liter of fuel, not 3/5. To evaluate whether the guide is reliable, which of the following is the most appropriate first step?','Ask a colleague for their opinion','Use the new measurement immediately','Check the publication date and the source''s credibility','Search for more guides and average the recommendations','C','Before using new information, check when it was published and whether the source can be trusted.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,7,'A team of engineers are designing custom fuel cells for drones. Each drone requires a precise amount of a special fuel mixture. A large container holds 6 1/2 liters of this fuel. The engineers plan to fill smaller tanks, where each tank holds 3/5 of a liter. Additionally, a portion of the fuel needs to be set aside for testing, which uses 1 3/4 liters.','Suppose engineers need to save at least 1/3 of the total fuel for emergencies. They also must set aside 1 3/4 liters for testing. If each tank is still 3/5 liter, what is the maximum number of full tanks they can fill?','3','4','5','6','B','Emergency: 1/3 × 13/2 = 13/6 L. Left: 13/2 − 13/6 − 7/4 = 31/12 L. 31/12 ÷ 3/5 = 155/36 ≈ 4.3, so 4 full tanks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,8,'A team of engineers are designing custom fuel cells for drones. Each drone requires a precise amount of a special fuel mixture. A large container holds 6 1/2 liters of this fuel. The engineers plan to fill smaller tanks, where each tank holds 3/5 of a liter. Additionally, a portion of the fuel needs to be set aside for testing, which uses 1 3/4 liters.','After setting aside the fuel needed for testing, how many full small tanks (3/5 liter each) can the engineers fill from the remaining fuel?','7','8','10','12','A','6 1/2 − 1 3/4 = 26/4 − 7/4 = 19/4 L. 19/4 ÷ 3/5 = 95/12 ≈ 7.9, so 7 full tanks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,9,'Diana is a meat shop owner. She sells meat in packs as shown on the table. Meat product Weight chicken wings 0.875 kg chicken breast 0.780 kg chicken legs 0.960 kg beef 0.985 kg ground meat 0.675 kg','If Elias only wanted 1.765 kilograms of meat. Among the items presented in the table, which two items will be taken by Elias?','Beef and ground meat','Chicken wings and beef','Chicken breast and beef','Chicken legs and ground meat','C','Chicken breast and beef because if you’re going to add the two decimal numbers the result is 1.765. 0.780 + 0.985 1.765','LS3-L3-09.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,10,'Diana is a meat shop owner. She sells meat in packs as shown on the table. Meat product Weight chicken wings 0.875 kg chicken breast 0.780 kg chicken legs 0.960 kg beef 0.985 kg ground meat 0.675 kg','If Elias only needs to buy 2 packs of chicken wings, 2 packs of chicken legs for his garlic chicken recipe. How many kilograms of chicken does Elias all together?','4.250 kg','4. 120 kg','3.670 kg','3. 460 kg','C','It is stated in the problem that 2 packs of chicken wings and 2 packs of chicken legs ,so we need to double the weight of each item 0.875 0.960 + 0.875 + 0.960 1.750 1.920 Then add both items 1.750 + 1.920 3.670 kg So, the total number of kilograms for the two items is 3.670.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,11,'Diana is a meat shop owner. She sells meat in packs as shown on the table. Meat product Weight chicken wings 0.875 kg chicken breast 0.780 kg chicken legs 0.960 kg beef 0.985 kg ground meat 0.675 kg','If Elias will buy a pack of each kind, How many kilograms of meat do Elias have in all?','4.275 kg','4.585 kg','4.845 kg','4.965 kg','A','To answer the problem, you need to add all the decimal numbers mentioned in the problem. To add decimal numbers, write in column form and align all the decimal points then add 0.875 0.780 + 0.960 0.985 0.675 4.275 kg. Therefore, the total weight is 4.275 kg.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,12,'Von has PHP 28,263.13 savings in a bank.','Von experienced a machine error when he withdrawn cash via ATM machine, instead of withdrawing PHP 2,340.50, the machine doubled it. Based on the problem, what is now the remaining balance of Von’s savings.','PHP 23,582.13','PHP 23,615. 35','PHP 23,825. 52','PHP 23,928. 55','A','Subtract Von’s saving by twice the number of withdrawals since it doubled. Php 28 263.13 - 2 340.50 25 922.63 - 2 340.50 Php 23 582.13',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,13,'Von has PHP 28,263.13 savings in a bank.','Von needs to buy another P.E uniform because their school requires it, so he needs to withdraw additional PHP 1,340.50. How much money was left in the bank?','PHP 22,241. 63','PHP 20,237. 91','PHP 19,823.18','PHP 18,712. 07','A','After withdrawing the amounts needed for PE uniform, Php 23 582.13 - 1 340.50 Php 22,241.63. Von is left with Php 22,241.63.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,14,'Von has PHP 28,263.13 savings in a bank.','Von will buy a medical book for his subject which cost PHP 1,200.00. If he withdraws the exact amount for the book, how much money is left after the withdrawal?','PHP 23,586.54','PHP 21,041.63','PHP 20,356.85','PHP 20,041.63','B','Simply subtract Von’s Savings minus the Withdrawals Php 22 241. 63 - 1 200. 00 21 041. 63',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,15,'Janet is preparing for her birthday party. She wants to purchase supplies. She visits the store and purchases the following items: 50 balloons at PHP 8.25 per piece, 2 packs paper plates at PHP 25.75 per pack, 40 pieces party hats at PHP 5.75 each, and a cake worth ₱ 1250.','Janet wants to know how much the total cost of all the items she wants to purchase. What will be the operations that she will use to solve the problem?','Addition and Subtraction','Subtraction and Division','Multiplication and Addition','Division and Multiplication','C','To get the total cost of all the items, we simply need to multiply number of pieces or packs that Janet wants to purchase to the cost of each item, Then altogether the cost. (50 x PHP 8.25) + (2 x PHP 25.75) + (40 x PHP 5.75) + Php 1 250 = n Hence, we used Multiplication & Addition',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,16,'Janet is preparing for her birthday party. She wants to purchase supplies. She visits the store and purchases the following items: 50 balloons at PHP 8.25 per piece, 2 packs paper plates at PHP 25.75 per pack, 40 pieces party hats at PHP 5.75 each, and a cake worth ₱ 1250.','If Janet has PHP2,000.00 in her pocket and withdraw another PHP3,000.00 as additional to her money, if she bought all the items, how much money will she have left?','PHP 4,325.25','PHP 4,150.00','PHP 3,256.20','PHP 3,056.00','D','This is the flow of cash on hand and dispense. The mathematical sentence shows like this PHP 2000 + 3000 – (50 x PHP 8.25) + 2 x PHP 25.75) +(40 x PHP 5.75) + PHP 1250) 5000 – (412.50 + 51.50+230 + 1250) = n If PHP 5000 – 1944 = PHP 3056 Therefore, Janet’s remaining money is Php 3 056.00',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,17,'Janet is preparing for her birthday party. She wants to purchase supplies. She visits the store and purchases the following items: 50 balloons at PHP 8.25 per piece, 2 packs paper plates at PHP 25.75 per pack, 40 pieces party hats at PHP 5.75 each, and a cake worth ₱ 1250.','How much money does she need to buy for balloons and party hats?','PHP 6,325.10','PHP 642.50','PHP 654.25','PHP 668.20','B','Since, balloons are sold at Php 8.25 per piece and Janet wants to buy 50, so we need to multiply; 50 x PHP 8.25 = 412.50 and 40 x PHP 5.75 = 230.00 Then add Php 412.50 + 230.00 Php 642.50 Therefore, Janet need Php 642.50 to buy for the balloons & party hats.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,18,'Miguel has four number cards as shown below. His teacher asks him to set up a proportion using the numbers. Help Miguel solve.\n\n5 8 24 1','After setting up the ratios in fraction form, how are you going to solve for the missing proportion?','By cross Multiplication','By adding all the numerator and denominators','By dividing the numerator and the denominator of each fraction','By subtracting both the numerators and denominators then divide the difference.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,19,'Miguel has four number cards as shown below. His teacher asks him to set up a proportion using the numbers. Help Miguel solve.\n\n5 8 24 1','In these ratios, 2 n ______ = ______ 4 1 8 6 What number should you replace n to form a proportion?','18','16','14','12','B','To solve if 2 ratios are equal, simple use cross multiplication 2=n 1 8 16 x n = 24 x 8 1n = 16 1 1 n = 16 Therefore, the value of n is 16.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,20,NULL,'Among the sets of ratios listed, which ratios form a proportion?','5/15 = 8/24 and 5/8 = 15/24','5/24 = 8/15 and 5/8 = 15/24','15/8 = 5/24 and 5/15 = 8/24','24/15 = 5/8 and 15/8 = 5/24','A','5/15 = 1/3 and 8/24 = 1/3; 5/8 × 3/3 = 15/24. Both pairs are equal, so they form proportions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,21,NULL,'An engineer hired 150 workers to pave a road in 25 days. How many workers would be hired to do the same work in 30 days?','125 workers','150 workers','180 workers','185 workers','A','The problem is an example of an Inverse proportion that states as one quantity increases, the other decreases or vice versa. Following the steps of solving the proportion, we need to set up first the given ratios. After the set-up, exchange the position of the terms to which the unknown is located. 150 = n , exchange the position of n and 150 then cross multiply 25 30 25 x n = 150 x 30 25n = 4 500 25 25 n = 180 Therefore, we need to hire 180 workers to do the job in 30 days.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,22,NULL,'Mang Ramon owns a 1-hectare animal farm located in Mindanao. There are 80 animals on his farm, with the ratio of cows to carabaos to goats to horses being 4:2:3:1. How many carabaos does Mang Ramon have?','24','20','16','12','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,23,NULL,'In the Dengue Information Campaign conducted by the Department of Health, there were 4 boys for every 3 girls. If there were 3 dozen girls, how many boys were there?','48','50','52','54','A','The problem is an example of a Direct proportion that states as one quantity increases the other quantity also increases and vice versa. To solve for the missing value of term simply use cross multiplication or multiply the means & extremes Set up the ratios 4: 3 and n : 36 ( in every dozen = 12 so 3 x 12 is 36) Multiply the means & extremes Means = extremes 3 x n = 4 x 36 3n = 144 3 3 n = 48 Another solution to find the missing value is by cross multiplication. Therefore, there were 48 boys during the Dengue Campaign.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,24,NULL,'Miss Padilla’s ALS Intermediate Class conducted a class election for president, with Julie and Jean as the candidates. Jean got 21 votes, while Julie received 29 votes. What percentage of the total votes did Julie receive?','60 %','58%','56%','54%','B','Given: • Jean received 21 votes • Julie received 29 votes Step 1: Find the total number of votes Total votes = 21 + 29 = 50 Step 2: Use the percentage formula Percentage of votes Julie received = (29/50) × 100 0.58 x 100= 58% Therefore, Julie received 58% of the total votes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,1,25,NULL,'Alden used 40% of his money for groceries, if he has PHP10,600.00 cash on hand, how much is the money spent for the groceries?','PHP 6,340.00','PHP 4,240.00','PHP 3,340.00','PHP 2,240.00','B','Given: Php10,600 40% spent for grocery So, 10 600 x .40 4240.00',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,26,NULL,'Mr. Larot, a government employee, regularly uses his car to commute to work. He was glad to hear the news about a rollback in gasoline prices. Currently, gasoline costs PHP 60.00 per liter, but next month, the price will drop to PHP 54.00. By what percent did the gasoline price decrease?','16%','14%','12%','10%','D','Given: Original price = PHP 60 New price = PHP 54 Find the amount of decrease PHP 60 − PHP 54 = PHP 6 Use the percent decrease formula Percent Decrease = Decrease x 100 Orig. Price = 6 x 100 = 10% 60 Therefore, the gasoline price decreased by 10%',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,27,'Ruel owns a factory that manufactures 100,000 light bulbs each day. How will you express the total number of light bulbs produced in a day using exponential notation with powers of 10?','How will you express the total number of light bulbs produced in a day using exponential notation with powers of 10?','10⁴','10⁵','10⁶','100³','B','In writing numbers in exponential form Step 1: Start by writing 100,000 in expanded form: 100,000=10 × 10 × 10 × 10 x 10 There are five 10s multiplied together, so: 10 0,000=105 Therefore, 100,000=105 means you''re multiplying 10 by itself 5 times.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,28,'Ruel owns a factory that manufactures 100,000 light bulbs each day. How will you express the total number of light bulbs produced in a day using exponential notation with powers of 10?','If Ruel’s factory runs for 100 days, based on the result, how many times will you multiplying 10 by itself?','4 times','5 times','6 times','7 times','D','The factory produces 105 light bulbs per day • The condition is the factory runs for 100 days so, Express 100 days in exponential notation 100 = 10 × 10 = 102 Then, multiply to find total production 105 × 102 = 105 + 102= 107 Therefore, Ruel’s factory produces 10⁷ light bulbs in 100 days. Hence, multiply 10 by itself 7 times.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,29,NULL,'Glenda started with PHP 5.00 as her savings on the first day in her piggy bank. The table below shows the amount of her savings that increases exponentially for 4 days. Days 1 2 3 4 5 Savings PHP PHP PHP PHP ? amount 5.00 25.00 125.00 625.00 How much money would Glenda had saved by the time she makes on the fifth day in her piggy bank?','PHP 3,125.00','PHP 3,250.00','PHP 3,515.00','PHP 3,730.00','A','To find the answer to the problem, we can use exponents 1st drop – 5 or 5¹ 2nd drop – 5 x 5 or 5² 3rd drop – 5 x 5 x 5 or 5³ 4th drop – 5 x 5 x 5 x 5 or 5⁴ 5th drop – 5 x 5x 5x 5 x 5 or 5⁵ = 3125 Therefore, Glenda had saved PHP 3125 after five drops.','LS3-L3-29.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,30,NULL,'Sarah and Rodrigo are comparing how many people watched their online videos. Sarah’s video received 7⁵ views, while Rodrigo’s video received 10³ views each day. How many total views did Rodrigo’s video receive after 10 days?','20000','15000','10000','5000','C','The problem stated that Sarah’s video got 10⁵ views (which is 100,000 views). Rodrigo’s video got 10³ views each day for 10 days. We need to find how many total views Rodrigo''s video got. Step 1: Express 10³ in standard form 10 × 10 × 10 = 1000 So, Rodrigo’s video gets 1000 views per day. Step 2: Multiply by 10 days 1000 × 10 = 10000 Therefore, Rodrigo’s video got 10,000 total views after 10 days.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,31,NULL,'Delia wants to build a quadrilateral garden in her backyard. Each side of the garden is 8 meters long. Which quadrilateral shape represents a square garden?','A shape with 4 equal sides and 4 right angles','A diamond shape (rhombus) with no right angles','A trapezoid with only one pair of parallel sides','A parallelogram with slanted sides','A','A square has 4 equal sides and 4 right angles.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,32,NULL,'During Math class, Myrna was asked to sketch three different quadrilaterals: square, rhombus, and parallelogram. After drawing them, her teacher asked her how are these three shapes different to each other?','They are all equal sides but slanted angles.','They are all regular shape with equal sides and right angles.','They are all opposite sides equal but no requirement for all sides or right angles.','They are all quadrilaterals with parallel opposite sides, equal opposite sides and angles, and diagonals that bisect each other.','D','A square, rhombus, and parallelogram are similar because they are all quadrilaterals with parallel opposite sides, equal opposite sides and angles, and diagonals that bisect each other.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,33,NULL,'Isagani and Joshua are playing a guessing game. Isagani challenges Joshua to draw a quadrilateral based on a set of clues. He describes the shape by saying: "All four sides are equal, opposite sides are parallel, opposite angles are the same, and the diagonals intersect at right angles and bisect each other. “Based on these properties, what type of quadrilateral is Isagani describing?','Square','Rhombus','Trapezoid','Parallelogram','B','Based on these properties, the quadrilateral Isagani describing is a Rhombus A Rhombus is a four-sided shape (quadrilateral) where all four sides are equal in length. It looks like a slanted or tilted square, often called a "diamond shape.". It’s opposite sides are parallel, opposite angles are equal and the diagonals bisect each other at 90° (right angles).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,34,NULL,'Orlando believes that a square and a rectangle are the same shape because they both have four right angles. However, Amir disagrees and argues that they are different. What feature make a square different from a rectangle?','A square is a special kind of rectangle, but A rectangle is not always a square','A square is only opposite sides are equal while a rectangle is all 4 sides are equal','A square has 2 lines of symmetry while a rectangle has 4 lines of symmetry','A square has equal in length, but not perpendicular while a rectangle has equal in length & perpendicular','A','A square has all 4 sides are equal, equal in length & perpendicular, is a special kind of rectangle and Has more symmetry (4 lines) while A rectangle has only opposite sides are equal, Equal in length, but not perpendicular, is not always a square and has 2 lines of symmetry. Therefore, only statement A is correct: “A square is a special kind of rectangle but A rectangle is not always a square”',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,35,'Rowena is preparing for a camping trip. She packs a few essentials: a rope that is 3.5 meters long, a water bottle with a capacity of 1 liter, a bag of rice that weighs 1,000 grams, and a flashlight that lasts for 2.5 hours. Her younger brother wants to help, but he has some limits. He can only carry up to 250 centimeters of rope, 1,000 milliliters of water, 1.5 kilograms of food, and a flashlight that runs no more than 120 minutes.','Based on these limits, which items would be too much for him to carry or use on his own?','Rope and Water','Rice and Flashlight','Water and Food','Rope and Flashlight','C','Let''s solve this step by step by converting the measurements so we can compare them with the brother’s limits. Given Items: 1. Rope = 3.5 meters 2. Water = 1 liter 3. Rice = 1,000 grams 4. Flashlight = 2.5 hours Brother’s Maximum Limits: 1. Rope = 250 cm 2. Water = 1,000 mL 3. Food = 1.5 kg 4. Battery = 120 minute Convert Rowena’s items to the same units as her brother’s limits:',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,36,NULL,'Marlon has a rectangular container measures 24 cm by 16 cm by 12 cm. Given that 1 Liter = 1,000 cm3, how many liters of water was left in the container, if 2 L of water is drawn from it?','2.305 L','2.480 L','2.560 L','2.608 L','D','The problem is asking for the number of liters left in the container We must know first the volume of the container And to get the volume Simply apply the formula V Rectangular Prism = L x W x H 24 cm x 16 cm x 12 cm = 4608 cm³ Since in 1 liter = 1,000 cm³ 2 liters drawn from it so 2 liters = 2000 cm³ Subtract 4608 – 2000 = 2608 cm³ Convert by dividing 2608 cm³ x __1L__ 1000 cm³ 2608 = 2.608 L 1000 Therefore, there are 2.608 L left in the container.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,37,'Carol spent 2 hours and 45 minutes doing her house chores and 1 hour doing her math assignment.','How many minutes did she spend doing her house chores and math assignment?','240 minutes','225 minutes','180 minutes','100 minutes','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,38,'Iyana is preparing for a science experiment. She needs to measure 2.5 liters of water, 1.2 kilograms of sand, and 150 centimeters of wire. However, the available measuring tools are marked only in milliliters, grams, and meters.','What should Iyana do first to correctly record the required measurements using the tools available?','Use only one tool and try to guess the remaining values','Estimate the values and record them without converting the units','Convert all the measurements to match the units of the tools she has','Skip the experiment until she finds tools with matching units','C','Information literacy involves identifying, locating, and using relevant data effectively. Iyana must first recognize that the measurements she has (liters, kilograms, centimeters) are not the same units as those on her tools (milliliters, grams, meters). Therefore, she should convert: 2.5 liters → 2500 milliliters 1.2 kilograms → 1200 grams 150 centimeters → 1.5 meters This ensures she uses accurate data, a key part of information literacy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,39,'Iyana is preparing for a science experiment. She needs to measure 2.5 liters of water, 1.2 kilograms of sand, and 150 centimeters of wire. However, the available measuring tools are marked only in milliliters, grams, and meters.','After converting all the measurements, how much total weight (in grams) will Iyana prepare if she adds another 800 grams of salt to the materials?','2,000 grams','1,800 grams','1,200 grams','800 grams','A','Iyana initially has 1.2 kilograms of sand, adding 800 grams of salt. Convert 1.2 kilograms to grams 1.2 kg × 1000 g/1 kg = 1200 g (Eliminate kg unit, multiply 1.2 by 1000 and divide by 1 to get 1200 g) Thus, 1200 g + 800 g = 2000 grams.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,40,'Liam is building a garden with three different shapes: a parallelogram, a trapezoid, and a rhombus. He wants to put a fence around each garden, so he needs to calculate the perimeter of each shape. He measured the sides as follows: ● Parallelogram: Two sides measure 8 meters, and the other two measure 5 meters. ● Trapezoid: The sides measure 6 meters, 7 meters, 5 meters, and 4 meters. ● Rhombus: All four sides measure 6 meters.','Which step should Liam take first to ensure he correctly calculates the total length of fencing he needs?','Multiply the lengths of all sides for each shape','Convert all side lengths to kilometers before calculating','Identify and organize the side lengths of each shape to prepare for perimeter calculation','Choose only one shape to calculate the fencing for and ignore the rest','C','Information literacy involves gathering and organizing relevant data before using it. Liam needs to identify and group the side measurements for each shape before computing perimeters. This organization ensures that calculations are done correctly and completely.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,41,'Liam is building a garden with three different shapes: a parallelogram, a trapezoid, and a rhombus. He wants to put a fence around each garden, so he needs to calculate the perimeter of each shape. He measured the sides as follows: ● Parallelogram: Two sides measure 8 meters, and the other two measure 5 meters. ● Trapezoid: The sides measure 6 meters, 7 meters, 5 meters, and 4 meters. ● Rhombus: All four sides measure 6 meters.','Which statement best explains why the perimeter of a rhombus is easier to calculate than the perimeter of a trapezoid?','A trapezoid has more sides than a rhombus','The perimeter of a trapezoid is the same as its area, which is confusing','All sides of a rhombus are equal, so you only need to multiply one side by 4','A rhombus has unequal sides, which makes it more challenging to calculate','C','Critical thinking involves analyzing patterns or relationships. A rhombus has four equal- length sides, so its perimeter can be calculated by simply multiplying one side by 4, unlike a trapezoid which requires adding four different side lengths. This makes the rhombus simpler to calculate in this case.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,42,'Liam is building a garden with three different shapes: a parallelogram, a trapezoid, and a rhombus. He wants to put a fence around each garden, so he needs to calculate the perimeter of each shape. He measured the sides as follows: ● Parallelogram: Two sides measure 8 meters, and the other two measure 5 meters. ● Trapezoid: The sides measure 6 meters, 7 meters, 5 meters, and 4 meters. ● Rhombus: All four sides measure 6 meters.','What is the total length of fencing Liam needs to enclose all three gardens?','90 meters','76 meters','84 meters','72 meters','D','Let''s calculate the perimeter of each shape: • Parallelogram: 8 + 8 + 5 + 5 = 26 meters • Trapezoid: 6 + 7 + 5 + 4 = 22 meters • Rhombus: 6 × 4 = 24 meters Total fencing needed: 26 + 22 + 24 = 72 meters',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,43,'An ALS teacher is helping a learner understand how to find the circumference of a circular table. The learner measures the table''s radius as 35 cm, and the teacher asks the learner to use the formula for circumference.','What should the learner do first to correctly calculate the circumference of the table?','Change the radius into the diameter before calculating','Use any formula as long as the answer looks reasonable','Estimate the area of the table instead of the circumference','Search for the formula that matches the given measurement (radius)','D','Since the measurement given is the radius, the learner should use the formula that involves radius: C = 2πr This choice shows the learner understands how to match the given data with the appropriate formula.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,44,'An ALS teacher is helping a learner understand how to find the circumference of a circular table. The learner measures the table''s radius as 35 cm, and the teacher asks the learner to use the formula for circumference.','The learner tells the teacher that they used the formula C=πd instead of C=2πr. What should the teacher explain to help the learner think critically about their method?','Both formulas are correct, but the learner must find the diameter first to use C=πd.','The learner used the wrong formula for the shape and must start over.','The teacher should ask the learner to guess the answer and move on.','The learner cannot use π\\piπ in any formula without a calculator.','A','The formula C = πd is valid, but the learner was given the radius. The teacher can guide the learner to realize that the diameter is twice the radius, so: d = 2 × 35 cm = 70 cm Then the learner can correctly use: C = π × 70 cm This helps the learner understand how different formulas relate and when each is appropriate.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,45,'An ALS teacher is helping a learner understand how to find the circumference of a circular table. The learner measures the table''s radius as 35 cm, and the teacher asks the learner to use the formula for circumference.','Which formula is most appropriate for the learner to use based on the given measurement?','C = 2πr, because the radius is given.','C = d ÷ π, because it finds the radius.','C = πr², because it’s the formula for circumference.','C = πd, because the radius and diameter are the same.','A','Since the learner is given the radius (35 cm), the most efficient and direct formula to use is C = 2πr. Using this avoids unnecessary steps and helps the learner focus on understanding how radius relates to circumference.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,46,'An ALS teacher is helping a learner understand how to find the circumference of a circular table. The learner measures the table''s radius as 35 cm, and the teacher asks the learner to use the formula for circumference.','Using formula C = 2πr and taking π as 3.14, what is the circumference of the table?','219.8 cm','220 cm','230.5 cm','245 cm','A','The learner is given the radius = 35 cm, and the formula is: C = 2 × π × r = 2 × 3.14 × 35 = 219.8 cm',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,47,'Juana is solving problems involving the area of different geometric shapes. She knows that to find the area of each shape, she must first identify the correct types of information (such as the base, height, sides, or diagonals), and then apply the appropriate area formula. She is given the following shapes and dimensions: ● Triangle: base = 10 cm, height = 8 cm ● Parallelogram: base = 12 cm, height = 5 cm ● Trapezoid: base₁ = 10 cm, base₂ = 6 cm, height = 4 cm ● Rhombus: diagonal₁ = 10 cm, diagonal₂ = 8 cm','What should Juana do first before solving for the area of each shape?','Memorize the final answers to each formula','Choose one formula and use it for all shapes','Estimate the area based only on the size of the numbers','Identify which formula matches the given dimensions of each shape','D','Juana must match the type of given information (e.g., base and height, diagonals) with the appropriate formula for each shape: Triangle: Area = ½ × base × height Parallelogram: Area = base × height Trapezoid: Area = ½ × (base₁ + base₂) × height Rhombus: Area = ½ × diagonal₁ × diagonal₂ Identifying the right formula for the right shape is the essential first step.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,48,'Juana is solving problems involving the area of different geometric shapes. She knows that to find the area of each shape, she must first identify the correct types of information (such as the base, height, sides, or diagonals), and then apply the appropriate area formula. She is given the following shapes and dimensions: ● Triangle: base = 10 cm, height = 8 cm ● Parallelogram: base = 12 cm, height = 5 cm ● Trapezoid: base₁ = 10 cm, base₂ = 6 cm, height = 4 cm ● Rhombus: diagonal₁ = 10 cm, diagonal₂ = 8 cm','What is the total area Juana will find when she correctly calculates the area of all four shapes? A. 160 cm² A. 172 cm² B. 180 cm² D. 190 cm²','160 cm²','172 cm²','180 cm²','190 cm²','B','Problem solving involves applying the correct formulas and computing the answers step-by-step: • Triangle: ½ × 10 × 8 = 40 cm² • Parallelogram: 12 × 5 = 60 cm² • Trapezoid: ½ × (10 + 6) × 4 = ½ × 16 × 4 = 32 cm² • Rhombus: ½ × 10 × 8 = 40 cm² Total area: 40 + 60 + 32 + 40 = 172 cm²',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,49,'Imagine designing a playground where it''s necessary to calculate the area of various sections. One section is a composite figure made up of a rectangle and a triangle. The rectangle is 10 meters long and 6 meters wide. The triangle sits on top of the rectangle and shares the same base (10 meters), with a height of 4 meters. To determine how much soft flooring to use, you must calculate the total area of this section.','Which is the best strategy for finding the total area of the composite figure?','Multiply all the given numbers and divide by 2.','Use the perimeter of the rectangle to estimate the area.','Use only the area of the triangle, since it''s the shape on top.','Add the areas of the rectangle and the triangle using their correct formulas.','D','Information literacy is about selecting the right information and method. To calculate the total area of a composite figure, identify the shapes and apply the correct formula for each: • Rectangle area = length × height = 10 × 6 • Triangle area = ½ × base × height = ½ × 10 × 4 Then add both areas to get the total. This approach uses both correct identification and appropriate use of formulas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,2,50,'Imagine designing a playground where it''s necessary to calculate the area of various sections. One section is a composite figure made up of a rectangle and a triangle. The rectangle is 10 meters long and 6 meters wide. The triangle sits on top of the rectangle and shares the same base (10 meters), with a height of 4 meters. To determine how much soft flooring to use, you must calculate the total area of this section.','What is the total area of the playground section that needs soft flooring?','60 m²','70 m²','80 m²','100 m²','C','Juana calculates the total area by adding the area of both shapes: • Rectangle: 10 × 6 = 60 m² • Triangle: ½ × 10 × 4 = 20 m² Total: 60 + 20 = 80 m²',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,51,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, the facilitator asks the learners to help plan a simple community garden. The learners are given the task of sketching different shapes that can be used for garden plots and storage sheds. They need to determine which shapes are plane figures and which are solid figures.','Which of the following BEST demonstrates that a learner understands the difference between plane and solid figures when sketching a design for the community garden?','Using only solid figures to design the entire garden','Choosing only plane figures because they are easier to draw','Sketching cubes and cylinders but labeling them as flat shapes','Drawing both a circle and a cone to represent shapes for planting areas and storage bins','D','It shows that the learner can differentiate between plane figures (like a circle for flat planting areas) and solid figures (like a cone for 3D structures such as storage bins).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,52,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, the facilitator asks the learners to help plan a simple community garden. The learners are given the task of sketching different shapes that can be used for garden plots and storage sheds. They need to determine which shapes are plane figures and which are solid figures.','Which of the following is the BEST way for learners to correctly identify and relate plane figures to solid figures using models?','Memorize all shape names and avoid using models.','Choose shapes based only on what looks nice in a sketch.','Only draw circles and rectangles because they are easier.','Use pictures of real objects, such as cans, boxes, and tiles, to connect flat and solid shapes.','D','By using pictures of real-life objects, learners can visually connect plane figures (like rectangles and circles) to solid figures (like boxes and cans). For example, a rectangle relates to a box (rectangular prism) and a circle relates to a can (cylinder). This helps learners understand shapes using concrete and pictorial models, a key step in building spatial understanding.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,53,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, the facilitator asks the learners to help plan a simple community garden. The learners are given the task of sketching different shapes that can be used for garden plots and storage sheds. They need to determine which shapes are plane figures and which are solid figures.','Which of the following shows that a learner is thinking critically when choosing shapes for the garden design?','Avoiding 3D shapes because they are hard to draw.','Drawing only squares because they are easy to measure.','Using random shapes without checking whether they are planar or solid.','Choosing a cylinder for the water tank because it has circular faces like a circle.','D','Option D shows the learner understands how a plane figure (circle) relates to a solid figure (cylinder) and applies that knowledge to a practical situation, designing a water tank. This demonstrates clear reasoning and relating 2D shapes to 3D objects in real life.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,54,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, learners are studying solid figures such as cubes, rectangular prisms, and cylinders. The ALS teacher brings boxes, cans, and paper models to help them understand that solid figures are made up of plane shapes. They are then asked to identify the plane figures in these solids and find the total surface area to determine how much material would be needed to cover them completely.','Which of the following best helps a learner determine the plane figures that make up a rectangular prism?','Measuring only one face and ignoring the rest.','Labeling it only as a box without breaking it into shapes.','Guessing what the faces are without touching or observing the model.','Observing and counting the flat faces of the model and identifying each as a rectangle.','D','A rectangular prism is made up of 6 rectangular plane figures. Carefully observing and analyzing the model allows learners to connect 3D forms with 2D components, which is essential in understanding surface area.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,55,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, learners are studying solid figures such as cubes, rectangular prisms, and cylinders. The ALS teacher brings boxes, cans, and paper models to help them understand that solid figures are made up of plane shapes. They are then asked to identify the plane figures in these solids and find the total surface area to determine how much material would be needed to cover them completely.','Why is it important for learners to understand the plane figures in a solid figure when finding the surface area?','Because the surface area is the total of all the flat surfaces, which are plane figures','Because solid figures are more interesting than flat ones','So, they can color the model more easily','So, they can name the shape faster','A','To find the surface area of a solid figure, learners must realize it is the sum of the areas of the flat (plane) faces that make up the figure. Without this connection, they cannot compute surface area correctly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,56,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, learners are studying solid figures such as cubes, rectangular prisms, and cylinders. The ALS teacher brings boxes, cans, and paper models to help them understand that solid figures are made up of plane shapes. They are then asked to identify the plane figures in these solids and find the total surface area to determine how much material would be needed to cover them completely.','If a rectangular prism has a length of 5 cm, a width of 3 cm, and a height of 2 cm, what is its surface area?','58 cm²','60 cm²','62 cm²','94 cm²','C','Solve using the surface area formula: SA = 2(lw × lh × wh) = 𝟐(𝟓 × 𝟑 + 𝟓 × 𝟐 + 𝟑 × 𝟐) = 𝟐(𝟏𝟓 + 𝟏𝟎 + 𝟔) = 𝟐(𝟑𝟏) = 𝟔𝟐 𝒄𝒎𝟐',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,57,'At the ALS Community Learning Center, learners are solving real-life math problems. The facilitator shows a can of sardines, which is shaped like a cylinder. The label on the can wraps around the curved surface and covers both the top and bottom. The learners are then asked to determine how much label material is needed to fully cover the can.','The radius of the can is 5 cm, and the height is 10 cm. What surface area will the label need to cover the entire can (curved surface and two circular ends)? Use π ≈ 3.14','157 cm²','314 cm²','471 cm²','785 cm²','C','SA = 2πr² + 2πrh = 2(3.14)(5 cm)² + 2(3.14)(5 cm)(10 cm) = 157 cm² + 314 cm² = 471 cm².',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,58,'Juana is reading an online article where a community elder explains how they used the length of a forearm to measure cloth in the past, instead of using standard units like meters. Juana is curious about this practice and wants to understand how it relates to estimation and how to determine whether this kind of source provides useful and trustworthy information.','Which of the following BEST demonstrates that Juana is thinking critically about the article she read?','She only uses the elder’s method when the internet is not working.','She ignores the article because it doesn''t use standard measurements.','She accepts the elder’s method without question because it is part of tradition.','She compares the elder’s method to standard units, checks whether it was used commonly in the past, and considers who published the article.','D','Juana shows critical thinking by: Comparing non-standard (forearm) measures to standard units (like meters) Investigating the historical use of the method (cultural relevance and context) Evaluating the source, including the publisher or author credibility This helps her decide if the article is trustworthy and if the method can be reasonably used for estimation today.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,59,'While researching online, Ruth finds a blog that says, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','Which of the following BEST explains why Ruth should calculate the volume differently for a cube and a rectangular prism, even though they share the same number of faces, edges, and vertices?','Because both shapes have curved surfaces.','Because the cube is larger than any rectangular prism.','Because volume depends on the color of the faces, not their shape.','Because a cube and a rectangular prism have different face shapes.','D','A cube and a rectangular prism both have 6 faces, 12 edges, and 8 vertices, the dimensions of their faces differ. A cube has equal edges, but a rectangular prism can have different lengths, widths, and heights. This means the volume is calculated based on different side lengths, even though their structure seems similar.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,60,'While researching online, Ruth finds a blog that says, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','Ruth wants to find the volume of a rectangular prism that is 5 cm long, 3 cm wide, and 4 cm high. What is the volume of the prism?','12 cm³','20 cm³','60 cm³','80 cm³','C','Volume of prism: 𝑉 = 𝑙 × 𝑤 × ℎ V = 5 cm × 3 cm × 4 cm V = 60 cm3',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,61,'While researching online, Ruth finds a blog that says, “A cube and a rectangular prism have the same number of faces, edges, and vertices.”','Ruth also measures a cube where each side is 6 cm long. What is the volume of the cube?','18 cm³','36 cm³','96 cm³','216 cm³','D','To find the volume of a cube, use the formula: Volume = side3 = 6 cm × 6 cm × 6 cm = 216 cm3 Cubes have equal-length edges, so multiplying the side three times gives the correct volume.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,62,'An ALS learner is riding his bicycle to the community learning center. On the way, he notices that his ride feels slower and more difficult. He stops checking the tire pressure using a small pressure gauge. The gauge reads 20 psi, while the recommended pressure on the tire is 35 psi.','What should the learner do next, and why?','Ignore the reading and continue riding, as the tire is still round.','Record the pressure as 20 psi and ride slower to stay safe.','Deflate the tire a bit more, as lower pressure provides more grip.','Inflate the tire until the gauge reads 35 psi, matching the recommended pressure.','D','Evaluating the ability to: • Interpret the gauge reading (20 psi) • Compare it with the recommended value (35 psi) • Decide on an action that ensures both safety and efficiency B is correct because keeping the tire pressure at the recommended level helps maintain proper balance, reduces tire wear, and makes riding easier and safer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,63,'Anna''s family checks their electricity meter every month. Last month, the reading was 1,250 kWh, and this month, it is 1,430 kWh. She wants to know how much electricity her family used this month and whether they used more or less than last month.','Anna notices that her electric bill is higher this month. Which of the following is the BEST explanation for why the bill increased?','The meter numbers are just random and don’t affect the bill.','The family used more electricity this month than last month.','The electric company increased the meter reading on purpose.','The numbers on the meter always stay the same each month.','B','Anna analyze and connect the change in meter reading (from 1,250 to 1,430) with the increase in the electric bill. A higher meter reading means more consumption, which leads to a higher bill. This reflects understanding how energy use impacts cost.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,64,'Anna''s family checks their electricity meter every month. Last month, the reading was 1,250 kWh, and this month, it is 1,430 kWh. She wants to know how much electricity her family used this month and whether they used more or less than last month.','If electricity costs PHP 10.00 per kWh, how much will Anna''s family need to pay for this month''s usage?','PHP 2,000.00','PHP 1,800.00','PHP 1,600.00','PHP 1,450.00','B','Calculate the number of kilowatt-hours (kWh) used: 1,430 kWh − 1,250 kWh = 180 kWh Now multiply by the rate: 180 Kwh x Php 10 = Php 1,800.00 This shows the learner can apply basic subtraction and multiplication to a real-world problem involving cost of electric consumption.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,65,'In the peaceful town of Kalilangan, Bukidnon, paying electric bills used to be very difficult. However, in January, the barangay initiated a solar project called “Solar sa Tagbungtod.” By March, families received solar panels, and by April, everyone had learned how to use electricity more efficiently turning off lights, charging devices during the day, and saving energy. Every month, the electric bill decreased. By December, the town had a night market illuminated only by solar lamps - a symbol of saving money, helping the environment, and building a brighter future.\n\nElectric Bill Savings: ● January: PHP 0.00 ● March: PHP 200.00 ● April: PHP 500.00 ● June: PHP 700.00 ● December: PHP 1,000.00','If you are asked to present the monthly electric bill savings for the town from January to December, which of the following is the BEST way to show the information in a clear and organized tabular form?','Write a short story about how each family saved electricity.','Draw pictures of solar panels for each month on a calendar.','Create a table with columns for "Month" and "Amount Saved."','Color each month based on how bright the town lights were.','C','Using a table with appropriate labels (e.g., Month, Amount Saved) allows for easy interpretation and tracking of patterns over time.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,66,'In the peaceful town of Kalilangan, Bukidnon, paying electric bills used to be very difficult. However, in January, the barangay initiated a solar project called “Solar sa Tagbungtod.” By March, families received solar panels, and by April, everyone had learned how to use electricity more efficiently turning off lights, charging devices during the day, and saving energy. Every month, the electric bill decreased. By December, the town had a night market illuminated only by solar lamps - a symbol of saving money, helping the environment, and building a brighter future.\n\nElectric Bill Savings: ● January: PHP 0.00 ● March: PHP 200.00 ● April: PHP 500.00 ● June: PHP 700.00 ● December: PHP 1,000.00','Which table correctly shows the monthly electric bill savings?','','','Amount Saved Amount Saved Month Month (PHP) (PHP) December PHP 1,000.00 January PHP 0.00 June PHP 700.00 March PHP 200.00 April PHP 500.00 April PHP 500.00 March PHP 200.00 June PHP 700.00 January PHP 0.00 December PHP 1,000.00','Amount Saved Amount Saved Month Month (PHP) (PHP) January PHP 0.00 December PHP 1,000.00 March PHP 200.00 June PHP 700.00 April PHP 500.00 April PHP 500.00 June PHP 700.00 March PHP 200.00 December PHP 1,000.00 January PHP 0.00','B','','LS3-L3-66a.png',1,0),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,67,'In the peaceful town of Kalilangan, Bukidnon, paying electric bills used to be very difficult. However, in January, the barangay initiated a solar project called “Solar sa Tagbungtod.” By March, families received solar panels, and by April, everyone had learned how to use electricity more efficiently turning off lights, charging devices during the day, and saving energy. Every month, the electric bill decreased. By December, the town had a night market illuminated only by solar lamps - a symbol of saving money, helping the environment, and building a brighter future.\n\nElectric Bill Savings: ● January: PHP 0.00 ● March: PHP 200.00 ● April: PHP 500.00 ● June: PHP 700.00 ● December: PHP 1,000.00','Which of the following graph describes the data on Electric Bill Savings?','','','','',NULL,'','LS3-L3-67.png',1,0),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,68,'In the peaceful town of Kalilangan, Bukidnon, paying electric bills used to be very difficult. However, in January, the barangay initiated a solar project called “Solar sa Tagbungtod.” By March, families received solar panels, and by April, everyone had learned how to use electricity more efficiently turning off lights, charging devices during the day, and saving energy. Every month, the electric bill decreased. By December, the town had a night market illuminated only by solar lamps - a symbol of saving money, helping the environment, and building a brighter future.\n\nElectric Bill Savings: ● January: PHP 0.00 ● March: PHP 200.00 ● April: PHP 500.00 ● June: PHP 700.00 ● December: PHP 1,000.00','Which of the following is the BEST interpretation of the graph?','The savings decreased in the middle of the year but increased again in December.','The community saved the most in January because solar panels were first installed then.','The electric bill savings increased over time, showing that people learned to save energy.','The amount saved remained the same every month, so there was no real improvement.','C','','LS3-L3-68.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,69,'In 2022, 320 learners joined ALS in Magandang Buhay. They were eager to learn and finish school. In 2023, more people joined—410 learners! They told their friends and family how fun learning was. By 2024, the number grew to 540. The classrooms were full of happy learners, all ready to reach their dreams. Each year, the number grew, showing that more people believe in the power of education!','Based on the bar graph, which of the following statements most accurately describes the number of ALS learners in Magandang Buhay from 2022 to 2024?','The number of learners increased every year.','The number of learners remained the same.','The number of learners decreased over time.','The number of learners doubled each year.','A','','LS3-L3-69.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,70,'In 2022, 320 learners joined ALS in Magandang Buhay. They were eager to learn and finish school. In 2023, more people joined—410 learners! They told their friends and family how fun learning was. By 2024, the number grew to 540. The classrooms were full of happy learners, all ready to reach their dreams. Each year, the number grew, showing that more people believe in the power of education!','Which year had the greatest increase in the number of enrolled learners compared to the previous year?','2022','2023','2024','All years had the same increase','C','From 2022 to 2023, the increase was 410 - 320 = 90 learners. From 2023 to 2024, the increase was 540 - 410 = 130 learners. The largest increase occurred in 2024.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,71,'The Malipayon family lives in a small, happy home. Every month, they spend money on the things they need. Mama says, “We need to spend wisely, children!” Most of their money goes to food PHP 6,000 each month. “We eat healthy to stay strong,” says Papa. For electricity, they spend PHP1,200, but they always turn off the lights to save. They use PHP 500 for water and PHP1,000 for transportation, like riding the jeep to school and work. The kids need PHP800 for school supplies, such as notebooks, pencils, and projects. By planning and tracking their expenses, the Malipayon family stays happy and prepared every month. “Being smart with money helps us live well,” says Ate Joy with a smile.','Which of the following conclusions can best be drawn from the pie graph about the Malipayon family''s priorities?','The family spends most of their money on luxury items.','The family values entertainment more than basic needs.','The family should stop spending money on school supplies.','The family prioritizes essential needs such as food and utilities.','D','The pie chart shows that a large portion (63.2%) of the family’s budget goes to food, followed by electricity, water, transportation, and school needs, these are all basic or essential needs, indicating wise prioritization.','LS3-L3-71.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,72,'The Malipayon family lives in a small, happy home. Every month, they spend money on the things they need. Mama says, “We need to spend wisely, children!” Most of their money goes to food PHP 6,000 each month. “We eat healthy to stay strong,” says Papa. For electricity, they spend PHP1,200, but they always turn off the lights to save. They use PHP 500 for water and PHP1,000 for transportation, like riding the jeep to school and work. The kids need PHP800 for school supplies, such as notebooks, pencils, and projects. By planning and tracking their expenses, the Malipayon family stays happy and prepared every month. “Being smart with money helps us live well,” says Ate Joy with a smile.','If the Malipayon family plans to lower their monthly spending, which expense should they consider reviewing first, according to the pie graph?','Transportation, even though it’s already low.','Water, since they barely spend anything on it.','School supplies, because education is less important.','Food, since it takes up the largest portion of their budget.','D','Since food expenses make up more than 60% of their monthly budget, it is the most significant cost. Reviewing this area first can potentially lead to more impactful savings without necessarily sacrificing nutrition. Options B, C, and D suggest areas that contribute much less to the total expense and may not be logical or beneficial to reduce.','LS3-L3-72.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,73,'The pie graph shows the ALS learner’s age profile. There are a total of 200 learners enrolled in the ALS Community Learning Center. ALS Learner’s Age Profile','Based on the graph, how many learners are between the ages of 16 to 20?','43','54','86','100','C','From the pie graph, 43% of the learners are between 16–20 years old. To find the number of learners in this group: • Multiply 200 by 43%: 200 × 0.43 = 86 Therefore, 86 learners are aged 16 to 20.','LS3-L3-73.png',0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,74,NULL,'An ALS learner is playing a game where they draw one token from a box. The box contains 3 red tokens, 2 blue tokens, and 1 green token. What is the theoretical probability of drawing a blue token?','1/6','1/3','2/5','2/3','B','2 blue out of 6 tokens: 2/6 = 1/3.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS3',3,3,75,NULL,'An ALS teacher spins a wheel divided into 4 equal parts labeled A, B, C, and D. What is the theoretical probability that the pointer will land on the letter C?','1/2','1/3','1/4','1/5','C','1 part out of 4 equal parts: 1/4.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,1,NULL,'Liza is good at making crafts like bags and wallets. Her teacher asked her to identify what PEC she is showing. What Personal Entrepreneurial Competency (PEC) is she demonstrating?','Patience','Creativity','Laziness','Carelessness','B','Creating crafts like bags and wallets requires imagination and artistic skill, which are signs of creativity, a key PEC.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,2,NULL,'John helps his father sell vegetables in the market. What kind of job opportunity does this relate to? Choose the most appropriate job category.','Cooking in restaurant','Farming and trading','Playing','Painting','B','Selling vegetables is a form of trading or agricultural entrepreneurship, not entertainment or art.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,3,NULL,'Carlo is good at talking to people and convincing them to buy things. What PEC does Carlo have?','Shyness','Persuasiveness','Laziness','Fearfulness','B','Convincing others to buy is a clear example of persuasion, a useful skill in marketing or sales-related entrepreneurship.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,4,NULL,'Gina knows how to bake bread and cookies. Which job matches her skill?','Bicycle repair','Barber','Baker','Tailor','C','Gina’s skill in baking matches the job of a baker, not a mechanic or barber.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,5,NULL,'Ana is good at expressing her thoughts clearly and listening to others. What Personal Entrepreneurial Characteristic (PEC) does she show?','Keep making accessories and give them away for free','Sell her handmade accessories online or in local markets','Focus on learning construction skills','Apply for a job unrelated to crafting','B','Aligning her hobby with an income-generating activity shows entrepreneurial thinking and matches PECs with job opportunities.',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,6,NULL,'Pedro is good at baking, has patience, and pays attention to detail. He wants to start a small business. Which job opportunity best suits his personal entrepreneurial competencies?','Tricycle driver','Online selling of gadgets','Home-based bakery','Construction worker','C','His skills and traits match well with starting a bakery, using his PECs in a suitable business.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,7,NULL,'Teacher asked Jay, “Which of the following is an example of a Personal Entrepreneurial Competency (PEC)?” Jay must pick the correct one. Which of these is a Personal Entrepreneurial Competency?','Tall height','Patience','Favorite color','Shoe size','B','Among the options, only patience is a Personal Entrepreneurial',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,8,NULL,'Mila always finishes her tasks on time even when no one is watching. TASK: Which PEC does Mila show?','Laziness','Self-confidence','Self-discipline','Risk-taking','C','Mila demonstrates self-discipline, a PEC that shows responsibility and internal motivation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,9,NULL,'Antonio reads a chart listing different Personal Entrepreneurial Competencies (PECs). One of them is “Persistence – not giving up even when facing challenges in business.” Which PEC from the chart describes Antonio’s behavior?','Patience','Creativity','Persistence','Talkativeness','C','Antonio continues working hard even when business is slow, which shows he does not give up easily.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,10,NULL,'Carlo asks, “Which of the following is a Personal Entrepreneurial Competency (PEC)?” Choose the correct answer. Which one is a PEC?','Dishwashing','Creativity','Shoe size','Tall height','B','Creativity is a core PEC. Shoe size and height are not related to entrepreneurial skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,11,NULL,'Pedro always wakes up early to prepare his goods for selling. What Personal Entrepreneurial Competency does Pedro show?','Laziness','Hard work','Dishonesty','Sleepiness','B','Waking up early and preparing goods shows dedication and hard work, an essential PEC.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,12,NULL,'Which of the following is a key Personal Entrepreneurial Competency?','Cheating','Confidence','Shyness','Laziness','B','Confidence helps entrepreneurs make decisions and deal with people. The other choices are negative traits',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,13,NULL,'Rico reads about Mang Ramon, a successful baker in his town. Rico wants to know what helped Mang Ramon succeed. Which of the following is a quality that that will help Mang Ramon?','Laziness','Creativity','Impatience','Dishonesty','B','As a baker, Mang Ramon likely used creativity to invent recipes or designs, contributing to his success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,14,NULL,'Which of the following is a common quality of a successful person?','Laziness','Dishonesty','Hardworking','Carelessness','C','Hard work is one of the most important and common PECs of successful individuals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,15,NULL,'Rosa always studies her lessons, listens carefully, and asks questions when she does not understand. What trait is Rosa showing?','Determination','Carelessness','Disobedience','Confusion','A','Rosa is showing determination to learn and succeed, a key trait in both school and entrepreneurship.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,16,'In a small barangay, several individuals have earned the respect of the community. Aling Rosa runs a small store and is known for being honest and fair to customers. Mang Jun is a farmer who works hard and helps neighbors during harvest time. Ate Liza is a teacher who volunteers to tutor out-of-school youth. They are all considered successful by the people in the community.','What should a person do to become like these successful individuals in the community?','Ignore other people’s needs','Work hard, be fair, and help others','Focus only on making money','Wait for others to offer help first','B','The story highlights three individuals who: • Work hard (Mang Jun, the farmer) • Are fair and honest (Aling Rosa, the store owner) • Are helpful and generous (Ate Liza, the volunteer teacher)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,17,'In a small barangay, several individuals have earned the respect of the community. Aling Rosa runs a small store and is known for being honest and fair to customers. Mang Jun is a farmer who works hard and helps neighbors during harvest time. Ate Liza is a teacher who volunteers to tutor out-of-school youth. They are all considered successful by the people in the community.','What common quality is shared by Aling Rosa, Mang Jun, and Ate Liza that makes them successful in their own ways?','Laziness','Greed','Helpfulness','Dishonesty','C','Each person contributes to the community by helping others',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,18,'In Barangay Maligaya, countless individuals are admired for their contributions. Mang Berto, a retired carpenter, helps repair the barangay hall for free. Aling Nena, a sewer, teaches young mothers how to sew and earn income. Tatay Carlo, a farmer, shares his harvest with poor families and teaches sustainable gardening. The people in the community are thankful for their service.','What impact does Aling Nena’s work have on the young mothers in her community?','It helps them learn a skill and earn income','It forces them to buy sewing machines','It prevents them from working','It gives them free time to watch TV','A','The story says Aling Nena teaches young mothers how to sew and earn income. This clearly benefits the mothers by giving them a useful skill (sewing) and the opportunity to earn money.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,19,'In Barangay Maligaya, countless individuals are admired for their contributions. Mang Berto, a retired carpenter, helps repair the barangay hall for free. Aling Nena, a sewer, teaches young mothers how to sew and earn income. Tatay Carlo, a farmer, shares his harvest with poor families and teaches sustainable gardening. The people in the community are thankful for their service.','What contribution did Mang Berto make to the community?','He started a business for himself','He repaired the barangay hall for free','He opened a store','He collected garbage','B','The passage clearly states that Mang Berto helps repair the barangay hall for free. This is a community service showing dedication and generosity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,20,'In Barangay Maligaya, countless individuals are admired for their contributions. Mang Berto, a retired carpenter, helps repair the barangay hall for free. Aling Nena, a sewer, teaches young mothers how to sew and earn income. Tatay Carlo, a farmer, shares his harvest with poor families and teaches sustainable gardening. The people in the community are thankful for their service.','Which value is shown by Tatay Carlo through his contributions to the community?','Selfishness','Greed','Generosity','Laziness','C','Tatay Carlo shares his harvest with poor families and teaches sustainable gardening. These are acts of generosity—giving without expecting something in return and sharing knowledge.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,21,'In a community career fair, successful individuals shared their stories. Engineer Liza started as a working student but finished her degree and now builds houses for low- income families. Chef Mario trained abroad, returned home, and opened a restaurant employing out-of-school youth. Nurse Carla volunteered during health missions and is now a head nurse at a local hospital. They are admired for their achievements and dedication.','Which of the following individuals succeeded as a nurse?','Architect Jonel','Chef Mario','Nurse Carla','Social Worker Mina','C','The story says: "Nurse Carla volunteered during health missions and is now a head nurse at a local hospital." This clearly shows that Carla is the one who became a successful nurse.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,22,'In a community career fair, successful individuals shared their stories. Engineer Liza started as a working student but finished her degree and now builds houses for low- income families. Chef Mario trained abroad, returned home, and opened a restaurant employing out-of-school youth. Nurse Carla volunteered during health missions and is now a head nurse at a local hospital. They are admired for their achievements and dedication.','What action helped Engineer Liza succeed in her career?','She stopped school and looked for work','She depended on her parents for everything','She worked while studying to earn her degree','She stayed at home and waited for opportunities','C','The passage says: "Engineer Liza started as a working student but finished her degree...” This means she worked hard and studied at the same time, which shows determination and perseverance, leading to her success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,23,'Mark is a Grade 10 learner who wants to improve himself and prepare for future job opportunities. He started writing a simple Personal Development Plan (PDP). His goals include finishing high school, learning basic computer skills, and building self-confidence. He also listed activities like attending ALS classes regularly, enrolling in a free computer training course, and joining group discussions to improve communication.','What is one of Mark’s goals in his Personal Development Plan (PDP)?','To become famous','To avoid school','To build self-confidence','To improve study habits','C','The story clearly states that Mark’s goals include: • Finishing high school • Learning basic computer skills • Building self-confidence',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,24,'Mark is a Grade 10 learner who wants to improve himself and prepare for future job opportunities. He started writing a simple Personal Development Plan (PDP). His goals include finishing high school, learning basic computer skills, and building self-confidence. He also listed activities like attending ALS classes regularly, enrolling in a free computer training course, and joining group discussions to improve communication.','Mark wants to improve the way he talks and listens to others. Which activity will best help him achieve this goal?','Playing online games','Joining group discussions','Sleeping longer','Watching movies alone','B','One of Mark’s activities is “joining group discussions to improve communication”. This clearly shows that B is the best answer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,1,25,'Mark is a Grade 10 learner who wants to improve himself and prepare for future job opportunities. He started writing a simple Personal Development Plan (PDP). His goals include finishing high school, learning basic computer skills, and building self-confidence. He also listed activities like attending ALS classes regularly, enrolling in a free computer training course, and joining group discussions to improve communication.','What is the connection between attending ALS classes regularly and Mark’s goal of finishing high school?','ALS classes offer an alternative pathway to completing high school education','ALS classes are not related to his goal','ALS classes only focus on job training, not academics','ALS classes are only for adults, not teenagers','A','Mark is attending ALS classes regularly as part of his goal to finish high school. ALS (Alternative Learning System) provides non-formal education for learners like Mark to complete their basic education outside the traditional school setting.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,26,'Lara is a high school student who wants to improve her math grades. She decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Her goal is to raise her grade from a C to a B in the next two months. To achieve this, she plans to do the following: • Study for one hour every day after school • Ask her teacher for extra help once a week • Practice math problems on an online app','Why is Lara’s goal of improving her math grade from a C to a B considered a personal development goal?','Because it helps her become more popular at school','Because it contributes to her academic growth and self-improvement','Because her parents want her to improve','Because she wants to avoid doing homework','B','It connects her goal to the broader concept of personal development, which is a key aspect of critical thinking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,27,'Lara is a high school student who wants to improve her math grades. She decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Her goal is to raise her grade from a C to a B in the next two months. To achieve this, she plans to do the following: • Study for one hour every day after school • Ask her teacher for extra help once a week • Practice math problems on an online app','Where can Lara get reliable help to understand math better?','Her teacher or an online math app','Random social media posts','A comedy shows','A cooking blog','A','Lara’s teacher and online math apps are good sources for learning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,28,'Lara is a high school student who wants to improve her math grades. She decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Her goal is to raise her grade from a C to a B in the next two months. To achieve this, she plans to do the following: • Study for one hour every day after school • Ask her teacher for extra help once a week • Practice math problems on an online app','Which of the following is the most effective study habit Lara can include in her routine to help improve her math grade?','Study for one hour every day after school','Wait until the night before the exam to study','Study for hours without taking breaks','Skip math homework','A','Studying for one hour daily after school is an effective and manageable habit that promotes consistency and prevents cramming.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,29,'Lara is a high school student who wants to improve her math grades. She decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Her goal is to raise her grade from a C to a B in the next two months. To achieve this, she plans to do the following: • Study for one hour every day after school • Ask her teacher for extra help once a week • Practice math problems on an online app','What should Lara do if she has trouble understanding some math topics?','Ask her teacher for extra help once a week','Ignore the problem and do nothing','Skip those topics completely','Copy someone else’s work','A','Seeking help from the teacher when needed ensures that Lara gets the support to overcome difficulties.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,30,'Alice is a high school student who wants to improve her time management skills. She feels that she often procrastinates, which affects her school performance. She creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) with the goal of improving her ability to manage time effectively. Alice plans to: • Set clear daily goals each morning. • Use a planner to track her assignments. • Focus on one task at a time instead of multitasking. • Avoid distractions like her phone during study time.','What is Alice’s main goal in her personal development plan?','To improve her time management skills','To read more books','To become better at sports','To take more breaks during study time','A','Alice’s goal is focused on managing her time better, which is the key focus of her personal development plan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,31,'Alice is a high school student who wants to improve her time management skills. She feels that she often procrastinates, which affects her school performance. She creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) with the goal of improving her ability to manage time effectively. Alice plans to: • Set clear daily goals each morning. • Use a planner to track her assignments. • Focus on one task at a time instead of multitasking. • Avoid distractions like her phone during study time.','What would be a reliable way for Alice to track her assignments?','Using a planner','Writing them on a napkin','Memorizing them without writing anything down','Asking her friends to remind her','A','A planner is a practical, reliable tool for tracking assignments. Information literacy involves using tools or resources that will help organize tasks effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,32,'Alice is a high school student who wants to improve her time management skills. She feels that she often procrastinates, which affects her school performance. She creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) with the goal of improving her ability to manage time effectively. Alice plans to: • Set clear daily goals each morning. • Use a planner to track her assignments. • Focus on one task at a time instead of multitasking. • Avoid distractions like her phone during study time.','What should Alice do to avoid distractions while studying?','Keep her phone away from her study area','Leave her phone next to her and check it often','Study while watching TV','Multitask with homework and chatting online','A','To solve the problem of distractions, keeping her phone away helps Alice stay focused on her study tasks, which is a simple but effective solution.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,33,'Alice is a high school student who wants to improve her time management skills. She feels that she often procrastinates, which affects her school performance. She creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) with the goal of improving her ability to manage time effectively. Alice plans to: • Set clear daily goals each morning. • Use a planner to track her assignments. • Focus on one task at a time instead of multitasking. • Avoid distractions like her phone during study time.','What is the first step Alice should take to begin her personal development plan?','Set clear daily goals each morning','Start studying without any plan','Skip setting a goal and just hope for the best','Only focus on one task once a week','A','The first step in any plan is to set clear goals. Alice should start each day by deciding what she wants to accomplish, which will guide her time management process.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,34,'Jake is a student who wants to improve his public speaking skills. He recognizes that he struggles with nervousness when speaking in front of groups. To address this, he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that includes the following elements: Name: Jake Martinez Date: October 10, 2025 Time frame: 2 months (until December 10, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve public speaking skills by giving at least one speech or presentation every week. Why this Goal: Jake wants to become more confident and effective at communicating in front of an audience. Action Steps: • Practice speaking in front of a mirror for 10 minutes every day. • Deliver a speech to a small group of friends once a week. • Record each speech to identify areas of improvement. • Attend a public speaking workshop. Resources Needed: Mirror, a small group of friends, recording device, public speaking workshop, books on public speaking. Measurement of Success: Jake feels more confident when speaking in front of a group and receives positive feedback on his speeches. Jake is ready to follow his plan to improve his public speaking over the next two months.','What is Jake’s main goal in his personal development plan?','To improve public speaking skills','To stop being nervous about presentations','To attend a public speaking workshop','To memorize speeches word for word','A','Jake’s overall goal is to become a more confident and effective communicator, which he aims to achieve by practicing speeches regularly and attending workshops. The other options describe parts of the process or misunderstandings of effective public speaking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,35,'Jake is a student who wants to improve his public speaking skills. He recognizes that he struggles with nervousness when speaking in front of groups. To address this, he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that includes the following elements: Name: Jake Martinez Date: October 10, 2025 Time frame: 2 months (until December 10, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve public speaking skills by giving at least one speech or presentation every week. Why this Goal: Jake wants to become more confident and effective at communicating in front of an audience. Action Steps: • Practice speaking in front of a mirror for 10 minutes every day. • Deliver a speech to a small group of friends once a week. • Record each speech to identify areas of improvement. • Attend a public speaking workshop. Resources Needed: Mirror, a small group of friends, recording device, public speaking workshop, books on public speaking. Measurement of Success: Jake feels more confident when speaking in front of a group and receives positive feedback on his speeches. Jake is ready to follow his plan to improve his public speaking over the next two months.','What resources will Jake need to achieve his public speaking goal?','Mirror, friends, recording device, workshop materials','Only books on public speaking','A microphone for practicing speeches','A new phone','A','Jake’s resources are varied and useful for practicing and improving his public speaking. These resources will support his efforts to develop confidence and skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,36,'Jake is a student who wants to improve his public speaking skills. He recognizes that he struggles with nervousness when speaking in front of groups. To address this, he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that includes the following elements: Name: Jake Martinez Date: October 10, 2025 Time frame: 2 months (until December 10, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve public speaking skills by giving at least one speech or presentation every week. Why this Goal: Jake wants to become more confident and effective at communicating in front of an audience. Action Steps: • Practice speaking in front of a mirror for 10 minutes every day. • Deliver a speech to a small group of friends once a week. • Record each speech to identify areas of improvement. • Attend a public speaking workshop. Resources Needed: Mirror, a small group of friends, recording device, public speaking workshop, books on public speaking. Measurement of Success: Jake feels more confident when speaking in front of a group and receives positive feedback on his speeches. Jake is ready to follow his plan to improve his public speaking over the next two months.','If Jake is still feeling nervous about his speeches after a few weeks, what should he do next?','Continue practicing and seek feedback from others','Stop giving speeches and avoid the problem','Skip the recording and feedback step','Rely only on the public speaking workshop','A','If Jake still feels nervous, continued practice and feedback from others are essential for improving and addressing his nervousness, not avoiding the issue.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,37,'Jake is a student who wants to improve his public speaking skills. He recognizes that he struggles with nervousness when speaking in front of groups. To address this, he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that includes the following elements: Name: Jake Martinez Date: October 10, 2025 Time frame: 2 months (until December 10, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve public speaking skills by giving at least one speech or presentation every week. Why this Goal: Jake wants to become more confident and effective at communicating in front of an audience. Action Steps: • Practice speaking in front of a mirror for 10 minutes every day. • Deliver a speech to a small group of friends once a week. • Record each speech to identify areas of improvement. • Attend a public speaking workshop. Resources Needed: Mirror, a small group of friends, recording device, public speaking workshop, books on public speaking. Measurement of Success: Jake feels more confident when speaking in front of a group and receives positive feedback on his speeches. Jake is ready to follow his plan to improve his public speaking over the next two months.','Why does Jake need to set a timeline in his personal development plan?','It helps him stay focused and measure progress within a specific period','It allows him to delay his public speaking goal indefinitely','It provides no real purpose in his development plan','It forces him to complete his plan quickly without any breaks','A','The timeframe creates a sense of urgency and structure, allowing Jake to measure his progress over the next two months and stay focused on his goal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,38,'Sophia is a college student who wants to improve her time management skills. She has often felt overwhelmed with her studies and extracurricular activities, so she decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her manage her time more effectively. Her plan includes the following key elements: Name: Sophia Reyes Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 1 month (until November 5, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve time management by completing all assignments a day before their deadlines. Why this Goal: Sophia wants to reduce stress and improve her grades by being more organized with her time. Action Steps: • Create a weekly schedule every Sunday night. • Set specific time blocks for studying, exercise, and rest each day. • Prioritize assignments based on deadlines. • Use a time tracking app to monitor her progress. Resources Needed: Weekly planner, time tracking app, reminders, a quiet study space. Measurement of Success: Completing all assignments a day before their deadlines and feeling less stressed. Sophia is now ready to follow her personal development plan to improve her time management skills over the next month.','Why did Sophia choose to set the goal of completing her assignments a day before the deadline in her Personal Development Plan?','Because she wants to avoid using a time tracking app','Because she wants to reduce stress and improve her academic performance','Because her friends told her to','Because she has fewer extracurricular activities','B','Sophia''s reason for setting her goal is clearly stated in her Personal Development Plan: "Sophia wants to reduce stress and improve her grades by being more organized with her time." By completing her assignments a day early, she aims to be more proactive, lessen last-minute pressure, and ultimately perform better in school.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,39,'Sophia is a college student who wants to improve her time management skills. She has often felt overwhelmed with her studies and extracurricular activities, so she decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her manage her time more effectively. Her plan includes the following key elements: Name: Sophia Reyes Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 1 month (until November 5, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve time management by completing all assignments a day before their deadlines. Why this Goal: Sophia wants to reduce stress and improve her grades by being more organized with her time. Action Steps: • Create a weekly schedule every Sunday night. • Set specific time blocks for studying, exercise, and rest each day. • Prioritize assignments based on deadlines. • Use a time tracking app to monitor her progress. Resources Needed: Weekly planner, time tracking app, reminders, a quiet study space. Measurement of Success: Completing all assignments a day before their deadlines and feeling less stressed. Sophia is now ready to follow her personal development plan to improve her time management skills over the next month.','What resources will Sophia need to keep track of her time and progress?','Weekly planner and time tracking app','A new study textbook','A secondhand computer','Extra study materials','A','Sophia uses a weekly planner and a time tracking app to stay organized and monitor her progress, which are essential tools for improving her time management.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,40,'Sophia is a college student who wants to improve her time management skills. She has often felt overwhelmed with her studies and extracurricular activities, so she decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her manage her time more effectively. Her plan includes the following key elements: Name: Sophia Reyes Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 1 month (until November 5, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve time management by completing all assignments a day before their deadlines. Why this Goal: Sophia wants to reduce stress and improve her grades by being more organized with her time. Action Steps: • Create a weekly schedule every Sunday night. • Set specific time blocks for studying, exercise, and rest each day. • Prioritize assignments based on deadlines. • Use a time tracking app to monitor her progress. Resources Needed: Weekly planner, time tracking app, reminders, a quiet study space. Measurement of Success: Completing all assignments a day before their deadlines and feeling less stressed. Sophia is now ready to follow her personal development plan to improve her time management skills over the next month.','If Sophia starts missing deadlines, what should she do next?','Review her weekly schedule and adjust her time blocks','Stop using the time tracking app','Complete assignments in a rushed manner','Stop planning and continue as usual','A','If Sophia starts missing deadlines, adjusting her schedule and time blocks is a practical solution to manage her time more effectively and stay on track.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,41,'Sophia is a college student who wants to improve her time management skills. She has often felt overwhelmed with her studies and extracurricular activities, so she decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her manage her time more effectively. Her plan includes the following key elements: Name: Sophia Reyes Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 1 month (until November 5, 2025) Goal Setting: Improve time management by completing all assignments a day before their deadlines. Why this Goal: Sophia wants to reduce stress and improve her grades by being more organized with her time. Action Steps: • Create a weekly schedule every Sunday night. • Set specific time blocks for studying, exercise, and rest each day. • Prioritize assignments based on deadlines. • Use a time tracking app to monitor her progress. Resources Needed: Weekly planner, time tracking app, reminders, a quiet study space. Measurement of Success: Completing all assignments a day before their deadlines and feeling less stressed. Sophia is now ready to follow her personal development plan to improve her time management skills over the next month.','Why is it important for Sophia to set a timeframe in her personal development plan?','It helps her stay focused on achieving her time management goal within a specific period.','It allows her to procrastinate until the last minute','It has no real impact on her goal achievement','It encourages her to spend all her time on assignments','A','Setting a timeframe provides structure and urgency to Sophia’s goal, helping her stay motivated to complete her tasks within the set period.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,42,'Emily is a recent graduate who has just started her first job as a marketing assistant. Although she’s excited, she’s also feeling a bit uncertain about managing her responsibilities and achieving her career goals. To ensure success, Emily decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help her focus on both her professional and personal growth. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following elements: Name: Emily Thompson Date: September 15, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until March 15, 2026) Goal Setting: Improve time management skills, gain leadership experience, and enhance communication abilities. Why this Goal: Emily wants to grow in her career, develop leadership skills, and build strong relationships with her colleagues. Action Steps: Set daily and weekly goals to manage time better. Volunteer for small leadership opportunities at work. Attend a communication skills workshop. Resources Needed: Time management tools, leadership training programs, communication books, feedback from mentors. Measurement of Success: Completing goals on time, receiving positive feedback from her supervisor, and feeling more confident in her leadership abilities. By creating this plan, Emily believes it will help her advance in her career while balancing her personal growth.','Why did Emily decide to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) at the start of her new job?','To get a promotion in the next month','To focus on her career and personal growth','To avoid making mistakes at work','To stop feeling nervous about her job','B','Emily’s PDP is designed to help her improve time management, gain leadership experience, and enhance communication — all of which support her long-term career advancement and personal development, not just short-term fixes or promotions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,43,'Emily is a recent graduate who has just started her first job as a marketing assistant. Although she’s excited, she’s also feeling a bit uncertain about managing her responsibilities and achieving her career goals. To ensure success, Emily decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help her focus on both her professional and personal growth. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following elements: Name: Emily Thompson Date: September 15, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until March 15, 2026) Goal Setting: Improve time management skills, gain leadership experience, and enhance communication abilities. Why this Goal: Emily wants to grow in her career, develop leadership skills, and build strong relationships with her colleagues. Action Steps: Set daily and weekly goals to manage time better. Volunteer for small leadership opportunities at work. Attend a communication skills workshop. Resources Needed: Time management tools, leadership training programs, communication books, feedback from mentors. Measurement of Success: Completing goals on time, receiving positive feedback from her supervisor, and feeling more confident in her leadership abilities. By creating this plan, Emily believes it will help her advance in her career while balancing her personal growth.','Which resource will Emily use to improve her communication skills?','Leadership Training Programs','Communication Skills Workshop','Time Management Tools','Feedback from Mentors','B','To improve her communication skills, Emily plans to attend a communication workshop, which is a targeted resource that will directly help her in this area.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,44,'Emily is a recent graduate who has just started her first job as a marketing assistant. Although she’s excited, she’s also feeling a bit uncertain about managing her responsibilities and achieving her career goals. To ensure success, Emily decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help her focus on both her professional and personal growth. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following elements: Name: Emily Thompson Date: September 15, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until March 15, 2026) Goal Setting: Improve time management skills, gain leadership experience, and enhance communication abilities. Why this Goal: Emily wants to grow in her career, develop leadership skills, and build strong relationships with her colleagues. Action Steps: Set daily and weekly goals to manage time better. Volunteer for small leadership opportunities at work. Attend a communication skills workshop. Resources Needed: Time management tools, leadership training programs, communication books, feedback from mentors. Measurement of Success: Completing goals on time, receiving positive feedback from her supervisor, and feeling more confident in her leadership abilities. By creating this plan, Emily believes it will help her advance in her career while balancing her personal growth.','If Emily faces difficulty completing her goals on time, what should she do next?','Reassess her goals and adjust the timeframe','Continue to work without making any changes','Seek help or advice from a mentor or supervisor','Quit the Personal Development Plan','A','The most effective way for Emily to handle challenges in meeting her goals is to evaluate her current plan and make necessary adjustments. While seeking help (Option C) is a good support strategy, reassessing and modifying the plan directly addresses the core issue—making it the best next step.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,45,'Maria, a 22-year-old graduate from Quezon City, Philippines, recently started working as a marketing assistant in a local company. After a few months on the job, she realizes that to move up in her career, she needs to improve her skills in communication, digital marketing, and time management. Maria decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her stay on track. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following basic elements: Name: Maria Santos Date: June 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until December 1, 2025) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills. • Learn digital marketing strategies. • Manage time better for work-life balance. Why this Goal: Maria wants to be more effective in her role and increase her chances of promotion by developing relevant skills. Action Steps: • Attend communication and digital marketing webinars. • Use a time management app to track daily tasks. • Read marketing books and apply learning in her work. Resources Needed: Access to webinars, time management tools, and marketing books. Measurement of Success: • Feeling more confident during presentations. • Successfully completing a digital marketing project. • Having better control over her work schedule.','What is the main purpose of Maria’s Personal Development Plan (PDP)?','To focus only on her personal goals','To improve her skills and advance in her career','To make her work easier without learning new skills','To avoid any professional development at all','B','Maria’s PDP is designed to help her improve her skills and prepare for career advancement through focused goal-setting and actionable steps.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,46,'Maria, a 22-year-old graduate from Quezon City, Philippines, recently started working as a marketing assistant in a local company. After a few months on the job, she realizes that to move up in her career, she needs to improve her skills in communication, digital marketing, and time management. Maria decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her stay on track. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following basic elements: Name: Maria Santos Date: June 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until December 1, 2025) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills. • Learn digital marketing strategies. • Manage time better for work-life balance. Why this Goal: Maria wants to be more effective in her role and increase her chances of promotion by developing relevant skills. Action Steps: • Attend communication and digital marketing webinars. • Use a time management app to track daily tasks. • Read marketing books and apply learning in her work. Resources Needed: Access to webinars, time management tools, and marketing books. Measurement of Success: • Feeling more confident during presentations. • Successfully completing a digital marketing project. • Having better control over her work schedule.','Which of the following is one of the resources Maria needs to achieve her goal of improving communication skills?','Marketing books','Time management app','Communication webinars','Presentation software','C','Maria wants to improve her communication skills, so attending communication webinars is a resource that will directly help her achieve this goal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,47,'Maria, a 22-year-old graduate from Quezon City, Philippines, recently started working as a marketing assistant in a local company. After a few months on the job, she realizes that to move up in her career, she needs to improve her skills in communication, digital marketing, and time management. Maria decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to help her stay on track. Her Personal Development Plan includes the following basic elements: Name: Maria Santos Date: June 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until December 1, 2025) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills. • Learn digital marketing strategies. • Manage time better for work-life balance. Why this Goal: Maria wants to be more effective in her role and increase her chances of promotion by developing relevant skills. Action Steps: • Attend communication and digital marketing webinars. • Use a time management app to track daily tasks. • Read marketing books and apply learning in her work. Resources Needed: Access to webinars, time management tools, and marketing books. Measurement of Success: • Feeling more confident during presentations. • Successfully completing a digital marketing project. • Having better control over her work schedule.','If Maria feels overwhelmed with managing both work tasks and her personal life, what should she do?','Ignore time management and focus only on work','Use a time management app to organize and track tasks','Take a break from work entirely','Forget about personal development','B','By using a time management app, Maria can better organize her tasks, helping her manage her work responsibilities and personal life effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,48,'Juan, a 19-year-old high school graduate from Cebu City, is exploring different career paths before deciding what to pursue after graduation. He is particularly interested in four sectors: Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA). Juan wants to understand the unique aspects of each field so he can choose a career path that fits his interests and strengths.','Which of the following is the main focus of the Information and Communication Technology (ICT) sector?','Enhancing food production and resource management','Improving communication, data management, and technology use','Providing family counseling and household management skills','Creating products using mechanical skills and tools','B','The ICT sector is primarily focused on the use of technology for communication, managing data, and enhancing digital systems, which is different from the other sectors that focus on hands-on work or service-based roles.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,49,'Juan, a 19-year-old high school graduate from Cebu City, is exploring different career paths before deciding what to pursue after graduation. He is particularly interested in four sectors: Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA). Juan wants to understand the unique aspects of each field so he can choose a career path that fits his interests and strengths.','Which of the following best describes the Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA) sector?','Working with animals, plants, and natural resources for food production','Designing furniture and tools using machines','Offering counseling services for families and individuals','Using computers for various digital tasks','A','AFA focuses on agriculture, aquaculture, and natural resource management. This sector is centered around food production and sustainable use of natural resources, unlike ICT, which involves technology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,2,50,'Juan, a 19-year-old high school graduate from Cebu City, is exploring different career paths before deciding what to pursue after graduation. He is particularly interested in four sectors: Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA). Juan wants to understand the unique aspects of each field so he can choose a career path that fits his interests and strengths.','If Juan enjoys working with computers and technology, which sector should he focus on?','Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA)','Family and Consumer Services (FCS)','Industrial Arts (IA)','Information and Communication Technology (ICT)','D','Since Juan enjoys working with computers and technology, the ICT sector would be the best fit for him. ICT focuses on digital systems, software, and communication technologies, which aligns with his interest in technology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,51,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, Grade 9 students are learning about different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. Their teacher, Ma’am Liza, asks them to describe the basic ideas of each area — Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA) — as they relate to common jobs found in their town.','What is one thing you learn in ICT?','How to plant vegetables','How to use a computer','How to cook rice','How to sew clothes','B','This shows a basic understanding of ICT, which includes learning computer skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,52,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, Grade 9 students are learning about different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. Their teacher, Ma’am Liza, asks them to describe the basic ideas of each area — Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA) — as they relate to common jobs found in their town.','What is Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA) about?','Cleaning the house','Fixing electric tools','Farming and fishing','Using the internet','C','AFA focuses on agricultural and fishing skills, showing basic recall of its area.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,53,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, Grade 9 students are learning about different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. Their teacher, Ma’am Liza, asks them to describe the basic ideas of each area — Information and Communication Technology (ICT), Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA), Family and Consumer Services (FCS), and Industrial Arts (IA) — as they relate to common jobs found in their town.','How can Industrial Arts help someone in Barangay Maligaya?','By teaching how to bake cakes','By teaching how to use email','By teaching how to fix things','By teaching how to swim','C','IA provides hands-on skills like repairing, helpful for solving local problems.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,54,NULL,'Your community has plenty of farms growing vegetables and raising animals. What is the single most important advantage of having these farms?','More pollution in the area','Employment opportunities for','Less space for houses','Higher prices for food agricultural workers','B','Fixing computers and designing digital posters fall under ICT.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,55,NULL,'People in your town often travel far to find a good place to eat. What one important job opportunity does this situation suggest?','People should eat at home','There is a need for food service','Buses should run more often','Food is better in other towns workers','B','Farming and aquaculture are core components of AFA.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,56,NULL,'The community website keeps crashing when people try to access local services. Which one specialist should solve this?','Web Developer','Animal Caretaker','Interior Designer','Plumber','A','Tailoring and teaching cooking are activities related to FCS.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,57,NULL,'A new manufacturing facility offers several benefits to the community. What are they?','Only makes products','Creates industrial jobs, provides technical training, and supports local businesses','Just uses water resources','Only benefits factory owners','B','A new manufacturing facility can be a major contributor to community development. It creates employment opportunities, helping residents earn a living; provides technical training, which upgrades local skills and employability; and supports local businesses through supply chains, partnerships, and increased demand for goods and services.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,58,NULL,'A smart farming project is launching in your community. How would specialists from different sectors work together effectively?','Only farmers work on the project','AFA specialists manage crops, ICT specialists implement monitoring systems, and IA specialists maintain equipment','Only ICT specialists handle everything','Only IA specialists are needed','B','AFA focuses on food production through agriculture and aquaculture.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,59,NULL,'In a construction site, you observe workers doing MULTIPLE tasks. Which combination of Industrial Arts specializations are they most likely using?','Web design and coding','Carpentry, masonry, and electrical work','Cooking and baking','Farming and fishing','B','FCS deals with household management, family care, and consumer education.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,60,NULL,'The community center needs someone to teach basic computer skills. Who is the one right specialist for this job?','ICT Training Instructor','Fish Farmer','Baker','Carpenter','A','This is a key AFA activity focused on fishery production.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,61,NULL,'The school cafeteria needs help planning better food storage. Which ONE specialist should they consult?','Website Designer','Rice Farmer','Food Safety Specialist','Mechanic','C','A core function of FCS is to teach healthy and effective home and food practices.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,62,NULL,'A local shop needs their cash register system fixed. Which SINGLE specialist should they call?','Point-of-Sale Systems Technician','Gardener','Tailor','Plumber','A','AFA workers must understand how to manage aquatic farming systems.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,63,NULL,'John creates furniture by working with wood in his workshop. Which ONE sector specialization matches his work?','ICT - Data Entry','IA - Carpentry and Woodworking','FCS - Interior Design','AFA - Landscaping','B','Diagnosing before acting ensures the right treatment for plant issues.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,64,NULL,'Your community is developing a new marketplace. Which combination of specialists from different sectors would be needed to make this project successful?','Only ICT specialists for the website','Only construction workers from IA','ICT specialists for digital systems, IA specialists for construction, and FCS specialists for food stalls','Only FCS specialists for food preparation','C','Fish gasping at the surface often indicates a lack of oxygen.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,65,NULL,'Lisa watches her aunt perform TWO main jobs: designing websites and creating digital artwork for companies. Which sector and specialization are this?','IA – Construction','FCS - Fashion Design','ICT - Digital Arts and Web Design','AFA – Landscaping','C','Area = length × width; divide by spacing (4) to get number of plants.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,66,NULL,'At a house fire, you observe someone wearing protective gear and using special equipment to put out the flames. Which professional training would this person need?','Police academy training','medical school education','Firefighter certification','Emergency medical technician license','C','Climate affects what crops can grow and when, so it’s a top priority in planning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,67,NULL,'Lisa is working on a class presentation. She needs to show Both her research skills and speaking abilities. What approach demonstrates the best work readiness?','Reading directly from her notes without making eye contact','Making an organized presentation with clear speaking and good eye contact','Having a friend present for her','Using only pictures without any explanation','B','Assessing the problem allows for targeted, cost-effective solutions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,68,NULL,'Maria arrives at school 10 minutes before the bell rings every day. Which important work readiness skill is she demonstrating?','Punctuality','Creativity','Computer skills','Leadership.','A','Start with eco-friendly solutions before turning to chemicals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,69,NULL,'"In their town, there is a Christmas tree farm that hires extra workers during the holiday season to help with tree sales. After the holidays, the farm doesn''t need as many workers.” How do seasonal businesses affect community job opportunities?','They reduce job opportunities for everyone','They stop all businesses from opening','They make people work all year long','They provide jobs only during certain times of the year','D','Water temperature greatly affects fish metabolism and growth.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,70,NULL,'"Liam is choosing what kind of job he might want in the future. His teacher explains that some jobs, like being a doctor or a teacher, are always needed, while other jobs might only be available sometimes. Liam wants a job that he can keep for a long time.” Why should Liam consider the stability of different employment sectors?','So he can find a job that lasts longer and is more secure','So he can switch jobs every week','So he can avoid working with people','So he can get paid for doing nothing','A','Compost enriches soil and boosts nitrogen levels naturally.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,71,NULL,'"Mark helps his uncle repair computers and install new software. He is learning how to solve basic computer problems.” What sector does this belong to?','Agri-Fishery Arts','Family and Consumer Services','ICT','Industrial Arts','C','Environment and nutrition directly impact egg production in poultry.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,72,NULL,'Jenny’s grandmother taught her how to cook meals and bake pastries. Jenny dreams of having her own bakery someday.” What specialization is this?','ICT','Family and Consumer Services','Industrial Arts','Agri-Fishery Arts','B','The skills Jenny is developing—cooking, baking, and planning for a future food business—fall under Family and Consumer Services, which focuses on home economics, culinary arts, and food-related services. The other options are not directly connected to food preparation or consumer-related skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,73,NULL,'"Leo wakes up early to help his parents plant vegetables and feed the chickens. He wants to become a farmer someday. “What sector is Leo interested in?','Agri-Fishery Arts','ICT','Family and Consumer Services','Industrial Arts','A','Leo helps his parents plant vegetables and feed chickens, which are both activities directly related to agriculture and animal production.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,74,NULL,'Which of the following indicates that someone is prepared for work or school?','Arriving late and unprepared','Finishing tasks only when reminded','Coming on time with the needed materials','Waiting for others to do your job','C','Arriving on time and being equipped with necessary tools or materials demonstrates reliability, responsibility, and readiness—key work readiness skills highlighted in Learning Strand 4.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',1,3,75,NULL,'"Tomas is learning how to build small shelves and wooden chairs in his grandfather’s workshop. What specialization is Tomas practicing?"','Family and Consumer Services','Industrial Arts','ICT','Agri-Fishery Arts','B','Tomas’s hands-on activity – constructing wooden shelves and chairs – is directly related to carpentry and woodworking. These skills are part of the Industrial Arts strand under the TVL track.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,1,NULL,'Tony is hardworking, patient, and skilled at fixing things. In his barangay, some broken chairs and tools need repair. Based on his Personal Entrepreneurial Competencies (PECs) and local needs, which pair of jobs best fit Tony’s traits?','Mechanic and Carpenter','Baker and Janitor','Clerk and Cashier','Fisherman and Tailor','A','Tony’s traits (hardworking, patient, skilled at fixing things) are ideal for mechanical and carpentry work, which involve repairing, building, and maintaining tools, furniture, or equipment.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,2,NULL,'Mila found out that many people in her community need help cleaning and organizing their homes. She is neat, organized, and punctual. Based on her Personal Entrepreneurial Competencies (PECs) and the community''s needs, which TWO jobs best match her strengths and the available opportunities?','Housekeeping and Home Decorator','Barber and Welder','Farmer and Fisherman','Tailor and Cook','A','Mila''s PECs: • Neat and organized – ideal for housekeeping or laundry work • Punctual (always on time) – important in service-based jobs',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,3,'Ella enjoys baking and is skilled at making creative cake designs. She wants to earn money by selling her baked goods. Ella conducts research on local cafes to determine their interest in purchasing custom-designed cakes for their menus. She also looks into opening an online store to reach more customers.','What steps did Ella take to identify job opportunities aligned with her entrepreneurial competencies in baking?','She stopped baking and focused on other hobbies.','She researched local cafes and explored online store options.','She waited for people to come to her house to buy cakes.','She joined a singing competition instead.','B','Ella is using her skills in baking and cake design, and she is: • Researching local cafes to see if they need cakes (local business opportunity) • Exploring online stores to expand her reach v This step shows initiative, market research, and strategic thinking, all important in entrepreneurship.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,4,'Ella enjoys baking and is skilled at making creative cake designs. She wants to earn money by selling her baked goods. Ella conducts research on local cafes to determine their interest in purchasing custom-designed cakes for their menus. She also looks into opening an online store to reach more customers.','Why is exploring an online store a good opportunity for Ella?','It guarantees instant success.','It allows her to reach more customers beyond her local area.','It helps her avoid the hassle of baking.','It is a way to avoid competition with other bakers.','B','Selling online means Ella can: • Market her products to a wider audience, not just her local neighborhood • Grow her customer base and income potential',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,5,'Liam has the skill for fixing gadgets, such as mobile phones and laptops. He notices that many people in his town struggle to find reliable technicians. Liam decides to promote his repair services on social media and offers discounts for first-time customers.','How did Liam advertise his repair services to potential clients?','By offering discounts on social media.','By keeping his skills a secret.','By working without any payment.','By focusing only on fixing his own gadgets.','A','The passage says Liam promoted his repair services on social media and offered discounts to first-time customers, which is a simple marketing strategy to attract clients.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,6,'Liam has the skill for fixing gadgets, such as mobile phones and laptops. He notices that many people in his town struggle to find reliable technicians. Liam decides to promote his repair services on social media and offers discounts for first-time customers.','What opportunity did Liam identify in his town that matched his competency in fixing gadgets?','The lack of dependable technicians in his area.','The availability of free repairs from others.','The high demand for gadget repairs in the community.','Long waiting times at repair shops.','A','The story says "many people in his town struggle to find reliable technicians". Liam recognized this gap in the market and used his skills to fill that need, showing entrepreneurial thinking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,7,'Nina enjoys gardening and has a green thumb. She discovers that her neighbors are interested in buying organic vegetables and herbs. Nina decides to grow a variety of vegetables and plants in her backyard and offers delivery services to her customers.','Why is offering delivery services beneficial for Nina’s gardening business?','It guarantees customers will buy more vegetables.','It provides convenience to customers who cannot visit her backyard.','It increases her gardening expenses.','It limits her customer base to her neighbors.','B','Delivery services allow more people to buy from Nina—even if they are too busy, elderly, or live farther away. This adds value and helps her reach more customers conveniently.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,8,'Nina enjoys gardening and has a green thumb. She discovers that her neighbors are interested in buying organic vegetables and herbs. Nina decides to grow a variety of vegetables and plants in her backyard and offers delivery services to her customers.','What job opportunity did Nina identify that matched her gardening skills?','Selling organic vegetables and herbs to neighbors.','Using her plants to decorate her home only.','Joining a gardening club without selling her produce.','Buying groceries instead of gardening.','A','Nina used her gardening skills and community interest to start a business. Selling to neighbors shows she is matching her talent with a local demand, which is what entrepreneurship is all about.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,9,'Ben is talented in creating artwork, such as sketches and paintings. He realizes that local businesses need customized artwork for promotional materials. Ben offers his artistic services to design posters, logos, and advertisements for these businesses.','What type of service does Ben offer to local businesses?','Cleaning services.','Customized artwork for promotional materials.','Free samples of his sketches.','Mass production of posters without consulting customers.','B','Ben uses his artistic talent to help businesses promote their services or products by designing posters, logos, advertisements.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,10,'Ben is talented in creating artwork, such as sketches and paintings. He realizes that local businesses need customized artwork for promotional materials. Ben offers his artistic services to design posters, logos, and advertisements for these businesses.','Why is providing customized artwork a valuable opportunity for Ben?','It allows him to explore job opportunities unrelated to his art.','It meets the specific needs of local businesses while displaying his skills.','It guarantees he will become the most famous artist in his town.','It helps him avoid working long hours.','B','Customized artwork helps Ben: • Meet the needs of clients (businesses need unique promotional materials) • Showcase his creative skills • Earn income using his PEC (artistic talent)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,11,'John has always been creative and resourceful. He notices that his classmates often have trouble organizing their school supplies. Using his organizational skills, John designs small, colorful storage boxes made from recycled materials. His classmates love them, and John begins selling them at affordable prices.','How did John find out that there was a need for storage boxes?','He noticed his classmates'' struggles with organizing school supplies.','He read about storage boxes online.','His teacher gave him the idea.','He copied another student''s project.','A','John used observation—a key entrepreneurial skill. He saw that his classmates struggled with organizing their things, so he designed a product that solved that problem.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,12,'John has always been creative and resourceful. He notices that his classmates often have trouble organizing their school supplies. Using his organizational skills, John designs small, colorful storage boxes made from recycled materials. His classmates love them, and John begins selling them at affordable prices.','Why do you think John''s classmates decided to buy his storage boxes?','They were colorful, affordable, and helped solve their organizational problems.','They were the only storage boxes available.','John gave them away for free.','The teacher forced them to buy.','A','The product was: • Useful (solved a problem) • Attractive (colorful) • Accessible (affordable)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,13,'John has always been creative and resourceful. He notices that his classmates often have trouble organizing their school supplies. Using his organizational skills, John designs small, colorful storage boxes made from recycled materials. His classmates love them, and John begins selling them at affordable prices.','What could John do to improve his business further?','Design more products using recycled materials.','Stop creating new designs.','Ask customers for feedback to improve their products.','Only sells to teachers.','A','By expanding his product line, John can attract more customers, help the environment, and continue applying his creativity and resourcefulness—his key PECs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,14,'Maria has effective communication skills. She realizes that her community often struggles to stay informed about local events. Maria creates a newsletter that she delivers to neighbors every weekend, keeping them updated on events and important announcements.','Why are Maria''s communication skills important for her newsletter?','They ensure the newsletter is clear, accurate, and helpful.','They make the newsletter difficult to understand.','They make her neighbors stop reading.','They have no impact on the newsletter.','A','Maria’s strong communication skills allow her to:',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,15,'Maria has effective communication skills. She realizes that her community often struggles to stay informed about local events. Maria creates a newsletter that she delivers to neighbors every weekend, keeping them updated on events and important announcements.','What can Maria do to improve her newsletter?','Add feedback from neighbors to include information they find most useful.','Reduce the number of newsletters she delivers.','Make a newsletter only about herself.','Include photos and visuals to make it more engaging.','A','By asking for feedback, Maria can: • Understand what her readers really need or want • Improve the relevance and value of her newsletter • Show she listens—an important trait in communication',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,16,'Maria has effective communication skills. She realizes that her community often struggles to stay informed about local events. Maria creates a newsletter that she delivers to neighbors every weekend, keeping them updated on events and important announcements.','What does Maria need to research to make her newsletter better?','Events and announcements of her community values.','Other communities'' events only.','How to create uninformative newsletters.','How to avoid writing in her newsletter.','A','Maria’s newsletter should contain information that matters to her readers. Researching local events and announcements helps her include: • Barangay meetings • Health services • School activities • Community celebrations',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,17,'Carlos enjoys fixing broken bicycles. His neighborhood has many cyclists who often need bike repairs but have no nearby service. Carlos uses his skills to fix bikes and earns money by offering his repair services.','What problem did Carlos solve for his neighborhood?','The lack of nearby bike repair services.','The need for a car repair shop.','The shortage of bicycles.','The inconvenience of going to too far places for bike repairs.','A','The passage states that many cyclists in Carlos''s neighborhood needed bike repairs but had no nearby service. Carlos used his skills to fill this gap in the community',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,18,'Carlos enjoys fixing broken bicycles. His neighborhood has many cyclists who often need bike repairs but have no nearby service. Carlos uses his skills to fix bikes and earns money by offering his repair services.','Why is Carlos''s business important to his neighborhood?','It provides a convenient solution for cyclists who need bike repairs.','It forces people to buy bikes from Carlos.','It creates more broken bicycles.','It makes him the only cyclist in town.','A','His business is important and useful because: • It gives cyclists a nearby, reliable option • Solves an actual community need • Supports local mobility and safety',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,19,'Carlos enjoys fixing broken bicycles. His neighborhood has many cyclists who often need bike repairs but have no nearby service. Carlos uses his skills to fix bikes and earns money by offering his repair services.','What skill did Carlos use to succeed in his bike repair service?','His ability to fix broken bicycles.','His lack of interest in bikes.','His ability to sell cars.','His skill in cooking','A','Carlos used a practical, hands-on skill—bike repair—to provide a valuable service and earn income. This shows how PECs can lead to successful livelihood.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,20,'Carlos enjoys fixing broken bicycles. His neighborhood has many cyclists who often need bike repairs but have no nearby service. Carlos uses his skills to fix bikes and earns money by offering his repair services.','How can Carlos expand his business?','Offer bike maintenance lessons to his neighbors.','Stop repairing bikes for others.','Only repair his friends'' bikes.','Avoid learning new repair techniques.','A','Offering lessons helps Carlos: • Earn extra income • Empower others with basic skills • Grow his business reputation in the community',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,21,NULL,'Sophia is known for her initiative and ability to take responsibility. One day, her teacher announced a school project that involved raising funds for class supplies. Sophia suggested organizing a mini bazaar where students could sell handmade crafts, food, and drinks to contribute to the cause. She took charge of planning and encouraged her classmates to participate. How did Sophia''s suggestion help solve the need for funds for class supplies?','It provided a creative way to raise money through collaboration.','It discouraged students from participating.','It prevented students from selling anything.','It ignored the need for raising funds.','A','Sophia took initiative, encouraged teamwork, and suggested a mini bazaar—a creative and practical solution to raise funds. This action shows leadership and problem- solving using collaboration.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,22,NULL,'Ana dreamed of becoming a successful tailor. Despite facing financial difficulties and not having the best sewing tools, Ana practiced daily using scrap fabrics. She took every opportunity to learn by attending free workshops. Eventually, her hard work paid off, and she opened her own tailoring shop. How did Ana overcome her challenges in becoming a tailor?','She practiced daily and attended free workshops to improve her skills.','She gave up on tailoring when things got difficult.','She waited for others to give her money to start her shop.','She only relied on others to do her work for her.','A','Despite financial difficulty and limited tools, Ana showed perseverance, resourcefulness, and dedication to her goal. She practiced and sought free learning opportunities—key traits of a self-driven learner.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,23,NULL,'Ms. Clara, a retired teacher, noticed that some children in her neighborhood could not afford school supplies. She started a program where she distributed free books, notebooks, and pencils to children. She also held free weekend classes to help them improve in reading and writing. Why is Ms. Clara’s program important for the children in her neighborhood?','It gives them access to education, which can help improve their future opportunities.','It forces children to learn against their will.','It encourages children to stop going to school.','It replaces the need for formal education.','A','Ms. Clara helps provide both materials and learning support, which are essential for children’s growth. Her program supports literacy and education, opening future doors for these kids.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,24,NULL,'Ms. Amelia, a passionate teacher, started a literacy program in a rural area where many children could not read. With her dedication and innovative teaching methods, she helped the children improve their reading and writing skills. Over time, many of her students became successful in their studies and careers. How did Ms. Amelia address the lack of literacy skills in her community?','By introducing innovative teaching methods and working directly with children.','By leaving the rural area to teach elsewhere.','By focusing only on adult learners.','By training volunteer tutors to assist the children.','A','Ms. Amelia tackled the issue by actively teaching and using creative approaches, which led to visible improvements in her students’ learning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,1,25,NULL,'Ali wants to improve his math skills, especially solving word problems. He decides to set a goal of mastering one math topic each week. Ali plans to spend an hour every day practicing problems and seeks help from his teacher when he encounters difficulties. What resources does Ali use to ensure he understands difficult problems?','Help from his teacher','Online games unrelated to math','Avoidance of math textbooks','Reading novels about history','A','Ali practices math daily and knows when to ask for help, showing self- discipline and initiative. His teacher is a reliable resource when problems become difficult',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,26,'John is a learner who wants to improve his fitness and lose ten kilograms in the next three months. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). To achieve this, he plans to: • Exercise 4 times a week (alternating between running and strength training) • Track his food intake using a nutrition app • Drink more water and reduce sugary drinks • Join a fitness group for motivation and accountability','Which combination of habits will best help John achieve his goal of losing 10 kilograms in three months?','Exercise 4 times a week, track food intake, and drink more water','Sleep more than 12 hours a day','Only focus on drinking water','Spend more time watching TV','A','John’s Personal Development Plan includes a balanced approach that combines physical activity, healthy eating habits, and hydration, all of which are essential for sustainable weight loss. The other options either ignore important actions or are counterproductive to his goal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,27,'John is a learner who wants to improve his fitness and lose ten kilograms in the next three months. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). To achieve this, he plans to: • Exercise 4 times a week (alternating between running and strength training) • Track his food intake using a nutrition app • Drink more water and reduce sugary drinks • Join a fitness group for motivation and accountability','Where can John find reliable information to help him track his food intake properly?','A nutrition app recommended by a healthcare professional','Social media influencers’ diets','A random website with no expert credentials','An unverified article with no sources','A','Reliable information should come from credible, expert-backed sources, such as tools or advice recommended by healthcare professionals. The other options may lack scientific accuracy or professional credibility, making them less trustworthy for achieving health-related goals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,28,'John is a learner who wants to improve his fitness and lose ten kilograms in the next three months. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). To achieve this, he plans to: • Exercise 4 times a week (alternating between running and strength training) • Track his food intake using a nutrition app • Drink more water and reduce sugary drinks • Join a fitness group for motivation and accountability','What is a good strategy John can use to stay committed to his fitness routine?','Join a fitness group for motivation and accountability','Skip all exercises for a week','Only focus on eating less, and stop exercising','Give up on the goal entirely','A','When facing challenges in sticking to an exercise routine, finding external support and motivation, such as joining a fitness group, can help John stay consistent. The other options involve avoidance or quitting, which won’t help him achieve his fitness goal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,29,'John is a learner who wants to improve his fitness and lose ten kilograms in the next three months. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). To achieve this, he plans to: • Exercise 4 times a week (alternating between running and strength training) • Track his food intake using a nutrition app • Drink more water and reduce sugary drinks • Join a fitness group for motivation and accountability','What should John do first when designing his personal development plan?','Set clear goals for fitness, such as losing 10 kilograms','Start exercising without any plan','Skip setting a goal and just start eating healthier','Wait until next month to begin','A','Setting a clear and measurable goal (e.g., losing 10 kilograms) is the first step in any successful plan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,30,'James is a learner who wants to improve his academic performance. He recognizes that he struggles with time management, and he often leaves assignments until the last minute. As part of his Personal Development Plan (PDP), James sets the following goals to improve his academic performance in the upcoming semester: • Allocate specific time slots each day to study. • Break down larger assignments into smaller tasks. • Avoid procrastination by setting mini deadlines for each task. • Stay organized using digital tools such as calendars and task management apps.','What is James’ primary goal in his personal development plan?','To improve his academic performance','To spend more time with friends','To stop using digital tools','To avoid studying altogether','A','James’ goal is to improve his academic performance, which he can achieve by enhancing his time management and study habits.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,31,'James is a learner who wants to improve his academic performance. He recognizes that he struggles with time management, and he often leaves assignments until the last minute. As part of his Personal Development Plan (PDP), James sets the following goals to improve his academic performance in the upcoming semester: • Allocate specific time slots each day to study. • Break down larger assignments into smaller tasks. • Avoid procrastination by setting mini deadlines for each task. • Stay organized using digital tools such as calendars and task management apps.','Which tool would James’s use to stay organized and manage his tasks effectively?','Digital tools like calendars and task management apps','A handwritten notebook with random notes','A friend’s personal notes','A calendar without specific task planning','A','James uses reliable, modern tools like digital calendars and task management apps, which are effective for tracking and organizing his tasks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,32,'James is a learner who wants to improve his academic performance. He recognizes that he struggles with time management, and he often leaves assignments until the last minute. As part of his Personal Development Plan (PDP), James sets the following goals to improve his academic performance in the upcoming semester: • Allocate specific time slots each day to study. • Break down larger assignments into smaller tasks. • Avoid procrastination by setting mini deadlines for each task. • Stay organized using digital tools such as calendars and task management apps.','What should James do to avoid procrastination while working on assignments?','Set mini deadlines for each task','Wait until the last day to finish everything','Take long breaks every hour','Keep delaying tasks with no plan','A','By setting mini-deadlines, James can break his tasks into smaller, manageable steps, helping him stay focused and avoid procrastination.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,33,'Alex is a young professional working as a software developer at a tech company. He feels that while he''s doing well in his job, he could be more organized and proactive about his career and personal growth. Alex decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help him improve his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance. His PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Alex Garcia Date: October 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until April 1, 2026) Goal Setting: • Enhance technical programming skills (learn Python). • Improve time management (complete projects on time). • Achieve a better work-life balance (spend more time with family and friends). Why this Goal: Alex wants to increase his technical capabilities for future career growth, reduce stress by managing his time better, and ensure he has enough time for his personal life. Action Steps: • Dedicate 1 hour every day to learning Programing skills. • Create a weekly schedule to prioritize tasks and projects. • Set boundaries at work to leave the office on time and enjoy weekends with family. Resources Needed: Programing course, time management tools, support from colleagues for better work boundaries. Measurement of Success: • Mastering Python basics by the end of the timeframe. • Consistently meeting project deadlines. • Feeling more relaxed and spending quality time with loved ones. Alex hopes that his Personal Development Plan will help him grow in his career, maintain a balanced lifestyle, and reduce stress.','What are Alex’s main goals in his Personal Development Plan?','To learn Programing skills, improve time management, and achieve a better work- life balance','To change his job and get a promotion','To stop working and focus on his personal life','To work longer hours to finish more tasks','A','Alex''s PDP is focused on three key areas: enhancing his technical skills (learning Python), improving time management, and maintaining a healthy work-life balance. These goals are aimed at long-term personal and professional growth, not just immediate job changes or overworking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,34,'Alex is a young professional working as a software developer at a tech company. He feels that while he''s doing well in his job, he could be more organized and proactive about his career and personal growth. Alex decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help him improve his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance. His PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Alex Garcia Date: October 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until April 1, 2026) Goal Setting: • Enhance technical programming skills (learn Python). • Improve time management (complete projects on time). • Achieve a better work-life balance (spend more time with family and friends). Why this Goal: Alex wants to increase his technical capabilities for future career growth, reduce stress by managing his time better, and ensure he has enough time for his personal life. Action Steps: • Dedicate 1 hour every day to learning Programing skills. • Create a weekly schedule to prioritize tasks and projects. • Set boundaries at work to leave the office on time and enjoy weekends with family. Resources Needed: Programing course, time management tools, support from colleagues for better work boundaries. Measurement of Success: • Mastering Python basics by the end of the timeframe. • Consistently meeting project deadlines. • Feeling more relaxed and spending quality time with loved ones. Alex hopes that his Personal Development Plan will help him grow in his career, maintain a balanced lifestyle, and reduce stress.','Which resource will Alex use to learn Programing skills in his Personal Development Plan?','Time management tools','Programing course','Work meetings','Feedback from friends','B','Alex plans to use an online Programing course as a resource to enhance his technical programming skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,35,'Alex is a young professional working as a software developer at a tech company. He feels that while he''s doing well in his job, he could be more organized and proactive about his career and personal growth. Alex decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help him improve his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance. His PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Alex Garcia Date: October 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until April 1, 2026) Goal Setting: • Enhance technical programming skills (learn Python). • Improve time management (complete projects on time). • Achieve a better work-life balance (spend more time with family and friends). Why this Goal: Alex wants to increase his technical capabilities for future career growth, reduce stress by managing his time better, and ensure he has enough time for his personal life. Action Steps: • Dedicate 1 hour every day to learning Programing skills. • Create a weekly schedule to prioritize tasks and projects. • Set boundaries at work to leave the office on time and enjoy weekends with family. Resources Needed: Programing course, time management tools, support from colleagues for better work boundaries. Measurement of Success: • Mastering Python basics by the end of the timeframe. • Consistently meeting project deadlines. • Feeling more relaxed and spending quality time with loved ones. Alex hopes that his Personal Development Plan will help him grow in his career, maintain a balanced lifestyle, and reduce stress.','If Alex struggles to keep up with his Programing lessons, what should he do?','Reduce his learning hours and make smaller goals','Quit learning Python entirely','Spend more time on other goals and ignore Programing class','Stop taking breaks and study continuously','A','If Alex finds it challenging, breaking his goal into smaller tasks and reducing study hours can make learning more manageable, helping him stay on track.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,36,'Alex is a young professional working as a software developer at a tech company. He feels that while he''s doing well in his job, he could be more organized and proactive about his career and personal growth. Alex decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help him improve his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance. His PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Alex Garcia Date: October 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until April 1, 2026) Goal Setting: • Enhance technical programming skills (learn Python). • Improve time management (complete projects on time). • Achieve a better work-life balance (spend more time with family and friends). Why this Goal: Alex wants to increase his technical capabilities for future career growth, reduce stress by managing his time better, and ensure he has enough time for his personal life. Action Steps: • Dedicate 1 hour every day to learning Programing skills. • Create a weekly schedule to prioritize tasks and projects. • Set boundaries at work to leave the office on time and enjoy weekends with family. Resources Needed: Programing course, time management tools, support from colleagues for better work boundaries. Measurement of Success: • Mastering Python basics by the end of the timeframe. • Consistently meeting project deadlines. • Feeling more relaxed and spending quality time with loved ones. Alex hopes that his Personal Development Plan will help him grow in his career, maintain a balanced lifestyle, and reduce stress.','How can completing his Personal Development Plan impact Alex’s career?','It will help him learn new skills, become more productive, and potentially get promotions.','It will not affect his career at all.','It will make him feel more stressed.','It will make him too focused on personal life','A','By improving his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance, Alex is setting himself up for career advancement and productivity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,37,'Alex is a young professional working as a software developer at a tech company. He feels that while he''s doing well in his job, he could be more organized and proactive about his career and personal growth. Alex decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) that will help him improve his technical skills, time management, and work-life balance. His PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Alex Garcia Date: October 1, 2025 Timeframe: 6 months (until April 1, 2026) Goal Setting: • Enhance technical programming skills (learn Python). • Improve time management (complete projects on time). • Achieve a better work-life balance (spend more time with family and friends). Why this Goal: Alex wants to increase his technical capabilities for future career growth, reduce stress by managing his time better, and ensure he has enough time for his personal life. Action Steps: • Dedicate 1 hour every day to learning Programing skills. • Create a weekly schedule to prioritize tasks and projects. • Set boundaries at work to leave the office on time and enjoy weekends with family. Resources Needed: Programing course, time management tools, support from colleagues for better work boundaries. Measurement of Success: • Mastering Python basics by the end of the timeframe. • Consistently meeting project deadlines. • Feeling more relaxed and spending quality time with loved ones. Alex hopes that his Personal Development Plan will help him grow in his career, maintain a balanced lifestyle, and reduce stress.','What action should Alex take if he finds that he is not meeting his project deadlines at work?','Reassess his weekly schedule and adjust priorities','Skip some family activities to focus more on work','Work longer hours without a plan','Ignore the deadlines and hope for the best','A','If Alex is not meeting deadlines, adjusting his schedule to prioritize important tasks will help him improve time management and meet goals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,38,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','What is Jasmin’s main goal in creating her Personal Development Plan (PDP)?','To improve her skills for job advancement and personal growth','To focus only on her personal goals, ignoring her job','To relax and avoid stress management','To improve only her technical computer skills','A','Jasmin’s PDP is designed to help her grow professionally by enhancing communication, leadership, and stress management skills. Her ultimate aim is to advance in her career and maintain her well-being, which reflects a balance of personal and professional development.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,39,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','Which resource is Jasmin using to improve her communication skills?','Time management seminars','Stress management tools','Communication courses and active listening practice','Attending fitness classes','C','Jasmin’s PDP specifically mentions taking communication courses and practicing active listening to enhance her communication skills. This shows she is using appropriate and targeted resources to improve in that area. The other options do not directly support her communication goals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,40,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','If Jasmin faces difficulty in managing her stress at work, what should she do?','Ignore stress management and continue working without change','Learn stress management techniques through online resources','Take a long break and ignore work responsibilities','Quit her job','B','Jasmin can improve her stress management by learning techniques through online resources, which can help her stay calm and focused during work.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,41,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','Why did Jasmin include leadership development as one of her goals in her PDP?','To qualify for a promotion to a team leader position','To avoid having to interact with other employees','To remain at the same level in her job','To focus only on personal development without considering work','A','Jasmin included leadership development in her PDP because she wants to enhance her leadership skills and become eligible for a team leader position.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,42,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','Which action step is Jasmin taking to develop her leadership skills?','Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops','Focus on individual tasks without collaboration','Focus only on customer interaction and avoid team roles','Spend more time working alone','A','Jasmin plans to volunteer for leadership opportunities and attend workshops to develop the necessary skills to become a leader in her company.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,43,'Jasmin, a 26-year-old call center agent, works for a BPO company in Mandaluyong City, Philippines. Jasmin enjoys helping customers but feels that she could improve her communication and leadership skills to advance in her career. After discussing with her supervisor, Jasmin decides to create a Personal Development Plan (PDP) to set clear goals for her growth. Her PDP includes:\n\nName: Jasmin Reyes Date: June 15, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until June 15, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve communication skills for clearer customer interaction. • Develop leadership abilities to qualify for a team leader position. • Improve stress management to stay calm under pressure. Why this Goal: Jasmin wants to enhance her job performance, secure promotion, and maintain her well-being. Action Steps: • Take communication courses and practice active listening. • Volunteer for team leadership opportunities and attend leadership workshops. • Learn stress management techniques through online resources. Resources Needed: Access to communication courses, leadership workshops, stress management tools, and a mentor. Measurement of Success: • Successfully leading a team meeting. • Completing a communication course and using skills in her daily work. • Feeling less stressed and more focused during work hours.','If Jasmin achieves all her goals, what will be the result?','She will stay in her current role without any changes','She will improve her career prospects, take on leadership roles, and feel less stressed','She will feel overwhelmed and stressed at work','She will avoid taking on more responsibilities','B','By successfully completing her PDP goals, Jasmin will enhance her job performance, qualify for leadership positions, and feel better equipped to handle work stress.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,44,'In the town of Baybay, Leyte, four students are assigned to explore different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components in their community. • Carlos interviews a local computer technician. • Marites visits a nearby rice and fish farm. • Ella talks to a barangay nutritionist and daycare worker. • John observes workers at a carpentry shop. They later share their experiences to help each other choose a specialization for Senior High School.','Which of the following sectors is best represented by Marites'' experience at the rice and fish farm?','ICT','FCS','AFA','IA','C','Marites'' visit to the rice and fish farm falls under Agri-Fishery Arts, which includes agriculture, aquaculture, and farming-related practices.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,45,'In the town of Baybay, Leyte, four students are assigned to explore different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components in their community. • Carlos interviews a local computer technician. • Marites visits a nearby rice and fish farm. • Ella talks to a barangay nutritionist and daycare worker. • John observes workers at a carpentry shop. They later share their experiences to help each other choose a specialization for Senior High School.','If Ella is interested in helping families with nutrition and childcare, which TLE component should she choose?','ICT','IA','FCS','AFA','C','Family and Consumer Services (FCS) deals with nutrition, childcare, home economics, and family wellness. Ella’s interest aligns with FCS.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,46,'In the town of Baybay, Leyte, four students are assigned to explore different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components in their community. • Carlos interviews a local computer technician. • Marites visits a nearby rice and fish farm. • Ella talks to a barangay nutritionist and daycare worker. • John observes workers at a carpentry shop. They later share their experiences to help each other choose a specialization for Senior High School.','John wants to learn how to use tools to build furniture and fix household items. Which TLE track matches his goal?','Family and Consumer Services','Agri-Fishery Arts','Information and Communication Technology','Industrial Arts','D','Industrial Arts (IA) includes carpentry, welding, electrical work, and other hands- on skills related to construction and repair.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,47,'In the town of Baybay, Leyte, four students are assigned to explore different TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components in their community. • Carlos interviews a local computer technician. • Marites visits a nearby rice and fish farm. • Ella talks to a barangay nutritionist and daycare worker. • John observes workers at a carpentry shop. They later share their experiences to help each other choose a specialization for Senior High School.','Match the correct TLE component with each student''s experience: Carlos works with computers, Marites grows corn, Ella sews and cooks, and John repairs things with tools.','ICT, AFA, FCS, IA','FCS, ICT, AFA, IA','AFA, IA, FCS, ICT','IA, AFA, FCS, ICT','A','Carlos = ICT (computers) Marites = AFA (farm) Ella = FCS (nutrition and childcare) John = IA (carpentry)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,48,'In Barangay Mabini, the Grade 6 students of Mabini Elementary School observed how different people apply TLE skills in their everyday lives: • Kuya Jomar works at a computer shop where he helps customers print and edit documents. • Aling Nena grows vegetables in her backyard and sells them in the market. • Ate Carla manages her sari-sari store while making sure her home is clean, and meals are prepared. • Mang Rudy, a skilled carpenter, builds chairs and cabinets for the barangay school. Their teacher asked them to analyze how each TLE component helps improve community life and daily survival.','Which four TLE components are demonstrated in the scenario?','ICT (Information and Communication Technology) AFA (Agri-Fishery Arts) FCS (Family and Consumer Services) IA (Industrial Arts)','Home Economics AFA (Agri-Fishery Arts) Entrepreneurship ICT (Information and Communication Technology)','Computer Literacy Gardening Retail Management Carpentry','FCS (Family and Consumer Services) ICT (Information and Communication Technology) TLE Industrial Design','A','Each individual in the scenario demonstrates a skill from one of the four main components of TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education): • Kuya Jomar uses ICT (Information and Communication Technology) – through document editing and printing at a computer shop. • Aling Nena represents AFA (Agri-Fishery Arts) – by growing and selling vegetables. • Ate Carla practices FCS (Family and Consumer Services) – through home management and managing a sari-sari store. • Mang Rudy applies IA (Industrial Arts) – by building furniture like chairs and cabinets.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,49,'In Barangay Mabini, the Grade 6 students of Mabini Elementary School observed how different people apply TLE skills in their everyday lives: • Kuya Jomar works at a computer shop where he helps customers print and edit documents. • Aling Nena grows vegetables in her backyard and sells them in the market. • Ate Carla manages her sari-sari store while making sure her home is clean, and meals are prepared. • Mang Rudy, a skilled carpenter, builds chairs and cabinets for the barangay school. Their teacher asked them to analyze how each TLE component helps improve community life and daily survival.','How does each person in the scenario help the community using their TLE skills?','Kuya Jomar (ICT): Builds furniture for the barangay. Aling Nena (AFA): Prepares meals for her family. Ate Carla (FCS): Grows vegetables in her backyard. Mang Rudy (IA): Offers digital services.','Kuya Jomar (ICT): Helps with digital documents and printing services. Aling Nena (AFA): Provides healthy vegetables and earns income. Ate Carla (FCS): Runs a small business and takes care of household tasks. Mang Rudy (IA): Builds useful furniture for public use.','Kuya Jomar (ICT): Cooks meals at home. Aling Nena (AFA): Teaches carpentry. Ate Carla (FCS): Designs logos and posters. Mang Rudy (IA): Offers internet services.','Kuya Jomar (ICT): Cleans houses and washes clothes. Aling Nena (AFA): Fixes broken furniture. Ate Carla (FCS): Catches fish and sells them. Mang Rudy (IA): Sells canned goods at the market.','B','Each character contributes to the community through their specific TLE skill: • Kuya Jomar (ICT): Supports the community by providing digital assistance, such as printing and document editing. • Aling Nena (AFA): Supplies fresh vegetables to the community while also earning income through backyard farming. • Ate Carla (FCS): Manages a sari-sari store and handles household responsibilities, reflecting good home and business management. • Mang Rudy (IA): Uses his carpentry skills to create useful furniture like chairs and cabinets, aiding local schools.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,2,50,'In Barangay Mabini, the Grade 6 students of Mabini Elementary School observed how different people apply TLE skills in their everyday lives: • Kuya Jomar works at a computer shop where he helps customers print and edit documents. • Aling Nena grows vegetables in her backyard and sells them in the market. • Ate Carla manages her sari-sari store while making sure her home is clean, and meals are prepared. • Mang Rudy, a skilled carpenter, builds chairs and cabinets for the barangay school. Their teacher asked them to analyze how each TLE component helps improve community life and daily survival.','If the school needs new classroom tables, which TLE component should help, and why?','ICT (Information and Communication Technology) – because it deals with computers and digital tools.','AFA (Agri-Fishery Arts) – because it focuses on growing and harvesting plants.','FCS (Family and Consumer Services) – because it involves managing the home and family needs.','IA (Industrial Arts) – because it involves woodworking and furniture building.','D','because students must identify a practical need (new classroom tables) and match it to the correct TLE component.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,51,NULL,'Which solution best shows how these sectors can work together to create job opportunities?','Only focus on computer jobs for young people','Just help farmers sell their products','Digital platforms created for farmers to sell products and food workers can buy supplies','Only concentrate on building maintenance','C','This answer shows a collaborative, multi-sector approach: ICT supports AFA and FCS to generate jobs and streamline commerce.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,52,NULL,'Which solution best shows how these teams should work together to make the market successful?','Only let the computer team handle everything','Have each team work alone in different areas','Connect all teams: Computer team helps garden team track products, food team uses garden team''s fresh ingredients, and equipment team keeps everyone''s tools working','Just let the food team run the market','C','It presents a comprehensive, cooperative solution that includes all teams with specific interdependent roles.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,53,NULL,'Which response best describes the MULTIPLE specializations shown in these zones?','Only look at Tech Zone jobs','The zones demonstrate different specializations','Just focus on Farm Zone activities','Only consider Workshop Zone tasks','B','It is the only one recognizing the variety of sectors shown, which is the point of the question.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,54,NULL,'You visited a local computer shop where people were fixing computers and designing posters for businesses. Your teacher asked what types of jobs these are. Which component do these jobs belong to?','Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA)','Family and Consumer Services (FCS)','Information and Communication Technology (ICT)','Industrial Arts (IA)','C','Fixing computers and digital design fall under ICT.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,55,NULL,'Which sector in your community do activities like planting vegetables and tending to fishponds belong to?','Family and Consumer Services (FCS)','Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA)','Industrial Arts (IA)','Information and Communication Technology (ICT)','B','Planting vegetables and fishpond management are both core activities in the Agri-Fishery Arts sector.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,56,NULL,'What sector in your community where you see your aunt works at a tailoring shop and teaches children cook simple meals do these jobs fall under?','Industrial Arts (IA)','Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA)','Family and Consumer Services (FCS)','Information and Communication Technology (ICT)','C','Tailoring and teaching cooking fall under FCS, which focuses on home economics and family care.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,57,NULL,'Which sector and specialization match Lara’s interest?','Family and Consumer Services – Caregiving','Industrial Arts – Carpentry','ICT – Computer Programming and Hardware Servicing','Agri-Fishery Arts – Fish Processing','C','Website creation and hardware repair are part of ICT specialization.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,58,NULL,'Which of the following best describes the main focus of Agri-Fishery Arts (AFA)?','Manufacturing clothing and textiles','Managing household finances','Production and management of food resources','Interior design and decoration','C','AFA is about managing land and aquatic resources for food production.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,59,NULL,'In Family and Consumer Services (FCS), what is a primary area of specialization?','Deep-sea fishing techniques','home management and family living','Crop rotation methods','Livestock breeding','B','FCS includes homemaking, nutrition, and family life management.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,60,NULL,'Which activity is most associated with the Agri-Fishery Arts sector?','Menu planning for families','Creating household budgets','Fishpond management and maintenance','Organizing family events','C','Fishpond management is a specific AFA activity involving aquaculture.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,61,NULL,'What is a key responsibility in Family and Consumer Services?','Operating fishing vessels','Teaching food preparation and nutrition','Managing large-scale farms','Harvesting agricultural crops','B','FCS includes areas like nutrition, food prep, home management, and caregiving.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,62,NULL,'Which skill set is most important for someone specializing in Agri-Fishery Arts?','Understanding fashion design','Knowledge of aquaculture systems','Interior decorating expertise','Financial planning skills','B','Aquaculture systems are directly related to the fishery component of Agri- Fishery Arts.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,63,NULL,'A farmer notices his tomato plants have yellow leaves. What should be the FIRST step in solving this problem?','Immediately spray pesticides','Observe and identify the specific problem areas','Remove all the plants','Water the plants more frequently','B','The first step in any agricultural issue should be observation and diagnosis, not action without understanding the cause.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,64,NULL,'In a fishpond, several fish are swimming near the surface gasping for air. What is the most likely problem?','The water is too cold','The fish are hungry','Low oxygen levels in the water','The pond is too small','C','Gasping at the surface is a classic sign of low dissolved oxygen in aquaculture systems.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,65,NULL,'If a farmer has 100100 square meters of land and needs to plant vegetables with spacing between plants, how should they solve for the number of plants needed?','Multiply the length by width and divide by 4','Add the length and width','Multiply 100100 by 22','Divide 100100 by 22','D','To find how many plants fit, divide total area by area per plant (or spacing requirement).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,66,NULL,'When planning a vegetable garden, what is the first factor to consider?','What tools to buy','The local growing season and climate','How many workers to hire','The color of the vegetables','B','Climate and season affect which crops will grow and when. This must be planned first.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,67,NULL,'A fisherman''s net keeps breaking. What is the best problem-solving approach?','Buy a new net immediately','Stop fishing altogether','Check the net''s material and how it''s being used','Use a smaller net','C','Identifying why the net is breaking helps determine if it''s due to material failure, wear, or misuse—an analytical approach.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,68,NULL,'If crops are damaged by pests, what should be the first solution to try?','Use chemical pesticides right away','Give up on the crop','Try natural pest control methods first','Plant different crops immediately','C','When pests start damaging crops, the best first response is to use natural pest control methods. This means using techniques like: • Introducing beneficial insects (e.g., ladybugs that eat pests) • Using organic or homemade pest repellents • Practicing crop rotation or companion planting • Removing pests by hand if the problem is small',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,69,NULL,'When fish in a pond are growing slower than expected, what should be checked first?','The water temperature','The fish''s age','The size of the pond','The color of the fish','A','Compost adds organic nitrogen naturally, improving soil health without synthetic inputs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,70,NULL,'A farmer''s soil test shows low nitrogen levels. What is the best initial action?','Stop planting immediately','Add organic matter like compost','Ignore the results','Plant only trees','B','When a soil test shows low nitrogen levels, the best initial action is to add organic matter like compost. Compost and other organic materials (like manure or green manure crops) slowly release nitrogen into the soil as they break down, helping to improve soil fertility naturally and sustainably. Nitrogen is an essential nutrient for plant growth, especially for producing healthy leaves. Adding organic matter: • Enriches the soil gradually • Improves soil structure and water retention • Supports soil microorganisms that help make nutrients available to plants',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,71,NULL,'In managing a small poultry farm, what''s the first step if egg production decreases?','Sell all the chickens','Check the feeding and living conditions','Buy new chickens','Change the chicken coop location','B','The most logical first step in solving the problem is to assess the chickens’ environment and nutrition, as these directly affect egg production.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,72,NULL,'If a crop shows signs of disease, what''s the most appropriate first response?','Remove affected plants and isolate them','Water the plants more','Apply all available chemicals','Harvest everything immediately','A','The responsible first action is containment—removing diseased plants prevents spread and allows for further observation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,73,NULL,'What is the MOST important communication skill needed to be work-ready?','Speaking multiple languages','Using complex vocabulary','Listening and following directions carefully','Speaking loudly at all times','C','While other skills help, effective listening and direction-following are key for professional communication and job readiness.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,74,NULL,'Which of the following shows good time management at work?','Doing all tasks at the last minute','Arriving on time and completing tasks by deadline','Working only when supervised','Taking long breaks between tasks','B','Time management includes punctuality and meeting deadlines consistently.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',2,3,75,NULL,'When working on a team project, what is the best way to show responsibility?','Letting others do most of the work','Working alone and ignoring teammates','Taking credit for everyone''s work','Completing your assigned tasks and helping others','D','Responsibility in a team means doing your part and contributing to group success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,1,NULL,'Paolo is confident, likes speaking in public, and has a talent for storytelling. He notices that his barangay has tourism events and needs guides. He is thinking of applying as a tour guide. Why is being a tour guide a good match for Paolo’s PECs?','He likes reading books','He is shy but hardworking','He is confident and good at speaking','He wants to be alone most of the time','C','Tour guiding requires strong communication skills, confidence, and the ability to tell stories well—all of which Paolo already has. His PECs are perfect for the tourism industry',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,2,NULL,'Jenny is good at making crafts like wallets and keychains using recycled materials. She also knows how to sell them on social media. She noticed her classmates are interested in her products. She wants to earn extra income and help the environment. What is the best plan for Jenny and why?','Sell her crafts online because it fits her creative and marketing PECs','Work as a street sweeper because it is near home','Ask others to sell her products for free','Stop making crafts and focus on chores','A','Jenny is creative and has marketing skills (selling on social media), and she wants to earn money while helping the environment. Selling crafts online is the best match for her abilities and values.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,3,NULL,'Rico is hardworking, patient, and enjoys fixing bicycles. Many people in his barangay use bicycle for transportation. Based on his skills and the needs of his community, what small business suits him best?','Cellphone loading station','Bicycle repair shop','Water delivery service','Food vending cart','B','Rico’s skills and interests match well with starting a bicycle repair business, especially since there''s a local demand due to frequent bicycle use in his community.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,4,NULL,'Arnel is creative, enjoys recycling materials, and lives near a public market. He wants to start a small business. What business matches his PECs and location?','Junk shop or handicraft business','Car rental','Internet café','Barber shop','A','Arnel is creative, loves recycling, and lives near a public market – a good place to sell crafts or collected/recycled items. This aligns perfectly with both his skills and his location.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,5,NULL,'Jerome is confident when talking to others and enjoys fixing phone problems. His neighbors in the barangay often ask him to repair their phones. He wants to earn money using these skills. Which job best suits Jerome and why?','Phone technician because he is confident and good with gadgets','Jeepney barker because he talks loudly','Fisherman because he is hardworking','Store assistant because it is a common job','A','Jerome’s communication skills and technical ability with phones make him a good fit for a phone repair business, especially since people already seek his help.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,6,NULL,'Joy is friendly, honest, and responsible. She plans to start a sari-sari store in her barangay. How can her Personal Entrepreneurial Competencies (PECs) help her run the business successfully?','Customers will trust and return to her store','She will be lazy and close the store early','She will give items away for free','She will argue with every customer','A','Joy''s positive traits—being friendly, honest, and responsible—help build customer loyalty and trust, which are essential for a successful sari-sari store.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,7,'Rico is a young boy from a small barangay. He wants to sell snacks after school. He is confident, hardworking, and good at talking to people.','How can Rico’s Personal Entrepreneurial Competencies help him succeed in his small business?','They allow him to complain to customers.','They make him popular in games.','They help him manage the business and attract customers.','They allow him to avoid school.','C','Rico is described as confident, hardworking, and good at talking to people.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,8,'Rico is a young boy from a small barangay. He wants to sell snacks after school. He is confident, hardworking, and good at talking to people.','Why is it important for someone to know their own PECs before starting a business?','So, they can compare themselves to others','So, they can give up early','So, they can choose the right kind of job or business','So, they can ask others to do the work','C','Knowing one’s PECs helps a person Identify their strengths, choose a business that matches their skills and interests, and Plan realistically based on what they are good at.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,9,NULL,'Aling Rosa owns a small eatery. She is hardworking, creative, and responsible. Her customers keep coming back. Why do her PECs help her succeed?','Because these traits help her serve better and improve her business','Because she does not need to work hard','Because she copies from other stores','Because her customers have no choice','A','Being hardworking, creative, and responsible directly improves customer service and product quality, which are key to running a successful eatery.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,10,NULL,'Carlo loves cooking and wants to open a food stall in his barangay. He is creative with recipes, works hard, and always finishes what he starts. Why are Carlo’s PECs important for his business?','They help him relax and sleep longer.','They help him become popular in school.','They help him create tasty food, work well, and finish tasks.','They help him avoid responsibilities.','C','Carlo’s creativity, hard work, and persistence help him stand out with his food, serve well, and follow through on his business goals',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,11,NULL,'Joel wants to become a successful electrician. He is determined, careful, and eager to learn. He is thinking about how these qualities will help in his career. How can these traits lead Joel to success?','They help him stay safe, do excellent work, and continue improving','They make him work faster without thinking','They help him relax all day','They let him take shortcuts to finish early','A','Being careful ensures safety (very important for electricians) and being determined and eager to learn helps him improve and offer quality service.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,12,NULL,'Aling Maria is a well-known baker in her town. She started her business with limited tools and ingredients. Despite early challenges, she learned from her mistakes and kept improving her products. What most likely helped her become successful?','Because she gave up when she failed','Because she copied others'' recipes','Because she worked hard and improved herself','Because she kept her recipes secret','C','Aling Maria’s success came from persistence, learning from mistakes, and continuously improving—important traits of a successful entrepreneur.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,13,NULL,'‘Ate’ Lorna is a successful mananahi (sewer). She is known to be hardworking, friendly, and honest. People keep coming to her for clothes and repairs. What is the most the reason people continue to return to her?','People trust her and like her work','People avoid her because she is strict','She works less and rests more','She copies others’ work','A','Ate Lorna’s positive traits – being hardworking, friendly, and honest – build strong relationships with customers and improve her business reputation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,14,NULL,'Mang Tonyo is a well-known carpenter in the community. He always finishes projects on time, listens carefully to what his clients want, and uses quality materials. Because of this, people recommend him to others and keep hiring him for more work. How do Mang Tonyo’s qualities help him succeed?','People trust him and like his work','People complain because he is slow','He avoids talking to customers','He copies other workers'' techniques','A','Mang Tonyo is described as punctual, attentive, and committed to quality—all of which are positive personal and professional traits. These build trust and satisfaction among his customers. As a result, people continue to hire and recommend him, leading to his success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,15,NULL,'The class presented posters of successful individuals in their barangay— a midwife, a jeepney driver, and a school janitor. They all show similar traits. How do these common qualities help in their success?” What is the best answer?','They work well, treat others kindly, and do not give up','They don’t care about others','They avoid hard work and get lucky','They keep switching jobs often','A','These core values—hard work, kindness, and perseverance—are universal traits of successful people, regardless of their job. These PECs build trust, reliability, and long- term success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,16,'Sarah struggled with math but wanted to become an accountant. Despite her challenges, Sarah sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and refused to give up. Her perseverance paid off, and she eventually graduated with honors and began working for a reputable firm.','How did Sarah''s perseverance contribute to her success?','By ensuring she gained the skills needed to achieve her goal of becoming an accountant.','By discouraging her from continuing her studies.','By relying on others to do her work.','By avoiding practice and tutoring.','A','Despite struggling with math, Sarah didn’t give up. Her perseverance helped her develop the skills and discipline necessary to achieve her goal. This is a clear example of resilience leading to success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,17,'Sarah struggled with math but wanted to become an accountant. Despite her challenges, Sarah sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and refused to give up. Her perseverance paid off, and she eventually graduated with honors and began working for a reputable firm.','What steps did Sarah take to overcome her struggles in math?','She switched to a different career that did not require math.','She ignored her struggles and hoped they would go away.','She sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and refused to give up.','She only studied during exams and relied on luck.','C','Sarah took concrete steps: • Tutoring for help • Consistent practice • Refusal to give up These actions reflect self-discipline, initiative, and perseverance—all essential PECs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,18,'Sarah struggled with math but wanted to become an accountant. Despite her challenges, Sarah sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and refused to give up. Her perseverance paid off, and she eventually graduated with honors and began working for a reputable firm.','What steps did Sarah take to overcome her struggles in math?','She sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and stayed determined despite challenges.','She ignored her difficulties and hoped they would resolve themselves.','She avoided studying and focused on other subjects.','She relied solely on her classmates to help her.','A','Same as above—Sarah showed determination and took responsible actions to overcome obstacles, rather than avoiding or relying on others.',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,19,'Sarah struggled with math but wanted to become an accountant. Despite her challenges, Sarah sought extra tutoring, practiced consistently, and refused to give up. Her perseverance paid off, and she eventually graduated with honors and began working for a reputable firm.','Why is perseverance an important quality for achieving success?','It helps individuals remain focused and determined, even when faced with difficulties.','It guarantees immediate success without effort.','It discourages individuals from setting ambitious goals.','It leads to unnecessary stress without benefits.','A','Perseverance means not giving up, especially when things are hard. It allows individuals to stay focused, continue learning, and reach long-term goals—just like Sarah.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,20,'Ms. Angela, a retired professor, saw that children in her village lacked access to quality education. She organized free reading and math classes for them. Over time, many of her students performed well in school, and the local government recognized her contributions by building a community learning center.','What personal quality enabled Ms. Angela to make a difference in her community?','Dedication to improving education','Lack of interest in teaching','Avoidance of public involvement','Focus only on her personal achievements','A','Ms. Angela used her experience and passion for teaching to help children who lacked access to education. Her dedication led to real results – students improved, and a learning center was built in her honor. This shows her commitment to community development.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,21,'Ms. Angela, a retired professor, saw that children in her village lacked access to quality education. She organized free reading and math classes for them. Over time, many of her students performed well in school, and the local government recognized her contributions by building a community learning center.','How did Ms. Angela address the lack of education in her village?','By offering free classes and helping children excel in school.','By ignoring the educational needs of the children.','By focusing only on adults’ education.','By stopping her teaching efforts after one month.','A','Ms. Angela directly responded to the need by: • Organizing free reading and math classes • Improving student performance • Her actions led to long-term impact—a community learning center was built because of her efforts.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,22,NULL,'Mr. Ramon, a carpenter, noticed the increasing plastic waste in his community. He began collecting plastic bottles and repurposing them into eco-friendly furniture. His creativity gained the attention of local environmental groups, inspiring his neighbors to join his recycling efforts. What quality did Mr. Ramon display in addressing his community’s plastic waste problem?','Advocacy for environmental protection and creativity in recycling','Avoidance of waste management issues','Focus only on traditional carpentry methods','Lack of interest in community involvement','A','Mr. Ramon showed environmental awareness, creativity, and community leadership by: • Collecting plastic waste (initiative and concern for the environment) • Turning plastic bottles into furniture (creativity and innovation) • Inspiring others to join (community involvement and advocacy)',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,23,'Mr. Santos, a retired teacher, noticed that children in his community were struggling with basic literacy and math skills. To address this, he organized free weekend classes where he taught young learners. He also encouraged older students to become peer tutors and provided them with teaching materials. Over time, the program improved literacy rates and empowered youth to take responsibility for their education.','How did Mr. Santos encourage the youth to get involved in education?','By training older students as peer tutors and providing teaching materials.','By limiting his classes to only few children.','By stopping the program after a few months.','By avoiding interaction with the youth.','A','Mr. Santos not only taught the younger learners himself but also empowered older students by training them as peer tutors and giving them the tools they needed to help others. This encouraged youth leadership and participation in learning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,24,'Mr. Santos, a retired teacher, noticed that children in his community were struggling with basic literacy and math skills. To address this, he organized free weekend classes where he taught young learners. He also encouraged older students to become peer tutors and provided them with teaching materials. Over time, the program improved literacy rates and empowered youth to take responsibility for their education.','Why is Mr. Santos’s program important for the community?','It improved literacy and instilled a sense of responsibility among the youth.','It discouraged participation in education.','It focused only on the younger students.','It replaced the need for formal schools entirely.','A','The program resulted in: • Higher literacy rates • Empowered youth who became responsible for their own learning and others'' • This is a clear example of positive community impact through education',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,1,25,'Mr. Santos, a retired teacher, noticed that children in his community were struggling with basic literacy and math skills. To address this, he organized free weekend classes where he taught young learners. He also encouraged older students to become peer tutors and provided them with teaching materials. Over time, the program improved literacy rates and empowered youth to take responsibility for their education.','How did Mr. Santos’s initiative demonstrate a relationship between community involvement and educational improvement?','It showed that only professionals can improve education','It proved that retirement ends a teacher''s role in society','It showed how active community efforts can lead to better literacy and responsible youth','It suggested that schools alone are enough to fix learning gaps','C','Mr. Santos’s initiative demonstrates that community-based efforts, even led by retirees, can fill educational gaps, build a culture of learning, and develop responsible young leaders. It reflects grassroots education reform.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,26,'Mario is a university student who wants to improve his study habits and achieve better grades in his upcoming exams. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) for the next 2 months. To achieve this, he plans to: • Set aside 3 hours every day for focused study time. • Break his study time into 1-hour blocks with 10-minute breaks in between. • Use active recall and spaced repetition techniques to study. • Meet with a tutor once a week for additional support in difficult subjects. • Join a study group to stay motivated and share learning tips.','What is the main goal that Mario is trying to achieve in his development plan?','To improve his study habits and achieve better grades in exams','To relax more and stop studying','To join more university clubs','To study for only 30 minutes per day','A','Mario’s goal is to improve her study habits, which will help her achieve better grades. This is the central focus of her personal development plan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,27,'Mario is a university student who wants to improve his study habits and achieve better grades in his upcoming exams. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) for the next 2 months. To achieve this, he plans to: • Set aside 3 hours every day for focused study time. • Break his study time into 1-hour blocks with 10-minute breaks in between. • Use active recall and spaced repetition techniques to study. • Meet with a tutor once a week for additional support in difficult subjects. • Join a study group to stay motivated and share learning tips.','Where can Mario find helpful methods for improving his study habits?','From online articles, study guides, or advice from experienced students','From random social media posts','From watching TV shows','From spending time playing video games','A','Information literacy involves finding trustworthy sources of information. Online articles, study guides, and advice from peers or tutors provide useful, reliable strategies for improving study habits.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,28,'Mario is a university student who wants to improve his study habits and achieve better grades in his upcoming exams. He creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP) for the next 2 months. To achieve this, he plans to: • Set aside 3 hours every day for focused study time. • Break his study time into 1-hour blocks with 10-minute breaks in between. • Use active recall and spaced repetition techniques to study. • Meet with a tutor once a week for additional support in difficult subjects. • Join a study group to stay motivated and share learning tips.','Mario finds it hard to focus for extended periods. What can he do to improve this?','Break study sessions into 1-hour blocks with 10-minute breaks','Study non-stop for 3 hours straight','Give up on studying','Spend more time on social media during study time','A','Breaking study sessions into manageable chunks with short breaks is a proven problem-solving strategy to improve focus and prevent burnout.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,29,'Lena is a high school student who wants to improve her physical fitness. She sets a goal to exercise more regularly to build strength and stay healthy. In her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Lena identifies the following steps: • Exercise for 30 minutes every day. • Mix cardio and strength training exercises. • Join a fitness group for accountability and motivation. • Track her progress using a fitness app to stay on track.','What is Lena’s main goal in her personal development plan?','To improve her physical fitness','To join a fitness group','To become a fitness trainer','To stop exercising completely','A','Lena’s goal is to improve her physical fitness, which is the focus of her personal development plan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,30,'Lena is a high school student who wants to improve her physical fitness. She sets a goal to exercise more regularly to build strength and stay healthy. In her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Lena identifies the following steps: • Exercise for 30 minutes every day. • Mix cardio and strength training exercises. • Join a fitness group for accountability and motivation. • Track her progress using a fitness app to stay on track.','Where can Lena find useful tools to track her progress and stay motivated?','Using a fitness app to log her exercises and progress','Asking her friends to remind her to exercise','Ignoring progress tracking tools','Only relying on her memory to track workouts','A','Information literacy involves using reliable tools and resources. A fitness app helps Lena track her progress, giving her measurable results and motivation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,31,'Lena is a high school student who wants to improve her physical fitness. She sets a goal to exercise more regularly to build strength and stay healthy. In her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Lena identifies the following steps: • Exercise for 30 minutes every day. • Mix cardio and strength training exercises. • Join a fitness group for accountability and motivation. • Track her progress using a fitness app to stay on track.','If Lena feels unmotivated to exercise on certain days, what can she do to stay on track?','Join a fitness group for accountability and support','Skip exercise completely on those days','Focus on other non-fitness related activities','Avoid sharing her goals with anyone','A','Joining a fitness group creates a support system that can help Lena stay motivated and accountable, which is an effective way to overcome lack of motivation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,32,'Lena is a high school student who wants to improve her physical fitness. She sets a goal to exercise more regularly to build strength and stay healthy. In her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Lena identifies the following steps: • Exercise for 30 minutes every day. • Mix cardio and strength training exercises. • Join a fitness group for accountability and motivation. • Track her progress using a fitness app to stay on track.','How does mixing cardio and strength training exercises contribute to Lena’s goal?','It provides a balanced approach to building both endurance and strength','It makes her exercise routine boring and repetitive','It focuses only on one aspect of fitness, like strength','It prevents her from tracking her progress','A','Mixing cardio and strength training exercises allows Lena to work on multiple aspects of fitness, creating a well-rounded exercise routine that supports her goal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,33,'Mary is a college student who wants to improve her study habits to achieve better grades. She has identified that she struggles with procrastination and often feels overwhelmed by her assignments. As part of her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Mary decides to: • Break down her large assignments into smaller, manageable tasks. • Set aside dedicated study time every day. • Create a realistic study schedule and stick to it. • Seek advice from her professors if she feels stuck on certain topics. Mary is focused on designing a plan that will allow her to tackle her academic challenges and improve her grades over the next semester.','What is the first step in Mary’s personal development plan for improving her study habits?','Break down large assignments into smaller tasks','Set aside time for social activities','Ignore assignments until the deadline','Study only when exams are near','A','Mary’s plan begins with breaking down large assignments into smaller, manageable parts — a practical and strategic step to reduce procrastination and overwhelm. The other options either delay progress or lack consistency, which do not support her goal of improving study habits.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,34,'Mary is a college student who wants to improve her study habits to achieve better grades. She has identified that she struggles with procrastination and often feels overwhelmed by her assignments. As part of her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Mary decides to: • Break down her large assignments into smaller, manageable tasks. • Set aside dedicated study time every day. • Create a realistic study schedule and stick to it. • Seek advice from her professors if she feels stuck on certain topics. Mary is focused on designing a plan that will allow her to tackle her academic challenges and improve her grades over the next semester.','How will Mary stay organized in her study plan?','By creating a realistic study schedule and sticking to it','By procrastinating on assignments until the last minute','By depending only on her memory to remember assignments','By studying only when she feels like it','A','Sophia uses a study schedule, a reliable method to organize her time effectively. Information literacy involves using tools and strategies that help keep tasks in order and manageable.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,35,'Mary is a college student who wants to improve her study habits to achieve better grades. She has identified that she struggles with procrastination and often feels overwhelmed by her assignments. As part of her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Mary decides to: • Break down her large assignments into smaller, manageable tasks. • Set aside dedicated study time every day. • Create a realistic study schedule and stick to it. • Seek advice from her professors if she feels stuck on certain topics. Mary is focused on designing a plan that will allow her to tackle her academic challenges and improve her grades over the next semester.','If Mary feels stuck on a topic, what can she do to resolve the issue?','Seek advice from her professors','Give up on trying to understand the topic','Skip the assignment and move on to another one','Wait until the exam to figure it out','A','If Sophia faces difficulties with a topic, seeking help from her professors is a proactive way to address the problem, helping her understand the material and move forward.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,36,'Mary is a college student who wants to improve her study habits to achieve better grades. She has identified that she struggles with procrastination and often feels overwhelmed by her assignments. As part of her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Mary decides to: • Break down her large assignments into smaller, manageable tasks. • Set aside dedicated study time every day. • Create a realistic study schedule and stick to it. • Seek advice from her professors if she feels stuck on certain topics. Mary is focused on designing a plan that will allow her to tackle her academic challenges and improve her grades over the next semester.','Why is setting aside dedicated study time each day important for Mary?','It helps her develop a consistent study routine and reduces procrastination','It allows her to avoid studying for important exams','It takes up too much of her time and prevents her from socializing','It only works if she studies with friends','A','Setting aside daily study time supports structure, discipline, and focus, which helps Sophia manage her workload more effectively. This habit reduces last-minute cramming and improves long-term learning – essential for academic success.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,37,'Mary is a college student who wants to improve her study habits to achieve better grades. She has identified that she struggles with procrastination and often feels overwhelmed by her assignments. As part of her Personal Development Plan (PDP), Mary decides to: • Break down her large assignments into smaller, manageable tasks. • Set aside dedicated study time every day. • Create a realistic study schedule and stick to it. • Seek advice from her professors if she feels stuck on certain topics. Mary is focused on designing a plan that will allow her to tackle her academic challenges and improve her grades over the next semester.','If Mary finds herself still struggling with procrastination after following her plan, what should she do?','Reevaluate her study schedule and make adjustments as needed','Ignore the problem and continue procrastinating','Skip studying for a while to relieve stress','Abandon her personal development plan completely','A','Sophia should regularly review and adjust her study plan to make sure it’s still effective. Being flexible and adaptable in her approach is key to solving any problems that arise in her development process.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,38,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','Why did Ben create a Personal Development Plan (PDP)?','To focus solely on his career growth and ignore personal life','To focus on both her career growth and personal well-being','To quit her job and pursue a new career path','To stop working on her skills and relax','B','Sophie created her PDP to balance both her career and personal life by improving her skills, health, and work-life balance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,39,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','Which resource will Ben use to improve his leadership skills?','Gym membership','Leadership training sessions','Time management tools','Digital marketing tools','B','Ben plans to attend leadership training sessions to develop her management and leadership skills, which are crucial for her career growth.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,40,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','If Ben has trouble sticking to her exercise routine, what can he do to solve the problem?','Skip exercise and focus on work','Set smaller fitness goals and gradually increase her exercise routine','Ignore his health goals and focus only on work','Stop exercising completely','B','By setting achievable goals and gradually increasing her exercise time, Sophie can maintain her commitment to staying healthy while balancing work.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,41,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','How can improving his physical health impact Ben’s career?','It could lead to better energy levels, improved focus, and higher productivity at work','It will have no effect on his career','It will make him more stressed at work','It will distract him from her career goals','A','By improving his physical health, Ben will likely experience better energy and focus, which will positively affect his job performance and productivity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,42,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','What should Ben do if he finds it difficult to manage both his work and personal goals?','Reevaluate his priorities and with adjust to her schedule','Ignore his personal goals and focus solely on work','Stop setting any goals at all','Focus only on career goals and forget about personal development','A','If Sophie struggles to manage both career and personal goals, adjusting her schedule and prioritizing her goals will help her stay on track and avoid feeling overwhelmed.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,43,'Ben is a young marketing professional who has been working in a digital marketing firm for two years. While he enjoys his work, Ben feels like he could advance in his career and improve his work-life balance. He wants to focus on both his professional and personal development, so he creates a Personal Development Plan (PDP). Ben’s PDP includes the following key elements: Name: Ben Jenkins Date: October 5, 2025 Timeframe: 12 months (until October 5, 2026) Goal Setting: • Improve leadership and management skills. • Improve his physical and mental health by exercising regularly. • Advance his digital marketing skills by learning new tools and strategies. Why this Goal: Ben wants to lead a team, stay healthy, and improve his knowledge to take on higher-level roles in the marketing industry. Action Steps: • Attend leadership training sessions. • Exercise for 30 minutes daily and practice mindfulness. • Take online courses to learn new digital marketing tools. Resources Needed: Access to online courses, gym membership, time for self-care, mentorship from senior colleagues. Measurement of Success: • Successfully managing a small project team by the end of the year. • Feeling more energetic and balanced in both work and personal life. • Applying new digital marketing strategies in his job and seeing improvements in results. Through her PDP, Ben aims to enhance his leadership abilities, maintain a healthy lifestyle, and advance his professional skills to grow in his career.','How can Ben’s Personal Development Plan impact his relationships with others at work?','By improving his leadership skills, he can foster better teamwork and collaboration','By focusing only on his personal goals, he will isolate herself from colleagues','It will not affect his work relationships at all','It will create conflict with his team','A','As Sophie improves her leadership skills, she will be better able to work with her team, creating a more supportive and collaborative work environment.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,44,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, the Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) organized a community skills fair. The event highlighted the importance of TLE components: • ICT Booth: Students showed how to create posters and digital IDs for the barangay. • AFA Booth: Farmers and youth demonstrated how to plant herbs and raise tilapia in small ponds. • FCS Booth: Local mothers shared tips on preparing healthy meals and managing household chores. • IA Booth: Skilled workers taught basic repair of chairs, electric fans, and construction tools. After attending the fair, learners were asked how these components are connected to everyday needs and how they benefit both families and the community.','How do the four components (ICT, AFA, FCS, IA) work together to support a strong and self-reliant community?','They focus only on teaching students’ different skills separately.','Each component meets a basic need, and together they improve community life.','They all provide entertainment for the barangay during events.','They are only useful during school projects and not in real life.','B','This asks students to connect multiple ideas and show how components relate to one another for community development.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,45,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, the Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) organized a community skills fair. The event highlighted the importance of TLE components: • ICT Booth: Students showed how to create posters and digital IDs for the barangay. • AFA Booth: Farmers and youth demonstrated how to plant herbs and raise tilapia in small ponds. • FCS Booth: Local mothers shared tips on preparing healthy meals and managing household chores. • IA Booth: Skilled workers taught basic repair of chairs, electric fans, and construction tools. After attending the fair, learners were asked how these components are connected to everyday needs and how they benefit both families and the community.','If the barangay experiences frequent typhoon damage, how can each TLE component contribute to disaster recovery?','ICT can help create fun social media content about the disaster.','AFA and IA are enough; the others are not related to recovery.','Each component helps: ICT spreads info, AFA regrows food, FCS manages the home, and IA repairs damage.','FCS and AFA are for everyday use and not helpful after disasters','C','This choice shows a holistic and practical use of all four TLE components in responding to disaster situations: • ICT helps disseminate important information such as emergency hotlines, safety alerts, and community updates. • AFA (Agricultural and Fishery Arts) supports food recovery by teaching families how to replant crops or raise food sources like fish. • FCS (Home Economics) focuses on household management, health, and meal preparation, which are vital during disaster recovery. • IA (Industrial Arts) provides the skills needed to repair damaged structures, tools, and electrical equipment, helping restore daily life quickly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,46,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, the Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) organized a community skills fair. The event highlighted the importance of TLE components: • ICT Booth: Students showed how to create posters and digital IDs for the barangay. • AFA Booth: Farmers and youth demonstrated how to plant herbs and raise tilapia in small ponds. • FCS Booth: Local mothers shared tips on preparing healthy meals and managing household chores. • IA Booth: Skilled workers taught basic repair of chairs, electric fans, and construction tools. After attending the fair, learners were asked how these components are connected to everyday needs and how they benefit both families and the community.','Why is it not enough to focus only on one TLE component when planning for community improvement projects?','Because some components are more important than others.','One component can solve all problems in the community.','Most people only use ICT, so the others are not needed.','A complete project needs all components to address various needs and be effective.','D','Focusing on one limit the benefits. Using all components addresses different needs—technology, food, home life, and infrastructure—making the project completer and more effective. Explanation: Students show understanding of interdependence between components and the importance of a holistic approach.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,47,'In the town of Barangay Maligaya, the Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) organized a community skills fair. The event highlighted the importance of TLE components: • ICT Booth: Students showed how to create posters and digital IDs for the barangay. • AFA Booth: Farmers and youth demonstrated how to plant herbs and raise tilapia in small ponds. • FCS Booth: Local mothers shared tips on preparing healthy meals and managing household chores. • IA Booth: Skilled workers taught basic repair of chairs, electric fans, and construction tools. After attending the fair, learners were asked how these components are connected to everyday needs and how they benefit both families and the community.','Barangay Maligaya wants to teach out-of-school youth useful skills. How can all four components of TLE be integrated into a training program?','Focus only on FCS because youth need life skills more than technical ones.','Only teach IA since tools and repairs are in demand.','Teach AFA and ICT but ignore FCS and IA.','Use all four: ICT for tech skills, AFA for farming, FCS for life skills, and IA for repairs.','D','The answer connects each component to a real-life situation to solve a local issue: youth unemployment.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,48,'In Barangay San Roque, most families rely on farming, fishing, sari-sari stores, and small construction jobs for their daily income. The barangay council plans to improve the livelihood of the residents by enhancing their knowledge in TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. They invited local professionals to explain how each component of TLE can help the community strengthen and grow their small businesses and family support systems.','How does Information and Communication Technology (ICT) support the livelihood of sari- sari store owners in Barangay San Roque?','By teaching them how to plant vegetables in their backyards.','By helping them fix broken tools and household appliances.','By helping manage inventory, use mobile payments, and promote products online.','By allowing them to cook healthy meals for their families.','C','This shows the learner can connect ICT to real livelihood practices, especially how technology supports business efficiency and marketing.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,49,'In Barangay San Roque, most families rely on farming, fishing, sari-sari stores, and small construction jobs for their daily income. The barangay council plans to improve the livelihood of the residents by enhancing their knowledge in TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. They invited local professionals to explain how each component of TLE can help the community strengthen and grow their small businesses and family support systems.','If many families in the barangay are experiencing poor nutrition, how can FCS and AFA work together to help address this issue?','FCS can teach online marketing, while AFA can sell chemical fertilizers.','FCS and AFA can create social media awareness campaigns.','FCS teaches meal planning and food preservation, while AFA supports home gardening and livestock for sustainable nutrition.','FCS and AFA can focus on teaching sewing and wood carving for income.','C','This answer combines the health and nutrition focus of FCS with the food production skills of AFA to offer a real-world solution to malnutrition in the community.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,2,50,'In Barangay San Roque, most families rely on farming, fishing, sari-sari stores, and small construction jobs for their daily income. The barangay council plans to improve the livelihood of the residents by enhancing their knowledge in TLE (Technology and Livelihood Education) components. They invited local professionals to explain how each component of TLE can help the community strengthen and grow their small businesses and family support systems.','How can combining skills from ICT, AFA, FCS, and IA make a family business more successful in the barangay?','ICT and FCS are enough for managing and advertising a business.','AFA and IA are helpful but don''t contribute to customer service or marketing.','ICT helps promote and organize the business, AFA provides products, FCS manages operations, and IA supports physical setup and maintenance.','Only one or two components are needed, depending on the type of business.','C','Combining skills from all four areas ensures a holistic approach to running a family business.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,51,NULL,'In Barangay Maligaya, the people work in different jobs. Tito Jay fixes computers (ICT), Ate Lani cooks and serves food in a carinderia (FCS), Kuya Ron grows vegetables and catches fish (AFA), and Tatay Greg builds cabinets and repairs houses (IA). What does this show about the importance of different job sectors in the community?','These jobs are all fun hobbies that people do for fun.','All the jobs are the same, so it doesn’t matter who does what.','Each job serves a different purpose and helps the community by giving people services, food, tools, and technology.','Only farming is needed because food is the most important.','C','The question integrates knowledge from all four sectors—ICT, FCS, AFA, and IA – to understand that every job contributes uniquely to the functioning of the community.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,52,NULL,'A new technology park is being built in your community. What are THREE important benefits this brings?','Only provides jobs for computer programmers','Creates ICT jobs, provides training opportunities, and attracts new businesses','Just increases traffic in the area','Only benefits students','B','This answer connects economic, educational, and employment benefits, showing a comprehensive understanding of how development projects affect the community.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,53,NULL,'Your community has started a large urban farming project. What are the multiple advantages of this initiative?','Only produces vegetables','Creates farming jobs, provides fresh food supply, and teaches agricultural skills','Just takes up space','Only benefits market sellers','B','Recognizes the social, economic, and educational impact of the project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,54,NULL,'You notice that many students in your school don''t know how to use computers. What specific specialist is most needed?','ICT Education Specialist','Farm Worker','Cook','Carpenter','A','Identifies the direct connection between a community need and the right professional to address it.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,55,NULL,'Your community market has no fresh vegetables available. What SINGLE specialist could solve this problem? A. Computer Technician A. Baker B. Agricultural Production Specialist B. Electrician','Computer Technician','Agricultural Production Specialist','Baker','Electrician','B','Connects the community issue (lack of fresh produce) with the appropriate professional to improve local supply.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,56,NULL,'Many elderly people in your community need help with meal planning. What ONE specialist would be most helpful?','Web Designer','Fish Farmer','Nutrition Specialist','Welder','C','A nutritionist can address specific dietary needs, especially for older adults, ensuring health and well-being.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,57,NULL,'The playground equipment needs repair for safety. What SINGLE specialist should handle this?','Computer Programmer','Gardener','Chef','Metal Work Specialist','D','This specialist has the technical skills to safely repair metal structures, ensuring safety.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,58,NULL,'You observe someone fixing a computer at school. Which ONE specific job description best matches this work?','ICT Hardware Technician who repairs and maintains computers','Teacher who uses computers','Student who plays computer games','Parent who buys computers','A','Understands how specific roles in ICT apply to real-world school settings.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,59,NULL,'At the local farm, you see someone checking soil quality. Which ONE specialization describes this work?','Store clerk who sells plants','Agricultural Soil Specialist who tests and improves soil conditions','Truck driver who delivers soil','Worker who waters plants','B','This role links directly to improving crop productivity through scientific soil analysis.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,60,NULL,'In the community kitchen, someone is teaching food safety. What ONE specific job role describes this work?','Person who likes cooking','Store owner who sells food','Food Safety Instructor who teaches proper food handling','Cleaner who mops floors','C','Connects food safety education to public health and service quality.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,61,NULL,'At the construction site, you notice someone reading building plans. Which ONE specialization describes this task?','Person who buys buildings','Construction Foreman who interprets and follows building plans','Worker who carries materials','Guard who watches the site','B','Requires integrating construction knowledge, planning, and leadership.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,62,NULL,'In the computer lab, someone is teaching basic programming. What ONE job description fits this role?','Students using computers','ICT Programming Instructor who teaches coding basics','Person who plays games','Worker who cleans computers','B','This role develops technical skills in digital literacy and workforce readiness.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,63,NULL,'Sarah watches someone repairing a broken smartphone screen. Which ONE sector specialization is this person practicing?','ICT Mobile Device Repair Specialist','Farm Equipment Operator','Food Service Worker','Furniture Maker','A','Demonstrates specialization within ICT and application of skills to real-world needs.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,64,NULL,'Juan sees workers feeding fish in large ponds. Which ONE specific specialization is shown here?','Computer Technician','Aquaculture Specialist','Chef','Carpenter','B','Involves managing aquatic animals and water quality, linking to food production.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,65,NULL,'Your school''s computer lab needs someone to fix broken computers. Looking at the "Help Wanted" board, which ONE job opportunity matches this need?','ICT Computer Repair Technician needed - must know hardware repair','Farm Worker wanted - must know planting','Cook needed - must know baking','Carpenter wanted - must know woodwork','A','Connects school infrastructure needs to the correct technical job opportunity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,66,NULL,'The local fish farm posted a sign. Which ONE specific job opportunity is being offered?','Website Designer - create web pages','Aquaculture Worker - manage fishponds','Hairdresser - style hair','Electrician - fix wiring','B','This option clearly relates to the fish farming environment. Understanding the match between the job setting (fish farm) and profession (aquaculture) shows relational thinking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,67,NULL,'The community center has job posting. Which ONE position are they trying to fill?','Computer Programmer - write code','Rice Farmer - plant crops','Child Care Worker - supervise children','Welder - join metals','C','The community center typically offers social services, making childcare a highly appropriate match. This requires understanding community needs and aligning them with job roles.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,68,NULL,'A new factory opened with ONE specific job advertisement. What position is available?','Data Entry Clerk - type documents','Vegetable Grower - plant vegetables','Baker - make bread','Machine Operator - run industrial equipment','C','Factories involve machinery and equipment, so this role is directly relevant. Connecting the workplace type to the correct role shows deeper understanding.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,69,NULL,'Maya sees someone working at the town''s computer center. This person is teaching elderly community members how to use smartphones to connect with their families online. Which ONE job description best matches what Maya observed?','An ICT Digital Literacy Specialist who teaches basic technology skills to the community members.','A store clerk who sells smartphones','A delivery person who brings phones home','A student who knows how to use phones','A','This reflects both ICT knowledge and the educational/social function of digital literacy -perfect for community tech centers.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,70,NULL,'During a community event, Juan sees someone carefully checking plants for diseases and teaching farmers how to protect their crops. Which ONE job description best matches this work?','A store owner who sells plants','An AFA Plant Health Specialist who monitors crop conditions and educates farmers','A truck driver who delivers vegetables','A worker who waters plants','B','This shows clear understanding of agricultural support roles that combine observation, diagnosis, and education.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,71,NULL,'"Marco helps his mother cook meals and clean the kitchen. He enjoys preparing food for the family. What sector is this related to?"','Family and Consumer Services','Industrial Arts','ICT','Agri-Fishery Arts','A','Cooking and home management fall under FCS. Recognizing domestic tasks as part of a professional sector shows integrated understanding.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,72,NULL,'"Tina is learning to fix broken chairs and tables with her grandfather. She enjoys using a hammer and nails. What specialization is Tina learning?"','ICT','Industrial Arts','Family and Consumer Services','Agri-Fishery Arts','B','The task involves basic tech troubleshooting, directly related to Information and Communication Technology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,73,NULL,'"Kyle helps his older brother install apps and fix simple problems on their family’s computer. What field is this activity a part of?"','Family and Consumer Services','Industrial Arts','ICT','Agri-Fishery Arts','C','The task involves basic tech troubleshooting, directly related to Information and Communication Technology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,74,NULL,'During the morning assembly, Ms. Rodriguez talks about being ready for work. She shows a video of two students: Learner A arrives 5 minutes late and rushes to his seat. Learner B arrives 10 minutes early and sits quietly. Which ONE important work-readiness skill is Student B demonstrating?','Punctuality - arriving early and being prepared','Creativity - thinking of new ideas','Leadership - telling others what to do','Technology - using computers well','A','Demonstrates readiness for work and discipline, both essential soft skills. It requires applying the concept of time management in context.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS4',3,3,75,NULL,'During group work, the teacher observes two learners: Learner C talks while others are speaking. Learner D waits for others to finish before sharing ideas. Which ONE essential work readiness skill is Student D showing?','Listening and communication skills','Mathematical ability','Athletic talent','Computer knowledge','A','This behavior is part of respectful and effective communication, essential in teamwork and professional settings.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,1,NULL,'“Natutukoy ang mga personal na impormasyon na nagpapakilala sa sarili at naaayon sa tanong.” Anong mga mahahalagang impormasyon ang kailangan mong malaman upang makilala ang isang tao o maipakilala ang iyong sarili sa iba?','Antas ng edukasyon','Hilig sa mga libangan','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Paboritong pagkain','C','Ang petsa ng kapanganakan ay isang mahahalagang personal na impormasyon dahil ito ay tumutulong upang tukoy na makilala ang isang tao, lalo na kung may kapangalan o kapareho ng apelyido. Ito rin ay ginagamit sa mga opisyal na dokumento tulad ng birth certificate, school records, at iba pa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,2,NULL,'Kapag may bagong kaklase o guro na nagtatanong kung sino ka, kailangan mong ipakilala ang iyong sarili sa paraang makikilala ka nila.” Alin sa mga sumusunod ang madalas mong sabihin upang makilala ka ng iba??','Antas ng edukasyon','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Paboritong libangan','Mga kaibigan','B','Kapag nagpapakilala, ang pangalan at petsa ng kapanganakan ay kadalasang sinasabi upang makilala ka nang maayos. Ginagamit ito sa mga talaan at nagpapakita ng pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng mga taong may kaparehong pangalan. Mahalaga ito upang tukoy kang makilala ng guro o kaklase.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,3,NULL,'Mahalaga ang kalusugan ng ating katawan para tayo ay maging malakas at masigla. Alin sa mga ito ang may kinalaman sa pag-aalaga ng ating katawan?','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Antas ng pisikal na aktibidad','Paboritong pagkain','Mga kakayahan sa sining','B','Ang pisikal na aktibidad ay direktang may kinalaman sa pagpapanatili ng kalusugan at lakas ng katawan. Ang pagiging aktibo, tulad ng pag-eehersisyo o paglalaro, ay tumutulong sa pagpapatibay ng kalamnan, puso, at kalusugan sa kabuuan. Ang ibang pagpipilian gaya ng "petsa ng kapanganakan" ay mahalaga ngunit hindi ito kaugnay sa pangangalaga ng kalusugan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,4,NULL,'Kapag gusto mong ipakilala ang iyong sarili sa iba, mahalagang ibahagi ang ilang impormasyon tungkol sa iyong pagkakakilanlan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang mahalagang impormasyon na ginagamit mo kapag nagpapakilala ka sa iba?','Paboritong kulay','Pangalan','Paboritong hayop','Laruan sa bahay','B','Ang pangalan ang pangunahing impormasyon na unang ginagamit sa pagpapakilala. Ito ang pinaka-personal at natatanging pagkakakilanlan ng isang tao. Bagamat ang paboritong kulay, hayop, o laruan ay nagpapakita ng iyong kagustuhan, hindi ito sapat upang matukoy kung sino ka.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,5,NULL,'Mahalaga na alam natin ang ating mga pangunahing personal na impormasyon upang magkaroon tayo ng mas malinaw na pagkakakilanlan at upang mas madali tayong makilala ng iba. Alin sa mga sumusunod na impormasyon ang itinuturing na batayang personal na impormasyon na mahalaga sa pagkilala sa sarili?','Antas ng pisikal na kalusugan','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Paboritong libangan','Kakayahan sa paglikha ng sining','B','Ang petsa ng kapanganakan ay isang mahalagang personal na impormasyon na tumutulong upang matukoy ang iyong edad at pagkakakilanlan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,6,NULL,'Ang batayang personal na impormasyon ay mahalaga dahil ito ang nagsasabi kung sino tayo. Sa pamamagitan nito, mas madali tayong makilala ng iba. Halimbawa, kung gusto mong ipakilala ang iyong sarili sa iyong mga kaklase. Alin sa mga sumusunod na halimbawa ang itinuturing na batayang personal na impormasyon?','Antas ng edukasyon','Paboritong libangan','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Kakayahan sa pakikipag-usap','C','Ang batayang impormasyon ay may kinalaman sa pagkakakilanlan tulad ng pangalan, tirahan, at petsa ng kapanganakan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,7,NULL,'Mahalaga ang pag-aalaga sa ating katawan upang manatiling malusog at masigla. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang makatutulong upang mapanatiling malusog ang iyong katawan?','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Antas ng pisikal na aktibidad','Paboritong libro','Kakayahan sa sining','B','Ang pagkakaroon ng sapat at regular na pisikal na aktibidad ay susi sa kalusugan ng katawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,8,NULL,'Ang kalusugan ng ating katawan ay mahalaga upang tayo ay maging aktibo at masigla sa araw-araw. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang makatutulong upang mapanatiling malusog ang iyong katawan?','Petsa ng kapanganakan','Antas ng pisikal na aktibidad','Paboritong libro','Kakayahan sa sining','B','Kapareho ng nauna, ang ehersisyo at pagkilos ay makatutulong sa pagiging malusog.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,9,NULL,'Ang buhay ng tao ay may iba''t ibang yugto gaya ng pagkabata, pagdadalaga/pagbibinata, at pagtanda. Mahalagang malaman ang mga karaniwang pangyayari sa bawat yugto upang maunawaan ang ating paglaki at pag-unlad. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang karaniwang pangyayari sa yugto ng pagkabata?','Pag-aaral sa kolehiyo','Pagtatrabaho sa opisina','Paglalaro at pag-aaral sa mababang baitang','Pagreretiro sa trabaho','C','Sa pagkabata, karaniwan ang paglalaro, pag-aaral sa preschool o elementarya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,10,NULL,'"Natutukoy ang mga pangyayari sa bawat yugto ng buhay", ngunit nakatuon naman sa yugto ng pagtanda: Alin sa mga sumusunod ang karaniwang ginagawa ng tao sa yugto ng pagtanda?','Paglalaro ng laruan at panonood ng cartoons','Pagtapos sa elementarya','Pagreretiro mula sa trabaho at pagbibigay ng payo sa mga bata','Pagsisimula sa bagong trabaho','C','Sa pagtanda, tumitigil na sa pagtatrabaho at mas gumugugol ng panahon sa pamilya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,11,NULL,'Sa bawat bahagi ng ating buhay, may mga karanasang kaakibat na natatangi sa bawat yugto. Isa sa mga yugtong ito ay ang panahon ng pagbibinata, kung saan nagsisimula ang maraming pagbabago sa sarili at nagkakaroon ng mga bagong karanasan. Alin sa mga sumusunod na pangyayari ang karaniwang nauugnay sa yugto ng pagbibinata?','Pagsisimula ng pag-aaral sa elementarya','Pagtanggap ng unang trabaho','Pagkakaroon ng interes sa mga romantikong relasyon','Pagtanggap ng diploma sa mataas na paaralan','C','Sa pagbibinata o pagdadalaga, nagkakaroon ng mga pagbabagong emosyonal at sosyal, kabilang ang interes sa pakikipagkaibigan o romantikong damdamin.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,12,NULL,'Ang mga nakatatanda tulad ng ating mga magulang, lolo’t lola, at guro ay nagtuturo sa atin ng mga pagpapahalagang dapat taglayin sa araw-araw. Mahalaga na ito ay ating natatandaan at naisasabuhay. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang isang tiyak na pagpapahalagang madalas itinuturo ng mga nakatatanda sa tahanan?','Pagkakaroon ng maraming laruan','Paggalang sa matatanda','Paglalaro buong araw','Pagtulog nang huli sa gabi','B','Isa sa mga pangunahing asal na itinuturo sa tahanan ay ang paggalang.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,13,NULL,'Marami tayong natututunang pagpapahalaga mula sa ating mga magulang o mga nakatatanda sa bahay. Ano ang isang pagpapahalagang itinuturo ng mga nakatatanda na dapat mong isabuhay sa araw-araw?','Katamaran','Kawalang-galang','Katapatan','Pagpapabaya','C','Ang katapatan ay mahalagang pagpapahalagang isinasaalang-alang sa tahanan at lipunan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,14,NULL,'Si Angel ay palaging tumutulong sa kaniyang lola sa mga gawaing bahay kahit walang kapalit na gantimpala. Anong pagpapahalaga ang ipinapakita ni Angel sa sitwasyong ito?','Katamaran','Pagkamakasarili','Paggalang','Pagmamalasakit','D','Ang pagtulong sa lola kahit walang kapalit ay pagpapakita ng malasakit at pagmamahal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,15,NULL,'Sa panahon ngayon, maraming impormasyon ang ating nakikita mula sa iba’t ibang paraan tulad ng telebisyon, internet, at mga aklat. Mahalagang matutong pumili ng tama at kapaki-pakinabang na impormasyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang dapat mong gawin upang matiyak na totoo ang impormasyong nabasa mo sa internet?','Ibahagi agad ito sa social media','Tignan kung may maraming likes ang post','Basahin at alamin kung saan ito galing','Maniwala agad sa nabasa mo','C','Bahagi ng information literacy ang pag-verify ng source o pinagmulan ng impormasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,16,NULL,'Sa panahon ngayon, maraming impormasyon ang ating nakikita mula sa iba’t ibang paraan tulad ng telebisyon, internet, at mga aklat. Mahalagang matutong pumili ng tama at kapaki-pakinabang na impormasyon. Nakita mo sa isang website na may bagong balita tungkol sa iyong paaralan. Ano ang pinakamainam mong gawin?','Kopyahin ito at ipadala sa iyong mga kaklase','Alamin muna kung maaasahan ang pinanggalingan ng impormasyon','Sabihin sa lahat kahit hindi ka pa sigurado','Ipagkalat ito sa mga kaklase para sumikat ka','B','Bago ikalat ang impormasyon, kailangang suriin muna kung ito ay totoo at galing sa mapagkakatiwalaang source.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,17,NULL,'Mahalagang matutong mag-isip nang maayos bago maniwala sa anumang impormasyon, lalo na kung ito ay mula sa internet o social media. Ano ang dapat mong gawin upang matiyak na tama ang isang impormasyon na nabasa mo online?','Ibahagi agad sa iba','Paniwalaan kaagad','Tignan ang source o pinanggalingan nito','Hindi pansinin','C','Mahalaga ang pagsusuri sa pinanggalingan ng impormasyon upang matiyak ang katotohanan nito. Hindi lahat ng nababasa online ay totoo.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,18,NULL,'Ang pamilya ay ang mga taong kasama natin sa bahay, at sila ang tumutulong sa atin sa mga araw-araw na gawain. Ang pamilya ay may mga kasamang magulang, kapatid, at iba pang kamag-anak. Alin sa mga sumusunod na pahayag ang pinaka-angkop na naglalarawan sa konsepto ng pamilya?','Ang pamilya ay binubuo lamang ng mga magulang at mga anak.','Ang pamilya ay isang grupo ng mga tao na may ugnayan sa dugo o kasal at nagtutulungan sa isa''t isa.','Ang pamilya ay isang organisasyon na naglalayong kumita ng pera.','Ang pamilya ay isang koleksyon ng mga kaibigan na hindi nauugnay sa isa''t isa.','B','Ang pamilya ay binubuo ng mga taong magkakaugnay at nagkakaisa sa pagmamahalan at pagtutulungan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,19,NULL,'May iba''t ibang uri ng pamilya, at bawat isa ay may mga natatanging katangian. Ang pag-alam sa mga uri ng pamilya ay makakatulong sa atin na mas maunawaan ang ating mga kasama sa buhay. Alin sa mga sumusunod na uri ng pamilya ang binubuo ng isang magulang at kanyang mga anak?','Pamilyang nukleyar','Pamilyang extended','Pamilyang single-parent','Pamilyang blended','C','Ang single-parent family ay binubuo lamang ng isang magulang at kanyang mga anak.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,20,NULL,'Ang mga magulang ay may mahalagang gampanin sa loob ng pamilya. Sila ang nag- aalaga, nagtuturo, at nagbibigay ng suporta sa kanilang mga anak. Alin sa mga sumusunod na gampanin ang karaniwang tungkulin ng isang magulang sa loob ng pamilya?','Pagsusuri ng mga takdang-aralin ng mga anak','Pagbibigay ng emosyonal na suporta at pagmamahal','Paglalaro kasama ang mga kaibigan ng mga anak','Pagbili ng mga laruan para sa pamilya','B','Isa sa pangunahing tungkulin ng magulang ay magbigay ng pagmamahal at suporta, hindi lamang materyal kundi emosyonal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,21,NULL,'Ang bawat pamilya ay may kanya-kanyang kaugalian at tradisyon, lalo na tuwing may mahahalagang okasyon tulad ng Pasko. Ang mga ito ay nagpapakita ng pagmamahalan at pagkakaisa sa loob ng tahanan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang ginagawa ng maraming pamilya bilang tradisyon tuwing Pasko?','Pagsasalu-salo sa hapunan kasama ang pamilya','Paglalaro ng video games kasama ang mga kaibigan','Pagbili ng bagong gamit sa paaralan','Pagsasayaw at paligsahan sa sports','A','Karaniwang tradisyon sa Pasko ang pagsasalo-salo, na nagpapakita ng pagmamahalan at pagkakaisa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,22,NULL,'Sa araw-araw, mahalaga ang paggamit ng tamang pag-iisip upang makagawa ng mabuting pasya, lalo na kapag may problema o kailangang pumili. Kung may nakita kang kaklase na nahulog ang kanyang gamit sa sahig, ano ang tamang gawin?','Tumingin lang at magpatuloy sa paglalakad','Tawanan siya kasama ng iba','Tulungan siyang pulutin ang gamit','Kunin ang gamit at itago ito','C','Ipinapakita nito ang kabutihang-asal at pagpapakita ng malasakit sa kapwa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,23,NULL,'Ang pamilya ay may mahalagang papel sa ating buhay, lalo na kapag ito ay mga bagay na ating dapat malaman tungkol sa ating katawan at kalusugan. Ang mga magulang ay maaaring magbigay ng impormasyon at tulong sa kanilang mga anak tungkol sa mga pagbabago na nararanasan nila habang lumalaki. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sitwasyon ang naglalarawan ng kahalagahan ng pamilya sa pagbibigay ng kaalaman tungkol sa seksuwalidad at reproduktibong kalusugan?','Ang mga magulang ay nagbibigay ng impormasyon at nag-uusap sa kanilang mga anak tungkol sa mga pagbabago sa katawan sa panahon ng pagbibinata.','Ang mga kabataan ay nag-aaral sa paaralan nang walang tulong mula sa kanilang pamilya.','Ang mga magulang ay nag-aalaga lamang ng mga bata at hindi nakikialam sa kanilang edukasyon.','Ang mga kabataan ay nahihiyang magtanong tungkol sa seksuwalidad sa kanilang mga magulang.','A','Mahalaga ang gabay ng magulang sa pag-unawa ng anak sa seksuwalidad at kalusugan habang lumalaki.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,24,NULL,'Habang lumalaki ang isang bata, may mga pisikal at emosyonal na pagbabago siyang nararanasan. Mahalagang may gumagabay sa kanya upang maunawaan ang mga pagbabagong ito. Paano nakatutulong ang pamilya sa pag-unawa ng mga pagbabago sa katawan habang lumalaki?','Hindi dapat nakikialam ang pamilya sa desisyon ng bata','Tinutulungan ng pamilya ang bata sa pagbibigay ng payo at impormasyon','Hinahadlangan ng pamilya ang bata sa pag-unawa sa sarili','Hindi mahalaga ang pamilya sa pagbibigay ng kaalaman','B','Ang pamilya ay unang guro ng bata, lalo na sa mga pagbabagong pisikal at emosyonal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,1,25,NULL,'Isipin mo ang mga sitwasyon na nararanasan ng mga pamilya. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sitwasyon ang itinuturing na hamon na nararanasan ng isang pamilya?','Pagsasalu-salo sa mga espesyal na okasyon','Pagkakaroon ng hindi pagkakaunawaan sa loob ng tahanan','Pagkakaroon ng mga bagong kasapi sa pamilya','Pagtulong sa mga kaibigan sa kanilang mga problema','B','Ang mga hindi pagkakaintindihan ay halimbawa ng hamon o pagsubok sa loob ng pamilya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,26,NULL,'Sa bawat pamilya, may mga pagkakataon na sumasailalim sa mga pagsubok o hamon na dapat nating harapin. Ang mga hamong ito ay maaaring magdulot ng stress at mga isyu sa loob ng tahanan. Mahalaga na maunawaan ang mga ganitong sitwasyon upang makahanap tayo ng mga solusyon at mapanatili ang magandang relasyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sitwasyon ang maituturing na hamon na nararanasan ng isang pamilya?','Pagsasama-sama ng pamilya tuwing pista','Pagkakaroon ng problema sa pinansyal na aspeto','Pagtulong sa mga gawaing bahay','Paglalaro ng mga bata sa labas','B','Isa sa karaniwang hamon ng pamilya ay ang problema sa pera na nakaaapekto sa lahat ng miyembro.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,27,NULL,'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng problema o pagsubok na maaaring maranasan ng isang pamilya','Pagkakaroon ng hindi pagkakaintindihan sa mga desisyon','Pagsasagawa ng mga tradisyon tuwing Pasko','Paglalaro ng mga bata sa labas ng bahay','Pagsali sa mga aktibidad sa paaralan','A','Ang hindi pagkakaintindihan ay isang uri ng problema na kailangang pag-usapan at solusyunan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,28,NULL,'Ang komunidad ay isang grupo ng mga tao na nakatira sa isang tiyak na lugar. Sila ay nagtutulungan at may mga bagay na magkakaugnay sa kanila. Mahalaga ang pagkakaunawaan sa konsepto ng komunidad upang malaman natin kung paano tayo nakikilahok at nakikipag-ugnayan sa ating kapwa. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakasimpleng paglalarawan ng isang komunidad?','Isang malaking grupo ng mga tao na may iba''t ibang interes at pinagmulan na nagtutulungan para sa kaunlaran.','Isang lugar kung saan maraming gusali, negosyo, at iba''t ibang uri ng pamumuhay.','Isang pangkat ng mga tao na naninirahan sa isang tiyak na lugar at mayroong isang pangunahing bagay na magkakaugnay sa kanila.','Isang organisasyon na may sariling pamahalaan, batas, at sistema ng ekonomiya.','C','Ito ang pinakapayak na kahulugan ng komunidad — mga taong nagtutulungan at namumuhay nang magkakasama.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,29,NULL,'Ang salitang "komunidad" ay madalas nating naririnig sa paaralan, tahanan, at paligid. Mahalaga na alam natin ang kahulugan nito upang mas maunawaan ang ating ginagalawang kapaligiran. Ano ang pinakamadaling paliwanag ng salitang komunidad?','Isang kumplikadong grupo na gumagalaw sa ekonomiya, politika, at kultura','Isang grupo ng mga tao na may parehong paniniwala at layunin','Isang pangkat ng mga tao na sama-samang nakatira sa isang lugar','Isang samahan na may sariling pinuno at mga alituntunin','C','Simple at madaling maunawaan na paliwanag ng komunidad.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,30,NULL,'Sa bawat lugar, may mga ginagawa ang mga tao na nagpapakita kung anong klaseng pamumuhay at tradisyon ang mayroon sila. Alin sa mga sumusunod na uri ng kultura ang pinaka-angkop na naglalarawan sa espesyal na basket na ito?','Kulturang Materyal','Kulturang Di-Materyal','Tradisyunal na Kultura','Modernong Kultura','A','Ang espesyal na basket ay isang bagay, kaya ito ay kabilang sa kulturang materyal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,31,NULL,'Kung kailangan ng iyong pamilya ng tulong para sa iyong pag-aaral, saan ka maaaring humingi ng tulong sa inyong komunidad','Sa kapitbahay na mahilig maglaro','Sa tindahan malapit sa inyo','Sa barangay o lokal na pamahalaan','Sa kaibigan mong kalaro araw-araw','C','Ang lokal na pamahalaan ang may serbisyong pang-edukasyon at tulong pinansyal.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,32,NULL,'Sa ating komunidad, mahalaga ang pagkakaroon ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa mga bagong ordinansa at proyekto ng pamahalaan. Ang mga impormasyon na ito ay makakatulong sa atin na malaman kung ano ang mga pagbabago at mga patakaran na dapat nating sundin. Kung ang iyong komunidad ay may isang pangunahing pinagkukunan ng impormasyon tungkol sa mga bagong ordinansa at proyekto ng pamahalaan, alin sa sumusunod ang pinaka-direktang nagbibigay nito?','Ang mga usapan sa kanto ng mga residente.','Ang tanggapan ng punong barangay.','Ang mga post sa social media ng iba''t ibang indibidwal.','Ang mga patalastas sa mga pribadong tindahan.','B','Ang barangay office ang opisyal na pinanggagalingan ng impormasyon tungkol sa ordinansa at proyekto.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,33,NULL,'Sa pakikipag-usap, mahalaga ang pagiging isang mabuting tagapakinig. Ang aktibong pakikinig ay isang paraan upang maipakita ang respeto at pag-unawa sa kausap. Ano ang ibig sabihin ng aktibong pakikinig?','Pagbibigay ng mahabang payo habang may nagsasalita','Pakikinig at pagbibigay-pansin sa sinasabi ng kausap','Pagtanong ng maraming tanong kahit hindi pa tapos magsalita ang kausap','Pagsasalita agad tungkol sa sariling karanasan habang nakikinig','B','Ito ang tinatawag na aktibong pakikinig — may pokus at paggalang sa kausap.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,34,NULL,'Mahalaga ang pagkakaintindihan at pakikipag-usap sa ating komunidad. Kapag may mga tao na nagkukuwento ng kanilang mga problema, may mga miyembro ng komunidad na nagtatanong tungkol sa nararamdaman ng iba. Kung ang isang miyembro ng inyong komunidad ay palaging nagtatanong tungkol sa nararamdaman ng ibang tao kapag sila ay nagkukuwento ng kanilang problema, anong isang mabuting gawi ang pinaka-direkta niyang ipinapakita?','Epektibong komunikasyon','Empatiya','Aktibong pakikinig','Pagiging magalang','B','Ang empatiya ay ang pag-unawa at malasakit sa nararamdaman ng iba, lalo na sa panahon ng suliranin.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,35,NULL,'Ang pagkakaintindihan at mahusay na pakikipag-usap sa ating komunidad ay napakahalaga. Kapag ang mga tao ay nagbabahagi ng kanilang mga suliranin, may mga kasapi ng komunidad na nagtatanong tungkol sa kanilang mga nararamdaman. Alin sa sumusunod ang pinakapangunahing halimbawa ng "epektibong komunikasyon" sa pagitan ng mga miyembro ng komunidad?','Ang paggamit ng maraming teknikal na termino para magmukhang matalino.','Ang pagsasalita nang mahaba at walang tigil para maiparating ang lahat ng ideya.','Ang pagpaparinig ng opinyon kahit hindi tinatanong.','Ang pagpapahayag ng ideya nang malinaw at nauunawaan ng iba.','D','Ito ang epektibong komunikasyon — maayos, malinaw, at may layunin ang pagsasalita.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,36,NULL,'Ang mga patakaran sa komunidad ay ginagawa upang mapanatili ang kaayusan, kalinisan, at kaligtasan ng mga tao. Mahalagang malaman natin kung alin sa mga ito ang tumutulong upang mapanatiling malinis ang ating kapaligiran. Ano ang patakaran sa komunidad na makakatulong para mapanatiling malinis ang mga lugar?','Ipagbawal ang mga bagong tindahan sa mga lugar na tirahan','Magtakda ng oras ng pag-uwi para sa mga bata','Magmulta sa mga taong nagtatapon ng basura sa maling lugar','Hikayatin ang mga tao na magtanim ng puno sa bakuran','C','Ang disiplina sa pagtatapon ng basura ay susi sa malinis na kapaligiran.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,37,NULL,'Mahalagang malaman ng bawat mamamayan, lalo na ng kabataan, ang mga patakaran sa kanilang komunidad upang makasunod at makiisa sa mga layunin ng barangay. Kung gusto mong malaman ang mga patakaran sa inyong barangay, saan ka dapat tumingin?','Sa mga usapan ng mga matatanda sa kanto.','Sa mga lumang pahayagan na nakatago sa bahay.','Sa opisyal na website o bulletin board ng barangay hall.','Sa mga social media posts ng iba''t ibang residente.','C','Ang mga opisyal na patakaran at anunsyo ay makikita sa mga formal na sanggunian gaya ng barangay hall.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,38,NULL,'Mahalaga ang katahimikan sa ating komunidad, lalo na sa gabi, upang makapagpahinga ang lahat. Upang mapanatili ang katahimikan, may mga regulasyon o batas na ipinatutupad ang inyong barangay. Kung ang isang pangunahing layunin ng inyong komunidad ay mapanatili ang katahimikan lalo na sa gabi, aling isang regulasyon ang pinaka-direktang nagpapakita ng pagsisikap na makamit ito?','Ang pagbabawal sa pagbebenta ng alak pagkatapos ng hatinggabi.','Ang pagtatakda ng limitasyon sa lakas ng tunog ng musika paglampas ng isang tiyak na oras.','Ang pagbabawal sa pagpapastol ng hayop sa mga residential area.','Ang pag-require sa mga residente na maglinis ng kanilang harapan tuwing umaga.','B','Ito ay tahasang patakaran para mapanatili ang katahimikan, lalo na sa gabi.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,39,NULL,'Isang pangunahing problema sa inyong komunidad ay ang kakulangan ng malinis na inuming tubig. Aling isang proyekto ang direktang makakatulong upang malutas ito?','Ang pagtatayo ng bagong palaruan para sa mga bata','Ang pagpapagawa ng bagong kalsada papunta sa sentro ng bayan.','Ang pagbubuo ng isang sistema ng pagpapadaloy ng malinis na tubig sa mga kabahayan.','Ang pagbibigay ng libreng edukasyon sa mga out-of-school youth.','C','Direktang solusyon ito sa problema sa inuming tubig. Ang iba pang pagpipilian ay hindi kaugnay sa isyung binanggit.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,40,NULL,'Sa pag-aaral ng heograpiya, mahalagang malaman ang tiyak na lokasyon ng isang lugar upang madali itong matagpuan. Ang tiyak na lokasyon ay tumutukoy sa eksaktong kinaroroonan ng isang bagay o lugar. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng tiyak na lokasyon o eksaktong lugar kung saan matatagpuan ang isang bagay?','Ang paaralan ay nasa tabi ng simbahan.','Ang bahay ni Maria ay nasa Barangay San Isidro.','Ang pamilihan ay malapit sa paaralan.','Ang parkeng ito ay mas malaki kaysa sa iba.','B','Ito ay halimbawa ng tiyak na lokasyon dahil binanggit ang eksaktong lugar o address.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,41,NULL,'Sa pag-aaral ng lokasyon, may dalawang uri: tiyak na lokasyon at relatibong lokasyon. Ang relatibong lokasyon ay tumutukoy sa lugar batay sa kinaroroonan nito kaugnay ng ibang lugar. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng relatibong lokasyon, o paglalarawan ng lugar batay sa kinaroroonan ng ibang lugar?','Ang bahay ni Ana ay nasa 1234 Kalayaan St.','Ang paaralan ay nasa likod ng simbahan.','Ang pamilihan ay nasa Barangay Santo Niño.','Ang parkeng ito ay mayroong 20 puno ng mangga.','B','Ito ay relatibong lokasyon dahil inilalarawan ang kinaroroonan batay sa ibang lugar.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,42,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay binubuo ng iba''t ibang pulo at karagatan na bumubuo sa kabuuang teritoryo nito. Mahalagang malaman ng mga mamamayan ang lawak at hangganan ng ating bansa upang maprotektahan ito. Gaano kalawak ang buong teritoryo ng Pilipinas? Kung gusto mong malaman kung gaano kalawak ang teritoryo ng Pilipinas, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Makinig sa sabi-sabi ng iba tungkol sa laki ng bansa','Tumingin sa opisyal na mapa ng Pilipinas at basahin ang datos','Tanungin ang iyong kaibigan kung saan siya nakatira','Sumulat ng sariling palagay kung gaano kalawak ang bansa','B','Ang mapa at opisyal na datos ang tamang sanggunian upang malaman ang lawak ng bansa. • Snaggunian: Agoncillo, T. A. (1990). History of the Filipino people (8th ed.). Garotech Publishing.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,43,NULL,'Ang mga mahahalagang kaganapan sa kasaysayan ng Pilipinas ay nagbigay-daan sa pagbuo ng ating bansa. Sa mga yugtong ito, makikita ang mga pagbabago at pangyayari na humubog sa ating pagkakakilanlan at kasarinlan bilang isang nasyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod na yugto ang unang bahagi ng pagkabuo ng Pilipinas bilang isang bansa?','Pagsasailalim sa mga Amerikano','Pagkakaroon ng sariling saligang batas','Pagsasailalim sa mga Espanyol','Pagsasarili mula sa mga dayuhan','C','Ang pananakop ng mga Espanyol ang unang yugto ng kolonyalismo sa Pilipinas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,44,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas bilang isang bansa ay nabuo sa pamamagitan ng ilang mahahalagang yugto ng kasaysayan — mula sa sinaunang pamayanan, panahon ng pananakop, rebolusyon, at pagkakamit ng kalayaan. Mahalaga na maunawaan ng bawat mag-aaral ang ilan sa mga mahahalagang pangyayari sa pagbuo ng ating bansa. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang unang yugto sa pagkabuo ng Pilipinas bilang isang bansa?','Pananakop ng mga Amerikano','Panahon ng mga katutubong pamayanan','Pagdeklara ng kalayaan sa Kawit, Cavite','Pagpapasa ng Saligang Batas ng 1987','B','Bago pa man dumating ang mga dayuhan, may mga katutubong pamayanan na umiiral na sa Pilipinas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,45,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas bilang isang bansa ay nabuo sa pamamagitan ng ilang mahahalagang yugto ng kasaysayan — mula sa sinaunang pamayanan, panahon ng pananakop, rebolusyon, at pagkakamit ng kalayaan. Mahalaga na maunawaan ng bawat mag-aaral ang ilan sa mga mahahalagang pangyayari sa pagbuo ng ating bansa. Ano ang isang mahalagang pangyayari na nagpahayag ng kasarinlan ng Pilipinas mula sa pananakop?','Paglagda sa Kasunduan sa Biak-na-Bato','Pagdeklara ng Kalayaan noong Hunyo 12, 1898','Pagdating ni Magellan noong 1521','Pagkakatatag ng mga barangay','B','Ito ang opisyal na pahayag ng kalayaan ng Pilipinas mula sa pananakop ng mga Espanyol.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,46,NULL,'Ang mga pambansang sagisag ay nagbibigay ng pagkakakilanlan sa ating bansa. Mahalaga na kilalanin ng bawat mamamayan, lalo na ang mga kabataan, ang mga pangunahing sagisag ng pagiging Pilipino upang mapangalagaan ang ating kultura at pagkakakilanlan. Alin sa mga ibong ito ang tinatawag na pambansang ibon ng Pilipinas?','Agila','Maya','Pigeon','Tagak','A','Ang Philippine Eagle o Agila ang pambansang ibon ng Pilipinas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,47,NULL,'Ang gobyerno ay may iba''t ibang sangay na may kanya-kanyang tungkulin sa ating bansa. Ang bawat sangay ay may mahalagang papel sa pagpapatakbo ng gobyerno at sa paggawa ng mga batas na dapat sundin ng lahat. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sangay ng pamahalaan ang responsable sa pagpapatupad ng mga batas?','Ehekutibo','Lehislatibo','Hudikatura','Pangkalahatang Kawanihan','A','Ang sangay ehekutibo ang nagpapatupad ng mga batas, kabilang ang Pangulo at mga ahensiya',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,48,NULL,'Ang pamahalaan ng Pilipinas ay may tatlong sangay na may kanya-kanyang tungkulin upang matiyak ang kaayusan at kaunlaran ng bansa. Mahalagang malaman ng bawat mamamayan kung alin sa mga ito ang gumagawa ng batas. Alin sa mga sangay ng pamahalaan ang may tungkulin na gumawa at magpasa ng mga batas para sa bansa?','Sangay na nagpapatupad ng batas (Ehekutibo)','Sangay na gumagawa ng batas (Lehislatibo)','Sangay na nagpapaliwanag ng batas (Hudikatura)','Sangay ng lokal na pamahalaan','B','Ang lehislatibo ay binubuo ng Senado at Kongreso na siyang gumagawa ng batas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,49,NULL,'May tatlong pangunahing sangay ang pamahalaan ng Pilipinas: Ehekutibo, Lehislatibo, at Hudikatura. Bawat isa ay may natatanging tungkulin upang mapanatili ang kaayusan at katarungan sa bansa. Alin sa mga sangay ng pamahalaan ang may tungkulin na magpaliwanag o mag-interpret ng mga batas?','Sangay na nagpapatupad ng batas (Ehekutibo)','Sangay na gumagawa ng batas (Lehislatibo)','Sangay na nagpapaliwanag ng batas (Hudikatura)','Pamahalaang Barangay o Lokal','C','Ang hudikatura, sa pamumuno ng Korte Suprema, ang nagpapaliwanag o nag-i-interpret ng batas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,2,50,NULL,'Ang pamahalaan ng Pilipinas ay binubuo ng tatlong sangay na may kanya-kanyang tungkulin. Isa sa mga ito ang responsable sa paggawa ng mga batas na ipinatutupad sa buong bansa upang mapanatili ang kaayusan at kaunlaran. Alin sa mga sangay ng pamahalaan ang may tungkulin na gumawa ng mga batas para sa bansa?','Sangay na nagpapatupad ng batas (Ehekutibo)','Sangay na gumagawa ng batas (Lehislatibo)','Sangay na nagpapaliwanag ng batas (Hudikatura)','Pamahalaang Barangay o Lokal','B','Paulit-ulit na tanong pero ang tamang sagot ay nananatiling Lehislatibo.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,51,NULL,'Ang mga batas ay mahalagang gabay sa pamumuhay ng mga mamamayan. Ngunit upang maging epektibo ito, kailangang may sangay ng pamahalaan na responsable sa pagpapatupad ng mga batas sa buong bansa. Sa Alin sa mga sangay ng pamahalaan ang may tungkulin na magpatupad ng mga batas sa Pilipinas?','Sangay na nagpapatupad ng batas (Ehekutibo)','Sangay na gumagawa ng batas (Lehislatibo)','Sangay na nagpapaliwanag ng batas (Hudikatura)','Sangay na nangangalaga sa paaralan (Pangasiwaan)','A','Ang Ehekutibo ay nagpapatupad ng mga batas, kabilang ang mga programang panserbisy',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,52,NULL,'Mayroong iba''t ibang sangay ang gobyerno ng Pilipinas, at bawat isa ay may kanya- kanyang tungkulin. Ang mga sangay na ito ay may mahalagang papel sa pamamahala ng bansa at sa pagbuo ng mga batas na kailangang sundin ng lahat ng mamamayan. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sangay ng pamahalaan ang may pangunahing tungkulin sa paggawa ng mga batas?','Sangay na nagpapatupad ng batas (Ehekutibo)','Sangay na gumagawa ng batas (Lehislatibo)','Sangay na nagpapaliwanag ng batas (Hudikatura)','Sangay na nangangalaga sa paaralan (Pangasiwaan)','B','Ulit na tanong sa paggawa ng batas — Lehislatibo pa rin ang sagot.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,53,NULL,'Ang iba''t ibang sangay ng gobyerno sa Pilipinas ay may kani-kaniyang mga tungkulin. Ang bawat sangay ay mahalaga sa pamamahala ng bansa at sa pagbuo ng mga batas na kinakailangang sundin ng lahat ng mamamayan. Alin sa mga sumusunod na sangay ng pamahalaan ang responsable sa pagpapatupad ng mga batas?','Ehekutibo','Lehislatibo','Hudikatura','Pangkalahatang Kawanihan','A','Ang Ehekutibo ang nagpapatupad, gaya ng mga programang panlipunan at batas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,54,NULL,'Ang kalusugan ng mga mamamayan ay isang mahalagang aspeto ng ating komunidad. Upang mapabuti ang kalusugan, may mga programa ang gobyerno na nakatuon sa pagtulong at pagsasanay sa mga tao sa ating barangay. Alin sa mga sumusunod na programa ng pamahalaan ang nakatuon sa pagpapaunlad ng kalusugan ng mga mamamayan?','Barangay Health Workers Program','Livelihood Assistance Program','National Literacy Program','Sustainable Agriculture Program','A','Ito ay programang nakatuon sa kalusugan, sa pamamagitan ng mga community health workers.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,55,NULL,'Isa sa mga pangunahing tungkulin ng pamahalaan ay ang tiyakin na may sapat na serbisyong pangkalusugan para sa lahat ng mamamayan. May mga programang pangkalusugan ang ipinatutupad upang mapanatili ang kalusugan ng mga Pilipino. Anong programa ng pamahalaan ang nagbibigay ng libreng bakuna sa mga bata upang sila ay maprotektahan laban sa sakit?','Feeding Program','Oplan Linis','National Immunization Program','Balik Eskwela Program','C','Ito ang programang nagbibigay ng libreng bakuna upang maprotektahan ang kalusugan ng bata.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,56,NULL,'Isa sa mga pangunahing tungkulin ng pamahalaan ay ang tiyakin na may sapat na serbisyong pangkalusugan para sa lahat ng mamamayan. May mga programang pangkalusugan ang ipinatutupad upang mapanatili ang kalusugan ng mga Pilipino. Kapag may sakit ang isang mahirap na pamilya at wala silang pambayad sa ospital, anong ahensiya ng pamahalaan ang makatutulong sa kanila sa pamamagitan ng libreng serbisyong medikal?','PAGASA','PhilHealth','DOST','DepEd','B','Ang PhilHealth ay ahensiyang nagbibigay ng tulong sa gastusing medikal, lalo na sa mga mahihirap.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,57,NULL,'Sa panahon ngayon, maraming impormasyon ang ating nakukuha mula sa internet, telebisyon, at iba’t ibang babasahin. Mahalaga na matutunan nating piliin ang tama, totoo, at kapaki-pakinabang na impormasyon upang hindi tayo malinlang. Ano ang dapat mong gawin upang matiyak na totoo ang impormasyong nabasa mo sa isang website?','Ibahagi agad sa social media','Basahin ito nang mabuti at alamin ang pinagmulan','Tanungin ang iyong kaklase kung totoo ito','Maniwala agad kung ito ay viral','B','Ang pagsusuri sa source at pag-unawa sa nilalaman ang pinakamahalaga upang masigurong totoo ang impormasyon',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,58,NULL,'Sa panahon ngayon, maraming impormasyon ang ating nakukuha mula sa internet, telebisyon, at iba’t ibang babasahin. Mahalaga na matutunan nating piliin ang tama, totoo, at kapaki-pakinabang na impormasyon upang hindi tayo malinlang. Kung gusto mong maghanap ng tamang sagot para sa iyong takdang-aralin, saan ka dapat unang tumingin?','Sa mga kwento ng kaklase','Sa maaasahang aklat o opisyal na website','Sa mga komento sa social media','Sa tsismis ng kapitbahay','B','Ang maaasahang sanggunian gaya ng aklat at opisyal na website ang tamang unang puntahan para sa tumpak at totoong impormasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,59,NULL,'Sa araw-araw na buhay, humaharap tayo sa iba’t ibang sitwasyon kung saan kailangan nating gumawa ng tamang pasya. Sa pamamagitan ng pag-iisip nang mabuti, natututo tayong pumili ng tamang hakbang sa bawat problema. Kung may nakita kang naiwan na pitaka sa silid-aralan, ano ang tamang gawin?','Itago ito at huwag ipaalam sa iba','Ibigay ito sa guro o awtoridad ng paaralan','Iuwi ito at gamitin ang laman','Iwan na lamang ito sa mesa','B','Ang tamang gawain ay isauli ang pitaka sa isang taong may kapangyarihang hawakan ito, tulad ng guro o school authority.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,60,NULL,'Sa araw-araw na buhay, humaharap tayo sa iba’t ibang sitwasyon kung saan kailangan nating gumawa ng tamang pasya. Sa pamamagitan ng pag-iisip nang mabuti, natututo tayong pumili ng tamang hakbang sa bawat problema. Kung hindi mo naiintindihan ang aralin, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Tumigil na lang sa pag-aaral','Kopyahin na lang ang sagot ng kaklase','Magtanong sa guro o magbasa muli','Huwag na lang pansinin ang leksyon','C','Kung nahihirapan sa aralin, magtanong o magreview upang matuto at hindi umasa sa pandaraya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,61,NULL,'Isa sa mga pangunahing tungkulin ng pamahalaan ay ang pagbibigay ng edukasyon para sa lahat. Iba’t ibang programa ang isinasagawa upang matulungan ang mga mag- aaral na makapasok at makapagtapos sa pag-aaral Alin sa mga sumusunod ang programa ng pamahalaan na naglalayong mabigyan ng libreng edukasyon ang mga kabataan sa pampublikong paaralan?','Feeding Program','Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps)','Libreng Edukasyon sa Pampublikong Paaralan','Oplan Kalusugan','C','Isa sa mga pangunahing programa ng pamahalaan ay ang pagbibigay ng libre at dekalidad na edukasyon sa mga pampublikong paaralan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,62,NULL,'Sa panahon ngayon, napakaraming impormasyon ang makikita sa internet, aklat, telebisyon, at iba pang babasahin. Mahalaga na matutunan ng mga mag-aaral kung paano pumili ng tama at mapagkakatiwalaang impormasyon. Alin sa mga programang ito ng pamahalaan ang tumutulong upang mapanatili ang kapayapaan at kaligtasan sa mga barangay? Ano ang dapat mong gawin upang matiyak na tama at maaasahan ang isang impormasyon mula sa internet?','Ibahagi agad ito sa mga kaibigan','Basahin lamang ang pamagat at hindi ang buong nilalaman','Tiyaking galing ito sa opisyal na website o mapagkakatiwalaang sanggunian','Maniwala agad kung marami ang nag-share sa social media','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,63,NULL,'Sa araw-araw na buhay, humaharap tayo sa mga sitwasyong kailangan nating mag-isip nang mabuti upang makagawa ng tamang desisyon. Ang paggamit ng tamang pag-iisip ay tumutulong upang malutas ang simpleng suliranin sa paraang responsable. Kung may nakita kang kaklaseng niloloko o binu-bully ng iba, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Tumawa at sumama sa pambubully','Hindi makialam at lumayo','Sabihin sa guro o matanda upang matulungan ang kaklase','Kunan ng video at i-post sa social media','C','Ang pakikisangkot sa tama ay isang uri ng pagtatanggol sa naaapi at pagpapakita ng malasakit.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,64,NULL,'Isa sa mga layunin ng pamahalaan ay ang mapanatili ang kapayapaan at kaayusan sa bansa. Upang maisakatuparan ito, may mga programang ipinatutupad para maiwasan ang gulo, labanan ang krimen, at itaguyod ang katahimikan sa bawat komunidad. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang programa ng pamahalaan na may layuning labanan ang kriminalidad at panatilihin ang katahimikan sa mga komunidad?','Oplan Balik Eskwela','Oplan Tokhang','National Feeding Program','Brigada Eskwela','B','Ang Oplan Tokhang ay programa ng gobyerno para labanan ang kriminalidad, lalo na ang droga.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,65,NULL,'Sa panahon ng makabagong teknolohiya, maraming impormasyon ang mabilis nating nakukuha mula sa internet, telebisyon, at iba’t ibang babasahin. Mahalaga na matutunan natin kung alin ang mapagkakatiwalaan upang hindi tayo malinlang. Paano mo malalaman kung ang impormasyon sa isang website ay mapagkakatiwalaan?','Kapag ito ay may makulay na disenyo at maraming larawan','Kapag ito ay galing sa kilalang tao sa social media','Kapag ito ay galing sa opisyal na website ng pamahalaan o edukasyonal na institusyon','Kapag ito ay maraming likes at shares','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,66,NULL,'Sa pang-araw-araw na buhay, mahalagang gamitin ang tamang pag-iisip sa pagharap sa mga simpleng suliranin. Ang pagiging mapanuri at responsable sa paggawa ng desisyon ay nagpapakita ng mabuting pag-uugali.? Kung may hindi pagkakaunawaan sa inyong grupo habang gumagawa ng proyekto, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Tumigil sa pagtulong at hayaang matapos ng iba','Sigawan ang kagrupo upang mapansin ang iyong opinyon','Makinig sa opinyon ng bawat isa at magtulungan','Umalis sa grupo at gumawa mag-isa','C','Ang pakikipag-ugnayan at pakikinig sa grupo ay susi sa mabisang kolaborasyon',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,67,NULL,'Upang mapaunlad ang kabuhayan ng mga mamamayan at ekonomiya ng bansa, ang pamahalaan ay naglulunsad ng mga programang nagbibigay ng tulong sa hanapbuhay, negosyo, at pagkakaroon ng sapat na kita. Mahalagang malaman natin ang mga programang ito. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang programa ng pamahalaan na tumutulong sa mga mahihirap na pamilya sa pamamagitan ng pagbibigay ng tulong-pinansyal at oportunidad sa kabuhayan?','Brigada Eskwela','Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program (4Ps)','National Immunization Program','Oplan Balik Eskwela','B','Ang 4Ps ay nagbibigay ng pinansyal na tulong sa mahihirap upang matulungan sa edukasyon, kalusugan, at kabuhayan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,68,NULL,'Araw-araw tayong humaharap sa mga sitwasyong kailangan nating pag-isipan nang mabuti ang ating kilos at desisyon. Sa pamamagitan ng maayos na pag-iisip, nakapipili tayo ng tamang hakbang upang maiwasan ang problema at makagawa ng mabuti.? Kung may nakita kang kaklaseng nangongopya habang may pagsusulit, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Gayahin siya upang makapasa rin','Huwag pansinin at magpanggap na walang nakita','Sabihin sa guro upang maitama ang ginagawa','Pagsabihan sa harap ng buong klase','C','Dapat ipagbigay-alam sa awtoridad upang matigil ang maling gawaing pang-akademiko.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,69,NULL,'Araw-araw tayong humaharap sa mga sitwasyong kailangan nating pag-isipan nang mabuti ang ating kilos at desisyon. Sa pamamagitan ng maayos na pag-iisip, nakapipili tayo ng tamang hakbang upang maiwasan ang problema at makagawa ng mabuti. Kung may problema sa inyong bahay at nalulungkot ka, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Sarilinin ang problema at huwag magsalita','Magalit sa mga kaklase kahit wala silang kasalanan','Maghanap ng taong mapagkakatiwalaan at magbahagi ng saloobin','Laktawan ang klase at manatili sa bahay','C','Ang pagsasalita at pagbabahagi ng nararamdaman ay makatutulong upang mapagaan ang kalooban.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,70,NULL,'Isa sa mga layunin ng pamahalaan ay ang mapabuti ang daloy ng transportasyon, komunikasyon, at serbisyo sa bansa. Kaya’t may mga proyektong imprastruktura na ipinatutupad upang mapaunlad ang mga lansangan, gusali, at iba pang estruktura para sa kapakinabangan ng mamamayan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang programa ng pamahalaan na may layuning magtayo at mag-ayos ng mga daan at tulay sa buong bansa?','Oplan Balik Eskwela','Build, Build, Build Program','National Feeding Program','4Ps (Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program)','B','Ang programang ito ay nagpapaunlad ng imprastruktura, tulad ng mga kalsada, tulay, at gusali.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,71,NULL,'Isa sa mga layunin ng pamahalaan ay ang mapabuti ang daloy ng transportasyon, komunikasyon, at serbisyo sa bansa. Kaya’t may mga proyektong imprastruktura na ipinatutupad upang mapaunlad ang mga lansangan, gusali, at iba pang estruktura para sa kapakinabangan ng mamamayan. Anong pangunahing benepisyo ang naidudulot ng maayos na imprastruktura tulad ng kalsada at tulay?','Mas mabilis ang paglalakbay at pagdadala ng produkto','Nadadagdagan ang bilang ng pulis','Bumababa ang presyo ng kuryente','Tumataas ang sahod ng mga guro','A','Ang maayos na imprastruktura ay nagpapabilis sa paglalakbay, negosyo, at ekonomiya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,72,NULL,'Sa panahon ng makabagong teknolohiya, maraming impormasyon ang madaling makuha mula sa internet, telebisyon, aklat, at iba’t ibang babasahin. Mahalagang matutunan kung paano tukuyin ang tama, tumpak, at mapagkakatiwalaang impormasyon upang makaiwas sa maling paniniwala o balita.? Kapag naghahanap ka ng impormasyon para sa takdang-aralin, saan ka dapat unang tumingin?','Sa tsismis ng kapitbahay','Sa mga kwento ng kaklase','Sa opisyal na website o aklat na may awtor','Sa social media posts ng hindi kilalang tao','C','Ang awtorisado at maaasahang mga sanggunian ay nagbibigay ng tumpak na impormasyon.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,73,NULL,'Sa panahon ng makabagong teknolohiya, maraming impormasyon ang madaling makuha mula sa internet, telebisyon, aklat, at iba’t ibang babasahin. Mahalagang matutunan kung paano tukuyin ang tama, tumpak, at mapagkakatiwalaang impormasyon upang makaiwas sa maling paniniwala o balita.? Ano ang tamang gawin kapag may nabasa kang balitang hindi ka sigurado kung totoo?','I-share agad sa social media','Ipasa sa mga kaibigan kahit di pa nababasa ng buo','Suriin muna ang pinagmulan at ikumpara sa ibang mapagkakatiwalaang sanggunian','Maniwala agad basta maraming likes at comments','C','Mahalaga ang fact-checking upang maiwasan ang fake news.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,74,NULL,'Araw-araw, humaharap tayo sa mga sitwasyong kailangang pag-isipan kung ano ang tama o mali. Sa paggamit ng tamang pag-iisip, natututo tayong gumawa ng mabuting desisyon para sa sarili at sa kapwa. Kung may nakita kang kaklase na nahulog ang kanyang pera, ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Kunin ito at itago','Bilhin ng kendi ang nakita mong pera','Isauli ito sa kaklase o ibigay sa guro','Tawanan at huwag pansinin','C','Ang katapatan ay mahalagang asal, kaya dapat isauli ang anumang naiwang bagay.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',1,3,75,NULL,'Araw-araw, humaharap tayo sa mga sitwasyong kailangang pag-isipan kung ano ang tama o mali. Sa paggamit ng tamang pag-iisip, natututo tayong gumawa ng mabuting desisyon para sa sarili at sa kapwa. Kung may hindi pagkakaintindihan sa inyong pangkat, ano ang dapat gawin upang ito ay maresolba?','Layuan ang grupo at gumawa ng sariling proyekto','Makinig sa opinyon ng bawat isa at mag-usap ng maayos','Magalit at isumbong agad sa punong-guro','Pumili ng kakampi at palalain ang sitwasyon','B','Sa hindi pagkakaunawaan, ang dayalogo at respeto sa opinyon ay susi sa pagkakasundo.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,1,NULL,'May problema si Albert dahil marami siyang larawan at VIDEO pero maliit lang ang STORAGE ng SOFTWARE. Ano ang pinakamainam na solusyon?','Tanggalin ang lahat ng larawan at VIDEO maliban sa mga pinakamahalaga.','Paggamit ng mas malaking STORAGE DEVICE ay maaring maging kumplikado at hindi praktikal para sa lahat ng gumagamit.','I-compress ang lahat ng larawan at VIDEO para mabawasan ang laki ng FILES.','Hatiin ang kanyang SCAPBOOM sa dalawang bahagi, isa para sa kanyang pagkabata at isa para sa kanyang pagtanda.','C','I-compress ang lahat ng larawan at video para mabawasan ang laki ng files. Ang compression ay isang epektibong paraan upang mabawasan ang laki ng mga larawan at video files nang hindi kailangang burahin ang mga ito o bumili agad ng bagong storage. Gumagamit ito ng software o algorithm na nagsisiksik ng data para maging mas maliit ang file size habang pinananatili ang sapat na kalidad.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,2,NULL,'Si Bobby ay naghahanda para sa MARATHON. Ano ang makatulong para tumagal siya sa pagtakbo at maiwasan ang sakit ng kalamnan pagkatapos?','Magpatugtog ng masiglang musika habang tumatakbo','Uminom ng maraming tubig bago, habang, at pagkatapos tumakbo','Magdagdag ng WEIHGT TRAINING sa kanyang ROUTINE','Magpahinga ng isang linggo bago ang marathon','B','Ang hydration o sapat na pag-inom ng tubig ay mahalaga para sa performance at recovery ng katawan ng mga tumatakbo, lalo na sa mahahabang distansya tulad ng marathon.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,3,NULL,'Si Edward ay gumagawa ng DIGITAL SCRAPBOOK pero kulang ang STORAGE ng SOFTWARE. Ano ang pinakamainam na solusyon sa problema niya?','Tanggalin ang ibang larawan at VIDEO at piliin lang ang pinakamahalaga','Gumamit ng mas malaking STORAGE DEVICE kahit medyo komplikado','I-compress ang mga larawan at VIDEO para lumiit ang file SIZE','Hatiin ang scrapbook sa dalawang bahagi – pagkabata at pagtanda Sabihin lang kung gusto mong gawing mas maikli pa o iayon sa partikular na grade level.','C','Ang pag-compress ng mga larawan at video ay isang mabisang paraan upang paliitin ang laki ng mga file nang hindi kinakailangang burahin ang mga ito. Sa ganitong paraan, makakatipid si Edward ng storage space at maipagpapatuloy niya ang paggawa ng digital scrapbook nang hindi nawawala ang mga mahahalagang alaala.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,4,NULL,'Nais malaman ni Ana kung paano nakaapekto ang mga aral ng kanyang lolo at lola sa kanyang paniniwala. Ano ang makatulong sa kanya para maunawaan ito?','Magbasa ng libro tungkol sa pagpahalaga pero hindi isama ang karanasan niya sa lolo at lola','Magtanong sa mga kaibigan kung ano ang pinapahalagahan nila','Magnilay sa mga aral ng kanyang lolo at lola at ikumpara sa sarili niyang paniniwala','Manood ng pelikula tungkol sa pamilya pero hindi iugnay sa sarili niyang buhay','C','Upang maunawaan ni Ana kung paano nakaapekto ang mga aral ng kanyang lolo at lola sa kanyang paniniwala, kailangan niyang pag-isipan at suriin ang mga turo ng kanyang mga lolo’t lola at ikumpara ito sa mga paniniwala at pagpapahalaga na mayroon siya ngayon. Sa pamamagitan ng pagmumuni-muni (o pag-ninilay), mas mauunawaan niya kung alin sa mga ito ang kanyang naipamana, tinanggap, o binago.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,5,NULL,'Si Edna ay gumagawa ng isang ulat tungkol sa iba’t ibang anyo ng pamilya sa lipunan. Nais niyang matiyak na tama at mapagkatiwalaan ang impormasyong kanyang ilalahad. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamainam na hakbang upang makamit ito?','Manood lamang ng mga palabas sa telebisyon na tumatalakay sa pamilya kahit hindi tiyak ang pinagmulan ng impormasyon.','Umasa sa mga POST sa SOCIAL MEDIA at BLOG na nagpapakita ng mga larawan at personal na opinyon tungkol sa pamilya.','Magsaliksik gamit ang mga aklat, JOURNAL na sinusuri ng mga eksperto (peer- reviewed), at mga WEBSITE ng kilalang institusyon sa larangan ng sosyolohiya at pamilya, at tiyaking suriin ang pagiging maaasahan ng mga ito.','Humingi lamang ng personal na salaysay mula sa mga kakilala at gamitin ito bilang pangunahing batayan ng ulat.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,6,NULL,'Kung kailangan mong ipaliwanag sa isang taong hindi pamilyar sa inyong pamilya ang kahalagahan at gampanin ng bawat kasapi nito, alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraan upang maunawaan nila ito nG malinaw?','Magsulat ng isang napakahabang sanaysay na naglalaman ng lahat ng detalye tungkol sa inyong pamilya.','Magpakita lamang ng mga larawan ng inyong pamilya ng walang anumang paliwanag.','Maghanda ng isang malinaw at organisadong presentasyon na may mga larawan at maikling paglalarawan ng papel at kontribusyon ng bawat miyembro.','Magbahagi lamang ng mga hiwa-hiwalay na karanasan na walang malinaw na pagkakaugnay.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,7,NULL,'Nais mong iparating sa iyong mga kamag-aral ang kahalagahan ng bawat miyembro ng iyong pamilya sa isang malinaw at organisadong paraan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraanupang maisagawa ito?','Sumulat ng isang mahabang salaysay na naglalahad ng lahat ng detalye ng inyong buhay pamilya.','Gumawa lamang ng isang payak na FAMILY TREE na nagpapakita ng mga pangalan at ugnayan ng bawat isa.','Maghanda ng isang presentasyon na may kasamang mga larawan at maikling paliwanag tungkol sa papel at kontribusyon ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya.','Magbahagi ng magkakahiwalay na kwento tungkol sa mga miyembro ng pamilya na walang malinaw na pagkakaugnay.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,8,NULL,'Nahihirapan si Aling Rosa na itakda ang araw at oras ng kanilang lingguhang salu-salo dahil hindi tugma ang iskedyul ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya. Ano ang pinakamainam na paraan upang makahanap ng solusyon sa sitwasyong ito?','Siya na lamang ang magpapasya kung kailan ito gaganapin, kahit hindi ito angkop sa lahat.','Gumamit ng isang ONLINE POLL o SURVEY upang hayaan ang bawat isa na pumili ng araw at oras na akma sa kanilang iskedyul.','Tanggalin na lamang ang planong magkaroon ng REGULAR na FAMILY DINNER.','Magdaos ng isang porum o pag-uusap ng buong pamilya upang malaman ang iskedyul ng bawat isa at makabuo ng kasunduan.','D','Ang bukas na pag-uusap at pagkakaroon ng porum ay ang pinakamahusay na paraan upang maresolba ang problema ni Aling Rosa. Sa pamamagitan nito, malalaman ang iskedyul ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya, at magkakaroon sila ng pagkakataon na makapag-usap, magpaliwanag, at magkasundo. Mahalaga ang kompromiso upang masigurong ang napiling araw at oras ay katanggap-tanggap sa nakararami, at upang mapanatili ang diwa ng pagkakaisa at paggalang sa bawat isa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,9,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Mang Bernard ay may mahalagang tradisyon ng pagdiriwang tuwing Pasko. Subalit sa loob ng dalawang taon, hindi nila ito naisagawa dahil sa pandemya at iba''t ibang lokasyon ng mga miyembro ng pamilya, kabilang na ang mga nasa ibang bansa. Paano nila mapapanatili ang koneksyon at diwa ng kanilang tradisyon sa kabila ng mga limitasyong kinahaharap?','Huwag na lamang ipagpatuloy ang tradisyon dahil mahirap itong isagawa sa kasalukuyan.','Magplano ng VIRTUAL na pagtitipon kung saan maaaring makadalo ang lahat, anuman ang kanilang kinaroroonan, gamit ang mga ONLINE PLATFORM tulad ng ZOOM o GOOGLE MEET.','Ipagdiwang lamang ng mga miyembrong nasa iisang lugar ang tradisyon, kahit hindi kumpleto ang pamilya.','Maghintay na lamang ng tamang panahon upang maipagdiwang ito nang personal muli.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,10,NULL,'Tuwing Bagong Taon, may tradisyon ang pamilya ni Aling Maria na magluto ng espesyal na kakanin. Sa taong ito, nawala ang kanilang orihinal na recipe. Ano ang pinakamabisang paraan upang maipagpatuloy ang tradisyon sa kabila ng sitwasyong ito?','Kalimutan na muna ang tradisyon at maghanda na lang ng ibang pagkain.','Lumikha ng bagong bersyon ng kakanin batay sa mga pamilyar na sangkap at ipagpatuloy ang tradisyon sa bagong anyo.','Huwag ipagdiwang ang Bagong Taon ngayong taon.','Umasa na lang na mahanap ang recipe sa susunod na taon bago muling gawin ang tradisyon.','B','Ang layunin ng tradisyon ay pagpapatuloy ng kaugalian at pagsasama-sama ng pamilya, hindi lamang ang eksaktong recipe. Sa halip na tuluyang itigil ang ginagawa taon-taon, ang paggawa ng bagong bersyon ng kakanin gamit ang mga pamilyar na sangkap ay nagpapakita ng pagkamalikhain, pag-aangkop sa sitwasyon, at pagpapahalaga sa diwa ng tradisyon. Sa ganitong paraan, naipagpapatuloy pa rin ang ugnayan ng pamilya at ang espesyal na selebrasyon kahit may pagbabago.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,11,NULL,'Napapansin ng isang pamilya na nagiging sanhi ng hindi pagkaunawaan ang labis na paggamit ng INTERNET at GADGET ng mga anak, na nakaapekto na rin sa kanilang pag-aaral at oras para sa pamilya. Ano ang pinakamainam na paraan upang masolusyunan ito sa paraang makatutulong sa lahat ng miyembro?','Tanggalin agad ang lahat ng GADGETS upang hindi na ito magamit.','Magtakda ng malinaw at makatuwirang oras para sa paggamit ng INTERNET at GADGET, at ipatupad ito nang may gabay at suporta mula sa mga magulang.','Ipaubaya na lamang sa mga anak ang desisyon kung gaano sila katagal gagamit ng INTERNET at GADGETS.','Huwag nang pakialaman ang oras ng paggamit ng INTERNET at hayaang patuloy ito kahit may epekto na sa ibang aspeto ng buhay.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,12,NULL,'Napansin ng mga residente sa barangay ni Aling Rosa na dumarami ang mga basurang nakakalat sa paligid, na nagdudulot ng epekto sa kalinisan at kalusugan ng pamayanan. Ano ang pinakamabisang hakbang upang matugunan ang suliraning ito sa paraang makabuluhan at pangmatagalan?','Hayaang ipagpatuloy ng mga tao ang pagtatapon ng basura kahit saan.','Maglagay ng mga basurahan sa mga tamang lugar at isulong ang maayos na sistema ng paghihiwalay at pangangasiwa ng basura.','Magdaos ng pagpupulong upang talakayin ang isyu, ngunit hindi gumawa ng konkretong hakbang.','Umasa na lang na may kusang maglinis ng paligid kahit walang koordinasyon.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,13,NULL,'Sa isang komunidad, nababahala ang mga tagapangalaga ng sining ng tradisyunal na paggawa ng palayok dahil unti-unti itong nawawala. Bagama’t may mga ONLIN na klase para ituro ito, kaunti lamang ang mga kabataang nakikilahok. Ano ang pinakamabisang hakbang upang mahikayat ang mga kabataan at mapanatili ang tradisyong ito?','Pilitin ang mga kabataan na dumalo sa ONLINE na klase kahit wala silang interes.','Tanggapin na lamang na mawawala na ang tradisyon ng paggawa ng palayok.','Magdaos ng HANDS-ON WORKSHOP upang bigyang pagkakataon ang kabataan na maranasan mismo ang paggawa ng palayok, at gamitin ang ONLINE PLARFORM bilang dagdag na suporta.','Umasa na lamang sa ONLINE PLAFORM kahit hindi ito gaanong pinapansin ng mga kabataan.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,14,NULL,'Sa isang komunidad, inilunsad ang isang programa para sa libreng pagsasanay sa paggamit ng COMPUTER at INTERNET na para lamang sa mga kabataang walang sariling kagamitan o ACCESS sa teknolohiya. Gayunpaman, kakaunti ang sumasali, kahit malinaw na sila ang pangunahing nangangailangan. Ano ang maaaring gawin upang mahikayat silang makibahagi sa programa?','Sabihing ang mga batang hindi sasali ay tinatanggihan ang tulong ng barangay.','Bigyan lamang ng pagkakataong sumali ang mga kabataang aktibong interesado—ang mga walang gana ay hindi na kailangang isali.','Gamitin ang programa bilang batayan sa pag-priyoridad ng ayuda para sa pamilya ng mga kalahok.','Alamin mula sa mga kabataan kung ano ang hadlang sa kanilang pakikilahok at bumuo ng mga hakbang upang gawing mas angkop ang programa sa kanilang pangangailangan.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,15,NULL,'Sa isang komunidad, napansin ng mga lider ang mababang pakikiisa ng mga residente sa mga proyektong pangkomunidad. Gumagamit sila ng online forum bilang pangunahing paraan ng komunikasyon, ngunit kakaunti lamang ang aktibong sumasagot o lumalahok. Sa iyong palagay, ano ang pinakamalamang na dahilan ng kawalan ng partisipasyon?','Tamad at walang pakialam ang karamihan sa mga residente kaya hindi sila sumasali.','Hindi interesado ang mga residente dahil hindi sila sanay makibahagi sa mga ganitong gawain.','Kulang ang kaalaman ng mga residente tungkol sa mga proyekto kaya hindi sila nakikilahok.','Hindi akma ang kasalukuyang paraan ng komunikasyon sa kakayahan o sitwasyon ng maraming residente.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,16,NULL,'Sa isang paaralan, ipinatupad ang bagong sistema ng segregated waste MANAGEMENT gamit ang kulay-coded na basurahan at isang mobile app para masubaybayan ang dami ng narecycle. Gayunpaman, marami sa mga estudyante ang hindi sumusunod sa wastong paraan ng pagtatapon. Ano ang pinakaangkop na solusyon sa ganitong sitwasyon?','Bigyan ng parusa ang mga estudyanteng hindi marunong sumunod upang matuto sila ng leksyon.','Kilalanin lamang ang mga masisipag na estudyante at huwag nang pansinin ang mga tamad at walang pakialam.','Ipaliwanag nang malinaw ang kahalagahan ng programa sa pamamagitan ng EDUCATION CAMPAIGNS at aktwal na pagsasanay, habang ginagamit ang APP para sa gabay at FEEDBACK.','Isuko na lamang ang programa dahil wala namang silbi kung ang mga estudyante ay hindi marunong makipagtulungan.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,17,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay binubuo ng maraming isla at malawak na katubigan. Gayunpaman, may mga bahagi ng teritoryo nito na mahirap bantayan dahil sa kawalan ng disiplina at kakayahan ng ilang lokal na komunidad. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pangunahing hamon sa pagpapanatili ng kaayusan at seguridad sa Pambansang Teritoryo ng Pilipinas?','Ang kapabayaan ng mga lokal na mangingisda na patuloy sa ilegal na aktibidad kahit ipinagbabawal.','Ang hindi paggalang ng ibang bansa sa soberenya ng Pilipinas sa mga pinag- aagawang teritoryo.','Ang kakulangan ng interes ng mga mamamayan sa pagbabantay at pangangalaga ng mga hangganan ng bansa.','Ang limitadong kakayahan ng pamahalaan sa pagpapatrolya at pamamahala sa mga malalayong lugar.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,18,NULL,'Sa kabila ng pagsisikap ng pamahalaan na pag-isahin ang bansa, marami pa ring rehiyon at pangkat etniko sa Pilipinas ang patuloy na kumikilos ayon sa kani-kanilang kultura at paniniwala. Paano ito nagiging hadlang sa pagbuo ng isang matatag at iisang pambansang identidad?','Ang mga lokal na kultura at paniniwala ay kadalasang salungat sa mga pambansang patakaran.','Ang mga pangkat etniko ay mas pinipiling ihiwalay ang kanilang sarili sa pambansang usapin.','Ang mga rehiyon ay mas inuuna ang pansariling interes kaysa sa kapakanan ng buong bansa.','Ang kakulangan sa interes ng mga minoridad na tanggapin ang pambansang wika at simbolo ng bansa.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,19,NULL,'Isang bagong paaralan ang nagpaplano na gumawa ng mural na magtatampok ng mga sagisag ng Pilipinas. Ayon sa ilang guro, ang tanging tamang paraan ng paglikha nito ay ang paggamit lamang ng mga tradisyonal na simbolo tulad ng watawat, kalabaw, at bahay kubo. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakatamang paraan upang matiyak na ang mural ay nagpapakita ng tunay na "Pilipinong" pagkakilanlan?','Gumamit lamang ng mga sagisag na matagal nang kinikilala sa mga aklat pangkasaysayan at opisyal na dokumento ng pamahalaan.','Iwasan ang paggamit ng modernong simbolo o mga representasyong konektado sa kabataan dahil hindi ito bahagi ng tradisyon.','Magpokus sa mga simbolo mula sa mga rehiyon na may mahalagang bahagi sa kasaysayan ng bansa, tulad ng Luzon.','Isama ang mga sagisag na nagmula sa mga kilalang bayani at relihiyon lamang upang maipakita ang tunay na pagkakakilanlan ng bansa.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,20,NULL,'Sa kabila ng malawakang paglaganap ng pekeng gamot sa isang rehiyon sa Pilipinas, may paniniwala ang ilang opisyal na ang problema ay maaaring masolusyunan nang mabilis kung bibigyan ng eksklusibong kapangyarihan ang sangay ng ehekutibo. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraan upang mapabilis ang pagtugon sa problemang ito ayon sa pananaw na ito?','Pahintulutan ang Ehekutibo na agad magpatupad ng mga regulasyong hindi na kailangang idaan sa batas, upang masugpo ang pekeng gamot.','Hayaang magsampa lamang ng kaso ang Hudikatura kung may reklamo, habang hinihintay ang bagong batas mula sa Lehislatura.','Gamitin ng Ehekutibo ang kapangyarihan nito para lumikha ng mga TASK FORCE at magpatupad ng agarang operasyon laban sa pekeng gamot kahit walang batas na nagbibigay ng partikular na mandato.','Maghintay ng hakbang mula sa Lehislatura at Hudikatura bago kumilos upang maiwasan ang paglabag sa proseso ng batas.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,21,NULL,'Ang pamahalaan ay naglunsad ng libreng pagsasanay sa mga manggagawang Pilipino sa sektor ng turismo upang mapabuti ang kita ng bansa mula sa turismo. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang tanging layunin na dapat pagtuunan ng programa upang makamit ang layuning ito?','Palakasin ang kakayahan ng mga manggagawa upang makapagbigay ng serbisyo na karapat-dapat sa mga dayuhang turista lamang.','Tiyakin na lahat ng turista ay positibo ang karanasan sa Pilipinas para sa mas magandang INTERNATIONAL REPUTATION.','Ituon ang pagsasanay sa mga lugar na may pinakamaraming turista kahit hindi ito naaabot ng lokal na komunidad.','Piliin lamang ang mga may dating karanasan sa industriya para sa libreng pagsasanay upang mas mabilis ang epekto sa turismo.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,22,NULL,'Isang mamamayan mula sa isang rural na komunidad ang nakararanas ng hirap dahil sa patuloy na pagtaas ng presyo ng mga pangunahing bilihin. Wala siyang sapat na edukasyon sa ekonomiya at limitado ang kanyang access sa impormasyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakaangkop na paraan upang matugunan ang kanyang alalahanin, habang isinasaalang-alang ang kanyang karapatan at kakayahang makilahok sa lipunan?','Manahimik na lamang at tanggapin ang sitwasyon dahil hindi siya eksperto sa ekonomiya.','Maghintay ng ayuda mula sa gobyerno nang hindi nakikilahok sa usapin.','Makipag-ugnayan sa mga lokal na opisyal upang maiparating ang kanyang saloobin at matulungan siyang maunawaan ang sitwasyon.','Umasa na lang sa opinyon ng ibang tao at sundin kung ano man ang kanilang mungkahi.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,23,NULL,'Isang residente sa isang komunidad ang nakapansin ng patuloy na pagtatapon ng basura ng isang pabrika sa ilog na malapit sa kanilang lugar. Wala siyang sapat na koneksyon sa mga lokal na opisyal at hindi rin siya sanay makipag-usap sa mga opisyal ng gobyerno. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang hakbang na maaaring gawin ng mamamayan upang gampanan ang kanyang tungkulin at protektahan ang kalikasan, habang isinasaalang-alang ang kanyang karapatang mamuhay sa isang malinis na kapaligiran?','Iwasan na lang dumaan sa ilog upang hindi na makakita ng mga ganitong uri ng polusyon.','Ibahagi ang impormasyon sa SOCIAL MEDIA na walang sapat na ebidensya upang mapahiya ang pabrika.','Makipag-ugnayan sa isang lokal na environmental group upang matulungan siyang maghain ng ulat sa tamang ahensya.','Siraan ang pabrika sa komunidad upang mahinto ang kanilang operasyon.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,24,NULL,'Si Jordan ay isang senior high school student na masigasig sa paggamit ng SOCIAL MEDIA. Mahilig siyang mag-POST ng kanyang mga DAILY ACTIVITIES, OPINION, at personal na karanasan. Alin sa mga sumusunod na gawain ang pinaka-hindi responsable at maaaring magdulot ng panganib sa kanyang sarili o sa iba?','Pag-SET ng kanyang PROFILE sa "PRIVATE" upang limitahan ang makakita ng kanyang mga POST.','Pagbabahagi ng kanyang opinyon tungkol sa mga isyung panlipunan nang may respeto sa iba.','Paglalagay ng kanyang buong ADDRESS at SCHOOL SCHEDULE sa kanyang SOCIAL MEDIA BIO.','Pag-LIKE at pag-SHARE ng mga educational content na may kaugnayan sa kanyang kurso.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,1,25,NULL,'Gagawa si Carlo ng DIGITAL TIMELINE para sa kanyang proyekto sa Araling Panlipunan, na naglalaman ng mahahalagang pangyayari mula sa kanyang kabataan hanggang kasalukuyan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakaangkop na hakbang upang matiyak na makatutuhanan at kapani-paniwala ang kanyang gawain?','Pumili ng mga EVENT na sa tingin niya ay pinakanatatangi, kahit walang sapat na dokumentasyon.','Gamitin ang kanyang memorya bilang pangunahing batayan ng lahat ng detalye sa TIMELINE.','Mangalap ng mga patunay tulad ng larawan, sertipiko, o pahayag ng magulang upang suportahan ang bawat pangyayari.','Gawing makulay at masining ang TIMELINE upang maging kaaya-aya sa paningin ng guro.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,26,NULL,'Gumagawa si Eliza ng isang sanaysay tungkol sa kung paano nakaimpluwensiya ang kanyang pamilya sa kanyang pananaw sa buhay. Nais niyang masigurong ang kanyang isinulat ay sumusunod sa prinsipyo ng INFORMATION LITERACY. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraan upang matiyak na ang kanyang sanaysay ay tumpak at mapagkakatiwalaan?','Isulat ang sanaysay base lamang sa kanyang damdamin at pansariling karanasan, kahit walang suporta mula sa iba pang sanggunian.','Mangalap ng impormasyon mula sa mga pamilyar na BLOG at SOCIALsocial MEDIA POST, kahit hindi ito na-VERIFY.','Gumamit ng mapagkakatiwalaang sanggunian gaya ng aklat, artikulo, at pahayag ng eksperto, at tiyaking nagbibigay siya ng tamang pagkilala sa mga pinagkunan.','Umasa lamang sa mga opinyon ng mga kaibigan at isama ang mga ito bilang batayan ng kanyang sanaysay.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,27,NULL,'Habang nagsasaliksik tungkol sa iba''t ibang uri ng pamilya para sa isang proyekto sa paaralan, nakakita ka ng magkakasalungat na impormasyon tungkol sa kahulugan ng "pamilya" sa iba''t ibang ONLINE na pinagkukunan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahusay na nagpapakita ng responsableng INFORMATION LITERACY?','Tanggapin ang unang kahulugan na nakita mo, dahil madali itong makuha.','Piliin ang kahulugan na pinakamabuti sa iyong personal na paniniwala tungkol sa pamilya.','Ihambing at i-CONTRAST ang maraming kahulugan mula sa mga mapagkakatiwalaang pinagkukunan, pag-aralan ang kanilang mga pananaw at pagkiling bago bumuo ng iyong sariling kaalaman.','Itapon ang lahat ng ONLINE na pinagkukunan at umasa lamang sa mga personal na karanasan upang tukuyin ang "pamilya."','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,28,NULL,'Nagsasaliksik siya tungkol sa mga tungkulin ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya para sa isang presentasyon, at nakakita ng ilang mga pinagkukunan na nag-aalok ng iba''t ibang pananaw. Anong paraan siya nagpapakita ng responsableng INFORMATION LITERACY?','Tanggapin ang unang pinagmulan na iyong nahanap bilang tiyak, para makatipid ng oras.','Umasa lamang sa iyong mga personal na karanasan at obserbasyon sa iyong sariling pamilya.','Ihambing at i-CONTRAST ang impormasyon mula sa maraming pinagkukunan, suriin ang kanilang kredibilidad at mga posibleng pagkiling bago gumawa ng mga konklusyon.','Huwag pansinin ang anumang magkakasalungat na impormasyon at gumamit lamang ng mga pinagkukunang sumusuporta sa iyong mga PRE-EXISTING na paniniwala.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,29,'konklusyon. D. Huwag pansinin ang anumang magkakasalungat na impormasyon at gumamit lamang ng mga pinagkukunang sumusuporta sa iyong mga PRE-EXISTING na paniniwala.\n\n• Sagot: C • Sanggunian: (Association of College and Research Libraries [ACRL], 2016)','Si Ramon ay gumagawa ng ulat tungkol sa mga papel at kahalagahan ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya para sa kanilang proyektong panlipunan. Nais niyang matiyak na ang impormasyong gagamitin niya ay tumpak at mapagkakatiwalaan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahusay na hakbang upang makamit ito?','Pumili ng unang artikulong makita sa internet kahit walang may-akda o petsa ng paglalathala.','Kunin lamang ang impormasyon mula sa personal na karanasan ng mga kakilala, kahit hindi ito napatotohanan.','Suriin ang kredibilidad ng mga pinagkukunan sa pamamagitan ng pagtingin sa may-akda, petsa, at sanggunian, at ikumpara ito sa iba pang mapagkakatiwalaang sources.','Gamitin ang isang website na may maraming graphics at makukulay na disenyo bilang batayan ng impormasyong gagamitin.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,30,NULL,'Si Elena ay gumagawa ng ulat tungkol sa dinamika ng kanilang pamilya. Nais niyang ipakita na may malalim siyang pag-unawa sa papel at kahalagahan ng bawat isa sa kanilang tahanan. Alin sa mga sumusunod na pahayag ang pinakamahusay na nagpapakita nito?','Ang bawat isa sa pamilya ay may papel, ngunit ang mga tungkulin ay dapat nakabatay sa tradisyunal na gampanin ng lalaki at babae.','Ang mga magulang ay dapat magtrabaho at magbigay ng lahat ng kailangan ng pamilya, habang ang mga anak ay mag-aral lamang.','Ang bawat miyembro ng pamilya ay may natatanging ambag batay sa kanilang kakayahan, at lahat ay dapat pakinggan, unawain, at bigyang halaga.','Ang ama ang namumuno, ang ina ang tagapangalaga ng bahay, at ang mga anak ay tagasunod.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,31,NULL,'Ang malalim na pag-unawa ay nagsisimula sa pagkilala sa natatanging katangian, talento, kahinaan, at pangangailangan ng bawat miyembro. Hindi ito simpleng pag-alam ng kanilang mga pangalan at edad, kundi ang pag-unawa sa kanilang mga pananaw, damdamin, at motibasyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang nagpapakita ng malalim na pag-unawa sa kahalagahan ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya?','Ang ama ay nagtatrabaho para kumita ng pera, ang ina ay nag-aalaga ng mga anak, at ang mga anak ay sumusunod sa kanilang mga magulang.','Ang bawat miyembro ng pamilya ay may kanya-kanyang tungkulin, ngunit ang kanilang mga kontribusyon ay nagtutulungan para sa ikabubuti ng lahat.','Ang pamilya ay mahalaga dahil nagbibigay ito ng pagmamahal at suporta sa bawat isa.','Ang mga magulang ay dapat magbigay ng lahat ng pangangailangan ng kanilang mga anak.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,32,NULL,'Si Juan ay nagsasaliksik tungkol sa pinagmulan ng isang natatanging tradisyon ng kanilang pamilya gamit ang INTERNET. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang mahalagang isaalang-alang ni Juan upang matiyak ang kredibilidad ng impormasyong makukuha niya ONLINE?','Magtiwala sa lahat ng impormasyong mababasa niya sa INTERNET dahil malawak ang saklaw nito.','Pumili ng mga WEBSITE na may magagandang disenyo at madaling basahin.','Suriin ang kredibilidad ng mga pinagkukunan, gaya ng awtor, petsa ng paglalathala, at reputasyon ng WEBSITE o organisasyon.','Hanapin lamang ang mga impormasyong sumusuporta sa kanyang paniniwala tungkol sa tradisyon.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,33,NULL,'Nais matuto ni Mang Jose tungkol sa tamang kaalaman sa edukasyon sa sekswalidad para sa kanyang mga anak. Saan siya dapat kumuha ng pinakatiyak at mapagkakatiwalaang impormasyon?','Mga POST sa SOCIAL MEDIA at ONLINE FORUMS','Mga artikulo mula sa eksperto at website ng mga kilalang organisasyon sa kalusugan','Payo mula sa mga kaibigan at kamag-anak','Mga palabas sa TV at pelikula','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,34,NULL,'Natatalakay ang mga hamon na nararanasan ng kinabibilangang pamilya. Isang pamilya ang nakaranas ng problema sa pagpaplano ng kanilang FAMILY VACATION. Nais nilang maghanap ng impormasyon ONLINE para sa mga murang pakete ng TRAVEL. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang mahalagang isaalang-alang upang matiyak ang kredibilidad ng impormasyong makukuha nila ONLINE?','Magtiwala sa lahat ng impormasyong mababasa nila sa mga social media ads.','Pumili ng mga WEBSITE na may magagandang disenyo at maraming followe.','Suriin ang kredibilidad ng mga pinagkukunan, gaya ng travel agency, petsa ng paglalathala ng impormasyon, at mga review mula sa mga tunay na CUSTOMER.','Hanapin lamang ang mga impormasyong sumusuporta sa kanilang gustong destinasyon.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,35,NULL,'Nagsasaliksik si Lorena gamit ang INTERNET tungkol sa iba''t ibang uri ng komunidad. Ano ang dapat niyang gawin para makasigurong totoo at mapagkakatiwalaan ang impormasyon?','Magtiwala agad sa mga nabasa sa BLOG at SOCIAL MEDIA POSTS','Piliin ang mga WEBSITE na maganda ang disenyo at maraming larawan','Suriin kung mapagkakatiwalaan ang pinanggalingan ng IMPORMATION o WEBSITE','Piliin lang ang mga impormasyon na sang-ayon sa kanyang paniniwala','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,36,NULL,'Gumagawa si Daniel ng isang presentasyon tungkol sa mga pagbabagong naganap sa mga lokal na gawi at tradisyon sa kanyang barangay. Gumamit siya ng mga lumang larawan, VIDEO, at panayam mula sa mga matatandang residente. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang hakbang upang matiyak niya ang katumpakan at kredibilidad ng kanyang presentasyon?','Piliin lamang ang mga materyal na nagpapakita ng kagandahan ng kultura upang maging kaaya-aya sa manonood.','Gamitin ang mga larawan at VIDEO basta ito ay galing sa INTERNET, kahit walang tiyak na pinagmulan.','Suriin ang konteksto ng bawat materyal, kabilang ang pinagmulan, petsa ng pagkakakuha, at ang taong nagdokumento nito.','Isali lamang ang mga impormasyon na sumusuporta sa kanyang personal na pananaw.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,37,NULL,'Si Luis ay gumagawa ng ulat tungkol sa mga hakbang ng pamahalaan upang suportahan ang mga mangingisda sa panahon ng tagtuyot. Gumagamit siya ng INTERNET sa pangangalap ng datos. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang hakbang na dapat niyang gawin upang matiyak ang katumpakan at kredibilidad ng kanyang impormasyon?','Piliin ang mga impormasyon mula sa mga sikat na SOCIAL MEDIA INFLUENCERS na may maraming tagasubaybay.','Gamitin ang mga impormasyon mula sa opisyal na WEBSITE ng pamahalaan at kilalang institusyon, at tiyaking suriin ang petsa ng paglalathala at awtoridad ng may-akda.','Gamitin ang mga komento at opinyon mula sa ONLINE FORUM bilang pangunahing batayan ng kanyang ulat.','Hanapin ang mga artikulo na nagpapakita lamang ng positibong epekto ng mga programa upang maiwasan ang kontrobersiya.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,38,NULL,'Ang Barangay San Roque ay may bagong inisyatibo para sa pag-aalaga sa kapaligiran ang "Linggo ng Kalinisan." Gumagamit sila ng isang mobile app para iulat ang mga lugar na kailangang linisin at upang magtala ng mga boluntaryo. Subalit, kakaunti ang gumagamit ng APP at lumalahok sa gawain. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraan upang mapalakas ang partisipasyon ng mga residente?','Ipagbawal ang paggamit ng APP at bumalik sa tradisyonal na pag-aanunsyo sa pamamagitan ng MEGAPHONE.','Maglabas ng mandatoryong ordinansa na nag-uutos sa lahat ng residente na mag-DOWNLOAD at gumamit ng APP.','Makipag-ugnayan sa mga kabataan at lider ng barangay upang magsagawa ng orientation tungkol sa paggamit ng app, ipaliwanag ang layunin ng programa, at ipakita kung paano maaaring tumulong ang bawat isa.','Magdaos ng COMMUNITY CLEAN-UP kahit walang abiso, at ipaabot na lang sa mga residente pagkatapos.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,39,NULL,'Ang bayan ng San Mateo ay nagpatupad ng bagong batas na nagbabawal sa paggamit ng CELLPHONE habang nagmamaneho. Gumamit sila ng mga SIGNAGES, MOBILE APP ALERTS, at impormasyon sa radyo upang ipaalam ito. Gayunman, patuloy pa rin ang paglabag ng maraming motorista. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamabisang paraan sa pagsusuri sa sitwasyong ito?','Hindi sapat ang impormasyon na ipinararating sa mga motorista tungkol sa batas.','Sanay na ang mga motorista sa lumang gawi kaya''t hindi nila agad maisabuhay ang bagong regulasyon.','Mas gusto ng mga motorista ang gumamit ng cellphone kaysa sundin ang batas.','Hindi naniniwala ang mga motorista na mapaparusahan sila kahit lumabag.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,40,NULL,'Saan matatagpuan ang Pilipinas kung ikukumpara sa ibang bansa? Alin sa mga sumusunod ang nagpapakita ng relatibong lokasyon ng Pilipinas?','Sa pagitan ng 4° at 21° hilagang latitud at 116° at 127° silangang longhitud.','Sa kanluran ng Karagatang Pasipiko.','Sa hilaga ng Indonesia.','Isang kapuluan na mayroong higit sa 7,000 na isla.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,41,NULL,'Ang mga mag-aaral sa isang pampublikong paaralan ay gumagawa ng isang presentasyon tungkol sa mga karapatan ng Pilipinas sa WEST PHILLIPINE SEA. Nais nilang tiyakin na ang kanilang impormasyon ay tumpak, legal, at kinikilala sa pandaigdigang antas. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang dapat nilang pangunahing gamitin bilang sanggunian?','Mga VIDEO sa SOCIAL MEDIA na nagpapaliwanag ng isyu sa simpleng paraan.','Mga opisyal na dokumento mula sa United Nations at desisyon ng Permanent Court of Arbitration tungkol sa kaso ng Pilipinas laban sa China.','Mga blog ng mga Pilipinong OFW na may karanasan sa rehiyon.','Mga panayam sa mga mangingisda sa Zambales na direktang naapektuhan ng sigalot.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,42,NULL,'Sa pag-aaral ng Pambansang Teritoryo ng Pilipinas, mahalagang malinaw ang mga konsepto tulad ng soberanya, MARITIME ZONES, at karapatang pandagat. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pangunahing hamon na humahadlang sa tamang pag-unawa ng mga Pilipino sa mga usaping ito?','Limitadong pagbanggit ng mga isyung ito sa mga aralin sa paaralan.','Pagkakaiba-iba ng opinyon ng mga eksperto tungkol sa teritoryo ng Pilipinas.','Pagkalito ng mga mamamayan sa pagkakaiba ng TERROTORIAL SEA, EXCLUSIVE ECONOMIC ZONE, at CONTINENTAL SHELF.','Kakulangan ng interes ng ibang bansa sa pakikipagtulungan sa Pilipinas sa usaping teritoryal.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,43,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay isang bansa na binubuo ng iba''t ibang kultura, wika, at mga pangkat etniko. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang salik na nag-ambag sa pagbubuo ng isang pambansang identidad at pagkakaisa sa Pilipinas?','Ang pagkakaiba-iba ng mga kultura at wika sa iba''t ibang rehiyon ng Pilipinas.','Ang paglaban ng mga Pilipino laban sa mga dayuhang mananakop.','Ang pagtataguyod ng edukasyon at pagpapalaganap ng karunungan sa mga Pilipino.','Ang pag-unlad ng ekonomiya at ang pagtaas ng antas ng pamumuhay ng mga Pilipino.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,44,NULL,'Nais ng isang guro na ipaliwanag sa kanyang mga mag-aaral ang kahulugan at pinagmulan ng mga opisyal na sagisag ng Pilipinas, tulad ng watawat, pambansang awit, at pambansang hayop. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamainam na sanggunian upang matiyak ang katumpakan ng kanyang aralin?','Mga disenyo ng sagisag na ibinahagi ng mga netizen sa SOCIAL MEDIA.','Mga opisyal na pahayag at dokumento mula sa mga ahensya ng pamahalaan tulad ng National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP).','Mga kwento at paliwanag mula sa mga YOUTUBE VLOGGERS tungkol sa kasaysayan ng mga sagisag.','Mga opinyon ng mga guro at estudyante mula sa iba’t ibang paaralan.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,45,NULL,'Kung gusto mong matutunan kung paano nagtutulungan ang tatlong sangay ng pamahalaan ng Pilipinas, saan ka dapat kumuha ng pinaka-tumpak na impormasyon?','Mga artikulo sa balita mula sa iba''t ibang MEDIA OUTLETS.','Mga opinyon at pananaw ng mga eksperto sa politika.','Mga aklat-aralin sa Araling Panlipunan at Sibika.','Ang Konstitusyon ng Pilipinas at mga opisyal na dokumento ng pamahalaan.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,46,NULL,'Nagbigay ng libreng TRAINING ang gobyerno para sa mga nagtatrabaho sa CONSTRUCTION. Ano ang pinakaimportanteng dahilan kung bakit nila ito ginagawa?','Para mas gumaling ang mga manggagawa sa paggawa ng gusali at kalsada.','Para mas maraming taong magkaroon ng trabaho sa construction.','Para mas gumanda ang kalidad ng mga gusali at mapaunlad ang ekonomiya ng bansa.','Para mas malaki ang kita ng mga manggagawa at gumanda ang kanilang buhay.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,47,NULL,'Ang Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE) ay nagsimula ng programang nagbibigay ng libreng teknikal na pagsasanay para sa mga nais magtrabaho sa larangan ng konstruksiyon. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pangunahing layunin ng programang ito, batay sa mga kasalukuyang suliranin sa sektor ng konstruksiyon sa bansa?','Makatulong sa mga dayuhang kompanya na makahanap ng murang lakas- paggawa sa Pilipinas.','Makalikha ng mas maraming oportunidad sa trabaho at matugunan ang kakulangan sa may kasanayang manggagawa sa sektor.','Mapalitan ang mga kasalukuyang manggagawa sa konstruksiyon ng mas bata at mas mabilis na lakas-paggawa.','Mas mapadali ang paggawa ng mga proyektong pampamahalaan sa pamamagitan ng pagtutok sa automation.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,48,NULL,'Laging binabaha ang lugar ni Jaime tuwing umuulan nang malakas. Bilang isang aktibong mamamayan na may kakayahang gumamit ng tamang impormasyon, ano ang pinakamabisang hakbang na maaari niyang gawin upang makapag-ambag sa pangmatagalang solusyon sa problema ng pagbaha sa kanilang komunidad?','Isisi ang lahat ng problema sa lokal na pamahalaan at tumigil na sa pakikilahok sa mga usaping pangkomunidad.','Makipag-away sa SOCIAL MEDIA sa mga taong may ibang pananaw tungkol sa sanhi ng pagbaha.','Magtipon ng impormasyon mula sa mga ulat ng DENR, DPWH, at lokal na datos, at makipagtulungan sa barangay upang magmungkahi ng konkretong solusyon.','Lumipat na lamang ng tirahan upang makaiwas sa baha sa halip na makialam sa suliranin.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,49,NULL,'Matapos ang matinding pagbaha sa kanilang barangay, ginamit ni Gng. Rosa, isang guro, ang kanyang kaalaman sa agham at teknolohiya upang gumawa ng pansamantalang sistema sa paglilinis ng tubig-inumin gamit ang mga simpleng materyales. Nag-organisa rin siya ng pagtulong sa mga naapektuhan. Ano ang pangunahing katangian ng aktibong mamamayan na ipinamalas ni Gng. Rosa sa ganitong sitwasyon?','Pagpapakita ng malasakit sa pamamagitan ng pagbibigay ng donasyon.','Pagtitiwala sa pamahalaan upang lutasin ang problema.','Paggamit ng kanyang kasanayan upang makabuo ng solusyong makatutulong sa komunidad.','Pagpapakalat ng balita tungkol sa baha sa mga social media platform.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,2,50,NULL,'Isang malaking baha ang tumama sa Barangay San Jose. Maraming bahay ang nasira, at maraming tao ang nawalan ng tirahan at pagkain. Si Aling Rosa, isang guro sa elementarya, ay nag-organisa ng isang pangangalap ng tulong para sa mga biktima. Gamit ang kanyang kaalaman sa Agham at teknolohiya, nag-SET up siya ng isang simpleng sistema ng pag-FILTER ng tubig gamit ang mga READILY AVAILABLE available na materyales para maiwasan ang pagkalat ng sakit. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang tungkulin na ipinakita ni Aling Rosa bilang isang mamamayan sa sitwasyong ito?','Pag-oorganisa ng pangangalap ng tulong.','Paggamit ng kanyang kaalaman sa Agham at teknolohiya para sa kapakanan ng komunidad.','Pagbabahagi ng impormasyon sa social media.','Lahat ng nabanggit.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,51,NULL,'Gumagamit si Ana ng isang FITNESS TRACKER na nag re-record ng kanyang mga aktibidad, tulad ng bilang ng hakbang, distansya na nilakad, at RATE ng kanyang puso. Ibinabahagi niya ang kanyang DATA sa isang ONLINE COMMUNITY para sa mga taong may parehong interes. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang kritikal na pagsusuri sa pagbabahagi ni Ana ng kanyang data sa ONLNE COMMUNITY?','Nakakatulong ito sa kanya na ma-MOTIVATE at ma-TRACK ang kanyang progreso.','Maaaring gamitin ng ibang tao ang kanyang data para sa kanilang sariling pakinabang.','Nakakakuha siya ng suporta at inspirasyon mula sa ibang mga miyembro ng community.','Nakakapagbahagi siya ng kanyang karanasan sa pag-ehersisyo sa iba.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,52,NULL,'Si Miguel ay gumagawa ng AUTOBIIOGRAPHY gamit ang isang DIGITAL STORYTELLING TOOL. Ipinapakita niya rito ang mga mahahalagang pangyayari sa kanyang buhay mula pagkabata hanggang ngayon. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahusay na paraan para maipakita niya ang kanyang paglago at pagbabago gamit ang teknolohiya?','Pag-lista lang ng mga mahahalagang petsa at pangyayari.','Paggamit ng mga larawan at video na may maikling paliwanag.','Pagsulat ng mahabang sanaysay na may lahat ng detalye ng buhay niya.','Gawa ng PowerPoint na puro BULLET POINTS lang.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,53,NULL,'Si Ben ay gumagawa ng proyekto tungkol sa kung paano nakaapekto ang mga nakatatanda sa kanyang mga pagpapahalaga. Habang nagsasaliksik ONLINE, nakabasa siya ng artikulo na nagsasabing "lahat ng pagpapahalaga ay natututuhan lamang mula sa mga magulang." Ano ang pinaka-kritikal na paraan para suriin ni Ben ang impormasyong ito?','Tatanggapin agad ang impormasyon dahil nasa artikulo ito.','Iisipin na tama ito dahil galing sa INTERNET.','Susuriin kung mapagkakatiwalaan ang pinagmulan, kung may ebidensya, at kung masyado bang nilalahat ang pahayag.','Ibabahagi agad sa mga kaklase kahit hindi pa nasusuri.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,54,NULL,'Si Lito ay nagsasaliksik tungkol sa iba''t ibang uri ng pamilya para sa kanyang REPORT. Nakakita siya ng website na nagsasabing "ang NUCLEAR FAMILY lang ang tunay na pamilya. Paano dapat suriin ni Lito ang impormasyong ito sa kritikal na paraan?','Tatanggapin agad ang impormasyon dahil nakita niya ito sa INTERNET.','Iisipin na tama ito dahil nasa isang WEBSITE.','Susuriin kung mapagkakatiwalaan ang website, ang sumulat nito, at kung may ebidensya. Pag-iisipan din kung masyado bang nilalahat ang pahayag.','Ibabahagi agad sa mga kaklase kahit hindi pa nasusuri.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,55,NULL,'Si Maria ay nagsasaliksik para sa isang proyekto tungkol sa mga tungkulin ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya. Nakabasa siya ng artikulo ONLINE na nagsasabing "ang ina lang ang dapat maging tagapangalaga ng tahanan. Ano ang dapat niyang gawin upang suriin ito nang kritikal?','Tatanggapin ang impormasyon dahil galing ito sa INTERNET.','Iisipin na tama ito dahil nasa isang artikulo.','Susuriin kung mapagkakatiwalaan ang pinagmulan, ang sumulat, at kung may ebidensiya.','Ibabahagi agad sa mga kaklase kahit hindi ito nasuri.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,56,NULL,'Nabasa mo sa isang BLOG na ang tanging tungkulin ng ina ay alagaan ang mga anak, at ang ama naman ay magtrabaho para sa pamilya. Paano mo ito susuriin gamit ang kritikal na pag-iisip?','Tatanggapin agad ang pahayag dahil galing ito sa INTERNET.','Iisipin na tama ito dahil ito ay karaniwang paniniwala.','Susuriin kung mapagkakatiwalaan ang pinagmulan, kung may ebidensya, at kung isinasaalang-alang nito ang iba’t ibang uri ng pamilya at pagbabago sa tungkulin ng mga magulang.','Ibabahagi agad sa mga kaibigan kahit hindi pa nasusuri.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,57,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Carlo ay naniniwala na hindi kailangan pag-usapan ang seksuwalidad hangga’t hindi nagtatanong ang bata. Ano ang maaaring maging problema sa ganitong paniniwala?','Ang paghihintay sa tanong ng anak ay maaaring magresulta sa pagkuha ng impormasyon mula sa hindi maaasahang pinagkukunan.','Ang pag-uusap tungkol sa seksuwalidad ay dapat lamang mangyari sa pagitan ng magulang at anak.','Ang pag-uusap tungkol sa seksuwalidad ay dapat na palaging may gabay ng isang propesyonal.','Ang mga magulang ay hindi dapat makialam sa seksuwal na buhay ng kanilang mga anak.','A','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,58,NULL,'Natatalakay ang mga hamon na nararanasan ng kinabibilangang pamilya. Isang pamilya ang gumagamit ng isang FAMILY BUDGETING APP para subaybayan ang kanilang mga gastos. Kahit na mayroon silang budget, palagi pa rin silang kulang sa pera sa dulo ng buwan. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pagsusuri sa sitwasyon ng pamilya?','Hindi sapat ang kita ng pamilya para matugunan ang kanilang mga pangangailangan.','May mga hindi inaasahang gastos na hindi naisama sa kanilang BUDGET.','Hindi epektibo ang paggamit nila ng FAMILY BUDGETING APP.','Ang pamilya ay gumagastos ng higit sa kanilang kaya.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,59,NULL,'Isang barangay ang may programa sa pag-RECYCLE ng basura gamit ang mobile app. Pero kahit may ganitong app, marami pa rin sa mga residente ang hindi nakikilahok. Ano ang maaaring dahilan kung bakit hindi ito epektibo, batay sa kritikal na pagsusuri?','Hindi epektibo ang MOBILE APP.','Hindi alam ng mga tao kung bakit mahalaga ang pag-recycle.','Kulang ang tulong ng barangay sa programa.','Hindi akma ang programa sa pangangailangan at kakayahan ng mga residente.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,60,NULL,'Isang komunidad ang gumagamit ng ONLINE PLARFORM para maipreserba ang kanilang mga kwento at awitin. Pero napansin na mas interesado ang mga kabataan sa modernong libangan tulad ng SOCIAL MEDIA at VIDEO GAMES. Ano ang maaaring dahilan kung bakit hindi masyadong interesado ang kabataan sa tradisyunal na kultura, ayon sa kritikal na pagsusuri?','Hindi epektibo ang ONLINE PLARFORM.','Wala talagang interes ang mga kabataan sa kultura.','Kulang ang suporta ng komunidad sa kultura.','Hindi akma ang paraan ng pagpreserba sa interes at kakayahan ng mga kabataan.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,61,NULL,'Ang paaralan ni Ana ay may bagong programa sa pag-RECYCLE ng basura. May hiwalay na lalagyan para sa nabubulok, di-nabubulok, at maaaring i-COMPOST. Pero napansin ng mga guro na maraming estudyante ang hindi sumusunod sa tamang pagtatapon. Ano ang maaaring dahilan kung bakit hindi epektibo ang programa?','Hindi epektibo ang sistema ng SEGREGATION at pag-COMPOST.','Hindi alam ng mga estudyante ang tungkol sa programa.','Hindi sapat ang suporta ng mga guro sa programa.','Hindi tugma ang programa sa pangangailangan at kakayahan ng mga estudyante.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,62,NULL,'Isang barangay ang may programa para tumulong sa mga SENIOR CITIZENS gamit ang BUDDY SYSTEM sa pamamagitan ng mobile app. Pero kakaunti lang ang mga kabataang gustong sumali bilang "buddy. Ano ang maaaring dahilan ng problema, ayon sa kritikal na pagsusuri?','Hindi epektibo ang MOBILE APP.','Wala talagang interes ang kabataan sa pagtulong sa matatanda.','Kulang ang impormasyon tungkol sa programa.','Hindi akma ang disenyo ng programa sa pangangailangan at kakayahan ng kabataan at matatanda.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,63,NULL,'Isang komunidad ang gustong panatilihin ang kanilang tradisyunal na pagdiriwang. Gumagamit sila ng online platform para ibahagi ang impormasyon, pero kakaunti lang sa mga kabataan ang nakikilahok. Ano ang maaaring dahilan nito, batay sa kritikal na pagsusuri?','A. Hindi epektibo ang ONLINE PLARFORM.','Wala talagang interes ang kabataan sa tradisyunal na pagdiriwang.','Kulang ang impormasyon sa ONLINE PLARFORM.','Hindi akma ang paraan ng pagbabahagi sa interes at kakayahan ng kabataan.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,64,NULL,'Isang lungsod ang may bagong sistema ng pag-uulat ng krimen gamit ang MOBILE APP. May GPS TRACKING at puwedeng mag-upload ng larawan o VIDEO. Pero kakaunti lang ang mga gumagamit nito. Ano ang maaaring dahilan nito, ayon sa kritikal na pagsusuri?','Mahirap gamitin ang mobile app.','Hindi alam ng mga tao ang tungkol sa bagong sistema.','Wala silang tiwala na aaksyunan ng awtoridad ang mga ulat.','Hindi akma ang sistema sa pangangailangan at kakayahan ng mga tao, lalo na ng mga nasa laylayan ng lipunan.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,65,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay isang kapuluan sa Timog-Silangang Asya. Ano ang pinakamahalagang paraan para matukoy ang relatibong lokasyon ng Pilipinas?','Gamit ang mga COORDINATE ng LATITUDE at LONGTUDE.','Sa pagtukoy ng mga kalapit na bansa at anyong tubig.','Sa pag-aaral ng mga anyong lupa at anyong tubig sa loob ng Pilipinas.','Sa pagsusuri ng mga mapa at SATELLITE IMAGE ng Pilipinas.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,66,NULL,'Mayroong isang hindi pagkakaunawaan sa pagitan ng Pilipinas at ng isang karatig na bansa tungkol sa isang maliit na isla sa South China Sea. Parehong nag-aangkin ng soberanya sa isla. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang salik na dapat isaalang-alang sa pagresolba ng hindi pagkakaunawaang ito?','Ang laki at mga likas na yaman ng isla.','Ang HISTORICAL CLAIM ng bawat bansa sa isla, batay sa mga lumang mapa at dokumento.','Ang mga internasyonal na batas at kasunduan, tulad ng UNCLOS, na may kinalaman sa MARITIME BOUNDARIES at ang legal na proseso para sa pagresolba ng mga TERRITORIAL DISPUTES.','Ang opinyon ng mga mamamayan ng bawat bansa tungkol sa pag-aangkin sa isla.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,67,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay may malawak na Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ) ayon sa batas ng UNCLOS. Sa loob ng EEZ, may karapatan ang bansa sa mga likas na yaman tulad ng isda, langis, at gas. Ano ang pinakamalaking hamon sa pagpapanatili ng kontrol at pakinabang ng Pilipinas sa EEZ?','A. Pagbabago ng klima na nakaaapekto sa tubig at likas na yaman.','Ilegal na pangingisda at iba pang ilegal na gawain sa EEZ.','Alitan sa teritoryo lalo na sa South China Sea.','Kakulangan ng kagamitan at kakayahan para bantayan ang EEZ.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,68,NULL,'Ang Pilipinas ay binubuo ng iba''t ibang kultura, wika, at mga pangkat etniko. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang salik na nag-ambag sa pagbubuo ng isang pambansang identidad at pagkakaisa sa Pilipinas?','Ang pagkakaiba-iba ng mga kultura at wika sa iba''t ibang rehiyon ng Pilipinas.','Ang paglaban ng mga Pilipino laban sa mga dayuhang mananakop.','Ang pagtataguyod ng edukasyon at pagpapalaganap ng karunungan sa mga Pilipino.','Ang pag-unlad ng ekonomiya at ang pagtaas ng antas ng pamumuhay ng mga Pilipino.','B','',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,69,NULL,'Tuwing Biyernes ay may "Flag Ceremony" sa paaralan nina Liza. Sa tuwing inaawit ang "Lupang Hinirang" at itinataas ang watawat ng Pilipinas, nararamdaman niyang masaya at PROUD siya bilang isang Pilipino. Nais niyang mas maintindihan kung bakit mahalaga ang mga sagisag ng bansa sa buhay ng bawat mamamayan.Bakit mahalaga ang mga sagisag ng bansa tulad ng watawat, pambansang awit, at pambansang hayop sa pagbubuo ng isang malakas at nagkakaisang bansa?','Ipinapakita ng mga sagisag ang ating kultura at kasaysayan.','Nagbibigay ng inspirasyon ang mga sagisag upang magsikap ang bawat Pilipino.','Nagpapakita ang mga sagisag ng pagkakaisa at pagmamalaki bilang Pilipino.','Nagbibigay ang mga sagisag ng pamantayan ng ugali na dapat sundin ng lahat ng Pilipino.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,70,NULL,'May panukalang batas na gustong magpataw ng bagong buwis sa produktong petrolyo. Iba''t ibang sangay ng pamahalaan ang may tungkulin sa bawat hakbang. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang tamang pagkakatugma ng tungkulin ng bawat sangay ng pamahalaan? I. Paggawa ng panukalang batas II. Pagpapatibay ng panukalang batas III. Pagpapatupad ng batas IV. Pagsusuri kung naaayon sa Konstitusyon ang batas','I–Lehislatura, II–Ehekutibo, III–Hudikatura, IV–Lehislatura','I–Ehekutibo, II–Lehislatura, III–Ehekutibo, IV–Hudikatura','I–Lehislatura, II–Lehislatura, III–Ehekutibo, IV–Hudikatura','I–Ehekutibo, II–Hudikatura, III–Lehislatura, IV–Ehekutibo','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,71,NULL,'Naglunsad ang pamahalaan ng programa para sanayin ang mga komunidad na madalas tamaan ng bagyo. Tinuturuan sila kung paano maging handa bago, habang, at pagkatapos ng sakuna. Ano ang pinakamahalagang layunin ng programang ito?','Mabawasan ang bilang ng masasaktan sa panahon ng bagyo.','Mas mapabilis ang tulong sa mga biktima.','Maiwasan ang pagkasira ng mga ari-arian.','Mapalakas ang kakayahan ng komunidad na harapin at makabangon mula sa epekto ng bagyo.','D','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,72,NULL,'May inilunsad na proyekto ang pamahalaan kung saan magpapatayo sila ng mga bagong tulay at kalsada sa mga malalayong lugar. Kabilang dito ang mga komunidad na hirap marating dahil sa sirang daan o kakulangan sa imprastraktura. Ano ang pinakamahalagang layunin ng programang ito para matulungan ang mga taong naninirahan sa mga lugar na ito?','Makalikha ng trabaho para sa mga taong naninirahan sa mga rural na lugar.','Mapadali ang pagpunta ng mga tao sa paaralan, ospital, at iba pang serbisyo.','Makahatak ng mga negosyo upang mapaunlad ang kabuhayan ng mga tao sa lugar.','Maging mas kaakit-akit ang lugar sa mga turista upang makapagpasok ng kita.','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,73,NULL,'Si Mang Ronald, isang PROGRAMMER, ay nag-aalala sa kakulangan ng TRAMSPARENCY sa paggamit ng datos ng SMART CITY SYSTEMS at sa kakulangan ng mekanismo para maprotektahan ang privacy ng mga mamamayan. Siya ay nagplano na mag-organisa ng isang FORUM para talakayin ang mga isyung ito at maghanap ng solusyon. Ano ang pinakamahalagang hakbang na dapat gawin ni Mang Ronald upang matiyak na maprotektahan ang karapatan sa privacy ng mga mamamayan habang ginagamit ang SMART CITY SYSTEMS?','Mag-organisa ng isang protesta laban sa SMART CITY SYSTEMS.','Magsumite ng pormal na reklamo sa pamahalaan.','Magsagawa ng isang malawakang pag-aaral tungkol sa mga benepisyo at panganib ng Smart City System at ibahagi ang impormasyong ito sa publiko upang makapamili sila ng tama.','Hayaan na lamang ang pamahalaan na magdesisyon kung ano ang gagawin.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,74,NULL,'Si Aling Rosa ay isang inhinyero at kasapi ng ENVIRONMENTAL GROUP. Nag-aalala siya sa kakulangan ng pag-aaral at konsultasyon tungkol sa itatayong DAM sa kanilang lugar. Ano ang pinakamabisang paraan para maipahayag niya ang kanyang alalahanin at makaapekto sa desisyon ng pamahalaan?','Mag-RALLY o magprotesta laban sa proyekto.','Sumulat ng bukas na sulat sa pamahalaan.','Gumawa ng pag-aaral na may datos at ebidensya, at ipresenta ito sa mga opisyal at sa publiko.','Hayaan na lang ang pamahalaan ang magdesisyon.','C','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',2,3,75,NULL,'May inilunsad ang pamahalaan na programang "Balik Probinsya, Bagong Pag-asa." Layunin nitong tulungan ang mga tao na makabalik sa kanilang lalawigan at magkaroon ng pabahay, trabaho, at suporta sa edukasyon. Isa rin itong paraan para mabawasan ang siksikan sa Metro Manila. Ano ang pangunahing layunin ng programang ito?','Dumami ang tao sa mga lungsod sa probinsya','Mabigyan ng mas maayos na buhay ang mga tao sa kanilang lalawigan','Mabawasan ang gastos ng gobyerno sa Metro Manila','Pilitin ang mga tao na lumipat ng tirahan kahit ayaw nila','B','',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,1,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Ana ay laging nagsisimba nang sama-sama tuwing Linggo. Pagkatapos ng misa, dumidiretso sila sa bahay ng kanilang lola para kumain ng pananghalian kasama ang iba pang mga kamag-anak. Kung hindi sila magsisimba, hindi rin sila pupunta sa bahay ng lola. Alin ang dalawang kaugalian o tradisyon na magkakaugnay sa pamilya ni Ana?','Pagsisimba at pagkain sa bahay ng lola','Panonood ng TV at paglalaro','Pag-aaral at pagtulog nang maaga','Paglilinis ng bahay at pamimili','A','Magkaugnay ang dalawang ito dahil kapag hindi sila nagsisimba, hindi rin sila pumupunta sa bahay ng lola.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,2,NULL,'Kung gusto mong malaman ang dalawang pinakakaraniwang ginagawa ng inyong pamilya tuwing Pasko saan ka makakukuha ng impormasyon na nagpapakita ng kaugnayan ng mga ito sa isa''t isa?','Sa listahan ng mga paboritong pagkain ng bawat miyembro ng pamilya.','Sa mga lumang litrato ng Pasko na nagpapakita ng pagsisimba ninyo at pagkatapos ay sama-samang nagbubukas ng regalo.','Sa talaan ng mga bisita ninyo tuwing Pasko sa nakaraang limang taon.','Sa listahan ng mga bagong laruan na natanggap mo noong nakaraang Pasko.','B','Makikita sa mga litrato ang aktwal na ginagawa ng pamilya tuwing Pasko, tulad ng pagsisimba at pagbubukas ng regalo, kaya malinaw ang kaugnayan ng mga ito sa isa’t isa bilang tradisyon o kaugalian.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,3,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Ben ay laging naghahanda ng espesyal na pansit tuwing kaarawan ng bawat miyembro. Sinasabi ng kanyang nanay na ito ay para humaba ang buhay ng nagdiriwang. Kung iisipin mong mabuti, ano ang koneksyon sa pagitan ng mahabang pansit at ng hiling para sa mahabang buhay?','Dahil masarap ang pansit kaya ito gustong kainin ng lahat sa kaarawan.','Dahil ang mahabang noodles ng pansit ay sumisimbolo o kumakatawan sa mahabang buhay.','Dahil maraming sangkap ang pansit kaya ito nakapagpapalusog.','Dahil ang pagluluto ng pansit ay isang mahirap na gawain kaya ito espesyal.','B','Ayon sa tradisyon, ang haba ng pansit ay sumisimbolo sa mahabang buhay, kaya ito inihahanda tuwing kaarawan bilang panalangin o hiling para sa mahabang buhay ng may kaarawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,4,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Leo ay nagtitinda ng mga bulaklak sa simbahan tuwing Linggo. Ang pamilya ni Maya naman ay nagluluto at nagbibigay ng pagkain sa mga taong nangangailangan tuwing Linggo din. Sila ay gustong magtulungan, ano ang pinakamainam na gagawin nila?','Sabay silang magsimba sa Linggo.','Magtulungan silang maglinis ng kanilang mga bahay sa Linggo.','Magtulungan silang mamigay ng bulaklak na may kasamang kaunting pagkain sa mga tao pagkatapos ng misa sa Linggo.','Magtulungan silang magbenta ng bulaklak at ang kita ay ibili ng pagkain na ibabahagi sa ibang araw.','C','Ito ang pinakamainam dahil pinagsasama nito ang gawain ng parehong pamilya — ang pagbebenta ng bulaklak at pamimigay ng pagkain. Sa ganitong paraan, natutulungan nila ang mas maraming tao habang pinapalakas ang kanilang pagtutulungan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,5,NULL,'Kung gusto mong paghambingin ang dalawang paraan ng pagdiriwang ng Pasko ng iyong pamilya noong nakaraang taon at ngayong taon. Ano ang dalawang uri ng impormasyon ang iyong gagamitin para makita ang pagkakatulad at pagkakaiba ng mga ito?','Ang listahan ng mga natanggap mong regalo noong nakaraang taon at ang listahan ng mga gusto mong matanggap ngayong taon.','Ang mga litrato at video ng pagdiriwang ninyo noong nakaraang taon at ang mga litrato at video ng pagdiriwang ninyo ngayong taon.','Ang bilang ng mga bisita ninyo noong nakaraang taon at ang bilang ng mga bisita ninyo ngayong taon.','Ang mga menu ng pagkain ninyo noong nakaraang taon at ang mga plano niyong kainin ngayong taon.','B','Sa pamamagitan ng mga litrato at video, makikita at maihahambing mo nang malinaw ang pagkakatulad at pagkakaiba ng pagdiriwang ng Pasko sa dalawang taon.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,6,NULL,'Ang pamilya ni Lito ay laging nagkakantahan pagkatapos ng kanilang hapunan tuwing Sabado. Ang pamilya naman ni Sarah ay laging nagkukuwentuhan at nagbabahaginan ng mga nangyari sa kanilang linggo pagkatapos din ng hapunan tuwing Sabado. Kung iisipin mong mabuti, ano ang pangunahing pagkakatulad ng kanilang mga kaugalian sa Sabado ng gabi?','Pareho silang kumakain ng hapunan tuwing Sabado.','Pareho silang may ginagamit na musika sa kanilang gawain.','Pareho silang gumagawa ng isang espesyal na aktibidad pagkatapos ng hapunan para magsama-sama ang pamilya.','Pareho silang nagkukuwentuhan tungkol sa kanilang mga naging araw.','C','Bagamat magkaiba ang kanilang ginagawa (pagkakantahan at pagkukuwentuhan), pareho silang may layunin na mag-bonding at magkasama-sama bilang pamilya tuwing Sabado ng gabi.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,7,NULL,'Si Marco ay nakararamdam ng pangangati sa kanyang pribadong bahagi. Alam niyang mahalagang maging malinis para sa kanyang kalusugan. Alin sa sumusunod na dalawang gawain ang pinakamahusay niyang pagsamahin para malutas ang kanyang problema at mapangalagaan ang kanyang reproduktibong kalusugan?','Ang pag-inom ng maraming tubig at ang paglalaro sa labas.','Ang paghuhugas ng kamay bago kumain at ang pagtulog nang maaga.','Ang paghuhugas ng kanyang pribadong bahagi gamit ang malinis na tubig at sabon, at ang pagsusuot ng malinis at tuyong damit panloob.','Ang pagkain ng prutas at gulay at ang pag-eehersisyo araw-araw.','C','Ang tamang paglilinis ng katawan at pagsusuot ng malinis na damit panloob ay direktang makatutulong sa pagpapanatili ng kalinisan at kalusugan ng reproduktibong bahagi, at makatutulong para mawala ang pangangati.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,8,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang mga pangunahing dahilan kung bakit mahalagang maghugas ng kamay pagkatapos gumamit ng banyo. Saan mo ito maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong sapatos.','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong guro o magulang at sa isang simpleng aklat tungkol sa kalusugan.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','C','Ang guro, magulang, at aklat tungkol sa kalusugan ay mapagkakatiwalaang pinagkukunan ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa wastong kalinisan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,9,NULL,'Sa aralin ninyo tungkol sa kalinisan ng katawan, tinalakay ng guro ang kahalagahan ng pagiging malinis, lalo na sa mga pribadong bahagi ng katawan. Sinabi niyang mahalaga ito para mapanatili ang kalusugan at makaiwas sa sakit. Bakit mahalaga ang pagiging malinis sa ating pribadong bahagi ng katawan at ang pag-iwas sa sakit?','Maging malinis para hindi tayo pagalitan.','Maging malinis para makaiwas sa anumang uri ng sakit.','Maging malinis para magmukha tayong mabango.','Maging malinis para maraming hahanga sa atin.','B','Ang tamang kalinisan sa pribadong bahagi ng katawan ay nakatutulong para maiwasan ang impeksyon at mapanatili ang kalusugan ng buong katawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,10,NULL,'Si Ana ay naguguluhan tungkol sa mga pagbabago sa kanyang katawan. Sino ang makatutulong sa kanya upang maunawaan ang mga ito at bakit?','Ang kanyang mga kaibigan, dahil pareho silang nagdadalaga.','Ang kanyang guro, dahil sila ay eksperto sa mga aralin sa paaralan.','Ang kanyang mga magulang o nakatatandang kapatid, dahil sila ay may personal na karanasan at pagmamahal.','Ang kanyang kapitbahay, dahil sila ay matanda na at maraming alam.','C','Ang mga magulang at kapatid ay mapagkakatiwalaan, may karanasan, at tunay na nagmamalasakit, kaya makatutulong sila kay Ana na maunawaan ang mga pagbabago sa kanyang katawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,11,NULL,'Si Ben ay naghahanap ng impormasyon tungkol sa mga pagbabago sa katawan ng mga lalaki sa panahon ng puberty. Saan niya mahahanap ang pinaka- mapagkatitiwalaan at angkop na impormasyon?','Sa mga usapan ng kanyang mga kaklase sa likod ng paaralan.','Sa mga social media posts ng mga hindi kilalang tao.','Sa isang website na nagbebenta ng mga gamot na pampalaki ng katawan.','Sa isang libro tungkol sa kalusugan ng mga kabataan na may rekomendasyon mula sa kanyang mga magulang o guro.','D','Ang aklat na inirekomenda ng magulang o guro ay mapagkakatiwalaan at may tamang impormasyon na angkop sa edad ni Ben.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,12,NULL,'Si Marco ay nakarinig ng mga kuwento mula sa kanyang mga kaklase tungkol sa mga "sikreto" ng pagdadalaga at pagbibinata. Alin sa mga sumusunod ang pinakamahalagang tanong na dapat niyang itanong upang malaman ang katotohanan?','Ano ang pinakamasayang kuwento na narinig ninyo?','Sino ang nagkuwento sa inyo ng mga bagay na ito?','Paano ninyo nasisiguro na tama ang mga impormasyong ito?','Ano ang pinakamagandang sikreto na maaari kong malaman?','C','Mahalagang alamin kung tama at totoo ang impormasyon, lalo na tungkol sa pagdadalaga at pagbibinata, upang hindi malito o malinlang.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,13,'pagkatapos. Si Sofia, isang 15 taong gulang, ay maraming tanong tungkol sa seksuwalidad at reproduktibong kalusugan ngunit nahihiyang magtanong sa iba. Alam niyang mahalagang magkaroon ng tamang impormasyon para sa kanyang kalusugan at pagdedesisyon.','Paano malalaman ni Sofia ang tamang impormasyon tungkol sa kanyang katawan?','Magtanong sa guro at health worker','Manood ng TV lang','Magtanong sa kaibigan na hindi sigurado','Maglaro ng computer games','A','Ang guro at health worker ay may tamang kaalaman at makatutulong kay Sofia na maintindihan ang mga pagbabago sa kanyang katawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,14,'pagkatapos. Si Sofia, isang 15 taong gulang, ay maraming tanong tungkol sa seksuwalidad at reproduktibong kalusugan ngunit nahihiyang magtanong sa iba. Alam niyang mahalagang magkaroon ng tamang impormasyon para sa kanyang kalusugan at pagdedesisyon.','Kung nais ni Sofia na humanap ng dalawang mapagkakatiwalaang mapagkukunan ng impormasyon tungkol sa seksuwalidad at reproduktibong kalusugan na inirerekomenda ng kanyang mga magulang, alin ang pinakamalamang na kanilang ituturo sa kanya?','Ang mga usapan sa social media at mga blog ng mga indibidwal na may iba''t ibang opinyon.','Ang mga libro, website ng mga respetadong organisasyong pangkalusugan, o mga propesyonal na direktang inirekomenda ng kanyang mga magulang.','Ang mga patalastas ng iba''t ibang produkto pangkalusugan na nakikita sa telebisyon o online.','Ang mga kuwento at karanasan ng kanyang mga kaklase o kapitbahay.','B','Ang mga ito ay mapagkakatiwalaan, may tamang impormasyon, at siguradong aprubado ng kanyang mga magulang para sa kaligtasan at tamang pag- unawa ni Sofia.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,15,'pagkatapos. Si Sofia, isang 15 taong gulang, ay maraming tanong tungkol sa seksuwalidad at reproduktibong kalusugan ngunit nahihiyang magtanong sa iba. Alam niyang mahalagang magkaroon ng tamang impormasyon para sa kanyang kalusugan at pagdedesisyon.','Bakit mahalagang tulungan pa rin ni Mama at Papa si Sofia tungkol sa kanyang katawan kahit maraming impormasyon sa internet?','Kasi mas alam nila ang mga computer at mas matagal mag-research.','Kasi maraming kaibigan ang Mama at Papa.','Kasi mahal nila si Sofia at gusto siyang tulungan nang tama.','Kasi mahigpit sila kaya susundin ni Sofia ang sabi nila.','C','Ang mga magulang ay nagmamalasakit at nais ang pinakamabuti para kay Sofia, kaya mahalagang sila ang tumulong sa pagbibigay ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa kanyang katawan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,16,'Minsan, may mga hindi magandang bagay tayong nararanasan. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano ito nakaaapekto sa atin at kung ano ang maaari nating gawin.','Kung lagi kang inaasar ng iyong kalaro, ano ang dalawang pinakamahusay mong gawin para malutas ang problemang ito?','Umiyak lang at umiwas.','Sabihin sa kalaro na hindi mo gusto iyon at sabihin sa iyong guro o magulang.','Gumanti ka rin ng pang-aasar at magsumbong.','Magtago ka na lang palagi.','B','Mahalagang magsabi ng totoo at humingi ng tulong sa nakatatanda para maayos ang problema sa mabuting paraan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,17,'Minsan, may mga hindi magandang bagay tayong nararanasan. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano ito nakaaapekto sa atin at kung ano ang maaari nating gawin.','Kung nalulungkot ka dahil wala kang kalaro, saan mo sabay hahanapin ang dalawang paraan para magkaroon ng bagong kaibigan?','Sa iyong unan at sa iyong sapatos.','Sa iyong magulang o guro at sa iyong mga kapitbahay','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong laruan.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Sila ay makatutulong sa iyo at maaaring magpakilala sa iyo ng bagong mga kaibigan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,18,'Minsan, may mga hindi magandang bagay tayong nararanasan. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano ito nakaaapekto sa atin at kung ano ang maaari nating gawin.','Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang iyong nararamdaman kapag may hamon at ang paghingi ng tulong sa nakatatanda?','Para hindi ka mapagalitan.','Para maunawaan mo ang iyong nararamdaman at makakuha ka ng tamang gabay.','Para hindi ka magmukhang mahina.','Para may ibang mag-ayos ng problema mo.','B','Kapag alam mo ang nararamdaman mo at humingi ka ng tulong, mas madali mong malalagpasan ang hamon sa tamang paraan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,19,'Ang pamilya ay sama-samang humaharap sa mga problema. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano tumutulong ang pamilya sa isa''t isa kapag may hamon.','Kung nawalan ng trabaho ang iyong Tatay, ano ang pinakamahusay na maaaring gawin ng iyong pamilya para malutas ito?','Magalit at magsisihan.','Magtulungan sa pagtitipid at maghanap ng bagong trabaho.','Maghintay na lang ng tulong mula sa iba.','Magwaldas pa rin ng pera.','B','Ang pagtutulungan ng pamilya ay mahalaga para makabangon at makahanap ng solusyon sa problema.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,20,'Ang pamilya ay sama-samang humaharap sa mga problema. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano tumutulong ang pamilya sa isa''t isa kapag may hamon.','Gusto mong malaman ang dalawang karaniwang paraan kung paano nagtutulungan ang mga pamilya kapag may sakit ang isang miyembro. Saan mo ito sabay maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong telebisyon.','Sa iyong Nanay o Tatay at sa mga kuwento ng ibang pamilya.','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Sila ay may karanasan at makapagbabahagi ng tunay na paraan ng pagtutulungan kapag may sakit.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,21,'Ang pamilya ay sama-samang humaharap sa mga problema. Mahalagang malaman natin kung paano tumutulong ang pamilya sa isa''t isa kapag may hamon.','Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang pagmamahalan ng pamilya at ang pagtulong sa isa''t isa kapag may problema?','Para mas madaling matapos ang problema.','Dahil ang pagmamahalan ang nagtutulak sa pamilya na magtulungan at magdamayan.','Para hindi mag-away ang mga miyembro ng pamilya.','Para mas mabilis na bumalik sa normal ang lahat.','B','Kapag may pagmamahalan, mas madali at bukal sa loob ang pagtutulungan sa panahon ng problema.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,22,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang pangunahing paraan para magkaroon ng maraming kaibigan sa komunidad. Saan mo ito maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong telebisyon.','Sa iyong magulang o guro at sa pakikipaglaro sa ibang bata','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Ang mga magulang at guro ay makatutulong, at ang pakikipaglaro ay isang paraan para makilala at magkaroon ng kaibigan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,23,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang pagiging magalang sa iba at ang pagkakaroon ng maraming kaibigan sa komunidad?','Para maraming magbigay sa iyo ng regalo.','Dahil ang pagiging magalang ay nagpapakita ng respeto sa iba, kaya mas gusto nilang makipagkaibigan sa iyo.','Para hindi ka mapagalitan ng nakatatanda.','Para ikaw ang laging masunod.','B','Ang pagiging magalang ay nagpapalapit ng loob ng iba, kaya mas madali kang magkaroon ng kaibigan. Sa ating komunidad, may mga patakaran o regulasyon na dapat sundin. Mahalagang malaman natin kung ano ang maaaring mangyari kapag sinusunod natin ang mga ito.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,24,NULL,'Kung ang regulasyon sa inyong komunidad ay "Bawal magtapon ng basura kahit saan," ano ang dalawang magandang resulta kung lahat ay susunod dito?','Magkakaroon ng maraming basura at masisira ang kapaligiran.','Magiging malinis ang kapaligiran at maiiwasan ang sakit.','Magagalit ang mga nanghuhuli at magmumulta','Magiging abala ang mga tao sa pagtatapon ng basura.','B','Ang pagsunod sa tamang pagtatapon ng basura ay nakatutulong upang mapanatiling malinis at ligtas ang kapaligiran.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,1,25,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang pangunahing dahilan kung bakit may regulasyon na "Bawal magpatakbo ng sasakyan nang mabilis sa kalsada." Saan mo ito maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong magulang o pulis at sa isang simpleng babasahin tungkol sa trapiko.','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Sila ay may kaalaman tungkol sa batas-trapiko at makapagbibigay ng tamang impormasyon.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,26,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang pagsunod sa regulasyon na "Bawal ang maingay na musika pag gabi" at ang pagkakaroon ng payapang pagtulog ng mga tao sa komunidad?','Para hindi tayo pagalitan ng ating mga kapitbahay.','Dahil ang pagsunod sa regulasyon ay tumutulong para makapagpahinga nang maayos ang lahat at maging mas maganda ang kanilang pakiramdam.','Para hindi masira ang ating mga speaker.','Para mas maraming magustuhan ang ating musika sa araw.','B','Ang katahimikan sa gabi ay mahalaga para sa maayos na tulog at kalusugan ng lahat sa komunidad.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,27,NULL,'May patakaran sa parke na bawal pumitas ng mga bulaklak. Kung dalawang bata ang pumitas ng maraming bulaklak, ano ang dalawang maaaring mawala sa parke?','Ganda ng tanawin at masayang pakiramdam ng mga bisita','Mga bangko at puno','Mga laruan ng mga bata','Mga pagkain at inumin','A','Kapag pinitas ang bulaklak, nababawasan ang ganda ng parke at kasiyahan ng mga bumibisita.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,28,NULL,'May dalawang kuwento. Una, lahat ay nagtapon ng basura sa tamang basurahan. Ikalawa, nagtapon sila kahit saan. Ano ang dalawang malamang na pagkakaiba sa kapaligiran sa dalawang kuwento?','Mas maraming bulaklak at mas maraming puno.','Mas malinis at mas marumi.','Mas maraming tao at mas kaunting tao','Mas maliwanag at mas madilim.','B','Ang tamang pagtatapon ng basura ay nagdudulot ng kalinisan, habang ang maling pagtatapon ay nagdudulot ng karumihan. Sa ating komunidad, may mga patakaran o regulasyon na dapat sundin. Mahalagang malaman natin kung ano ang maaaring mangyari kapag sinusunod natin ang mga ito.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,29,NULL,'Kung ang regulasyon sa inyong komunidad ay "Bawal magtapon ng basura kahit saan," ano ang dalawang magandang resulta kung lahat ay susunod dito?','Magkakaroon ng maraming basura at masisira ang kapaligiran.','Magiging malinis ang kapaligiran at maiiwasan ang sakit.','Magagalit ang mga nanghuhuli at magmumulta.','Magiging abala ang mga tao sa pagtatapon ng basura.','B','Kapag lahat ay sumunod sa tamang pagtatapon ng basura, mapapanatiling malinis at ligtas sa sakit ang komunidad.',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,30,NULL,'Gusto mong ang malaman pangunahing dahilan kung bakit may regulasyon na "Bawal magpatakbo ng sasakyan nang mabilis sa kalsada." Saan mo ito sabay maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong magulang o pulis at sa isang simpleng babasahin tungkol sa trapiko.','Sa iyong pagkain at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Ang magulang, pulis, at mga babasahin tungkol sa trapiko ay nagbibigay ng tamang paliwanag kung bakit mahalaga ang batas sa kalsada.',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,31,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang pagsunod sa regulasyon na "Bawal ang maingay na musika pag gabi" at ang pagkakaroon ng payapang pagtulog ng mga tao sa komunidad?','Para hindi tayo pagalitan ng ating mga kapitbahay.','Para hindi masira ang ating mga speaker.','Dahil ang pagsunod sa regulasyon ay tumutulong para makapagpahinga nang maayos ang lahat at maging mas maganda ang kanilang pakiramdam.','Para mas maraming magustuhan ang ating musika sa araw.','C','Ang katahimikan sa gabi ay mahalaga upang ang lahat ay makatulog nang mahimbing at maging masigla sa araw. Gustong tumulong ni Lea sa pagpapaganda ng kanilang komunidad. Pero may mga maaaring maging problema at may mga paraan din para masolusyunan ito.',NULL,0,0),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,32,NULL,'Kung gustong magtanim ni Lea ng mga bulaklak sa parke pero walang siyang pera at walang tumutulong sa kanya, ano ang dalawang pinakamahusay niyang gawin para malutas ito?','Umiyak na lang at huwag nang tumulong.','Magnakaw na lang ng bulaklak sa ibang lugar.','Magalit sa gobyerno dahil walang tumutulong.','Humingi ng tulong sa kanyang pamilya o kapitbahay at maghanap ng mga libreng binhi o donasyon.','D','Ang pagtutulungan at pagiging madiskarte ay makatutulong kay Lea na makapagtanim kahit wala siyang pera.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,33,NULL,'Gusto ni Lea na malaman ang dalawang karaniwang problema kapag maraming tao ang nagtutulong sa paglilinis ng komunidad at ang dalawang paraan para maiwasan ang mga ito. Saan niya ito sabay maaaring malaman?','Sa kanyang laruan at sa kanyang alagang hayop.','Sa kanyang panaginip at sa kanyang paboritong pagkain.','Sa pakikinig sa sinasabi ng mga nakatatanda sa komunidad at sa pagbabasa ng mga simpleng patnubay sa pagtutulungan.','Sa kanyang damit at sa kanyang sapatos.','C','Ang mga nakatatanda at babasahing patnubay ay may tamang impormasyon at karanasan sa pagtutulungan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,34,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang pagtulong sa komunidad at ang pagiging handa sa mga posibleng problema?','Para hindi tayo mainip.','Dahil kung alam natin ang mga maaaring maging problema, mas makapag-iisip tayo ng paraan para malutas ito at mas magiging matagumpay ang ating pagtulong.','Para mas maraming humanga sa atin.','Para mas mabilis tayong matapos sa ating gawain.','B','Ang pagiging handa ay mahalaga upang ang pagtulong sa komunidad ay maging maayos at epektibo. Gustong tumulong ang klase ninyo sa pagpapaganda ng inyong paaralan. Nag-iisip kayo ng simpleng plano kung paano kayo makikisali.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,35,NULL,'Gusto ninyong magtanim ng mga halaman sa bakanteng lupa sa paaralan. Alin sa sumusunod ang dalawang unang hakbang na magkaugnay sa inyong plano?','Magdilig ng halaman araw-araw at maghintay na lumaki ito.','Mag-usap-usap kung anong halaman ang itatanim at humingi ng pahintulot sa punong-guro.','Bumili agad ng maraming halaman at itanim ito kahit saan.','Magdrowing ng magagandang bulaklak at idikit sa pader.','B','Mahalagang pagplanuhan muna ang proyekto at kumuha ng pahintulot para maging maayos at legal ang gagawin.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,36,NULL,'Bakit kailangang isama sa plano ang mga gamit tulad ng lupa, binhi, at tubig?','Para may maisulat lang sa papel','Para mas madali at maayos ang gagawing pagtatanim','Para hindi gamitin ang mga ito','Para hindi mahuli sa laro','B','Ang tamang paghahanda ng mga gamit ay nakatutulong upang maging matagumpay at maayos ang pagtatanim.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,37,'Sa ating mga pagdiriwang at seremonya, may mga espesyal na bagay tayong ginagamit na may kahulugan.','Kung sa isang pista ay may parada at maraming watawat ang iwinawagayway, ano ang dalawang pangunahing dahilan kung bakit ito ginagawa?','Para maging maganda ang parada at maraming kulay.','Para ipakita ang pagmamahal sa bayan at pagkakaisa.','Para magkaroon ng maraming souvenir at ibenta ito.','Para maging abala ang mga tao at hindi mainip.','B','Ang watawat ay ginagamit sa parada upang ipakita ang respeto, pagmamahal sa bayan, at pagkakaisa ng mga mamamayan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,38,'Sa ating mga pagdiriwang at seremonya, may mga espesyal na bagay tayong ginagamit na may kahulugan.','Gusto mong malaman ang pangunahing kahulugan ng pagkakaroon ng kandila sa isang seremonya ng binyag. Kanino mo ito maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong panaginip.','Sa iyong magulang o sa pari/pastor at sa isang simpleng aklat tungkol sa binyag.','Sa iyong alagang hayop at sa iyong paboritong pagkain.','C','Sila ay may tamang kaalaman tungkol sa kahulugan ng kandila sa binyag bilang simbolo ng liwanag at bagong buhay.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,39,'Sa ating mga pagdiriwang at seremonya, may mga espesyal na bagay tayong ginagamit na may kahulugan.','Bakit mahalaga ang singsing sa kasal?','Dahil ito ay maganda at mamahalin','Dahil ito ay simbolo ng pangako ng pagmamahalan at pagtitiwala','Dahil ito ay parte ng handaan','Dahil gusto lang ito ng mag-asawa','B','Ang singsing sa kasal ay tanda ng walang hanggang pagmamahalan at pagtitiwala ng mag-asawa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,40,'• Sagot: B • Paliwanag: Ang singsing sa kasal ay tanda ng walang hanggang pagmamahalan at pagtitiwala ng mag-asawa.','Kung nakakita ka ng watawat ng Pilipinas na may kulay pula sa itaas, ano ang dalawang posibleng kahulugan nito?','Masaya ang bansa at maraming pista.','Maganda ang panahon at maraming bulaklak.','May bagong presidente at maraming proyekto.','May digmaan o kaguluhan at matapang ang mga Pilipino.','D','Kapag ang pulang bahagi ng watawat ay nasa itaas, ibig sabihin nito ay may digmaan sa bansa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,41,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang pangunahing kahulugan ng tatlong bituin sa watawat ng Pilipinas. Saan mo ito sabay hahanapin?','Sa iyong aklat sa Sibika at Kultura at sa iyong guro.','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong panaginip.','Sa iyong alagang hayop at sa iyong paboritong pagkain.','A','Ang aklat at guro ay may tamang impormasyon tungkol sa simbolismo ng tatlong bituin sa watawat ng Pilipinas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,42,NULL,'Bakit mahalaga ang watawat sa pagdiriwang ng Araw ng Kalayaan?','Dahil maganda ang kulay nito','Dahil ginagamit ito sa palamuti lang','Dahil ito ang simbolo ng ating kalayaan','Dahil may bituin at araw ito','C','Ang watawat ay mahalaga sa Araw ng Kalayaan dahil ito ay sumasagisag sa ating kasarinlan at pagkakaisa bilang isang bansa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,43,'Sa inyong klase sa Araling Panlipunan, tinalakay ang iba’t ibang sagisag ng Pilipinas tulad ng watawat, agila, sampaguita, at ang pambansang awit. Napag-usapan kung ano ang kahulugan ng mga ito at kung bakit mahalagang kilalanin at igalang ang mga sagisag ng bansa.','Isang araw, nakita mo ang kaklase mong nilalaro at nilulukot ang maliit na watawat ng Pilipinas. Ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Tawanan siya at sabihing wala lang iyon','Hayaan na lang dahil hindi naman totoo ang watawat','Sabihan siya nang maayos na hindi dapat nilalaro ang watawat dahil isa ito sa sagisag ng bansa','Kopyahin ang ginagawa niya at sumali sa laro','C','Mahalaga ang paggalang sa watawat dahil ito ay simbolo ng ating bayan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,44,'Sa inyong klase sa Araling Panlipunan, tinalakay ang iba’t ibang sagisag ng Pilipinas tulad ng watawat, agila, sampaguita, at ang pambansang awit. Napag-usapan kung ano ang kahulugan ng mga ito at kung bakit mahalagang kilalanin at igalang ang mga sagisag ng bansa.','Alin sa mga sumusunod ang hindi pambansang sagisag ng Pilipinas?','Sampaguita','Philippine Eagle','Jeepney','Lupang Hinirang','C','Ang jeepney ay kilalang sasakyan sa Pilipinas pero hindi ito opisyal na pambansang sagisag.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,45,'Sa inyong klase sa Araling Panlipunan, tinalakay ang iba’t ibang sagisag ng Pilipinas tulad ng watawat, agila, sampaguita, at ang pambansang awit. Napag-usapan kung ano ang kahulugan ng mga ito at kung bakit mahalagang kilalanin at igalang ang mga sagisag ng bansa.','Bakit mahalagang kilalanin at igalang ang mga pambansang sagisag ng Pilipinas?','Dahil uso ito sa paaralan','Para magka-premyo kapag nasagot sa quiz','Para ipakita ang pagmamahal at respeto sa bansa','Para matandaan ang mga kulay ng watawat','C','Ang paggalang sa pambansang sagisag ay pagpapakita ng pagmamalasakit sa ating bansa.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,46,NULL,'Kung maraming basura sa inyong parke, ano ang magandang resulta kung kayo ay magtutulungan sa paglilinis nito?','Magkakaroon ng maraming sakit at aalis ang mga ibon.','Magiging mas madumi ang parke at walang gustong pumunta.','Magiging malinis at magandang tingnan ang parke','Magagalit ang mga tao dahil kayo ang naglinis.','C','Ang pagtutulungan sa paglilinis ay nakatutulong upang mapanatiling maayos ang kapaligiran.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,47,NULL,'Ano ang pangunahing dahilan kung bakit mahalagang sumali sa "Brigada Eskwela" sa inyong paaralan. Saan mo ito maaaring malaman?','Sa iyong guro at sa mga patalastas sa paaralan.','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong panaginip.','Sa iyong alagang hayop at sa iyong paboritong pagkain.','A','Sila ay nagbibigay ng impormasyon kung bakit mahalaga ang pagsali sa Brigada Eskwela.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,48,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang ang pagtulong sa komunidad at ang pagkakaroon ng masayang samahan ng mga tao?','Para mas maraming premyo ang ibigay sa inyo.','Para mas mabilis matapos ang mga gawain.','Dahil ang pagtutulungan ay nagpapatibay ng samahan at nagdudulot ng kasiyahan.','Para mas maraming magawa ang mga lider ng komunidad.','C','Mas masaya at mas magaan ang gawain kapag nagtutulungan ang mga tao sa komunidad.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,49,NULL,'Kung may problema sa inyong barangay na kailangang ayusin ng mabilis, aling sangay ng pamahalaan ang pinakamadaling lapitan para humingi ng tulong?','Korte Suprema at Senado','Barangay at Munisipyo/Lungsod','Kongreso at Pangulo','Sandatahang Lakas at Pulisya','B','Sila ang pinakamalapit at madaling lapitan sa agarang problema sa lugar.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,2,50,NULL,'Kung nais mong malaman ang pangunahing tungkulin ng Pangulo ng Pilipinas, saan mo ito makikita?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong panaginip.','Sa iyong aklat sa Araling Panlipunan at sa balita.','Sa iyong alagang hayop at sa iyong paboritong pagkain.','C','Ang aklat at balita ay nagbibigay ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa tungkulin ng Pangulo.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,51,NULL,'Bakit mahalaga ang paggawa ng batas ng Kongreso at ang pagpapatupad nito ng Pangulo?','Para magkaroon ng maayos na pamamahala at masunod','Para mas mabilis na makauwi ang mga politiko.','Para mas maraming trabaho ang mga tao sa gobyerno.','Para mas maraming proyekto ang maipatayo agad.','A','Ang batas ay gabay sa kaayusan, at ang pagpapatupad nito ay tungkulin ng Pangulo.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,52,NULL,'Kung maraming bata sa inyong lugar ang hindi nakapag-aaral, aling dalawang programa ng gobyerno ang pinakamahusay na magkaugnay para matulungan sila?','Programang pangkalusugan at programang pangkapayapaan.','Programang pang-edukasyon at programang pangkabuhayan (para sa pamilya)','Programang pang-imprastraktura at programang pangkalusugan.','Programang pangkapayapaan at programang pang-imprastraktura.','B','Ang edukasyon ay para sa mga bata at ang kabuhayan ay tumutulong sa magulang para masuportahan ang pag-aaral.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,53,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang dalawang pangunahing layunin ng programang "Libreng Bakuna" ng gobyerno. Saan mo ito sabay hahanapin?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong kapitbahay.','Sa health center at sa website ng Kagawaran ng Kalusugan.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong paboritong pagkain.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alagang hayop.','B','Ito ang mapagkakatiwalaang pinanggagalingan ng impormasyon tungkol sa libreng bakuna.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,54,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang pag-ugnayin ang programang "Ayuda sa Pamilya" (pang-ekonomiyA. at ang programang "Feeding Program sa Paaralan" (pangkalusugan) para sa mga mahihirap na pamilya?','Para mas maraming pagkain ang makain ng mga bata sa paaralan.','Para matulungan ang mga pamilya na may sapat na makain sa bahay at maging malusog ang mga bata sa pag-aaral.','Para mas maraming pera ang matanggap ng mga pamilya mula sa gobyerno.','Para mas maraming trabaho ang malikha sa mga paaralan.','B','Pinagsasama ang kalusugan at kabuhayan upang matulungan ang buong pamilya.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,55,NULL,'Ang gobyerno ay may programang "Linis Bayan," ano ang dalawang simpleng paraan para ipakita ang suporta mo dito?','Magtago ng basura at magreklamo.','Maglinis sa paligid at hikayatin ang iba.','Manood lang at maghintay ng gagawa.','Magkalat pa at sisihin ang iba.','B','Simpleng gawaing tulad ng paglilinis at panghihikayat ay suporta na sa programang "Linis Bayan."',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,56,NULL,'Gusto mong malaman ang dalawang pangunahing dahilan kung bakit mahalaga ang programang "Plant for the Future" ng gobyerno. Saan mo ito sabay hahanapin?','Sa iyong laruan at sa iyong pagkain.','Sa poster ng programa at sa iyong guro.','Sa iyong kuwaderno at sa iyong damit.','Sa iyong panaginip at sa iyong alaga.','B','Ang mga poster at guro ay nagbibigay ng malinaw na paliwanag kung bakit mahalaga ang pagtatanim para sa kinabukasan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,57,NULL,'Ang gobyerno ay may programang "Basa Para sa Bata." Bakit mahalagang hikayatin ang ibang bata na sumali dito?','Para maraming maglalaro','Para maraming matuto at umunlad.','Para maraming magkakaroon ng bagong libro.','Para maraming hindi mag-away.','B','Ang pagbabasa ay nakatutulong sa pagkatuto at pag-unlad ng mga bata. May proyekto sa barangay para sa paglilinis ng kapaligiran ngunit kulang ang boluntaryo. Dahil dito, nahihirapan ang mga organizer na maisakatuparan nang maayos ang mga gawain sa itinakdang oras. May iilang residente ang nagpakita ng interes, ngunit karamihan ay abala o hindi interesado.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,58,NULL,'Ano ang maaaring gawin upang mahikayat ang mas maraming tao na sumali?','Hayaan na lang ang mga dati na sumasali','Magreklamo sa barangay','Magbigay ng impormasyon at imbitasyon sa mga residente','Itigil ang proyekto','C','Ang pagbibigay ng tamang impormasyon at imbitasyon ay nakatutulong upang mahikayat ang mas maraming tao na sumali sa proyekto.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,59,NULL,'Paano mo malalaman kung ang isang impormasyon tungkol sa proyekto sa komunidad ay totoo?','Basta galing sa kaibigan ay totoo na','I-check kung galing ito sa opisyal na tagapagbalita o opisyal na pahayagan','Kung maraming likes sa social media, totoo na','Wala nang kailangang beripikahin','B','Mahalagang tiyakin na ang impormasyon ay galing sa mapagkakatiwalaang pinagmulan upang makaiwas sa maling balita.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,60,NULL,'Isang grupo sa komunidad ang gustong magsagawa ng feeding program. Ano ang pinakamahalagang dapat isaalang-alang bago ito gawin?','Kung saan bibilhin ang pagkain','Kung sino ang mga kaibigan na isasama','Kung talagang kailangan ng feeding program sa lugar','Kung gaano kasaya ang aktibidad','C','Bago magsagawa ng feeding program, mahalagang alamin muna kung may pangangailangan dito upang masigurong makatutulong ito sa komunidad. Nais ng inyong barangay na maglunsad ng isang araw ng paglilinis sa inyong komunidad. Bilang isang kabataan, nais mong makatulong sa paggawa ng plano para dito.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,61,NULL,'Ano ang unang hakbang na dapat mong gawin para makatulong sa paggawa ng plano ng paglilinis?','Maglilinis agad nang hindi nagpaplano','Makipag-usap sa mga kapitbahay at alamin ang mga lugar na kailangan linisin','Manood na lang ng video tungkol sa paglilinis','Magreklamo na walang ginagawa ang barangay','B','Mahalagang malaman muna ang mga lugar na lilinisin upang makagawa ng maayos na plano at organisadong paglilinis.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,62,NULL,'Saan ka makakakuha ng impormasyon tungkol sa tamang paraan ng paglilinis ng kapaligiran?','Sa social media na walang malinaw na pinanggalingan','Sa mga balita, libro, o opisyal na website ng gobyerno tungkol sa kalinisan','Sa tsismis ng kapitbahay','Sa panaginip','B','Ito ay mga mapagkakatiwalaang sanggunian para sa tamang impormasyon tungkol sa kalinisan ng kapaligiran.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,63,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang magplano muna bago magsimula ng mga gawaing pangkomunidad tulad ng paglilinis?','Para malaman kung paano makikipagtulungan ang lahat at maiwasan ang gulo','Para mas madali ang reklamo sa barangay','Para lang makilala sa barangay','Para makatulog ng maaga','A','Ang pagpaplano ay mahalaga upang maayos ang takbo ng gawain at maging matagumpay ang proyekto.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,64,NULL,'Sa isang pagdiriwang sa inyong barangay, walang nakahandang watawat ng Pilipinas. Ano ang dapat gawin?','Ipagpatuloy ang programa kahit wala ito','Gumamit ng bandila ng ibang bansa','Gumawa ng sariling watawat ayon sa tamang disenyo','Kanselahin ang buong pagdiriwang','C','Ang watawat ay mahalagang sagisag ng bansa, kaya dapat may tamang representasyon sa pagdiriwang.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,65,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang malaman ang kahulugan ng mga sagisag tulad ng watawat, Barong Tagalog, o sinulog dance sa isang seremonya?','Para masabing uso ang mga ito','Para lang may masabi sa social media','Para maipakita ang tunay na diwa at kahulugan ng seremonya','Wala namang kahalagahan ang mga sagisag','C','Ang pag-unawa sa mga sagisag ay nagpapalalim ng respeto at pagmamalaki sa ating kultura.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,66,NULL,'Kung may seremonyang pagdiriwang ng Araw ng Kalayaan sa paaralan, ano ang pinakaangkop na sagisag na gamitin?','Bandila ng Pilipinas at tradisyunal na kasuotan','Christmas tree at parol','Costume ng mga superhero','Sports uniform','A','Ito ang mga angkop na sagisag sa pagdiriwang ng Araw ng Kalayaan upang ipakita ang pagmamahal sa bayan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,67,NULL,'Napansin mong mali ang kulay ng watawat ng Pilipinas na nakasabit sa barangay hall. Ano ang dapat mong gawin?','Hayaan na lang dahil hindi naman halata','Tawanan na lang ito','Sabihan ang barangay tungkol sa tamang kulay ng watawat','Sunugin ang maling watawat','C','Mahalagang itama ang maling pagpapakita ng watawat bilang respeto sa pambansang sagisag.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,68,NULL,'Saan ka makakakuha ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa mga pambansang sagisag ng Pilipinas tulad ng watawat, pambansang ibon, at pambansang awit?','Sa tsismis ng kapitbahay','Sa opisyal na libro o website ng gobyerno tulad ng DepEd o NHCP','Sa mga meme sa social media','Sa sabi-sabi ng mga kaklase','B','Ito ay mapagkakatiwalaang sanggunian para sa tamang impormasyon tungkol sa pambansang sagisag.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,69,NULL,'Bakit mahalagang kilalanin at igalang ang mga sagisag ng Pilipinas gaya ng watawat, pambansang awit, at kalabaw?','Dahil uso ito ngayon','Para may mai-post sa social media','Dahil simbolo ito ng ating pagkakakilanlan at kultura','Wala lang, kasi kailangan lang gawin','C','Ang mga pambansang sagisag ay nagpapakita ng ating kasaysayan at pagka-Pilipino kaya dapat itong igalang.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,70,NULL,'Kung nais mong tumulong sa maayos na pagpapatupad ng ordinansa sa inyong barangay, ano ang maaari mong gawin?','Magtinda ng murang plastic para hindi magreklamo ang iba','Mag-organisa ng information drive tungkol sa ordinansa','Mag-post ng hate comments sa social media','Manahimik na lang at huwag makialam','B','Sa ganitong paraan, mas marami ang makakaalam at susunod sa ordinansa para sa kapakanan ng lahat.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,71,NULL,'Saan ka makakakuha ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa nilalaman ng ordinansa at kung sino ang nagpasa nito?','Tsismis mula sa kapitbahay','Opisyal na pabatid mula sa barangay o munisipyo','Post sa social media na walang source','Opinyon ng mga tindera sa palengke','B','Ito ang tamang pinagmumulan ng impormasyon tungkol sa ordinansa at mga gumawa nito.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,72,NULL,'Bakit mahalaga na may kanya-kanyang tungkulin ang tatlong sangay ng pamahalaan sa ganitong sitwasyon?','Para mabilis maipatupad ang gusto ng mga opisyal','Para magkaiba ang trabaho nila at hindi magkagulo','Para mabalanse ang kapangyarihan at may nagsusuri kung tama ba ang batas','Para lahat sila ay may masabing ginawa','C','Ito ay para maiwasan ang abuso at magkaroon ng tamang proseso sa pamahalaan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,73,NULL,'May dalawang bata sa inyong barangay na nag-aaway. Ano ang dapat mong gawin upang matulungan silang magkaayos?','Tawanan sila habang nag-aaway','Paghiwalayin sila at kausapin ng mahinahon','Sumigaw at pagalitan silang pareho','Iwasan sila at huwag makialam','B','Ito ang tamang paraan para matigil ang away at magkaroon ng maayos na pag-uusap.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,74,NULL,'Gusto mong tumulong sa paglilinis ng inyong barangay. Saan ka makakakuha ng tamang impormasyon kung kailan at saan ito gaganapin?','Sa lihim na sulat ng kaklase','Sa tsismis ng mga bata sa kanto','Sa opisyal na paalala mula sa barangay o kay guro','Sa kwento ng panaginip ng kaibigan','C','Ang opisyal na paalala ang mapagkakatiwalaang pinanggagalingan ng tamang impormasyon tungkol sa aktibidad. Bawal magtapon ng basura sa ilog, pero may ilang tao sa barangay ninyo na patuloy pa rin sa pagtapon dito.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS5',3,3,75,NULL,'Ano ang maaaring masamang epekto ng hindi pagsunod sa patakarang ito?','Mas gaganda ang amoy ng ilog','Magiging marumi at mabaho ang ilog, at maaaring magkasakit ang mga tao','Dadami ang mga isda sa ilog','Gagaling ang mga may ubo at sipon','B','Ang hindi pagsunod sa patakaran, tulad ng pagtatapon ng basura sa ilog, ay nagdudulot ng polusyon. Dahil dito, maaaring kumalat ang sakit at masira ang kalikasan.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,1,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','Ana''s phone battery is running low while she is doing her research. What should she do?','Watch videos instead','Stop researching and go to sleep','Keep using the phone until it turns off','Plug it into a charger and continue working','D','Solving problems means managing tools properly so she can finish her task.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,2,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','Ana accidentally closed the browser and lost the page she was reading. What should she do?','Watch a movie instead','Start over and search again','Get angry and stop researching','Wait for her teacher to do it for her','B','When a page is lost, the best problem-solving approach is to stay calm and search again using the right keywords. This builds digital resilience and encourages independent learning—key parts of 21st-century skills',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,3,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','Which of the following websites would MOST LIKELY help Ana complete her Science project?','www.plantsforsale.net','www.fashiontrends.org','www.depedschools.edu.ph','www.onlineplantsgame.com','C','Educational websites (like.edu.ph) provide trustworthy information relevant to her project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,4,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','What is the BEST search phrase Ana should type into the search engine?','“plants”','“plants in games”','“plant TikTok videos”','“local plants used in the Philippines”','D','Using specific search terms helps in finding accurate and useful information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,5,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','Ana comes across an article titled ''Top 10 Magical Plants'' without any listed author or sources. What should she do?','Use the article right away','Send the link to her friends','Copy and paste it without reading','Ignore it and find a more reliable source','D','Critical thinkers evaluate the reliability of sources before using them.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,6,'Ana is an ALS A&E Elementary learner who wants to research local plants for her Learning Strand 2 project. She has a mobile phone with internet access. She types "plants" into a search engine and sees thousands of results, including games and online shops.','Ana finds two websites: one with scientific names and references, and another with cartoons and emojis. Which one should she use?','The one with scientific names and references','The cartoon one because it’s fun','Neither just ask a classmate','Both, without checking','A','The first website is more reliable because it contains scientific terms, author names, and sources, which are signs of credibility. These elements allow readers to verify the information and ensure it is accurate and trustworthy—important qualities for a science project. Cartoons and emojis without references may be entertaining but are not dependable for factual research.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,7,'During a weekend family visit, Mariel notices that each of her relatives is using a different device. Her uncle is working on a desktop computer in the study, her cousin is doinghomework on a laptop at the kitchen table, her aunt is reading an ebook on a tablet, and her younger brother is watching videos on a smartphone.','If Mariel wants to read e-books while traveling, which device would be the most convenient?','Desktop computer','Laptop','Tablet','Printer','C','Tablets are lightweight and portable, making them ideal for reading on the go.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,8,'During a weekend family visit, Mariel notices that each of her relatives is using a different device. Her uncle is working on a desktop computer in the study, her cousin is doinghomework on a laptop at the kitchen table, her aunt is reading an ebook on a tablet, and her younger brother is watching videos on a smartphone.','Which of the following is NOT considered a computing device?','Smartphone','Electric fan','Laptop','Tablet','B','A tablet, smartphone, and laptop are digital devices capable of running software and processing information. An electric fan, while useful for cooling, is not a digital device and cannot store, process, or transmit data.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,9,'During a weekend family visit, Mariel notices that each of her relatives is using a different device. Her uncle is working on a desktop computer in the study, her cousin is doinghomework on a laptop at the kitchen table, her aunt is reading an ebook on a tablet, and her younger brother is watching videos on a smartphone.','Which of the following devices that Mariel saw is most used for working in an office?','Tablet','Smartphone','Gaming Console','Desktop Computer','D','A desktop computer is best for office work because it has a full keyboard, larger screen, and greater processing power, making it easier to create documents, send emails, and manage files efficiently. While tablets and smartphones can do some of these tasks, they are less convenient for long hours of office work, and a gaming console is not designed for productivity.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,10,'During a weekend family visit, Mariel notices that each of her relatives is using a different device. Her uncle is working on a desktop computer in the study, her cousin is doinghomework on a laptop at the kitchen table, her aunt is reading an ebook on a tablet, and her younger brother is watching videos on a smartphone.','What is the BEST reason Mariel’s cousin uses a laptop for homework?','It plays loud music','It has colorful buttons','It is the only device in the house','It is portable and can run learning programs','D','Laptops are computing devices suitable for learning due to their flexibility and functionality.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,11,'During a weekend family visit, Mariel notices that each of her relatives is using a different device. Her uncle is working on a desktop computer in the study, her cousin is doinghomework on a laptop at the kitchen table, her aunt is reading an ebook on a tablet, and her younger brother is watching videos on a smartphone.','What makes a smartphone a type of computing device?','It can process data, access the internet, and run apps','It is used only for calls','It is small and shiny','It has games','A','Smartphones are minicomputers that perform tasks like laptops and desktops.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,12,'Mia is setting up a computer to work on her school project. She notices that the computer has different parts, such as the monitor, keyboard, and mouse, along with additional devices like a wireless printer and wired headphones. She begins to wonder which of these devices are considered peripherals and how each one helps her complete her tasks.','Mia is having trouble printing her project. What could be the reason the wireless printer isn''t working?','Mia’s computer is too old','The computer is turned off','Mia''s project is too big to print','The printer is not connected to the internet or network','D','For wireless printers to work, they need to be connected to the same network as the computer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,13,'Mia is setting up a computer to work on her school project. She notices that the computer has different parts, such as the monitor, keyboard, and mouse, along with additional devices like a wireless printer and wired headphones. She begins to wonder which of these devices are considered peripherals and how each one helps her complete her tasks.','If Mia wants to improve her computer''s performance, which of the following internal parts would most likely help?','Random Access Memory (RAM)','Monitor','Headphones','Wireless printer','A','Upgrading the RAM can improve the computer’s performance in tasks like running programs and multitasking.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,14,'Mia is setting up a computer to work on her school project. She notices that the computer has different parts, such as the monitor, keyboard, and mouse, along with additional devices like a wireless printer and wired headphones. She begins to wonder which of these devices are considered peripherals and how each one helps her complete her tasks.','Which of the following devices is an example of a wireless peripheral?','Wired printer','Wired keyboard','Wireless mouse','External hard drive with a Universal Serial Bus (USB) cable','C','A wireless mouse uses Bluetooth or another wireless technology to communicate with the computer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,15,'Mia is setting up a computer to work on her school project. She notices that the computer has different parts, such as the monitor, keyboard, and mouse, along with additional devices like a wireless printer and wired headphones. She begins to wonder which of these devices are considered peripherals and how each one helps her complete her tasks.','Mia is using a computer to write her report and needs to ensure she can hear the audio of her video presentation clearly. Which peripheral device will help her?','Printer','Monitor','USB flash drive','Speakers or headphones','D','Speakers or headphones are peripherals used to listen to audio from the computer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,16,'Carlos is considering buying a new device for his studies. He knows that there are different types of computing devices—such as laptops, tablets, and smartphones with its own unique features and functions. Carlos is looking for a device that will allow him to take notes, conduct research, watch educational videos, and participate in online classes.','Carlos wants a device that he can easily carry to class, use to take notes, and participate in online classes. Which of these devices would be the most appropriate for him?','Laptop','Smartphone','Digital camera','Desktop computer','A','Laptops are portable and have all the features needed for note taking, research, and attending online classes.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,17,'Carlos is considering buying a new device for his studies. He knows that there are different types of computing devices—such as laptops, tablets, and smartphones with its own unique features and functions. Carlos is looking for a device that will allow him to take notes, conduct research, watch educational videos, and participate in online classes.','If Carlos only needs a device for writing essays and browsing the internet, which of the following would best meet his needs?','Tablet','Smartphone','Gaming console','Desktop computer','A','Tablets can handle writing tasks and browsing the internet, making them suitable for simple academic tasks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,18,'Carlos is considering buying a new device for his studies. He knows that there are different types of computing devices—such as laptops, tablets, and smartphones with its own unique features and functions. Carlos is looking for a device that will allow him to take notes, conduct research, watch educational videos, and participate in online classes.','Which device has portability as its primary feature and is ideal for students who need to carry it between classes and perform light tasks?','Laptop','Smart watch','Gaming console','Desktop computer','A','Laptops are portable and ideal for students who need to work in different locations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,19,'Carlos is considering buying a new device for his studies. He knows that there are different types of computing devices—such as laptops, tablets, and smartphones with its own unique features and functions. Carlos is looking for a device that will allow him to take notes, conduct research, watch educational videos, and participate in online classes.','Carlos is considering whether to get a tablet or a desktop computer. He needs a device that is portable, has internet access, and features a touchscreen. What should Carlos choose?','Laptop','Tablet','Gaming console','Desktop computer','B','A tablet is portable, has a touch screen, and can access the internet, unlike a desktop computer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,20,NULL,'Ella notices that her computer is slow and takes a long time to open programs. What should she do first to improve her performance?','Uninstall the operating system','Leave all programs open while working','Restart the computer and close unused programs','keep using the computer until it eventually speeds up','C','Restarting the computer and closing unnecessary programs helps free up system resources and improve performance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,21,NULL,'Which of the following actions should be taken first before using a computer?','Begin downloading files','Open multiple programs at once','Start using the internet immediately','Turn on the computer and wait for it to load','D','The computer needs to be powered on and fully loaded before use to ensure that all systems are ready.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,22,NULL,'If Ella''s computer is getting too hot, which of the following is the MOST likely solution?','Turn off the computer immediately','Increase the brightness of the screen','Disconnect the internet to cool it down','Ensure that the computer has proper ventilation and is not covered','D','Ensuring proper ventilation is key to preventing overheating, which can damage internal components.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,23,NULL,'What should Ella do if she sees a pop-up message indicating that her computer''s software is out of date?','Ignore the message','Restart the computer without updating','Check for software updates and install them','Click on the pop-up to download random updates','C','Keeping software up to date ensures the computer runs smoothly and is protected from security vulnerabilities.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,24,'Mario is working on a school project using a computer. He has different types of files, such as documents, images, and videos. He needs to organize and manage these files efficiently to ensure he can find and use them when needed.','Which of the following options lists the correct types of files that Carlos might use for his school project, based on their features and functions?','.jpg (Image file), .txt (Text file), .mp4 (Video file)','.bat (Batch file), .sys (System file), .iso (Disk image file','.exe (Executable file), .zip (Compressed file), .html (Web page file)','.css (Cascading Style Sheet), .dll (Dynamic Link Library), .sys (System file)','A','.jpg is used for images, .txt is used for plain text,. mp4 is used for videos. These file types are commonly used in school projects for images, documents, and multimedia presentations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,1,25,NULL,'Mario needs to send several large documents and images to his teacher. Which file type would be best for compressing these files into one?','.txt','.zip','.html','.pptx','B','A .zip file is used to compress multiple files into one, making them easier to share and download.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,26,NULL,'Which of the following file types is primarily used to store a portable document that can be viewed on multiple devices?','.txt','.pdf','.exe','.css','B','The .pdf file format is commonly used for documents that need to be easily shared and viewed across different devices without losing formatting.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,27,'Mark has been working on a school project and has a variety of files saved on his computer—documents, images, and presentations. With the project deadline approaching, he realizes he needs a more organized way to manage these files to avoid confusion and save time. He also wants to ensure that, in case his computer crashes, he won’t lose his work.','Mark needs to ensure that his project files are safe in case of a computer failure. Which of the following steps would be most effective for backing them up?','Do not worry about backing up the files','Keep all files only on the computer’s desktop','Save files on a USB flash drive and in cloud storage','Store files only in the computer’s "Downloads" folder','C','Saving files in multiple locations (USB flash drive and cloud storage) ensures they are protected against data loss.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,28,'Mark has been working on a school project and has a variety of files saved on his computer—documents, images, and presentations. With the project deadline approaching, he realizes he needs a more organized way to manage these files to avoid confusion and save time. He also wants to ensure that, in case his computer crashes, he won’t lose his work.','What is Mark’s BEST reason for backing up project files to both external drive and cloud storage?','To save space on the computer','To make the computer run faster','To prevent files from being opened','To ensure that if one backup fails, the other is still available','D','Backing up files in two places increases the likelihood of data recovery in case of system failure.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,29,'Teacher Mia asked John to help her prepare materials for their school program. She told him that he could use the school computer to complete different tasks. First, John needs to write an invitation letter for the parents. Then, he wants to create a short slideshow for the event and record the attendance of students using a table. To accomplish all of this, John must choose the right tool for each task. He knows there are different types of software on the computer, some for writing, some for making presentations, and others for organizing data. John needs to identify which tool or application is best suited for each job.','John needs to record the attendance of students during the school program. He wants to organize the data by listing the students'' names and attendance statuses, then counting the number of students who attended. What steps should John follow in spreadsheet software to solve this problem effectively','Create a table with student names in one column and attendance statuses in another column. Use a formula like =COUNTIF (column, "Yes") to count the attendees.','Write the list of names and attendance statuses in paragraph format using word processing software to summarize the attendance.','Use presentation software to create slides that list the names and attendance statuses and manually count the attendees.','Organize the student names alphabetically in rows and use word processing software to write a summary of the attendees.','A','Spreadsheet software allows John to organize data in tables and use formulas like =COUNTIF to automatically count specific entries (e.g., those marked “Yes”). This is faster, more accurate, and easier to update than counting manually or using software not designed for data analysis.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,30,'Teacher Mia asked John to help her prepare materials for their school program. She told him that he could use the school computer to complete different tasks. First, John needs to write an invitation letter for the parents. Then, he wants to create a short slideshow for the event and record the attendance of students using a table. To accomplish all of this, John must choose the right tool for each task. He knows there are different types of software on the computer, some for writing, some for making presentations, and others for organizing data. John needs to identify which tool or application is best suited for each job.','John wants to show pictures and slides during the event to make his presentation more engaging. Why should John choose presentation software instead of word processing software for this task?','Because presentation software can format text more effectively than word processing software.','Because presentation software allows for visual features like animations and slide transitions.','Because presentation software requires less effort to type content compared to word processing software.','Because presentation software uses templates that automatically organize data into rows and columns.','B','Presentation software (like PowerPoint or Google Slides) is designed to showcase visual content effectively during events. It enables users to add images, animations, and transitions, making the presentation more engaging and interactive. Word processing software, while ideal for writing and formatting text, does not support the visual capabilities required for effective presentations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,31,'Teacher Mia asked John to help her prepare materials for their school program. She told him that he could use the school computer to complete different tasks. First, John needs to write an invitation letter for the parents. Then, he wants to create a short slideshow for the event and record the attendance of students using a table. To accomplish all of this, John must choose the right tool for each task. He knows there are different types of software on the computer, some for writing, some for making presentations, and others for organizing data. John needs to identify which tool or application is best suited for each job.','John has finished writing the invitation and creating the slideshow. Now, he wants to check which tool can help him with calculations, such as counting how many parents will attend. Which tool should he choose?','Web browser','Spreadsheet software','Paint software','Word processing software','B','Spreadsheet software is designed for handling data and performing calculations such as totals or averages. It''s the best tool for solving John’s problem of counting attendance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,32,'Maria needs to write a short thank-you letter to her parents. She goes to the learning center''s computer and opens a word processing program. On the screen, Maria sees several parts, such as the area where she can type her letter, buttons with pictures, and words at the top like "File" and "Home." To finish her letter, Maria needs to understand what these parts are and how they are used.','Which part of the word processing software should Maria click to begin typing her thank-you letter?','The toolbar','The “Save” button','The title bar','The blank white area (document area)','D','The document area is where users can type their content. This helps Maria know where to write her letter.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,33,'Maria needs to write a short thank-you letter to her parents. She goes to the learning center''s computer and opens a word processing program. On the screen, Maria sees several parts, such as the area where she can type her letter, buttons with pictures, and words at the top like "File" and "Home." To finish her letter, Maria needs to understand what these parts are and how they are used.','Maria wants to make her words bigger. Which part of the screen can help her find this option?','The keyboard','The scroll bar','The document area','The menu bar or toolbar','D','The menu bar or toolbar includes tools like font size, style, and formatting. Maria must identify where these tools are located to adjust text size.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,34,'Maria needs to write a short thank-you letter to her parents. She goes to the learning center''s computer and opens a word processing program. On the screen, Maria sees several parts, such as the area where she can type her letter, buttons with pictures, and words at the top like "File" and "Home." To finish her letter, Maria needs to understand what these parts are and how they are used.','If Maria wants to save her letter to print later, which option is best to choose?','Click on “Insert Picture”','Press the “Bold” button','Close the program right away','Click on the “File” tab, then select “Save”','D','Saving a document is an important step to avoid losing work. Maria needs to think ahead and decide the right action to keep her letter safe.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,35,'Jelai wants to create a flyer for a school event using the computer. She opens the desktop publishing software and looks at the screen. In the center, she sees a large area where she can type and add pictures. At the top of the screen, she notices options like “File,” “Home,” and “Insert,” which will help her save her work and add things like text or images. On the sides, there are buttons with icons that allow her to change colors, fonts, and shapes. Jelai needs to understand what these parts of the screen do so that she can use them to make the flyer look polished and professional for the event.','Jelai is trying to create a flyer for the school event and needs to add some text. Where should she click to start typing?','In the corners of the screen','On the buttons with pictures on the side','In the large area in the middle of the screen','On the words at the top like “File” and “Home”','C','The large area in the middle of the screen is where Jelai can type and add pictures. It''s the main space for her to create and design the flyer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,36,'Jelai wants to create a flyer for a school event using the computer. She opens the desktop publishing software and looks at the screen. In the center, she sees a large area where she can type and add pictures. At the top of the screen, she notices options like “File,” “Home,” and “Insert,” which will help her save her work and add things like text or images. On the sides, there are buttons with icons that allow her to change colors, fonts, and shapes. Jelai needs to understand what these parts of the screen do so that she can use them to make the flyer look polished and professional for the event.','Jelai needs to change the color of the text in her flyer. Where can she find the option to do so?','In the corners of the screen','On the buttons with pictures on the side','In the large area in the middle of the screen','In the words like “File” and “Insert” at the top of the screen','D','n most word-processing or design software (e.g., Microsoft Word), the text color (font color) option is located in the top menu bar—often under tabs like “Home”, which includes groups like Font. The Font Color dropdown icon—often represented by a letter “A” with a colored underline—is found there. You select your desired text, go to the Home (or similar) tab at the top, then click the Font Color dropdown to change the color',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,37,'Jelai wants to create a flyer for a school event using the computer. She opens the desktop publishing software and looks at the screen. In the center, she sees a large area where she can type and add pictures. At the top of the screen, she notices options like “File,” “Home,” and “Insert,” which will help her save her work and add things like text or images. On the sides, there are buttons with icons that allow her to change colors, fonts, and shapes. Jelai needs to understand what these parts of the screen do so that she can use them to make the flyer look polished and professional for the event.','Jelai wants to save her flyer and ensure she can finish it later. Where should she go to save her work?','In the corners of the screen','On the buttons with pictures on the side','In the large area in the middle of the screen','On the words like “File,” “Home,” and “Insert” at the top of the screen','D','To save her work, Jelai should click on "File" at the top of the screen. This is the section where she can find options to save, open, and manage her work.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,38,'Jelai wants to create a flyer for a school event using the computer. She opens the desktop publishing software and looks at the screen. In the center, she sees a large area where she can type and add pictures. At the top of the screen, she notices options like “File,” “Home,” and “Insert,” which will help her save her work and add things like text or images. On the sides, there are buttons with icons that allow her to change colors, fonts, and shapes. Jelai needs to understand what these parts of the screen do so that she can use them to make the flyer look polished and professional for the event.','Jelai wants to make her flyer more colorful by adding an image. Where can she go to do this?','In the corners of the screen','On the buttons with pictures on the side','In the large area in the middle of the screen','On the words like “File” and “Insert” at the top of the screen','D','To add a picture, Jelai should click on “Insert” at the top of the screen. This option allows her to insert images, shapes, and other elements into her flyer.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,39,'James wants to create a slideshow for his school project. He opens the computer''s presentation software and notices several parts of the screen: a large area in the middle where he will add text and pictures, some buttons at the top to help him format his slides, and a list on the left that shows all his slides. On the right side, he sees options for choosing colors and styles. James needs to understand what each part of the screen does so he can use the right tools to create his presentation.','James wants to add a new slide to his presentation. Where should he go in the presentation software to do so?','On the right side of the screen','In the buttons at the top of the screen','In the big area in the middle of the screen','In the list of slides on the left side of the screen','D','To edit the title on a slide, James should click directly on the title text box in the main editing area. This allows him to change the text right away. The scroll bar moves through slides, the “New Slide” button adds a slide, and the slide thumbnail only selects a slide—it doesn’t let him edit text directly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,40,'James wants to create a slideshow for his school project. He opens the computer''s presentation software and notices several parts of the screen: a large area in the middle where he will add text and pictures, some buttons at the top to help him format his slides, and a list on the left that shows all his slides. On the right side, he sees options for choosing colors and styles. James needs to understand what each part of the screen does so he can use the right tools to create his presentation.','Where can James find options to change the background color and style of his slides?','On the right side of the screen','In the buttons at the top of the screen','In the big area in the middle of the screen','In the list of slides on the left side of the screen','B','Themes, background colors, and overall slide design settings are usually found in the top toolbar or ribbon, often under a Design tab. The main editing area is for changing slide content, slide thumbnails are for selecting slides, and the scroll bar is for navigating, not formatting.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,41,'James wants to create a slideshow for his school project. He opens the computer''s presentation software and notices several parts of the screen: a large area in the middle where he will add text and pictures, some buttons at the top to help him format his slides, and a list on the left that shows all his slides. On the right side, he sees options for choosing colors and styles. James needs to understand what each part of the screen does so he can use the right tools to create his presentation.','James notices that the list of slides on the left shows all his slides in a small preview. How does this help James as he works on his presentation?','It makes the presentation longer.','It changes the color of his slides.','It helps him add pictures to his slides.','It allows him to see and organize all his slides easily.','D','The list on the left side of the screen shows a preview of each slide. This is helpful for James to quickly see all his slides and easily rearrange them, ensuring a clear and organized presentation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,42,'Ben wants to organize the class monthly attendance using the school’s computer. He opens the spreadsheet software and sees a grid with rows and columns where he can type information. At the top of the screen, there are options like ''File,'' ''Edit,'' and ''View'' that will help him open, save, and modify documents. On the side of the screen, Ben notices a row of numbers and letters to help him find the right place to type. He needs to understand what all these parts are and how to use them to organize the attendance sheet correctly.','Ben needs to enter the names of each student into a list. Which part of the spreadsheet interface should he use to input the names?','The “File” menu at the top','The button to change colors','The row of numbers on the side','The grid of boxes formed by rows and columns','D','The grid of boxes formed by rows and columns is where Ben will type the student names. This is the main area for entering data.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,43,'Ben wants to organize the class monthly attendance using the school’s computer. He opens the spreadsheet software and sees a grid with rows and columns where he can type information. At the top of the screen, there are options like ''File,'' ''Edit,'' and ''View'' that will help him open, save, and modify documents. On the side of the screen, Ben notices a row of numbers and letters to help him find the right place to type. He needs to understand what all these parts are and how to use them to organize the attendance sheet correctly.','Which menu option at the top of the screen will help Ben save the attendance sheet he is working on?','Edit','File','Rows','View','B','The "File" menu contains options like "Save" or "Save As," which will allow Ben to save his work.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,44,'Ben wants to organize the class monthly attendance using the school’s computer. He opens the spreadsheet software and sees a grid with rows and columns where he can type information. At the top of the screen, there are options like ''File,'' ''Edit,'' and ''View'' that will help him open, save, and modify documents. On the side of the screen, Ben notices a row of numbers and letters to help him find the right place to type. He needs to understand what all these parts are and how to use them to organize the attendance sheet correctly.','Why are the rows labeled with numbers and the columns labeled with letters important for Ben when entering attendance?','They help him print the sheet easily.','They help him add pictures to his sheet.','They automatically calculate the total attendance for him.','They allow him to know exactly where to type the names and other information.','D','The numbers for rows and the letters for columns help Ben find the correct spot to enter specific information, such as student names and attendance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,45,'Teacher Carla talked to her ALS elementary learners about how the internet can help them learn new things. She told them that the internet is like a big library where they can find lots of information using a computer or a cellphone. Gina, one of the learners, became curious and asked how she could use the internet for her homework. She wanted to search for facts about animals, watch videos about where they live, and find pictures for her project. Teacher Carla guided her by showing her how to open a web browser and type what she was looking for. Gina was amazed to see results like websites, pictures, videos, and even maps. She felt excited to use the internet for learning!','Which of the following steps should Gina take to find information about animals on the internet?','Turn off the computer and go outside.','Only use the search bar to play games.','Wait for the teacher to give her the information.','Open the web browser and type "animals" in the search bar.','D','Gina should use the web browser to search for the information she needs by typing keywords like "animals" in the search bar. This is how she can find useful information, videos, and pictures.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,46,'Teacher Carla talked to her ALS elementary learners about how the internet can help them learn new things. She told them that the internet is like a big library where they can find lots of information using a computer or a cellphone. Gina, one of the learners, became curious and asked how she could use the internet for her homework. She wanted to search for facts about animals, watch videos about where they live, and find pictures for her project. Teacher Carla guided her by showing her how to open a web browser and type what she was looking for. Gina was amazed to see results like websites, pictures, videos, and even maps. She felt excited to use the internet for learning!','Which of the following results can Gina find when she searches for animals on the internet?','Only text.','Only videos.','Only websites.','Websites, images, and videos.','D','When Gina searches for information, she can find a variety of results including websites, images, and videos. These are all helpful resources for her project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,47,'Teacher Carla talked to her ALS elementary learners about how the internet can help them learn new things. She told them that the internet is like a big library where they can find lots of information using a computer or a cellphone. Gina, one of the learners, became curious and asked how she could use the internet for her homework. She wanted to search for facts about animals, watch videos about where they live, and find pictures for her project. Teacher Carla guided her by showing her how to open a web browser and type what she was looking for. Gina was amazed to see results like websites, pictures, videos, and even maps. She felt excited to use the internet for learning!','What should Gina consider when choosing which result to click on for her project?','Whether the website has a lot of ads.','Whether the website is colorful and bright.','Whether the website has a lot of pictures, even if the information is not helpful.','Whether the website or video has good information, pictures, and videos that match what she needs for her project.','D','Gina should choose results that provide accurate and helpful information, along with relevant pictures and videos that will support her project on animals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,48,'John wants to share his science project with his class. He saved his project on the computer and needs to upload it to the school’s online platform. He also needs to download a template for his report. Since he’s not sure how to do this, Teacher Lara helps him. She shows him how to upload a file from the computer and how to download one from the internet. John learns that uploading means sending a file online, while downloading means saving a file to his computer.','John cannot find the upload button on the school''s online platform. What should he do?','Keep clicking random buttons','Wait until someone uploads it for him','Turn off the computer and forget about it','Ask Teacher Lara or check the instructions carefully','D','If John can’t find the upload button, the responsible approach is to check the platform’s instructions or seek help from a teacher. This ensures he submits the assignment correctly and avoids mistakes. Random clicking, giving up, or relying on others without trying to solve the problem are not responsible solutions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,49,'John wants to share his science project with his class. He saved his project on the computer and needs to upload it to the school’s online platform. He also needs to download a template for his report. Since he’s not sure how to do this, Teacher Lara helps him. She shows him how to upload a file from the computer and how to download one from the internet. John learns that uploading means sending a file online, while downloading means saving a file to his computer.','Why is it important for John to download the template for his report?','So, he can decorate his computer','Because his classmates told him to do it','Because the file will make his project look colorful','So, he has a guide to help him write his report properly','D','Information literacy involves knowing which resources help your complete tasks better and using them wisely.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,2,50,'John wants to share his science project with his class. He saved his project on the computer and needs to upload it to the school’s online platform. He also needs to download a template for his report. Since he’s not sure how to do this, Teacher Lara helps him. She shows him how to upload a file from the computer and how to download one from the internet. John learns that uploading means sending a file online, while downloading means saving a file to his computer.','What is the main difference between uploading and downloading?','Uploading is for fun, downloading is for school only','Uploading is for copying files, downloading is for deleting files','Uploading makes your computer faster, downloading makes it slower','Uploading is sending a file online, downloading is getting a file from the internet','D','Critical thinking means understanding how things work and knowing the correct meaning of terms.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,51,'John wants to share his science project with his class. He saved his project on the computer and needs to upload it to the school’s online platform. He also needs to download a template for his report. Since he’s not sure how to do this, Teacher Lara helps him. She shows him how to upload a file from the computer and how to download one from the internet. John learns that uploading means sending a file online, while downloading means saving a file to his computer.','Before downloading the template for his report, what should John check first to ensure it is safe and useful?','If the file is very large in size','If the file has a colorful design','If the website has fun pictures and sounds','If the website is trusted and the file matches what he needs','D','Information literacy means knowing how to choose safe and helpful online content. John should always check the source and make sure the file fits his task.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,52,'Teacher Jane teaches her ALS learners about different tools for communication and learning. Aslie wants to know how to communicate with her classmates and teachers, so Teacher Jane shows her how to use email, messaging apps, and video calls. She also explains how to find useful learning resources, such as websites, e-books, and videos online. Maria is excited to use these tools to help with her schoolwork.','Aslie wants to ask her classmate about their group project but is unsure which tool to use. She can choose between email, messaging apps, or video calls. Which tool should Aslie use if she wants to ask a quick question about the project?','E-book','Email','Messaging app','Video call','C','Messaging apps are best for quick, informal communication, making them a great choice when Aslie wants to ask a quick question about the project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,53,'Teacher Jane teaches her ALS learners about different tools for communication and learning. Aslie wants to know how to communicate with her classmates and teachers, so Teacher Jane shows her how to use email, messaging apps, and video calls. She also explains how to find useful learning resources, such as websites, e-books, and videos online. Maria is excited to use these tools to help with her schoolwork.','What is the best way for Aslie to find helpful information for her science project on animals?','Send an email to her teacher','Use a video call to ask her parents','Use a messaging app to ask her friend','Search online for educational websites and videos','D','Searching online for educational websites and videos will provide Aslie with reliable, relevant information for her science project on animals.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,54,'Teacher Jane teaches her ALS learners about different tools for communication and learning. Aslie wants to know how to communicate with her classmates and teachers, so Teacher Jane shows her how to use email, messaging apps, and video calls. She also explains how to find useful learning resources, such as websites, e-books, and videos online. Maria is excited to use these tools to help with her schoolwork.','Aslie is trying to decide whether to use a video or an e-book for her homework. She needs to choose the best resource to understand the different habitats of animals. What should Aslie choose?','E-book','Email','Messaging app','Video','D','A video would likely give Aslie a visual representation of different animal habitats, making it easier for her to understand the topic compared to an e-book.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,55,'Teacher Jane teaches her ALS learners about different tools for communication and learning. Aslie wants to know how to communicate with her classmates and teachers, so Teacher Jane shows her how to use email, messaging apps, and video calls. She also explains how to find useful learning resources, such as websites, e-books, and videos online. Maria is excited to use these tools to help with her schoolwork.','Aslie wants to ensure that the information she finds on the internet for her project is reliable. What should she do to verify if the website is trustworthy?','Ask her friend for the information','Only using information from social media','Use the first website that appears in the search results','Check if the website has an "About Us" section and is from a well-known organization or educational institution','D','Checking if the website is from a well-known organization or educational institution and has an "About Us" section helps ensure the information is reliable and trustworthy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,56,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','What should Mary Grace do immediately after noticing that a file has started downloading from a website without her clicking anything?','Click on the download to check what it is','Restart the computer to stop the download','Ignore it and continue searching for information','Inform the librarian and close the browser immediately','D','This is a potential case of malware or a harmful download. The correct response is to alert an adult or authority and close the site immediately to reduce the risk of infecting the computer or compromising data.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,57,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Why should Mary Grace not give her email address and password to Sonia, even if Sonia wants to help?','Because Sonia might forget the password','Because Sonia might not know how to open school files','Because passwords are private and sharing, they can cause problems','Because Mary Grace should only share her password with her teacher','C','Sharing passwords can lead to misuse or hacking, so it’s important to keep them private.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,58,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','How can Mary Grace tell if the message saying ''You won a prize! Enter your email and password!'' is not real?','Real prizes always ask for passwords','Legitimate websites rarely give prizes just for searching.','She thinks it is okay because she’s using a school computer.','Pop-ups with urgent messages that ask for personal information are often scams or phishing attempts.','D','Legitimate websites do not request sensitive information, such as passwords, through pop-up messages. Scammers often use these tactics to trick people into giving away personal data. Being on a school computer does not make unsafe pop-ups secure, and real prizes do not require passwords to claim',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,59,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Stephen Ace has started staying up very late using his tablet, and now he often feels tired and has trouble concentrating on his lessons. What can he do to manage his tablet use while taking care of his health?','Stop using the tablet completely','Use the tablet only during his free time at night','Set a schedule for using the tablet and take breaks to rest his eyes','Keep using the tablet as long as he wants to finish all his lessons and games','C','It''s important for Stephen to tell a trusted adult and block unknown contacts to stay safe online',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,60,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Stephen Ace receives messages from strangers while using his tablet. What should he do to stay safe?','Reply to the messages to find out who they are','Ignore the messages and continue using the tablet','Tell his parents or another trusted adult and block the strangers','Share his personal information to see if they are friendly','C','Digital health includes managing screen time and ensuring physical well- being. Setting a schedule and taking breaks can prevent eye strain and lack of sleep, helping Stephen Ace stay healthy and productive.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,61,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Why are Stephen Ace’s parents concerned about his tablet use, and how can he stay healthy and safe while using it?','He doesn''t like using the tablet at all.','He is not using the tablet to learn anything.','He is using the tablet to learn and play in a balanced way.','He plays games too much, which makes him tired and unhealthy.','D','Stephen Ace’s parents are concerned because too much screen time can affect his sleep, health, and safety. To balance learning and entertainment, he can follow a schedule, take breaks, use the tablet in a safe place, and avoid talking to strangers online.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,62,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up appeared, saying, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" Her classmate, Sonia, asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Stephen Ace wants to learn how to use his tablet safely. Where is the best place to find correct and safe information?','Social media posts from strangers','Comments section of online games','Videos from unknown sources on the internet','Websites of trusted organizations like DepEd or online safety resources','D','Websites from trusted educational institutions like DepEd provide accurate, safe, and reliable information on responsible technology use. Comments in games, posts from strangers, or unverified videos may contain false or misleading advice.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,63,NULL,'Ana is making a simple flowchart of how to turn on a computer. She wants to show the first step, "Press the power button." What flowchart symbol should she use to represent this step?','Decision symbol','Process symbol','Terminator symbol','Input/Output symbol','B','"Press the power button" is an action or process, so the correct symbol is the Process symbol (rectangle), which is used to show an activity or task being done in a flowchart.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,64,NULL,'Juanel wants to ask a "Yes or No" question in his flowchart: “Is the monitor turned on?” What symbol should he use to represent this decision point?','Process symbol','Decision symbol','Connector symbol','Terminator symbol','B','A Decision symbol (diamond) is used when a question must be answered with Yes or No or True or False, leading to different outcomes. Since Ben is asking a question, he must use this symbol.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,65,NULL,'Rutchel is looking at his classmate’s flowchart. He sees a Terminator symbol used in the middle to show "Save your work." What should he suggest?','Remove the step because saving is not important.','Use a Decision symbol because saving is a choice.','Change it to a Process symbol because "Save your work" is an action.','Keep it as it is because the Terminator symbol can be used anywhere.','C','"Save your work" is an action, so the correct symbol to use is a Process symbol, not a Terminator symbol.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,66,NULL,'Rutchel wants to learn more about flowchart symbols for his project. Which source is the best and most reliable?','A text message from a friend','A YouTube video by a gamer','A funny flowchart on social media','An article from a trusted website like GCFGlobal or Khan Academy','D','Trusted websites with educational content provide accurate and reliable information, making them the best source for learning.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,67,NULL,'Gracia has misplaced some of her files and needs to organize them again. She wants to use the same algorithm to do so. However, she doesn’t remember how to create a folder. What should she do?','Ask the teacher to organize the files for her.','Ignore the algorithm and just open all files in the "Documents" folder.','Follow the algorithm but skip creating a new folder and move all files into the "Documents" folder.','Open the "Documents" folder and try to find the "School Projects" folder. If it’s not there, create a new folder','D','Gracia should check if the "School Projects" folder already exists. If not, she can create a new one. This ensures the organization remains intact and aligns with the instructions given in the algorithm.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,68,NULL,'Which of the following is an example of a basic algorithm?','Watching a movie','Following a recipe to cook rice','Drawing a picture of artistic art','Listening to lovely music at home','B','A basic algorithm is a step-by-step set of instructions to solve a problem or complete a task. Just like in solving problems using computers, we follow a clear order of steps.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,69,NULL,'Gracia has organized her school project files. If her teacher asks her to organize files from other subjects the same way, what should she do next?','Move all the files into the "Documents" folder.','Delete all folders and make a new one for each subject.','Leave the files scattered in different places on her tablet.','Create a folder named "Other Subjects" and move the files into it.','D','This option makes sense because it keeps her files organized by grouping them under one folder named "Other Subjects," just like she did with her school project files.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,70,NULL,'What could happen if Gracia forgets to move a school project file into the "School Projects" folder, and how can she solve the issue?','The file will be deleted, and Gracia will need to create a new one.','She will not be able to find the file again and will need to start over.','She can simply search for the file using the tablet’s search bar to find it quickly.','The file will be automatically moved to the "School Projects" folder by the tablet.','C','If Gracia forgets to move the file into the folder, she can still find it using the tablet’s search feature. Starting over or deleting the file is unnecessary. The tablet will not automatically move files for her unless she follows the instructions to do so.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,71,NULL,'Why is it important for Gracia to follow the predefined steps when organizing her files?','To avoid losing her school project files.','To learn how to use a tablet in general.','To make the process of organizing files more complicated.','To teach her to memorize the steps without understanding.','A','Following these steps helps Gracia keep her files organized and makes sure important documents aren''t lost. This teaches her how to manage files properly and avoid confusion when looking for them later. The other options don’t help with this task.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,72,NULL,'What is the key benefit of following a predefined algorithm when performing tasks on digital devices, such as Gracia’s file organization task?','It saves time by simplifying complex tasks.','It ensures that the task is completed without errors.','It provides an opportunity to explore and create unique steps on your own.','It makes it easier to learn how to use the device without additional instructions.','D','Following step-by-step instructions reduces the chance of errors and ensures each part of the installation process is done correctly. This way, the app will work as intended. Skipping steps, speeding up downloads, or working without internet (when it’s required) are not guaranteed or effective methods.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,73,'Jade is an ALS learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade decides to use block coding to complete her project.\n\nBlock coding allows Jade to build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that perform different functions, such as making something move, playing a sound, or displaying a message.\n\nFor her project, Jade selects blocks to:\n\n● Make the character move (to show digital safety tips) ● Play a sound (when a tip is shown) ● Display a message (for each digital safety tip)\n\nShe uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the correct order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips, with a sound playing in the background.','Which of the following is the primary purpose of using a Motion block in Jade’s digital safety project?','To play a sound when a tip is displayed','To create the background for the project','To make the character move across the screen','To display a message about digital safety tips','C','The motion block is specifically designed to move objects or characters within the project. In this scenario, Jade uses it to make the character move across',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,74,'Jade is an ALS learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade decides to use block coding to complete her project.\n\nBlock coding allows Jade to build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that perform different functions, such as making something move, playing a sound, or displaying a message.\n\nFor her project, Jade selects blocks to:\n\n● Make the character move (to show digital safety tips) ● Play a sound (when a tip is shown) ● Display a message (for each digital safety tip)\n\nShe uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the correct order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips, with a sound playing in the background.','Jade wants her character to speak the digital safety tips instead of displaying them as text. Which block should she add to her project?','Events block','Motion block','Sound block','Looks block','C','To make the character speak or play a sound, Jade needs to use the sound block. This block can be used to trigger a sound when a certain action, like displaying a tip, takes place.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',1,3,75,'Jade is an ALS learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade decides to use block coding to complete her project.\n\nBlock coding allows Jade to build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that perform different functions, such as making something move, playing a sound, or displaying a message.\n\nFor her project, Jade selects blocks to:\n\n● Make the character move (to show digital safety tips) ● Play a sound (when a tip is shown) ● Display a message (for each digital safety tip)\n\nShe uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the correct order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips, with a sound playing in the background.','Jade realizes that the digital safety tip message appears too quickly for learners to read. What should she do to fix this?','Add a Wait block after each message','Use a Looks block to slow down the text','Use a Sound block to delay the message','Use a Motion block to slow down the character’s movement','A','Adding a wait block will pause the project for a moment after each message, giving learners more time to read the digital safety tips.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,1,'Jomar observes that his parents use smartphones to send messages, his teacher uses a computer for online classes, and he watches educational videos on a tablet. He’s starting to wonder how all these gadgets are part of something called Information and Communication Technology (ICT).','Jomar’s teacher was absent due to an emergency, but she uploaded a video lesson for her students to watch at home. What does this situation best show about the role of ICT in education?','ICT makes learning more entertaining','ICT replaces teachers in the classroom','ICT supports learning even outside the classroom','ICT prevents learners from socializing with classmates','C','ICT helps you continue learning even when the teacher is not physically present. It allows students to access lessons through videos, online platforms, or other digital tools—making education flexible and accessible anytime, anywhere.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,2,'Jomar observes that his parents use smartphones to send messages, his teacher uses a computer for online classes, and he watches educational videos on a tablet. He’s starting to wonder how all these gadgets are part of something called Information and Communication Technology (ICT).','Jomar wants to ask his teacher a question about the lesson. What ICT tool can help him communicate quickly?','A typewriter','A telephone','A television','A flashlight','B','ICT tools like telephones help solve communication problems by allowing quick voice conversations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,3,'Jomar observes that his parents use smartphones to send messages, his teacher uses a computer for online classes, and he watches educational videos on a tablet. He’s starting to wonder how all these gadgets are part of something called Information and Communication Technology (ICT).','Which of the following best describes Information and Communication Technology (ICT)?','Only machines used in factories','Toys used for playing games','Kitchen tools used for cooking','Tools used for sharing, storing, or finding information','D','ICT refers to tools like computers, phones, and tablets used to communicate and access information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,4,'Jomar observes that his parents use smartphones to send messages, his teacher uses a computer for online classes, and he watches educational videos on a tablet. He’s starting to wonder how all these gadgets are part of something called Information and Communication Technology (ICT).','Which of the following is NOT an example of ICT in daily life?','A broom used to clean the floor','A radio used to listen to the news','A computer used to send an email','A tablet being used to watch alphabet songs','A','ICT tools are devices that process, store, or communicate information. A broom is a basic cleaning tool and does not involve any form of information or communication processing, making it not part of ICT.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,5,'Jomar observes that his parents use smartphones to send messages, his teacher uses a computer for online classes, and he watches educational videos on a tablet. He’s starting to wonder how all these gadgets are part of something called Information and Communication Technology (ICT).','Jomar sees that smartphones are often used to send messages and browse the internet. Why is smartphone considered part of ICT?','It is colorful and small','It is fun to play games on it','It is used to take selfies only','It can be used to send messages and access information online','D','Smartphones are part of ICT because they help people communicate (like sending messages) and get information (like using the internet). ICT stands for Information and Communication Technology.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,6,'Sophia is preparing a presentation for her Business Proposal in the Be your Own Boss Program. She needs to gather information, create a slide show, and practice her speech. She also needs to communicate with her classmates to collaborate on the project and search for relevant articles online. Sophia uses her laptop, tablet, and smartphone to manage all her tasks efficiently.','Sophia wants to create a presentation for her business proposal. Which device would be most effective for designing the slides of the presentation?','Tablet','Laptop','Smartphone','Desktop computer','B','A laptop is portable and powerful enough for creating and designing presentations using software like PowerPoint or Google Slides. While a desktop computer can also be used, it lacks portability. A smartphone and tablet can help with viewing or editing slides but are less efficient for full-scale design due to screen size and limited input features.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,7,'Sophia is preparing a presentation for her Business Proposal in the Be your Own Boss Program. She needs to gather information, create a slide show, and practice her speech. She also needs to communicate with her classmates to collaborate on the project and search for relevant articles online. Sophia uses her laptop, tablet, and smartphone to manage all her tasks efficiently.','Sophia is running late to meet a deadline and needs to quickly edit a document while traveling. Which device would be the most practical and efficient for her to use on the go?','Printer','Laptop','Desktop computer','Smartphone with access to cloud storage','D','While laptops are also effective, a smartphone with cloud access is the most practical for editing on the go due to its portability and instant connectivity. A desktop and printer are not mobile, making them less suitable for Sophia''s situation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,8,'Sophia is preparing a presentation for her Business Proposal in the Be your Own Boss Program. She needs to gather information, create a slide show, and practice her speech. She also needs to communicate with her classmates to collaborate on the project and search for relevant articles online. Sophia uses her laptop, tablet, and smartphone to manage all her tasks efficiently.','Sophia needs to look up a video tutorial on creating a presentation. Which device would be MOST IDEAL for watching and following the tutorial?','Tablet','Laptop','Smartphone','Smartwatch','B','A laptop provides a larger screen and full keyboard, making it easier for Sophia to watch the video tutorial and follow along with the steps as she creates the presentation. Smartphones and tablets can also be used but are less convenient for multitasking or typing. A smartwatch is not suitable for watching videos or creating presentations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,9,'Sophia is preparing a presentation for her Business Proposal in the Be your Own Boss Program. She needs to gather information, create a slide show, and practice her speech. She also needs to communicate with her classmates to collaborate on the project and search for relevant articles online. Sophia uses her laptop, tablet, and smartphone to manage all her tasks efficiently.','Which of the following combinations of devices would allow Sophia to efficiently communicate with her classmates while working on her project?','Using a tablet to send emails','Using a desktop computer to send emails','Using a smartphone to call her classmates','Using a laptop to send emails and a smartphone for instant messaging','D','The combination of a laptop for formal communication (emails) and a smartphone for quick messages (instant messaging) provides flexibility for communication.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,10,'Sophia is preparing a presentation for her Business Proposal in the Be your Own Boss Program. She needs to gather information, create a slide show, and practice her speech. She also needs to communicate with her classmates to collaborate on the project and search for relevant articles online. Sophia uses her laptop, tablet, and smartphone to manage all her tasks efficiently.','Sophia wants to organize her research into different categories. Which device would BEST help her categorize and store her research for easy access later?','Tablet','Laptop','Smartphone','Desktop computer','B','A laptop is best suited for organizing, categorizing, and storing research into folders, especially with its larger screen and file management tools.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,11,'Maria is setting up a new computer system for her schoolwork. She has a desktop computer, a keyboard, a mouse, and a wireless printer. Maria needs to understand how the parts of the computer and its peripherals work together to ensure she can use them efficiently.','Maria is having trouble with her monitor not displaying anything. Which of the following actions should she take first?','Unplug and replug the monitor''s power cable and check the connections','Check if the keyboard is properly connected','Restart the computer''s operating system','Check if the wireless printer is on','A','If the monitor is not displaying anything, checking the power cable and connection is the first step to ensure the issue is not related to the hardware setup.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,12,'Maria is setting up a new computer system for her schoolwork. She has a desktop computer, a keyboard, a mouse, and a wireless printer. Maria needs to understand how the parts of the computer and its peripherals work together to ensure she can use them efficiently.','What is the main advantage of using a wireless mouse over a wired mouse?','Wireless mice are more durable','Wireless mice don''t require batteries','Wireless mice provide more precise control','Wireless mice offer greater mobility and reduce cable clutter','D','A wireless mouse provides the convenience of mobility without the restriction of a cable, making it easier to move around.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,13,'Maria is setting up a new computer system for her schoolwork. She has a desktop computer, a keyboard, a mouse, and a wireless printer. Maria needs to understand how the parts of the computer and its peripherals work together to ensure she can use them efficiently.','What is the main job of the CPU (Central Processing Unit) in a computer?','To store files.','To input text.','To display images.','To process data and follow commands.','D','The CPU is like the "brain" of the computer. It processes information and carries out instructions to make the computer work properly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,14,'Maria is setting up a new computer system for her schoolwork. She has a desktop computer, a keyboard, a mouse, and a wireless printer. Maria needs to understand how the parts of the computer and its peripherals work together to ensure she can use them efficiently.','Maria is setting up her computer system and needs to choose between a wired and a wireless keyboard. What is a key consideration when deciding which one to choose?','Wired keyboards are generally less expensive and don’t require batteries','Wireless keyboards work better with desktop computers','Wired keyboards take up more space','Wireless keyboards are more precise','A','A wired keyboard does not require batteries and is often cheaper than a wireless one, making it a cost-effective option. However, the choice depends on Maria''s specific needs for mobility or portability.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,15,'John is tasked with choosing the best computing device for his different needs. He has three options: a laptop, a tablet, and a smartphone. Each device has its own features and functions, which John needs to evaluate to make an informed decision for his work and personal use.','If John needs a device to write long documents and create presentations for school, which device will best suit his needs?','Tablet','Laptop','Smartphone','Desktop computer','B','Laptops are versatile for writing documents and creating presentations due to their larger screens and full keyboard support, making them ideal for productive tasks.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,16,'John is tasked with choosing the best computing device for his different needs. He has three options: a laptop, a tablet, and a smartphone. Each device has its own features and functions, which John needs to evaluate to make an informed decision for his work and personal use.','Which device would be MOST suitable for doing schoolwork and typing reports?','Tablet','Laptop','Smartphone','Smartwatch','B','A laptop has a physical keyboard and larger screen, making it more suitable for school tasks and writing reports compared to a tablet or smartphone.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,17,'John is tasked with choosing the best computing device for his different needs. He has three options: a laptop, a tablet, and a smartphone. Each device has its own features and functions, which John needs to evaluate to make an informed decision for his work and personal use.','Which of the following is a limitation of using a smartphone for long-term work tasks like writing and presentations?','It is the most portable device','They are more expensive than laptops','Smartphones can’t access the internet','The screen size and keyboard may not be comfortable for long typing sessions','D','While smartphones are portable, the small screen size and on-screen keyboard can make long-term work tasks like writing and creating presentations less comfortable.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,18,'John is tasked with choosing the best computing device for his different needs. He has three options: a laptop, a tablet, and a smartphone. Each device has its own features and functions, which John needs to evaluate to make an informed decision for his work and personal use.','Which of the following computing devices is MOST practical for doing research while traveling?','Laptop','Smartwatch','Smartphone','Desktop computer','C','Among the options, a smartphone is the easiest to carry and allows mobile internet access, making it the best choice for research on the go.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,19,'John is tasked with choosing the best computing device for his different needs. He has three options: a laptop, a tablet, and a smartphone. Each device has its own features and functions, which John needs to evaluate to make an informed decision for his work and personal use.','Which device combines the features of a tablet and a laptop, giving John both a touch screen and a keyboard in one unit?','Smartphone','Smartwatch','Desktop computer','Convertible laptop','D','A convertible laptop can be used as a tablet with its touchscreen, and as a laptop with its physical keyboard.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,20,'Joshua is excited to use the family computer to work on his school project. Before starting, he remembers that his teacher taught them how to properly turn the computer on, open the program he needs, and shut it down after use. While using the computer, he also notices it''s getting slow and dusty.','Joshua notices that the computer is running slower than usual. What could be one solution?','Close unused programs and restart the computer','Keep using it without closing any programs','Let the computer run all night','Keep adding more games to it','A','Restarting and closing unused programs can free up system resources, improving speed',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,21,'Joshua is excited to use the family computer to work on his school project. Before starting, he remembers that his teacher taught them how to properly turn the computer on, open the program he needs, and shut it down after use. While using the computer, he also notices it''s getting slow and dusty.','Joshua hears strange sounds coming from the computer. What should he do FIRST to avoid causing further damage?','Ignore it and continue working','Open the computer and try to fix it himself','Tell his parents or teacher about the problem','Restart the computer to see if the issue resolves','C','It''s safest for Joshua to inform a responsible adult or teacher, especially if he’s unsure about the cause. This prevents further damage and ensures proper handling of the issue.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,22,'Joshua is excited to use the family computer to work on his school project. Before starting, he remembers that his teacher taught them how to properly turn the computer on, open the program he needs, and shut it down after use. While using the computer, he also notices it''s getting slow and dusty.','What should you do FIRST before using a computer?','Turn on the computer and make sure it''s properly booted','Start playing games immediately','Open all the programs at once','Eat a snack','A','Properly turning on and waiting for the computer to boot ensures it’s ready for use.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,23,'Joshua is excited to use the family computer to work on his school project. Before starting, he remembers that his teacher taught them how to properly turn the computer on, open the program he needs, and shut it down after use. While using the computer, he also notices it''s getting slow and dusty.','What is a safe and recommended way for Joshua to clean his computer?','Never clean the computer','Use harsh chemicals to clean the computer','Use a vacuum cleaner to suck dust from the keyboard','Use soft, dry or slightly damp cloth to clean the keyboard and screen','D','This method helps avoid damage to sensitive parts and ensures safety while cleaning the device.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,24,'Joshua is excited to use the family computer to work on his school project. Before starting, he remembers that his teacher taught them how to properly turn the computer on, open the program he needs, and shut it down after use. While using the computer, he also notices it''s getting slow and dusty.','Why is it important to shut down a computer properly instead of just turning off the power?','To save electricity','It doesn''t really matter','To make the computer look good','To make sure all files are saved, and the system is safely turned off','D','Properly shutting down ensures files are saved and the system is protected from damage.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,1,25,'Ana is organizing her project files on her computer, including essays, research papers, images, and videos. To make it easier to locate and manage her files, she decides to use the components of the computer''s file management system, such as folders to group related files, file names to describe the content of each file, file extensions to identify the type of file (e.g., document, image, video), and storage locations to specify where each file is saved. By understanding and using these components, Ana can efficiently organize and access her files, which will help her stay on top of her work and quickly retrieve documents when needed. This approach promotes Problem Solving, Information Literacy, and Critical Thinking skills.','Is the primary purpose of file names in a file management system?','To describe the content of a file and make it easily identifiable','To protect files from being accessed','To create backup copies of files','To store files by their type','A','File names help you quickly recognize the contents of a file, which is essential for organizing and retrieving files effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,26,'Ana is organizing her project files on her computer, including essays, research papers, images, and videos. To make it easier to locate and manage her files, she decides to use the components of the computer''s file management system, such as folders to group related files, file names to describe the content of each file, file extensions to identify the type of file (e.g., document, image, video), and storage locations to specify where each file is saved. By understanding and using these components, Ana can efficiently organize and access her files, which will help her stay on top of her work and quickly retrieve documents when needed. This approach promotes Problem Solving, Information Literacy, and Critical Thinking skills.','Why is it important to use meaningful file names when organizing documents and other files?','To make the computer run faster','To avoid accidental deletion of files','To ensure files are properly backed up','To help quickly identify and locate files','D','Meaningful file names make it easier to recognize what each file contains, which improves efficiency when retrieving files later.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,27,'Anna has multiple files on her computer for her school project, but they are disorganized and difficult to find. She decides to follow a structured process to manage her files effectively.','Which action should you avoid when managing files on your computer?','Backing up files regularly','Naming files based on their content','Organizing files into logical folders','Storing all files in the same folder without categorizing them','D','Storing all files in the same folder can make it difficult to locate specific files, causing disorganization and inefficiency.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,28,'Anna has multiple files on her computer for her school project, but they are disorganized and difficult to find. She decides to follow a structured process to manage her files effectively.','Why is it important to back up your files regularly?','To avoid losing important data in case of system failure or accidental deletion','To prevent files from becoming corrupted','To increase the speed of the computer','To free up space on the computer','A','Regular backups ensure that data is protected from loss due to system crashes or accidental file deletions.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,29,'Teacher Eliza tells her ALS elementary learners that computers have different programs for different tasks. For example, if they want to write a letter or story, they can use a word processor, while for making a slideshow, they can use presentation software, and for organizing numbers, they can use a spreadsheet.\n\nOne day, Teacher Eliza asks Juan to create a slideshow for a school project. He wonders which program to use for writing his report, making his slideshow, and organizing some information. Juan needs to know which software will help him with each part of his project.','Juan needs to create a slideshow for his school project. Which program should he use to make the slideshow?','Paint Program','Word Processor','Presentation Software','Spreadsheet Software','C','Presentation software is the best choice for creating a slideshow, as it is designed to allow users to add slides, text, images, and other elements that are needed for presentations.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,30,'Teacher Eliza tells her ALS elementary learners that computers have different programs for different tasks. For example, if they want to write a letter or story, they can use a word processor, while for making a slideshow, they can use presentation software, and for organizing numbers, they can use a spreadsheet.\n\nOne day, Teacher Eliza asks Juan to create a slideshow for a school project. He wonders which program to use for writing his report, making his slideshow, and organizing some information. Juan needs to know which software will help him with each part of his project.','Juan is trying to decide which program to use to write his report. Which software will be the best for writing his report?','Music Player','Word Processor','Spreadsheet Software','Presentation Software','B','Word processors are specifically designed for writing, formatting, and editing text, making them the best choice for writing reports.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,31,'Teacher Eliza tells her ALS elementary learners that computers have different programs for different tasks. For example, if they want to write a letter or story, they can use a word processor, while for making a slideshow, they can use presentation software, and for organizing numbers, they can use a spreadsheet.\n\nOne day, Teacher Eliza asks Juan to create a slideshow for a school project. He wonders which program to use for writing his report, making his slideshow, and organizing some information. Juan needs to know which software will help him with each part of his project.','Juan is organizing information for his project, and he needs to sort numbers in rows and columns. Which software should he use?','Photo Editor','Word Processor','Presentation Software','Spreadsheet Software','D','Spreadsheet software is designed to organize and manipulate data in rows and columns, making it the best choice for organizing numbers and data.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,32,'Teacher Eliza tells her ALS elementary learners that computers have different programs for different tasks. For example, if they want to write a letter or story, they can use a word processor, while for making a slideshow, they can use presentation software, and for organizing numbers, they can use a spreadsheet.\n\nOne day, Teacher Eliza asks Juan to create a slideshow for a school project. He wonders which program to use for writing his report, making his slideshow, and organizing some information. Juan needs to know which software will help him with each part of his project.','Juan wants to find accurate information about his project topic. What should he do to make sure he gets reliable information?','Ask his friends for information','Only use pictures without reading the text','Search for random websites on the internet','Use trusted websites, such as online encyclopedias or educational websites','D','Using trusted, reliable websites ensures that Juan gets accurate and credible information for his project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,33,'Mark needs to write a letter to his parents using the computer. Mark opens the word processing software, and at the top of the screen, he notices a row of words like "File," "Edit," and "View." These words are part of the menu bar, which helps him choose different options. For example, if he needs to save his work, he can click on "File." If he wants to change the letters to make them bold, he can click on "Home." Mark needs to understand what these parts do so he can finish his letter correctly.','Mark wants to save his letter after writing it. Which menu option should he click to do this?','Edit','File','Home','View','B','The "File" menu is used for tasks like saving, opening, or printing documents, which is what Mark needs to do after writing his letter.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,34,'Mark needs to write a letter to his parents using the computer. Mark opens the word processing software, and at the top of the screen, he notices a row of words like "File," "Edit," and "View." These words are part of the menu bar, which helps him choose different options. For example, if he needs to save his work, he can click on "File." If he wants to change the letters to make them bold, he can click on "Home." Mark needs to understand what these parts do so he can finish his letter correctly.','Where can Mark find the option to make the text of his letter bold?','Edit','File','Home','View','C','The "Home" tab contains options to format the text, like changing the font style to bold, which is what Mark wants to do.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,35,'Mark needs to write a letter to his parents using the computer. Mark opens the word processing software, and at the top of the screen, he notices a row of words like "File," "Edit," and "View." These words are part of the menu bar, which helps him choose different options. For example, if he needs to save his work, he can click on "File." If he wants to change the letters to make them bold, he can click on "Home." Mark needs to understand what these parts do so he can finish his letter correctly.','Why is it important for Mark to understand the function of the menu bar in the word processing software?','To make the computer faster','To play games on the computer','To change the color of the screen','To help him choose the correct options for writing and editing his letter','D','Understanding the menu bar helps Mark navigate the software and complete his task effectively, whether it''s saving, editing, or formatting his letter.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,36,'Mark needs to write a letter to his parents using the computer. Mark opens the word processing software, and at the top of the screen, he notices a row of words like "File," "Edit," and "View." These words are part of the menu bar, which helps him choose different options. For example, if he needs to save his work, he can click on "File." If he wants to change the letters to make them bold, he can click on "Home." Mark needs to understand what these parts do so he can finish his letter correctly.','After finishing his letter, which menu should Mark click to find the option to print it?','Edit','File','Home','View','B','The File menu contains options like Save, Print, Open, and Close, which are used for managing the entire document.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,37,'Juan creates a poster for the school''s upcoming sports day using the computer. Juan opens the desktop publishing software. At the top of the screen, there is a menu bar with words like "File," "Insert," and "Format." Juan notices that each word on the menu bar gives him different options. For example, the "File" menu lets him save or print the poster, the "Insert" menu helps him add pictures and text, and the "Format" menu allows him to change the style of the words. Juan needs to understand what each of these menu options does so he can use the right tool to make his poster look great.','What should Juan do if he wants to add a picture of a trophy to his poster?','Click on "File"','Click on "View"','Click on "Format"','Click on "Insert','D','The "Insert" menu allows Juan to add pictures, text, and other elements to his poster.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,38,'Juan creates a poster for the school''s upcoming sports day using the computer. Juan opens the desktop publishing software. At the top of the screen, there is a menu bar with words like "File," "Insert," and "Format." Juan notices that each word on the menu bar gives him different options. For example, the "File" menu lets him save or print the poster, the "Insert" menu helps him add pictures and text, and the "Format" menu allows him to change the style of the words. Juan needs to understand what each of these menu options does so he can use the right tool to make his poster look great.','If Juan wants to save his work so he can finish it later, what menu option should he choose?','Edit','File','Format','View','B','The "File" menu allows Juan to save, print, or open files. This is where he would go to save his poster.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,39,'Juan creates a poster for the school''s upcoming sports day using the computer. Juan opens the desktop publishing software. At the top of the screen, there is a menu bar with words like "File," "Insert," and "Format." Juan notices that each word on the menu bar gives him different options. For example, the "File" menu lets him save or print the poster, the "Insert" menu helps him add pictures and text, and the "Format" menu allows him to change the style of the words. Juan needs to understand what each of these menu options does so he can use the right tool to make his poster look great.','Juan wants to change the font of the title on his poster to make it stand out. Which menu option should he use?','File','Format','Insert','View','B','The "Format" menu allows Juan to change the appearance of text, such as changing the font, size, or style.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,40,'Juan creates a poster for the school''s upcoming sports day using the computer. Juan opens the desktop publishing software. At the top of the screen, there is a menu bar with words like "File," "Insert," and "Format." Juan notices that each word on the menu bar gives him different options. For example, the "File" menu lets him save or print the poster, the "Insert" menu helps him add pictures and text, and the "Format" menu allows him to change the style of the words. Juan needs to understand what each of these menu options does so he can use the right tool to make his poster look great.','Juan notices that the text on his poster is too small. What should he do to make the text bigger?','Click on "File"','Click on "View"','Click on "Insert"','Click on "Format" and choose "Font Size"','D','The "Format" menu allows Juan to adjust the font size to make the text bigger, which helps solve the problem of the text being too small.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,41,'Lino needs to create a fun poster about his favorite animal, but first, he needs to know how to find the right tools on the computer. This task will teach him how to use the different tabs in the menu bar to help him do his work more easily!','Lino needs to change the font size of the title on his poster to make it bigger and more eye-catching. Which tab should Lino use to solve this problem?','File','Format','Insert','View','B','The Format tab is where Lino can change the appearance of the text, including adjusting the font size, color, and style. This is the best tab to solve the problem of making the title more eye-catching.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,42,'Lino needs to create a fun poster about his favorite animal, but first, he needs to know how to find the right tools on the computer. This task will teach him how to use the different tabs in the menu bar to help him do his work more easily!','Lino is not sure how to insert a picture of his favorite animal into his poster. Which tab in the menu bar will help him find the option to insert the picture?','Edit','Insert','Help','View','B','The Insert tab is where you can add elements like pictures, shapes, and tables to your document. To insert a picture of his favorite animal, Lino should use the Insert tab, which provides all the tools for adding visual content to the poster.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,43,'Lino needs to create a fun poster about his favorite animal, but first, he needs to know how to find the right tools on the computer. This task will teach him how to use the different tabs in the menu bar to help him do his work more easily!','Lino has added a picture of his favorite animal to his poster but feels it’s too large. He needs to resize it, so it fits better. Which option will help Lino solve this issue?','Use the View tab to zoom out.','Use the Insert tab to resize the picture.','Use the Format tab to adjust the picture''s size.','Use the Edit tab to undo the insertion of the picture.','C','The Format tab allows you to adjust the size of images, text, and other elements in your document. This would enable Lino to resize the picture of his favorite animal to better fit his poster. The View tab is for changing how the document is displayed, but it doesn''t affect the actual size of objects in the document.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,44,'Lino needs to create a fun poster about his favorite animal, but first, he needs to know how to find the right tools on the computer. This task will teach him how to use the different tabs in the menu bar to help him do his work more easily!','Lino wants to change the color and size of the text in his poster title to make it more attractive. Which tab should he click to find options for font styles, size, and color?','File','View','Insert','Home','D','The "Home" tab contains tools for formatting text, such as changing the font size, style, and color. Since Lino wants to make the title more attractive, he needs these formatting options, which are found under the Home tab.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,45,'Liza has been asked to help organize a school event. She needs to create a budget to make sure the event stays within the school''s allowance. To do this, she decided to use spreadsheet software like Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets. This is where she will list all the things the event will need and how much they will cost.','Liza is making a list of items and their costs for the school event. She wants to find out the total cost without adding the numbers one by one. What should she do to solve this problem quickly?','Guess the total cost','Ask a teacher to add the numbers for her','Write down the numbers on a piece of paper','Use the SUM formula in the spreadsheet to add the costs together','D','The SUM formula helps Liza easily add up the costs in the spreadsheet. It’s much faster than doing it by hand, and it makes sure the total is accurate.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,46,'Liza has been asked to help organize a school event. She needs to create a budget to make sure the event stays within the school''s allowance. To do this, she decided to use spreadsheet software like Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets. This is where she will list all the things the event will need and how much they will cost.','Liza is putting together a list of things she needs for the school event. What is the best way to organize the information in the spreadsheet to keep it clear and easy to understand?','Write the information in random places','Put all the items and prices in one column','Write everything in one big box without spaces','Use one column for the names of the items, one for the quantity, and one for the cost','D','By organizing the information into different columns (one for names, one for quantity, one for cost), Liza can see everything clearly. It helps her understand the information more easily and makes changes when needed.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,47,'Liza has been asked to help organize a school event. She needs to create a budget to make sure the event stays within the school''s allowance. To do this, she decided to use spreadsheet software like Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets. This is where she will list all the things the event will need and how much they will cost.','Liza sees that one of the items on her list is very expensive, and it will make her budget go over the top. What should she do to fix this problem?','Tell the teacher to pay for the item','Leave the item and ignore the budget','Buy extra items without worrying about the cost','Find a cheaper version of the item or remove some items from the list to save money','D','Critical thinking helps Liza make smart choices. Instead of just buying the expensive item, she can think of ways to stay within her budget, such as finding a cheaper version or removing unnecessary items.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,48,'Jayson is an elementary learner who loves learning new things. One day, his teacher explains that the internet is a powerful tool that can help him find information, talk to friends, and even learn new skills. Jayson is excited to know more, so his teacher guides him on how to use the internet safely and understand its key features.','Jayson wants to find out how to make a paper airplane. What should he do to find the best instructions on the internet?','Wait for a friend to show him','Ask his teacher to show him how to make one','Guess how to make the paper airplane without any help','Search for "How to make a paper airplane" on a search engine','D','By searching for instructions online, Jayson can quickly find helpful guides and videos that will show him exactly how to make a paper airplane. This is an efficient way to solve the problem.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,49,'Jayson is an elementary learner who loves learning new things. One day, his teacher explains that the internet is a powerful tool that can help him find information, talk to friends, and even learn new skills. Jayson is excited to know more, so his teacher guides him on how to use the internet safely and understand its key features.','Jayson is looking for information on elephants. Which of the following should he do to find reliable and useful information?','Only trust the first website he finds','Ask his friends to tell him about elephants','Read the first link that appears, no matter what it says','Check multiple sources and read carefully to make sure the information is correct','D','To make sure the information is accurate, Jayson should check different websites or sources, compare them, and read carefully to get the most reliable information. This helps develop good information literacy skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,2,50,'Jayson is an elementary learner who loves learning new things. One day, his teacher explains that the internet is a powerful tool that can help him find information, talk to friends, and even learn new skills. Jayson is excited to know more, so his teacher guides him on how to use the internet safely and understand its key features.','Jayson found two websites that explain how to stay safe on the internet. One website says it''s okay to share your name and address online, and the other says you should never share personal information. What should Jayson do?','Compare both websites and ask a trusted adult for advice','Choose a website that looks more colorful and fun','Share his name and address only on websites that are easy to understand','Follow the website that explains internet safety and warns against sharing personal information','D','Jayson should choose the website that gives safe and correct advice. Sharing personal information online can be dangerous. It’s important to follow trusted sources that promote internet safety.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,51,'Loreto is an elementary learner who is excited about finishing his school project on endangered animals. He has written a report and created a poster using a computer. His teacher tells the class that they will submit their projects online. Jayson is a bit unsure about how to upload and download files, but his teacher explains the process step by step.','Loreto wants to upload his project file, but he can’t find it on the computer. What should he do first?','Restart the computer and try again','Create a new project from the beginning','Ask his friend to upload a different file for him','Check the folder where he saved his project file','D','To solve the problem, Jayson should first look in the folder where he saved the file. This helps him find the project without wasting time or effort.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,52,'Loreto is an elementary learner who is excited about finishing his school project on endangered animals. He has written a report and created a poster using a computer. His teacher tells the class that they will submit their projects online. Jayson is a bit unsure about how to upload and download files, but his teacher explains the process step by step.','When Loreto downloads his classmate Maria’s project, how can he make sure it is the correct file?','Save it anywhere without checking it','Ask someone else to check and submit it','Download it and open it later without reading','Check the file name and open the file to confirm its content','D','Reading the file name and checking the content helps ensure Loreto downloaded the right file. This promotes responsible digital behavior and avoids errors.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,53,'Loreto is an elementary learner who is excited about finishing his school project on endangered animals. He has written a report and created a poster using a computer. His teacher tells the class that they will submit their projects online. Jayson is a bit unsure about how to upload and download files, but his teacher explains the process step by step.','Loreto sees two download links online. One is from his teacher’s school platform, and the other is from an unknown website. What should he do?','Click both links to test which one works','Choose the link from the teacher’s school platform','Skip downloading and ask someone else to finish his work','Download from the unknown site because it looks more attractive','B','Loreto should only trust official and secure sources like his teacher’s school platform to avoid downloading harmful or incorrect files.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,54,'Loreto is an elementary learner who is excited about finishing his school project on endangered animals. He has written a report and created a poster using a computer. His teacher tells the class that they will submit their projects online. Jayson is a bit unsure about how to upload and download files, but his teacher explains the process step by step.','After uploading his project, Jayson notices a message saying, “Upload Failed.” What should he do to make sure his project is properly submitted?','Close the computer right away and play games','Wait until the next day and hope it works on its own','Ignore the message and assume the teacher received it','Try uploading the file again and check if the message changes to “Upload Complete”','D','Critical thinking helps Jayson make smart choices. Instead of ignoring the error, he should act and ensure the upload is successful by checking the system message.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,55,'Ramon is an ALS elementary learner who is preparing for their learning session the next day. He wants to review his lessons on Learning Strand (LS) 2 and Learning Strand (LS) 3. To do this, Ramon looks at different tools and materials: he opens his printed module, watches a Learning Strand (LS) 2 video on YouTube, and asks his teacher a question through Messenger. Later, his teacher invites him to join a Google Meet for a group review.','Ramon cannot open the video on YouTube due to a slow internet connection. What should he do next?','Stop reviewing and just play games instead','Message a classmate to do the review for him','Wait until the next day and forget about the video','Use his printed module to review the lesson instead','D','Problem-solving involves finding another way to continue learning. Using the printed module is a smart solution when internet problems arise.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,56,'Ramon is an ALS elementary learner who is preparing for their learning session the next day. He wants to review his lessons on Learning Strand (LS) 2 and Learning Strand (LS) 3. To do this, Ramon looks at different tools and materials: he opens his printed module, watches a Learning Strand (LS) 2 video on YouTube, and asks his teacher a question through Messenger. Later, his teacher invites him to join a Google Meet for a group review.','Which of the following is an educational resource Ramon used to help him review?','His teacher','Google Meet','YouTube LS2 video','Facebook Messenger','C','Educational resources are materials that help learners understand lessons. The YouTube LS2 video contains content for Ramon to study.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,57,'Ramon is an ALS elementary learner who is preparing for their learning session the next day. He wants to review his lessons on Learning Strand (LS) 2 and Learning Strand (LS) 3. To do this, Ramon looks at different tools and materials: he opens his printed module, watches a Learning Strand (LS) 2 video on YouTube, and asks his teacher a question through Messenger. Later, his teacher invites him to join a Google Meet for a group review.','Why is it better for Ramon to use different tools and materials for his review?','Because it’s required by his teacher','So, he doesn’t get bored of just one tool','Because his classmates are doing the same','Because each tool and resource have a specific use and benefit','D','Critical thinking means understanding the purpose of each tool. Using a mix of communication tools and learning resources helps Ramon learn more effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,58,'Ramon is an ALS elementary learner who is preparing for their learning session the next day. He wants to review his lessons on Learning Strand (LS) 2 and Learning Strand (LS) 3. To do this, Ramon looks at different tools and materials: he opens his printed module, watches a Learning Strand (LS) 2 video on YouTube, and asks his teacher a question through Messenger. Later, his teacher invites him to join a Google Meet for a group review.','Ramon wants to make sure the video he found on YouTube is useful for reviewing LS2. What should he check first?','If the video has music and funny parts','How many people have watched the video','The number of likes and comments on the video','If the video is related to the lesson and explained clearly','D','Information literacy involves knowing how to find and evaluate good learning materials. Ramon should first check if the video matches the topic and helps him understand LS2.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,59,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up said: "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!". Her classmate Sonia asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Mary Grace saw a message that said, "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!" What should she do to stay safe?','Share the message with her classmates','Ignore the message and close the website','Restart the computer to make the message go away','Enter her email and password quickly to get the prize','B','Messages like that are often fake and can be scams. It''s safer to ignore and close them instead of giving personal information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,60,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up said: "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!". Her classmate Sonia asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','Sonia, Mary Grace’s classmate, asks for her email and password to help with school files. What is the best action for Mary Grace to take?','Tell Sonia to send the files instead','Change her password after sharing it','Say no and ask the teacher if sharing passwords is safe','Share her email and password because Sonia is her classmate','C','Mary Grace needs to think carefully about trust and privacy online. Even if Sonia is a friend, passwords should never be shared. By asking the teacher, Mary Grace shows responsible digital behavior and critical thinking, she questions the situation and looks for a trusted adult’s help before acting.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,61,'Mary Grace used a library computer to search for information for her ALS project. A pop-up said: "You won a prize! Enter your email and password!". Her classmate Sonia asked for her email and password to open school files. Something started downloading from a site without her clicking anything.','While searching a website, Mary Grace notices something started downloading without her clicking anything. What type of risk is this and what should she do?','Ignore it and continue using the website','It’s a fun surprise, so she should open the file','Share the file with her classmates to check what it is','It’s probably a virus or malware; she should delete the file and report it','D','Mary Grace saw a file downloading on her device without her permission. This could be a virus or something harmful. Being smart online means knowing what is safe or not. She should delete the file and tell her teacher or a trusted adult to help keep the device safe.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,62,NULL,'Stephen Ace feels tired and sleepy during the day because he stays up late using his cellphone. What is the best way to solve this problem so he can stay healthy?','Play games until midnight, then sleep after','Use the cellphone all day and take vitamins','Turn off the tablet only when the battery runs out','Set a specific time to stop using the tablet every night','D','Creating a routine or screen time schedule helps Stephen manage his tablet use and avoid staying up too late, supporting his digital health and overall well-being.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,63,NULL,'Stephen Ace receives messages from people he doesn''t know. What should he do to stay safe online?','Reply and ask who they are','Give them his personal information','Ignore the message and tell a trusted adult','Accept friend requests from everyone','C','This is a key step in online safety. Ignoring strangers and informing a parent or teacher helps prevent online dangers like scams, cyberbullying, or inappropriate contact.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,64,NULL,'Stephen Ace uses his tablet to learn and play games. What is the best way for him to balance learning and playing?','Only use the tablet for games','Stop using the tablet completely','Play games all day and study at night','Make a schedule with time for learning, games, and rest','D','This helps Stephen Ace manage his time wisely, focus on learning first, enjoy games for a short time, and take care of his eyes and health.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,65,NULL,'Stephen wants to know if the apps he is using are safe. What should he do before downloading or using any new app?','Download any app that looks fun','Try it first without asking anyone','Share the app with friends immediately','Check reviews and ask an adult before installing','D','This promotes information literacy. Verifying apps through reviews and getting help from a trusted adult helps ensure they are safe, reliable, and appropriate.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,66,'Ana wants to explain the steps involved in turning off a computer properly.\n\nShe lists these steps:\n\nI. Save all work II. Close all applications III. Click the Start button IV. Select "Shut Down" V. Wait until the computer powers off','Which type of flowchart should Ana use to best present this sequence of actions?','Cycle flowchart','Data flowchart','Decision flowchart','Process flowchart','D','A process flowchart is best for showing a step-by-step sequence of actions or operations. Since Ana''s task is a linear sequence of how to shut down a computer, a process flowchart clearly represents each step in the order it happens.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,67,'You are given a flowchart that starts with a question: "Is there an internet connection?"\n\nIf YES → "Open browser"\n\nIf NO → "Check Wi-Fi settings" → "Try again"','Which kind of flowchart is this?','It shows how data moves','It shows steps in order','It shows a decision and actions','It shows who is in charge','C','The flowchart begins with a question (“Is there an internet connection?”), which is a decision point. Depending on the answer (Yes or No), the flowchart shows different actions (like “Open browser” or “Check Wi-Fi settings”). This makes it a decision flowchart, which is used to show different paths based on choices.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,68,'While searching online, Jun sees a flowchart with symbols he doesn’t understand. He wants to find out what the shapes (like ovals, rectangles, and diamonds) mean in flowcharts.','What should Jun do to find accurate and reliable information?','Look at images only, without reading the content','Guess the meaning based on how the shapes look','Ask his classmate who might remember the symbols','Search “flowchart symbols and their meanings” from trusted educational websites','D','This tests information literacy — the ability to find and evaluate useful information. Choosing reliable sources (like educational websites) ensures Jun gets accurate explanations of flowchart symbols rather than relying on guesses or incomplete information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,69,'Gracia is an ALS student who loves learning how to use her tablet. One day, her teacher asks her to follow a simple set of instructions to help her organize her files. The teacher gives her a predefined algorithm to follow: Step 1: Open the “Documents” folder. Step 2: Create a new folder named "School Projects." Step 3: Move all the files related to her school project into that folder. Step 4: Close the folder when she’s done.\n\nGracia thinks this is easy! She follows the instructions step-by-step, and everything works out perfectly. She can now find all her school project files in one place. This simple set of instructions is called a basic algorithm.','Why should Gracia follow the steps exactly when organizing her files?','So, she can finish faster','So, her tablet looks colorful','So, she can use more storage','So, her files will be neat and easy to find','D','Following the steps carefully helps Gracia keep her files organized, making it easier to find and use them when needed.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,70,'Gracia is an ALS student who loves learning how to use her tablet. One day, her teacher asks her to follow a simple set of instructions to help her organize her files. The teacher gives her a predefined algorithm to follow: Step 1: Open the “Documents” folder. Step 2: Create a new folder named "School Projects." Step 3: Move all the files related to her school project into that folder. Step 4: Close the folder when she’s done.\n\nGracia thinks this is easy! She follows the instructions step-by-step, and everything works out perfectly. She can now find all her school project files in one place. This simple set of instructions is called a basic algorithm.','Gracia moved the wrong files into the "School Projects" folder by mistake. What should she do to fix it?','Turn off the tablet and turn it on again','Delete the whole folder and start again','Leave the files there and find them later','Use “Undo” or move the files to the right folder','D','This is the best way to fix the mistake without losing any files. It teaches problem-solving and organizing skills.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,71,NULL,'What could Gracia do to ensure she doesn''t lose important school project files in the future?','Share the files with all her friends.','Delete the files after finishing her project.','Save all files to her tablet without organizing them.','Create a backup of the files on a cloud storage service or external storage device.','D','Backing up files to a cloud storage service or external device ensures they are safe in case of data loss. This practice protects important files and provides a way to access them from different devices. Saving files without organizing them or deleting them after use would increase the risk of losing important data.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,72,'Jade is an ALS Learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project. Block coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip). Jade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Why is it important for Jade to use the correct blocks in the right order when designing her interactive media project?','To make the project easier to create','To follow the teacher’s instructions strictly','To make the project look more complex and colorful','To ensure the project works smoothly and communicates the digital safety tips effectively','D','Using the correct blocks in the right order ensures that each action in the project (moving, showing messages, playing sounds) occurs at the right time, making the project functional and able to communicate the intended message clearly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,73,'Jade is an ALS Learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project. Block coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip). Jade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade used the motion block, sound block, and looks block in her project. If Jade''s character does not move when she clicks the start button, what should she check first?','The message block''s text','The type of sound block used','The speed of the sound block','The connection of the motion block to the start button','D','The motion block needs to be properly connected to the start button to trigger the character''s movement. If the character isn''t moving, the connection of the motion block is the most likely cause of the issue.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,74,'Jade is an ALS Learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project. Block coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip). Jade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','If Jade wants to add more digital safety tips to her project, but the screen becomes cluttered and hard to read, what should she do to improve the user experience?','Use fewer blocks in the project','Make the character move faster','Reduce the font size of the messages','Add a pause between each tip to give users more time to read','D','Adding a pause between each tip will allow users enough time to read the message before the next one appears, improving clarity and the user experience without making the screen feel cluttered.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',2,3,75,'Jade is an ALS Learner who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project. Block coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip). Jade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade is using block coding to create a project that shows tips about staying safe online. She wants her character to say messages like “Don’t share your password” on the screen. Which type of block should she use to show these messages?','Motion block – to make the character move','Control block – to repeat or wait','Looks block – to show text or change how the character looks','Sound block – to play music or effects','C','The looks block is used to display messages or change the appearance of objects, which is why Jade uses it to show the digital safety tips on the screen.',NULL,0,1);
INSERT INTO items (grade,strand,level,activity,num,passage,question,opt_a,opt_b,opt_c,opt_d,answer,explanation,image,image_only,active) VALUES
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,1,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','If your computer is running slowly, which of the following maintenance tasks could help improve performance?','Cleaning the computer with water','Updating the computer and deleting unnecessary files','Opening the computer case and touching the motherboard','Shutting the computer down without performing any maintenance','B','Updating software ensures the system runs on the latest version, and deleting unnecessary files helps free up space, improving performance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,2,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','What is the first thing you should do before performing maintenance on your computer?','Clean the screen','Update the software','Open the computer case','Safely shut down the computer','D','It is important to shut down the computer to avoid data loss and prevent damage to hardware when performing maintenance.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,3,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','Which action is dangerous and should be avoided when performing computer maintenance?','Updating the software regularly','Turning off the computer before maintenance','Cleaning the screen with a dry microfiber cloth','Opening the computer case without using safety precautions','D','Opening the computer case without proper precautions (such as grounding yourself) can lead to electrical shock or static damage.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,4,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','What should Juan do if he saved the file in the wrong folder?','Ignore it','Delete it','Rename it with symbols','Move it to the correct folder','D','Moving the file keeps your computer organized and makes it easier to find later.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,5,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','You are saving multiple school documents on your computer. What is the best way to name your files so you can quickly find and open the correct one later?','Use random letters or numbers to make file names shorter','Name your files with your favorite word to remember them easily','Give every file a similar name, so they appear next to each other','Use specific and descriptive names that show what each file is about','D','Descriptive filenames help you quickly identify the file’s content without needing to open it. This is the best practice in digital organization.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,6,'Juan is using his computer to complete an assignment when he notices that the system is running slowly. He remembers that regular maintenance, like cleaning the system and updating software, helps keep the computer in good working condition. However, he also knows he needs to be careful when performing these tasks to avoid damaging the computer or causing any safety hazards.','If you are organizing files for a group project, what is the best approach to ensure that everyone can access the necessary files?','Keep files on your computer and don’t share them','Have each person organize their own files without a common structure','Send files individually to group members every time they ask for them','Share the entire folder structure with the group and ensure all files are organized by category','D','Sharing a well-organized folder structure helps the whole group access and work with files efficiently, reducing confusion.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,7,'Liza is working on her school project. She opens a word document and uses the menu bar to make her title bold and change the text size. Liza learns that the menu bar tools help her make her report look better and easier to read.','Liza is working on her school project. She wants her title to be easy to see and different from the rest of the text. Which is the best way for her to do this using the menu bar tools?','Change the text color to blue','Add more paragraphs under the title','Insert a picture at the top of the page','Make the title bold and increase the text size','D','Making the title bold and increasing its size helps it stand out clearly, which improves the readability and appearance of the report.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,8,'Liza is working on her school project. She opens a word document and uses the menu bar to make her title bold and change the text size. Liza learns that the menu bar tools help her make her report look better and easier to read.','How can Liza use the menu bar to improve the readability of her report?','Insert a chart.','Add a table of contents.','Change the background color.','Adjust the text size and font style.','D','Changing the text size and font style will make the report easier to read by creating a clear and readable format.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,9,'Liza is working on her school project. She opens a word document and uses the menu bar to make her title bold and change the text size. Liza learns that the menu bar tools help her make her report look better and easier to read.','Why is it important for Liza to use the menu bar to make her title bold and change the text size?','It makes the report look colorful.','It allows her to finish her report quickly.','It helps her organize the report into sections.','It improves the presentation and makes important parts of the report easier to notice.','D','Using the menu bar tools to adjust text formatting helps to emphasize important parts, making the report clearer and more professional.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,10,'Dave has been given the task of creating a poster for the district festival of talent using the computer. He needs to use the tools in the menu bar to make his poster look great. Dave wants to add a picture of the event, he uses the "Insert" tool. When he wants to change the colors and style of the text, he uses the "Design" tool. Dave will apply these tools to make sure his poster is colorful and looks nice for the talent show.','Dave is making a poster for the talent show. He wants the text to be bigger so that people can read it easily. What should he do to use the menu bar?','Use the "File" tool to save the poster','Use the "Print" tool to make a copy','Use the "Insert" tool to add pictures','Use the "Design" tool to change text size and style','D','The Design tool lets Dave change how the text looks, including the size and style, which makes the poster more readable and attractive',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,11,'Dave has been given the task of creating a poster for the district festival of talent using the computer. He needs to use the tools in the menu bar to make his poster look great. Dave wants to add a picture of the event, he uses the "Insert" tool. When he wants to change the colors and style of the text, he uses the "Design" tool. Dave will apply these tools to make sure his poster is colorful and looks nice for the talent show.','Which tool should Dave use to add a picture to his poster for the district festival?','Format','Insert','Home','View','B','The "Insert" tool is used to add pictures, charts, and other media to the poster, which is essential for including the event picture.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,12,'Dave has been given the task of creating a poster for the district festival of talent using the computer. He needs to use the tools in the menu bar to make his poster look great. Dave wants to add a picture of the event, he uses the "Insert" tool. When he wants to change the colors and style of the text, he uses the "Design" tool. Dave will apply these tools to make sure his poster is colorful and looks nice for the talent show.','Dave wants people to notice and enjoy reading his poster. Why should he use the "Design" tool to change the text style and colors?','To save his work faster','To write longer sentences','To make the computer run more smoothly','To make the poster look attractive and easy to read','D','The Design tool helps Dave improve the appearance of the poster, making it colorful, neat, and easy to understand, which is important for catching people’s attention.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,13,'John is working on a project and needs to make a slideshow on the computer. He opens the presentation software and adds a title slide. To change the title, he uses the "Design" tool to make the text bigger and change the color. When he wants to add a picture, he uses the "Insert" tool. John learns to use these tools to make his slideshow look nice.','What should John do first if he wants to add a picture to his slideshow?','Use the "Insert" tool','Use the "Design" tool','Change the text color','Close the presentation software','A','The "Insert" tool is used to add images or other elements to a slideshow',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,14,'John is working on a project and needs to make a slideshow on the computer. He opens the presentation software and adds a title slide. To change the title, he uses the "Design" tool to make the text bigger and change the color. When he wants to add a picture, he uses the "Insert" tool. John learns to use these tools to make his slideshow look nice.','Why did John use the "Design" tool in his slideshow?','To add a new slide','To delete the title slide','To add pictures to the slide','To make the text bigger and change its color','D','The "Design" tool helps to adjust the style and formatting of text, such as changing its size and color.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,15,'John is working on a project and needs to make a slideshow on the computer. He opens the presentation software and adds a title slide. To change the title, he uses the "Design" tool to make the text bigger and change the color. When he wants to add a picture, he uses the "Insert" tool. John learns to use these tools to make his slideshow look nice.','If John needs to make his slideshow look more professional, what else could he do use the "Design" tool?','Add more slides','Delete the title text','Increase the size of the images','Change the background color or use a pre-made template','D','The "Design" tool allows John to enhance the look of his slideshow by changing the background color or applying a template, making it more professional.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,16,'Jonas is helping her teacher with the class quiz scores. He types the students'' names and their scores into the computer. To find out the total score, Jonas uses the sum tool in the spreadsheet. Then, he uses another tool to find the average score. Jonas learns how to use these tools to organize and calculate the scores.','Jonas is using the sum tool to find the total score of the class. What should Jonas do if he accidentally includes an extra row with no score?','Ignore the extra row','Add the extra row manually','Change the extra row to a score of 0','Delete the extra row to get the correct total','D','To solve the problem of including an extra row with no score, Jonas should delete the extra row. This ensures the sum calculation is accurate and reflects only the valid scores.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,17,'Jonas is helping her teacher with the class quiz scores. He types the students'' names and their scores into the computer. To find out the total score, Jonas uses the sum tool in the spreadsheet. Then, he uses another tool to find the average score. Jonas learns how to use these tools to organize and calculate the scores.','Jonas is using a spreadsheet to help compute the class quiz scores. What does the SUM tool help him do?','Add all the quiz scores together','Find the average score of the class','Count how many students took the quiz','Arrange the scores from highest to lowest','A','The SUM tool adds all the numbers in a group of cells. Jonas uses it to get the total of the quiz scores.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,18,'Jonas is helping her teacher with the class quiz scores. He types the students'' names and their scores into the computer. To find out the total score, Jonas uses the sum tool in the spreadsheet. Then, he uses another tool to find the average score. Jonas learns how to use these tools to organize and calculate the scores.','Jonas uses the average tool to calculate the average quiz score. Why is it important to calculate the average score?','To find the highest score','To sort the scores from lowest to highest','To know how many students scored below 50%','To get a general idea of the overall class performance','D','The average score gives a general overview of the class''s performance. It helps Jonas and the teacher understand how the class did, rather than focusing on individual scores.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,19,'Teacher Ella asks Kurt to find information for her project about animals. Kurt uses the internet to search for websites and pictures. He also asks his classmates online if they find anything helpful. Kurt uses the information to finish his project and share it with the class.','What should Kurt do first to find the information needed for his project?','Ask his teacher for the answers.','Wait until his classmates finish their projects.','Start writing the project without gathering information.','Search the internet for websites and pictures related to animals.','D','Kurt needs to gather information first by searching the internet to ensure his project is accurate and well-informed',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,20,'Teacher Ella asks Kurt to find information for her project about animals. Kurt uses the internet to search for websites and pictures. He also asks his classmates online if they find anything helpful. Kurt uses the information to finish his project and share it with the class.','Which of the following is an important skill Kurt is using when he asks his classmates for help?','Ignoring other people''s ideas.','Avoiding the use of technology.','Completing the project without any help.','Collaborating and gathering information from different sources.','D','Kurt is using information literacy by seeking help from others, which allows him to gather more information and enrich his project.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,21,'Teacher Ella asks Kurt to find information for her project about animals. Kurt uses the internet to search for websites and pictures. He also asks his classmates online if they find anything helpful. Kurt uses the information to finish his project and share it with the class.','How can Kurt ensure the information he finds online is reliable for his project?','Only look at pictures and ignore the text.','Copy and paste everything from websites without checking.','Use any website that looks interesting, regardless of the source.','Check if the website is trustworthy and provides accurate facts about animals.','D','Kurt should critically assess the quality and trustworthiness of the sources to ensure his project is based on accurate information.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,22,'In Mr. Reymart''s class, learners are tasked with creating a poster for the upcoming sportsfest. He introduces the topic of document processing and explains the importance of using templates and illustrations to design professional-looking posters.','Which of the following steps would be the best first action for Mr. Reymart to take when designing the poster?','Only use text with no images or design elements.','Skip the template and create a new design from scratch.','Immediately start adding text and images without any design plan.','Choose a template that fits the sports fest theme and then customize it.','D','Choosing a template that fits the theme of the event first helps learners save time and focus on customizing the poster effectively, making it easier to organize and design the poster. This involves problem-solving by choosing the best approach to start the task.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,23,'In Mr. Reymart''s class, learners are tasked with creating a poster for the upcoming sportsfest. He introduces the topic of document processing and explains the importance of using templates and illustrations to design professional-looking posters.','Which of the following is the most important factor to consider when selecting illustrations for a sports fest poster?','The size of the illustrations','The price of the illustrations','The number of illustrations used in the poster','Whether the illustrations match the theme of the sports fest','D','Information literacy involves gathering and selecting relevant information. When creating a poster, selecting illustrations that match the sportsfest theme ensures the poster is clear and effective in conveying the message. Learners need to understand how to choose appropriate images for their design.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,24,'In Mr. Reymart''s class, learners are tasked with creating a poster for the upcoming sportsfest. He introduces the topic of document processing and explains the importance of using templates and illustrations to design professional-looking posters.','In Mr. Reymart''s class, learners create posters for the sports fest. He explains how using a template can help in designing. What is one main benefit of using a template when starting a poster design?','It replaces the need to add your own content','It limits your design choices to only one format','It automatically makes the poster more creative','It gives you a ready layout that you can customize','D','Templates help by giving you a starting layout for your design. You can still change the colors, text, and pictures to make it fit your event.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,1,25,'Learners are given the task of designing a welcome banner for the new students at their school. Mr. Bahian introduces the concept of document processing and explains how to use templates and illustrations to make the banner look welcoming and professional.','What should be the first step to make the banner look welcoming and professional?','Use only one color and type of illustration for the banner.','Immediately add as many pictures as possible to the banner.','Skip the template and create a design from scratch without any layout.','Start by choosing a template that fits the theme of the welcome banner.','D','The first step in designing the banner is to choose a template that fits the theme. Templates provide a good structure for learners to start their design, saving time and ensuring that the layout is organized and professional.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,26,'Learners are given the task of designing a welcome banner for the new students at their school. Mr. Bahian introduces the concept of document processing and explains how to use templates and illustrations to make the banner look welcoming and professional.','When selecting illustrations for the welcome banner, what is the most important factor to consider?','Whether the illustrations are colorful and bold.','How many illustrations are used in the banner.','Only using one type of illustration in the design.','Whether the illustrations match the theme of the banner and are appropriate for the occasion.','D','Information literacy involves selecting relevant and appropriate content. Choosing illustrations that match the theme (in this case, a welcoming design) helps make the banner more meaningful and appropriate for the event.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,27,'Learners are given the task of designing a welcome banner for the new students at their school. Mr. Bahian introduces the concept of document processing and explains how to use templates and illustrations to make the banner look welcoming and professional.','Why is it important to use templates and illustrations in the design of the welcome banner?','They make the banner look the same as others.','They make the design process faster and more organized.','Templates and illustrations are not important and should be avoided.','Templates and illustrations are only useful for adding text to the banner.','B','Critical thinking involves understanding why certain tools or methods are useful. Templates and illustrations help organize the design process, making it easier to create a professional-looking banner without starting from scratch.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,28,'ALS Learners of Libertad District are tasked with creating a presentation for the upcoming Portfolio Assessment. Mrs. Abecia explains how to use presentation software and highlights the difference between templates and illustrations to help learners create an engaging and colorful presentation.','When designing a presentation for the portfolio assessment, what is the first thing ALS learners should do to create an organized slide?','Add as many pictures as possible.','Write long paragraphs of text on each slide.','Skip the design step and focus only on the text.','Choose a template that fits the theme of the presentation.','D','Choosing a template first helps organize the layout and structure of the presentation. Templates provide a clean and organized foundation, allowing learners to focus on adding content and adjusting as needed.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,29,'ALS Learners of Libertad District are tasked with creating a presentation for the upcoming Portfolio Assessment. Mrs. Abecia explains how to use presentation software and highlights the difference between templates and illustrations to help learners create an engaging and colorful presentation.','What is the most important factor when selecting illustrations for a portfolio presentation?','Selecting illustrations that are the largest in size.','Choosing illustrations with bright, bold colors only.','Using illustrations on every slide, whether needed or not.','Picking illustrations that are relevant to the content of the slides.','D','Information literacy involves evaluating and selecting appropriate content. Illustrations should complement and enhance the content of the presentation, making it more meaningful and engaging for the audience.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,30,'ALS Learners of Libertad District are tasked with creating a presentation for the upcoming Portfolio Assessment. Mrs. Abecia explains how to use presentation software and highlights the difference between templates and illustrations to help learners create an engaging and colorful presentation.','Why is it important to use both templates and illustrations when creating a presentation?','They are not important and can be skipped.','They only help with adding text and numbers.','They make the presentation look like every other presentation.','They help make the presentation more organized and visually appealing.','D','Critical thinking involves understanding why certain tools are helpful. Templates help organize the structure of the presentation, while illustrations make it more engaging and visually attractive. Both tools work together to create a better overall presentation.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,31,'Jonas and Janneth are tasked with creating a budget plan for a school event using spreadsheet software. Their ALS teacher explains how to use built-in templates and illustrations to help learners organize their data and make the budget plan clear and visually appealing.','What should they do first to organize their budget efficiently using spreadsheet software?','Use illustrations before entering the data.','Add random numbers into the spreadsheet.','Skip templates and manually create all sections of the budget.','Select a pre-designed budget template from the spreadsheet software.','D','Using a pre-designed template helps Jonas and Janneth organize their budget efficiently. Templates provide structured rows and columns, making it easier to enter data and focus on the content rather than the format.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,32,'Jonas and Janneth are tasked with creating a budget plan for a school event using spreadsheet software. Their ALS teacher explains how to use built-in templates and illustrations to help learners organize their data and make the budget plan clear and visually appealing.','Why is it important for Jonas and Janneth to add relevant illustrations, such as food or money icons, in their spreadsheet?','Illustrations make the spreadsheet harder to understand.','Illustrations make the spreadsheet more colorful but not helpful.','Illustrations should only be used if there is enough space in the spreadsheet.','Illustrations help clarify and organize the information visually, making it easier to understand.','D','Illustrations enhance the clarity of the spreadsheet by providing visual cues that help categorize the information, making it easier to understand the budget plan immediately.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,33,'Jonas and Janneth are tasked with creating a budget plan for a school event using spreadsheet software. Their ALS teacher explains how to use built-in templates and illustrations to help learners organize their data and make the budget plan clear and visually appealing.','Why should Jonas and Janneth use a template instead of creating a budget plan from scratch when using spreadsheet software?','Templates are more fun to use but don’t help with organization.','Templates allow them to finish quickly without thinking about how to organize the budget.','Templates are not necessary; it’s better to create everything manually for better learning.','Templates provide an organized structure, saving time and helping them focus on entering the correct data.','D','Critical thinking involves understanding the benefits of tools. Templates save time by providing an organized layout, so Jonas and Janneth can focus on inputting accurate data rather than spending time on formatting and structure.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,34,'Learners of Libertad District are given the opportunity to create a flyer for an upcoming school event using word processing software. Their teacher, Mrs. Diango, explains how to select and use the tools in the menu bar to make the flyer look attractive and professional.','When creating a flyer for a school event, how would you use the Font Size tool in the menu bar to solve the problem of making the title of the flyer stand out?','Change the text color to green.','Use a smaller font size to fit more text.','Make the title bold to make it stand out.','Increase the font size to make the title bigger and more noticeable.','D','Increasing the font size makes the title bigger, making it more visible and attention-grabbing for readers, which solves the problem of making the title stand out.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,35,'Learners of Libertad District are given the opportunity to create a flyer for an upcoming school event using word processing software. Their teacher, Mrs. Diango, explains how to select and use the tools in the menu bar to make the flyer look attractive and professional.','How would using the Insert Image tool help learners organize their flyer for the event?','It allows you to change the font style.','It helps you sort the text alphabetically.','It automatically adds a table of contents.','It lets you add relevant pictures or logos to enhance the flyer’s appearance.','D','The Insert Image tool helps to add images like school logos or event pictures, which makes the flyer more visually appealing and informative.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,36,'Learners of Libertad District are given the opportunity to create a flyer for an upcoming school event using word processing software. Their teacher, Mrs. Diango, explains how to select and use the tools in the menu bar to make the flyer look attractive and professional.','Why is it important to use the Align Text tool when creating a flyer for the event?','To add colors to the text.','To change the font style of the text.','To automatically arrange the images in the flyer.','To make sure the text is centered and properly aligned for a professional look.','D','Using the Align Text tool ensures the text is neatly aligned, improving the flyer’s overall appearance and making it look more organized and professional.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,37,'Lani is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a birthday card for her friend. Her teacher, Mr. Reymart, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Lani wants to make a birthday card for her friend, but she can''t find a template she likes. What is the best thing she can do to make the card look special?','Use any template and leave it as it is','Skip the card and just say “Happy Birthday” in person','Copy a card from the internet without changing anything','Use a simple template and add her own designs and decorations','D','Using a simple template and adding personal touches like drawings or stickers shows creativity and effort, even without the perfect template.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,38,'Lani is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a birthday card for her friend. Her teacher, Mr. Reymart, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Lani needs to find illustrations for her birthday card. Where is the best place for her to look for free images?','Her friend''s social media page.','A random website she found on the internet.','A website that offers free and safe images for educational use.','A paid website without checking if she has permission to use the images.','C','This option teaches Lani to find reliable and safe sources for free images, which is an important aspect of information literacy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,39,'Lani is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a birthday card for her friend. Her teacher, Mr. Reymart, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Mr. Reymart suggests using balloons and cakes as illustrations for the birthday card. What should Lani consider when choosing these illustrations?','Whether the illustrations are her favorite colors.','Whether the illustrations are colorful and match the birthday theme.','Whether the illustrations are the same as the ones on her last card.','Whether the illustrations are the same as her friend''s favorite sports.','B','This option encourages Lani to think critically about the relevance and appropriateness of the illustrations, ensuring they match the birthday theme and make the card look special.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,40,'Axel is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a thank you card for his teacher. His teacher, Ms. Irish, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Axel wants to make his thank you card look special, but he can''t find a template he likes. What should he do?','Give up and do not make the card.','Ask his friend to make the card for him.','Use a plain template and add his own decorations.','Use the first template he sees, even if he doesn''t like it.','C','This option encourages Axel to solve the problem by using a plain template and adding his own decorations, which allows him to personalize the card and make it special.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,41,'Axel is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a thank you card for his teacher. His teacher, Ms. Irish, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Axel needs to find illustrations for his thank you card. Where is the best place for him to look for free images?','His friend''s social media page.','A random website he found on the internet.','A website that offers free and safe images for educational use.','A paid website without checking if he has permission to use the images.','C','This option teaches Axel to find reliable and safe sources for free images, which is an important aspect of information literacy.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,42,'Axel is an ALS elementary learner who wants to make a thank you card for his teacher. His teacher, Ms. Irish, explains how to select the right template and illustrations to make the card look special.','Ms. Irish suggests using flowers and hearts as illustrations for the thank you card. What should Axel consider when choosing these illustrations?','Whether the illustrations are his favorite colors.','Whether the illustrations are the same as the ones on his last card.','Whether the illustrations are the same as his friend''s favorite sports.','Whether the illustrations are colorful and match the thank you theme.','D','This option encourages Axel to think critically about the relevance and appropriateness of the illustrations, ensuring they match the thank you theme and make the card look special.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,43,'Learners are given the task of planning a school field trip. They need to use basic concepts to make sure the trip is fun, safe, and well-organized. Their teacher, Mrs. Helen, guides them in selecting the right concepts to apply to different parts of the planning process.','When planning a field trip, why is it important to calculate the budget and ensure the total amount is enough for transportation, tickets, and food?','To decide how much money to spend on souvenirs.','To spend money on the most expensive food items.','To calculate the number of animals visiting the zoo.','To ensure there is enough money for all necessary expenses and avoid running out of funds.','D','Calculating the budget ensures that enough money is available to cover all important aspects of the field trip, such as transportation, tickets, and food, and avoids any last-minute shortages.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,44,'Learners are given the task of planning a school field trip. They need to use basic concepts to make sure the trip is fun, safe, and well-organized. Their teacher, Mrs. Helen, guides them in selecting the right concepts to apply to different parts of the planning process.','Which of the following basic concepts should be used to ensure safety during the school field trip?','Deciding which animals to visit first.','Choosing the best food vendors at the zoo.','Calculating the total cost of the tickets for everyone.','Ensuring students follow safety rules like wearing seatbelts and staying with the group.','D','Safety is a priority when planning any event. Ensuring that students follow safety rules such as wearing seatbelts and staying with the group helps keep everyone safe during the trip.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,45,'Learners are given the task of planning a school field trip. They need to use basic concepts to make sure the trip is fun, safe, and well-organized. Their teacher, Mrs. Helen, guides them in selecting the right concepts to apply to different parts of the planning process.','Why is it important to select appropriate activities for the school field trip, such as visiting specific animal enclosures or having a picnic?','To make the trip shorter and less exciting.','To spend more time looking at the gift shop.','To ensure students will follow the safety rules.','To make sure students enjoy the trip and learn something new.','D','Selecting appropriate activities ensures that the students have an engaging, fun, and educational experience during the field trip, making the event enjoyable and memorable',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,46,'Ruelyn wants to apply and submit a letter to a company using word processing software. Her teacher, Mr. Bahian, explains how to use the basic tools in the word processing software, such as typing, saving, and printing, to create a neat and organized letter.','Why is it important for Ruelyn to save her letter while working on it using the word processing software?','To increase the size of the letter.','To make the letter look more colorful.','To make sure the letter prints clearly.','To prevent losing her work if the computer shuts down.','D','Saving letters regularly helps avoid losing any work in case of unexpected issues, like the computer shutting down, ensuring Ruelyn does not have to redo her progress.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,47,'Ruelyn wants to apply and submit a letter to a company using word processing software. Her teacher, Mr. Bahian, explains how to use the basic tools in the word processing software, such as typing, saving, and printing, to create a neat and organized letter.','Which of the following basic tools in word processing software would help Ruelyn format her letter, so it looks neat and professional?','The typing tool to write the text.','The save tool to store her work.','The bold tool to make the title stand out.','All of the above.','D','All the tools mentioned—typing, bold, and save—are essential for creating a well-organized and professional-looking letter. The typing tool allows for writing the content, the bold tool highlights important parts (like the title), and the save tool ensures the work is not lost.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,48,'Ruelyn wants to apply and submit a letter to a company using word processing software. Her teacher, Mr. Bahian, explains how to use the basic tools in the word processing software, such as typing, saving, and printing, to create a neat and organized letter.','Why should Ruelyn print her letter after she finishes it in the word processing software?','To practice using the printer.','To make the letter look longer.','To get a hard copy to submit to the company.','To keep a record of the computer’s settings.','C','Printing the letter gives Ruelyn a hard copy that she can physically submit to the company, which is typically required when applying for a job or submitting formal documents.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,49,'The ALS learners of Kimalok CLC are preparing for their Learning Exhibit. They want to make colorful certificates to give to their classmates who joined the reading contest. Their teacher, Ma’am Zebb, shows them how to use desktop publishing software to create the certificates. The learners choose a layout, type the names, add some clipart, and adjust the text style to make the certificates look neat and presentable. After finishing, they save and print their work, ready to hand out on exhibit day.','While making the certificates, some learners noticed that the text was too big and did not fit in the space provided. What should they do to fix the problem?','Change the paper size.','Print the certificate right away.','Remove the names from the certificate.','Make the text smaller or adjust the text box.','D','This is a basic problem-solving step. When text doesn’t fit properly, resizing the text or adjusting the layout helps make the content fit without removing important parts.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,2,50,'The ALS learners of Kimalok CLC are preparing for their Learning Exhibit. They want to make colorful certificates to give to their classmates who joined the reading contest. Their teacher, Ma’am Zebb, shows them how to use desktop publishing software to create the certificates. The learners choose a layout, type the names, add some clipart, and adjust the text style to make the certificates look neat and presentable. After finishing, they save and print their work, ready to hand out on exhibit day.','Which feature of the desktop publishing software helps the learners make the certificate more colorful and attractive?','Spell check tool','Save and exit buttons','Clipart and layout templates','Zoom in and zoom out buttons','C','Using layout templates and clipart helps learners organize content and make the certificates visually appealing, showing their ability to find and use the right tools in the software.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,51,'The ALS learners of Kimalok CLC are preparing for their Learning Exhibit. They want to make colorful certificates to give to their classmates who joined the reading contest. Their teacher, Ma’am Zebb, shows them how to use desktop publishing software to create the certificates. The learners choose a layout, type the names, add some clipart, and adjust the text style to make the certificates look neat and presentable. After finishing, they save and print their work, ready to hand out on exhibit day.','Why is it important for the learners to adjust the text style (like font size and color) on the certificate?','To finish the task quickly','To avoid using too much ink','To make the computer run faster','To make it look fun and easy to read','D','Choosing the right font style, size, and color helps make the certificate more attractive and readable. This reflects the learners'' ability to think critically about design and purpose.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,52,'Dave is a learner at Danao CLC who wants to share what he knows about keeping clean and healthy. He uses presentation software to make slides about proper hygiene. He adds short words, pictures like toothbrushes and soap, and picks nice colors. After making his slides, he saves and practices showing them to others.','Dave wants to make sure his pictures fit nicely on each slide. What should he do if the picture is too big?','Delete the picture right away','Move the picture off the slide','Resize the picture to make it smaller','Add more pictures on the same slide','C','Resizing allows the picture to fit well without deleting it. This shows Dave’s ability to solve layout problems using the tools in the software.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,53,'Dave is a learner at Danao CLC who wants to share what he knows about keeping clean and healthy. He uses presentation software to make slides about proper hygiene. He adds short words, pictures like toothbrushes and soap, and picks nice colors. After making his slides, he saves and practices showing them to others.','Why did Dave choose short words and clear pictures for his slides?','To use less electricity','To finish the task quickly','To make the slides load faster','To make his message easy to understand','D','Choosing short words and clear pictures helps the audience easily understand the message, which shows Dave is thinking about how to best communicate his ideas.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,54,'Learners at Tagpako CLC are helping their teacher, Sir Jun, list the names and scores of their classmates after a reading activity. They use spreadsheet software to type the names, record the scores, and even add the total scores using simple tools in the software. They learn how to use rows and columns to keep everything neat and easy to understand.','If Sir Jun wants to quickly find who got the highest score, what should the learners do?','Look at each score one by one','Rearrange the rows manually','Use a calculator to double-check','Use the “Sort” tool in the spreadsheet software','D','Using the Sort tool is a smart and efficient way to find the highest score. It shows the learner can solve problems using the features of the software.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,55,'Learners at Tagpako CLC are helping their teacher, Sir Jun, list the names and scores of their classmates after a reading activity. They use spreadsheet software to type the names, record the scores, and even add the total scores using simple tools in the software. They learn how to use rows and columns to keep everything neat and easy to understand.','Why is it a good idea to use rows and columns in listing names and scores?','It uses more space','It’s required by the teacher','It helps organize the data clearly','It makes the worksheet look fancy','C','Rows and columns are essential in spreadsheets because they help arrange information clearly. This shows the learner understands how structure supports clarity. Index',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,56,'Learners at Tagpako CLC are helping their teacher, Sir Jun, list the names and scores of their classmates after a reading activity. They use spreadsheet software to type the names, record the scores, and even add the total scores using simple tools in the software. They learn how to use rows and columns to keep everything neat and easy to understand.','Florelyn is making a flowchart about how to brush her teeth. She wants to show the step “Put toothpaste on the toothbrush.” Which symbol should she use to show this step as an action?','Arrow – to connect steps in the flowchart','Oval – to show where the flowchart starts or ends','Diamond – to ask a question like “Is the toothbrush ready?”','Rectangle – to show a task like putting toothpaste on the toothbrush','D','In a flowchart, a rectangle is used for actions or tasks, like putting toothpaste. The oval is for start/end, the diamond for decisions, and the arrow shows the flow from one step to another.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,57,NULL,'Why is it important to use the correct symbols in a flowchart when explaining a process?','To make the flowchart longer','To make the flowchart more artistic','To make the flowchart look colorful','To help people understand the steps clearly','D','Using the correct symbols helps people understand what each part of the flowchart represents — whether it’s a start, action, decision, or end. This makes the flowchart easier to follow and avoids confusion. The goal is clarity, not decoration or length.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,58,NULL,'Anna wants to explain the process of how to enroll in the ALS program step-by- step using a flowchart. Which type of flowchart should she use?','Data flow diagram','Organizational chart','Process flowchart','System flowchart','C','A process flowchart is best for showing a step-by-step procedure or workflow, such as the enrollment process. It helps illustrate the sequence of actions decisions needed to complete a task. This type of flowchart is ideal for Anna’s purpose.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,59,NULL,'You searched online for examples of flowcharts to use in your group activity. One website shows a chart with boxes connected by arrows showing steps like “Start → Input Name → Verify Data → Submit.” How do you verify if this is a flowchart process?','Check if it lists people in an organization','Check if it includes roles and responsibilities','Check if it follows a sequence of tasks or actions','Check if it shows data moving between systems','C','Information literacy involves knowing how to evaluate and verify information. In this case, the chart showing a sequence of tasks from start to finish is a clear sign of a process flowchart. Identifying the purpose and structure of the chart the learner confirm its type correctly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,60,NULL,'Jessa wants to create a flow chart that shows each step she follows when logging in to her email account—from typing her username to see her inbox. What type of flowchart should she use to show the steps in order?','Process flowchart – shows step-by-step actions','Decision flowchart – focuses only on yes/no questions','Organizational chart – shows roles in a company or group','Data flow diagram – shows how data moves between systems','A','A process flowchart shows sequential steps in doing a task—like logging in.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,61,NULL,'Mark is designing a flowchart to help users create a strong password. His flowchart asks questions like “Is it 8 characters or more?” and “Does it have a symbol?” What kind of flowchart works best when decisions or questions are involved?','Cycle diagram – shows repeating steps','Timeline chart – shows events in order over time','Process flowchart – shows steps but not decisions','Decision flowchart – shows questions with yes/no answers','D','A decision flowchart includes questions and gives different actions based on answers (yes or no).',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,62,NULL,'Anna is making a flowchart about how she prepares a cup of coffee. She wants to show the correct order of steps. Which of the following should be the first step in her flowchart?','Boil the water','Stir the coffee','Pour hot water into the cup','Add sugar and coffee to the cup','A','You must boil the water first before you can mix anything. It''s the starting action that makes all other steps possible when making coffee.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,63,'You are making a flowchart about “How to Wash Your Hands.” You included these steps: I. Wet hands II. Apply soap III. Rinse hands IV. Dry hands','What important step did you forget to include?','Count to 10','Use hand sanitizer','Rub hands with soap','Shake hands with others','C','Critical thinking is needed to recognize missing or incorrect steps in a sequence. “Rubbing hands together with soap” is essential in removing germs and is a critical part of the handwashing process.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,64,NULL,'Mark is asked to make a flow chart about how to log in to his e-mail. What should he do first to make sure his flowchart is correct?','Ask his friend to do it for him','Guess the steps based on what he remembers','Watch a video tutorial or read instructions online','Draw the chart immediately without checking the steps','C','Information literacy involves finding and using accurate information. By researching or watching a tutorial, Mark ensures he includes the correct steps in his flowchart. This develops the learner’s ability to locate reliable sources and apply them properly.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,65,'Lito wants to water his plants using a simple set of steps. He writes the following instructions: 1. Get the watering can. 2. Fill the watering can with water. 3. Walk to the garden. 4. Water the plants. 5. Return the watering can.','Which is the best order to follow these steps, so the task is done correctly and completely?','2 → 1 → 3 → 4 → 5','1 → 3 → 2 → 4 → 5','1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5','3 → 1 → 2 → 4 → 5','C','Lito should get the watering can first, then fill it, go to the garden, water the plants, and return the can. This follows the proper sequence of actions to complete the task effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,66,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade uses block coding to create a project that teaches others about digital safety. She builds it by dragging blocks to make a character move, play a sound, and show a message. What is one good reason why block coding is helpful for her project?','It makes her project hard for others to understand','It removes all images and sounds from the project','It only works if you use text commands instead of blocks','It lets her make an interactive project without writing complicated code','D','Block coding allows users to create programs by connecting blocks instead of typing code. It makes programming easier and more visual, which is perfect for beginners like Jade.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,67,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','If Jade''s character doesn''t move when she clicks the start button, what could be the problem?','She forgot to add the sound block.','She forgot to add a message block.','She may have used the wrong type of block.','She doesn''t need the character to move her project.','C','The issue could be that Jade chose an incorrect block for the movement action. She needs to ensure she uses the proper motion block to make the character move.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,68,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Where can Jade find more information if she needs help with using block coding?','By reading books that are not related to technology.','By ignoring the problem and continuing without help.','By asking a friend who doesn’t know about block coding.','By searching online tutorials or asking her teacher for guidance.','D','To effectively learn and troubleshoot block coding, Jade should seek guidance from reliable sources like tutorials or ask her teacher for help.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,69,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Why did Jade choose the motion block, sound block, and looks block to create her interactive media project?','To make her character talk and give tips.','To make the project look nice with colors.','To make a game where the character goes around in circles.','To make her character move, play sound, and show messages.','D','Jade selected these blocks because they allowed her to show digital safety tips in an interactive way by making the character move, playing a sound when each tip was shown, and displaying the message for the safety tip.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,70,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','If Jade wanted to add more tips and display them in different colors, which block would she need to use?','Looks block','Motion block','Sound block','Control block','A','The looks block is used to control how things appear on the screen, including changing colors and displaying messages, which Jade would need to use to show the digital safety tips in different colors.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,71,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Where can Jade find information on how to use the different blocks in block coding for her project?','By guessing which blocks might work.','By asking her teacher for instructions.','By watching a movie about digital safety.','By searching online for tutorials on block coding.','D','Jade can find helpful tutorials on how to use the blocks by searching online, which will provide her with clear instructions and examples on using block coding tools effectively.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,72,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','What is the main reason why Jade uses different types of blocks like motion, sound, and looks in her project?','To make an interactive project that works properly','To make the project look complicated and harder to understand.','To confuse the users of the project, so the users cannot use it easily.','To make the project take longer to complete, and it delays the results.','A','Jade uses different blocks to make her project interactive by ensuring the character moves, plays sounds, and displays messages, creating a smooth and engaging experience for users',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,73,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade wants the character to stop moving when the digital safety tip is displayed. Which block should she use?','Motion block','Repeat block','Stop block','Sound block','C','To make the character stop moving, Jade would need to use the "Stop" block. The "motion" block only controls movement, so she must add a stop action to prevent continuous movement.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,74,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade uses motion, sound, and looks blocks in her digital safety project. Why is using different types of blocks important for her project?','It limits the features Jade can add to her project','It increases the size of the file, so it looks more impressive','It makes the computer run faster while showing the project','It helps make the project more interactive and keeps the audience interested','D','Using different blocks allows Jade to include movement, sound, and messages, which makes the project engaging and easier to understand for others.',NULL,0,1),
('ELEM','LS6',3,3,75,'Jade is an ALS student who enjoys learning how to use technology. One day, her teacher asks her to create a simple project to teach other students about digital safety. Jade can use block coding to create her project.\n\nBlock coding lets Jade build programs by dragging and connecting blocks that do different things, like making something move, playing a sound, or showing a message. For her project, Jade chooses blocks to: 1. Make the character move (to show digital safety tips). 2. Play a sound (when a tip is shown). 3. Show a message (for each digital safety tip).\n\nJade uses the motion block to move the character, the sound block to play sounds, and the looks block to show messages. After arranging the blocks in the right order, Jade tests her project. When she clicks the start button, the character moves and shares the digital safety tips with a sound playing in the background.','Jade notices that when she clicks the start button, the character does not move across the screen. What might be the problem?','She forgot to add a sound block','She used too many looks blocks','She did not connect the motion block correctly','She added too many characters to the screen','C','The motion block is responsible for making the character move. If the character doesn''t move, the issue likely lies in how the motion block was connected or programmed.',NULL,0,1);
